{"scenario_id": "scn_0000", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.8, "cohesion_score": 7.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 66.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.01}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme e-commerce mature (1.8 ans) avec une stack Python/Django/PostgreSQL bien maîtrisée par une équipe majoritairement senior. La principale problématique identifiée est la fréquence des incidents en production malgré une codebase globalement saine.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques indiquent une architecture solide : faible couplage (1.8/10), bonne cohésion (7.1/10) et complexité cyclomatique très raisonnable (2.5). La couverture de tests (66.6%) est perfectible mais pas alarmante. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.01) suggèrent que les incidents proviennent probablement de causes externes (infra, données, intégrations).", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser l'amélioration de la fiabilité via : 1) Un audit des incidents passés pour identifier les patterns récurrents 2) Le renforcement des tests d'intégration et des contrats d'API 3) L'ajout de monitoring transactionnel.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyse rétrospective des 10 derniers incidents critiques avec l'équipe produit et ops", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de tests contractuels pour les intégrations externes identifiées comme fragiles", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de Synthetic Monitoring sur les parcours clients critiques", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les dépendances externes (paiement, logistique) dans la résolution des problèmes de fiabilité. Une attention particulière doit être portée aux timeouts et mécanismes de retry."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0000", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.8, "cohesion_score": 7.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 66.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.01}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 1.8-year-old e-commerce platform built with Python/Django and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 11 developers (mostly senior). While the codebase shows good structural health metrics, the team's primary pain point is production reliability, with frequent uptime incidents impacting operations.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a fundamentally healthy codebase: low coupling (1.8/10), high cohesion (7.1/10), reasonable test coverage (66.6%), and low cyclomatic complexity (2.5). The minimal bugfix-commit ratio (0.01) on hot files and absence of significant anti-patterns suggest the uptime issues likely stem from operational factors (deployment, monitoring, infrastructure) rather than code quality.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted operational improvements and incremental code enhancements. The metrics do not justify the risk of a full migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement enhanced monitoring and alerting for critical paths (checkout, payment processing). Instrument key transactions to isolate failure points.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Conduct a production incident retrospective to identify recurring patterns. Prioritize fixes for the top 3 root causes (likely infrastructure or third-party integrations).", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage for critical modules (e.g., order processing) to 80%+. Focus on integration tests for reliability-sensitive components.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is misdiagnosing uptime issues as code problems when they may be infrastructural. A rewrite would waste resources without addressing the actual constraint. Incremental improvements allow for measurable reliability gains while preserving team velocity."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0001", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.0, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme edtech mature (10+ ans) avec une base de code Java/Spring Boot critique pour la conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). L'équipe de 20 développeurs maintient activement le système tout en gérant des contraintes réglementaires strictes.", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une dette technique modérée (couplage/cohésion autour de 4/10) mais gérable. La couverture de tests à 58.7% et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5.0 indiquent une base raisonnablement maintenable. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont localisés (1 fichier 'hot' et 1 god class medium). La contrainte majeure reste la conformité, pas la technologie.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques et améliorer progressivement la couverture de tests dans les modules sensibles à la conformité. La stack actuelle reste adaptée aux besoins réglementaires.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du Long Parameter List dans handler.py avec extraction de DTOs spécifiques", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpage progressif de la God Class dans processor.py via l'extraction de services métiers", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests (+15%) sur les modules traitant des données sensibles", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est d'introduire des régressions sur les fonctionnalités critiques de conformité pendant les refactorings. Mitigation : revues de code renforcées et tests d'intégration automatisés avant chaque déploiement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0001", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.0, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10.6-year-old edtech platform built with Java, Spring Boot, and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 20 developers. Regulatory compliance (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) is identified as the dominant constraint, requiring the codebase to adhere to strict standards.", "analysis": "The codebase metrics indicate moderate coupling (4.0/10) and cohesion (4.5/10), with a fair test coverage of 58.7%. Cyclomatic complexity is well-managed at 5.0, and the bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is low (0.23). However, anti-patterns like Long Parameter List (high) and God Class (medium) are present, suggesting localized refactoring opportunities rather than systemic issues.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate. Instead, focus on targeted improvements to enhance compliance, refactor anti-patterns, and incrementally improve test coverage and cohesion. A full rewrite is unnecessary given the overall health of the codebase.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor Long Parameter List in src/edtech/handler.py and extract functionality from the God Class in src/edtech/processor.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Enhance test coverage by adding unit and integration tests for critical compliance-related modules.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a compliance audit and implement necessary adjustments to meet RGPD, PCI-DSS, and HDS standards.", "duration_days_range": "25-30 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks are delays in achieving compliance and potential regressions during refactoring. Mitigate these risks with thorough testing and phased rollouts."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0002", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.3, "cohesion_score": 3.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 24.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.84}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 3.3-year-old media streaming platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 42 developers (56% junior, 41% senior). The primary constraint is reliability, as frequent production incidents are impacting uptime. Despite a moderately coupled architecture, the codebase suffers from low cohesion, high cyclomatic complexity, and inadequate test coverage, with several anti-patterns identified in critical modules.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant technical debt, particularly in terms of coupling and cohesion, which is contributing to frequent production incidents. High cyclomatic complexity and low test coverage further exacerbate the reliability issues. While there are notable anti-patterns, they are concentrated in specific modules rather than pervasive across the entire codebase. This suggests that targeted improvements could yield significant benefits without requiring a full migration.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full rewrite. Focus on incremental improvements to reduce coupling, improve cohesion, and increase test coverage. Prioritize refactoring the most problematic modules, such as src/media/handler.py and src/media/processor.py, to address high coupling, circular dependencies, and long methods. Invest in enhancing test coverage to mitigate reliability issues.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/media/handler.py to reduce coupling and circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address long methods and duplicate code in src/media/processor.py and src/media/service.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage across the codebase, focusing on critical paths to improve reliability.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is that incremental refactoring may not fully resolve reliability issues if underlying architectural problems persist. Additionally, improving test coverage in a codebase with high cyclomatic complexity could be time-consuming and may require significant effort to stabilize. However, these risks are outweighed by the potential benefits of avoiding a costly and disruptive full rewrite."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0003", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.9, "cohesion_score": 4.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 36.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.46}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme médicale développée en Python/Django avec MongoDB pour le stockage des données sensibles. L'équipe mixte (juniors/seniors) maintient activement cette solution soumise à des exigences strictes de conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). La codebase, relativement jeune (1 an), présente des signes de complexité croissante dans les modules critiques de traitement des données santé.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase en phase de maturation avec des tensions architecturales localisées. Le couplage modéré (3.9/10) et la cohésion acceptable (4.8/10) ne justifient pas un refactoring complet. Les anti-patterns détectés sont concentrés sur 3 fichiers seulement, mais le ratio de commits correctifs (0.46) et la couverture de tests faible (36.3%) sur ces fichiers exigent une intervention ciblée. La complexité cyclomatique (6.8) reste dans les limites acceptables pour le domaine médical.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser un refactoring incrémental des modules critiques identifiés, accompagné d'une augmentation de la couverture de tests. Renforcer les pratiques de revue de code pour les juniors sur ces parties sensibles.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les méthodes problématiques dans processor.py (Long Method + Circular Dependency) avec pairing senior/junior", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration pour les modules refactorés (cible 70%+ sur ces fichiers)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit des dépendances circulaires dans handler.py et restructuration modulaire", "duration_days_range": "6-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : déstabilisation des fonctionnalités critiques liées au traitement des données santé pendant le refactoring. Mitigation : validation systématique par des tests manuels des flux métiers après chaque modification, avec traçabilité documentée pour la conformité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0003", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.9, "cohesion_score": 4.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 36.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.46}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "This medical technology project, built on Python/Django with MongoDB, focuses on healthcare data processing with strict regulatory compliance requirements (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS). The 6-person development team (mixed seniority) maintains a relatively young codebase (1 year old) showing moderate technical debt in critical processing components.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits concerning but not catastrophic metrics: low-to-moderate coupling (3.9/10) and cohesion (4.8/10), suboptimal test coverage (36.3%), and elevated cyclomatic complexity (6.8). Anti-patterns concentrate in core processing files, particularly circular dependencies and long methods in processor.py. The 0.46 bugfix ratio on hot files indicates stability risks in critical paths. Given the regulatory constraints, technical debt in core components poses compliance verification challenges.", "recommendation": "Targeted refactoring without stack migration. Prioritize: 1) Breaking circular dependencies in processor.py/handler.py, 2) Splitting long methods in processor.py, 3) Improving test coverage to 60%+ for compliance auditing. The young codebase and contained anti-patterns don't justify a rewrite, but core refactoring is urgent for maintainability under regulatory scrutiny.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in processor.py and handler.py with dependency inversion", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decompose long methods in processor.py using strategy pattern for regulatory logic", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Boost test coverage to 60% with focus on compliance-critical paths", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk lies in unaddressed circular dependencies during compliance audits. The long methods in processor.py could lead to interpretation errors during regulatory reviews. Test coverage below 50% makes certification processes more expensive. All risks are contained to specific modules and addressable within 4-6 weeks of focused work."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0004", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 7.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 78.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une marketplace mature (1,8 ans) construite sur une stack Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 11 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack, malgré une codebase globalement saine et bien testée.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont excellentes : faible couplage (1.1/10), bonne cohésion (7.3/10), couverture de tests élevée (78.8%) et complexité maîtrisée (3.4). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et un faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers sensibles (0.08) confirment une base de code stable. Le seul problème identifié est humain : la difficulté à recruter sur Java/Spring Boot.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique actuelle. La solution pragmatique consiste à : 1) Former les juniors en interne via un programme de mentorat senior/junior 2) Recruter 1-2 profils seniors complémentaires sur des stacks adjacentes (Kotlin/Spring ou TypeScript) pour diversifier progressivement les compétences.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Mise en place d'un programme de mentorat avec pairing obligatoire sur les PR critiques", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Introduction progressive de Kotlin pour les nouvelles features (sans modifier l'existant)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Recrutement ciblé de 1 senior fullstack (Kotlin/TypeScript) pour renforcer l'équipe", "duration_days_range": "30-45 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la frustration des juniors si le mentorat est mal encadré. Bien calibrer les sessions de pairing pour éviter le burnout des seniors. L'introduction de Kotlin doit rester optionnelle et mesurée (max 20% du nouveau code)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0005", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 4.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de streaming média mature, développée en Java/Spring Boot avec PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe expérimentée. La codebase montre des signes typiques de vieillissement modéré, avec quelques problèmes localisés de duplication et couplage, mais aucune dette technique critique.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales indiquent une codebase relativement saine pour son âge (10+ ans). Le couplage et la cohésion sont dans la moyenne basse (4.6/10 et 4.8/10), mais pas alarmants. La couverture de tests à 49% est insuffisante mais typique pour ce type de projet. Les anti-patterns détectés sont concentrés sur quelques fichiers (handler.py, service.py) et représentent des opportunités claires d'amélioration ciblée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser le refactoring incrémental des zones problématiques identifiées, en commençant par les duplications (high) et la God Class. Augmenter progressivement la couverture de tests pendant ces refactorings.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactorer les duplications (high) dans core.py et handler.py, avec tests unitaires associés", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Décomposer la God Class dans handler.py en modules plus ciblés", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Traiter les dépendances circulaires et long parameter lists dans service.py", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer l'impact des changements sur les parties couplées de la codebase. Une approche incrémentale avec des tests de non-régression est cruciale. Les phases 1 et 2 doivent être menées par des seniors compte tenu de la criticité des fichiers concernés."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0005", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 4.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature Java/Spring Boot media streaming platform with PostgreSQL, maintained by a 38-developer team (30% senior/junior split). While the codebase shows moderate structural health, it suffers from localized complexity in core media handling components and some duplication.", "analysis": "Metrics indicate a codebase with acceptable coupling (4.6/10) and cohesion (4.8/10), though test coverage is borderline (49.2%). The medium cyclomatic complexity (4.3) and bugfix ratio (0.33) don't suggest systemic instability. Anti-patterns are concentrated in media handling logic (God Class, duplicate code) and service layer (circular dependencies). No critical constraints were reported by the team.", "recommendation": "DO NOT migrate or rewrite. Execute targeted refactoring of high-impact anti-patterns first, then improve test coverage. The metrics don't justify the risk of a full stack migration for this mature system.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in core.py and handler.py (high severity), extract God Class functionality into dedicated services", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break circular dependencies in service.py through interface segregation, address long parameter lists", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to 65% with focused unit tests for refactored components", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low operational risk if refactoring is phased. The main risk is temporary velocity impact during media handler changes, mitigated by the senior-heavy team composition. Anti-pattern corrections will reduce long-term maintenance costs."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0006", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.3, "cohesion_score": 1.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 23.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.89}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 4-year-old fintech payment platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 22 developers (40% junior, 8% senior). The team reports difficulty in hiring talent for the current stack, and the codebase exhibits high coupling, low cohesion, and significant technical debt in critical modules.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal a codebase with severe structural issues: high coupling (8.3/10), very low cohesion (1.2/10), and inadequate test coverage (23.3%). Cyclomatic complexity (11.1) indicates overly complex logic, and the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.89) in critical files suggests instability. Anti-patterns are concentrated in core payment processing logic (processor.py, service.py), with duplication, long methods, and tight coupling. While the talent shortage is a concern, the technical state poses a greater immediate risk to maintainability.", "recommendation": "Do not rewrite. Prioritize targeted refactoring of high-risk modules (processor.py, service.py, handler.py) to reduce coupling and duplication while improving test coverage. Address talent shortages through upskilling and hiring mid-level engineers familiar with Python.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor processor.py to break up long methods, reduce parameter lists, and eliminate duplication. Add unit tests for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decouple handler.py from downstream dependencies using interfaces or events. Improve test coverage to at least 60% for this module.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a team workshop on Python/Flask best practices (dependency injection, SOLID principles) to address knowledge gaps.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are: (1) destabilizing the payment processing logic during refactoring, (2) failing to improve cohesion due to deeply embedded patterns, and (3) slow progress due to junior-heavy team. Mitigations: pair programming for critical refactors, incremental changes with feature flags, and allocating senior oversight for high-risk files."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0007", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 75.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.1}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace en croissance avec une base de code Ruby on Rails mature (1.5 ans), maintenue par une équipe expérimentée. La stack actuelle montre une bonne santé technique mais l'équipe anticipe des défis de scalabilité lors des pics de trafic imprévisibles.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont excellentes : couplage très faible (1.1/10), cohésion élevée (8.0/10), couverture de tests solide (75.4%) et complexité cyclomatique optimale (1.8). L'absence d'anti-patterns et le faible ratio de correctifs (0.1) indiquent une base de code stable et bien conçue. La scalabilité est le seul point d'attention identifié.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Optimiser l'architecture existante pour la scalabilité via des améliorations ciblées : caching stratégique, mise à l'échelle horizontale des composants critiques et profiling des goulots d'étranglement.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit de performance sous charge et identification des 2-3 endpoints les plus sensibles aux pics de trafic", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de Redis pour le caching des requêtes critiques + configuration de read replicas MySQL", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des services métier pour supporter le sharding futur si nécessaire", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les besoins réels de scalabilité. Recommandation : mettre en place un plan de load testing continu et des métriques temps-réel sur l'infra. Alternative si les optimisations échouent : migration partielle vers Elixir/Phoenix uniquement pour les services critiques, pas de rewrite complet."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0007", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 75.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.1}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 1.5-year-old Ruby on Rails marketplace application with MySQL, maintained by a team of 43 developers (mix of junior and senior). The primary challenge is handling unpredictable traffic spikes while maintaining system scalability. The codebase shows strong cohesion, low coupling, and decent test coverage, with no significant anti-patterns detected.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase: low coupling (1.1/10), high cohesion (8.0/10), reasonable test coverage (75.4%), and low cyclomatic complexity (1.8). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.1) suggests stable hot files. There is no technical debt or anti-patterns justifying a full rewrite. The scalability constraint is likely infrastructure-related rather than a code quality issue.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted scalability improvements, such as optimizing database queries, introducing caching layers, or refining the deployment pipeline. The existing code quality supports incremental enhancements.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a scalability audit (database, caching, background jobs) to identify bottlenecks.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement high-impact optimizations (e.g., query tuning, Redis caching for high-traffic endpoints).", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Enhance monitoring and auto-scaling configurations to handle traffic spikes.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is underestimating infrastructure limitations. If optimizations are insufficient, consider a partial migration (e.g., moving compute-heavy services to a more scalable runtime) rather than a full rewrite. The team composition (34% seniors) is well-suited for incremental improvements."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0008", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.3, "cohesion_score": 8.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.01}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace développée en Node.js/NestJS avec une base PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La codebase, vieille de près de 2 ans, présente une bonne santé technique avec une couverture de tests élevée et une complexité maîtrisée.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase saine : faible couplage (2.3/10), forte cohésion (8.1/10), couverture de tests satisfaisante (72.3%) et complexité cyclomatique très basse (3.6). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers sensibles confirment cette stabilité.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. La stack actuelle est adaptée au contexte et bien maîtrisée par l'équipe. Privilégier des améliorations incrémentales ciblant spécifiquement les rares points de couplage résiduels.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit architectural ciblé sur les 5% de composants présentant un couplage modéré (score >4)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Atelier d'architecture avec les seniors pour formaliser des guidelines de découplage", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque serait de perturber inutilement une codebase stable avec des modifications radicales. L'équipe junior bénéficierait davantage d'un mentoring ciblé sur les bonnes pratiques existantes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0009", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.8, "cohesion_score": 2.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 12.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 8.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.87}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The team maintains a 3‑year‑old fintech payment platform built with Java, Spring Boot, and PostgreSQL. With a nine‑person team that includes a high proportion of junior developers, they are struggling to attract talent for the current technology stack.", "analysis": "The static‑analysis data shows a codebase with severe quality issues: coupling is high (7.8/10), cohesion is very low (2.3/10), test coverage is only 12 %, and cyclomatic complexity averages 8.2, indicating many dense functions. The bug‑fix‑to‑commit ratio on the hottest file (0.87) suggests that most changes are corrective rather than feature‑focused. Anti‑pattern detection confirms systemic problems—duplicate code, circular dependencies, god classes, long methods, and high‑coupling hotspots across core, processor, and service modules. These symptoms collectively point to a codebase that is hard to maintain, difficult for junior staff to understand, and unattractive to new hires. However, the stack itself (Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL) is still mainstream in fintech, so a full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk and cost. The prudent path is a disciplined, incremental refactoring effort combined with a testing uplift.", "recommendation": "Begin a staged technical‑debt remediation program instead of a full migration. Prioritize establishing a solid test suite, modularising the most coupled components, and eliminating the most critical anti‑patterns. Parallelly, invest in mentorship and up‑skilling for junior developers to reduce the talent‑scarcity impact.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Introduce unit‑test scaffolding and enforce a minimum 30 % coverage target on the most volatile modules (core, processor).", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor high‑coupling and god‑class hotspots: extract interfaces, split responsibilities, and resolve circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "15-22 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Remove duplicate code and shorten long methods/parameter lists through extraction and reusable utilities.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement static‑analysis quality gates (e.g., SonarQube) and embed them into CI to enforce ongoing cohesion and complexity limits.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Launch a focused mentorship program and a targeted hiring campaign emphasizing Java/Spring expertise to mitigate the talent shortage.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risks are regression introduced by refactoring and the potential slowdown of feature delivery while tests are being written. Mitigation includes strict code‑review policies, automated regression test suites, and allocating dedicated capacity for debt work each sprint. The incremental approach keeps the system operational, limits disruption, and gradually improves maintainability, making the talent‑scarcity issue more manageable."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0010", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.8, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 77.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Nous analysons une plateforme edtech en production depuis 2.2 ans, construite avec Python/Flask et PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe de 7 développeurs (40% juniors). La contrainte principale exprimée par l'équipe est une vélocité de développement perçue comme insuffisante pour livrer rapidement de nouvelles fonctionnalités.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques montrent une codebase globalement saine : faible couplage (2.8/10), haute cohésion (7.7/10), couverture de tests satisfaisante (77.8%) et complexité cyclomatique basse (2.9). Le ratio de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud (0.08) indique une stabilité acceptable. Le seul anti-pattern significatif détecté concerne une liste de paramètres trop longue dans un fichier service, mais à faible impact.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technologique actuelle, qui ne semble pas être la cause principale du ralentissement de la vélocité. Concentrer les efforts sur l'amélioration des pratiques de développement et l'automatisation des tâches répétitives pour accélérer le cycle de livraison.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des workflows de développement pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement (ex: temps de CI/CD, processus de revue de code)", "duration_days_range": "5-7 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring ciblé du fichier service.py pour résoudre l'anti-pattern Long Parameter List", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de sessions de pair programming pour accélérer l'intégration des développeurs juniors", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les besoins de formation et d'accompagnement des développeurs juniors, qui représentent 40% de l'équipe. Une attention particulière doit être portée à leur intégration pour maximiser leur productivité sans compromettre la qualité du code."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0010", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.8, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 77.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an established edtech platform built with Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, maintained by a mixed team of junior and senior developers. While the codebase shows good structural health with high cohesion and reasonable test coverage, the team reports development velocity as their primary constraint, with feature delivery being slower than desired.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a fundamentally healthy codebase: low coupling (2.8/10), high cohesion (7.7/10), solid test coverage (77.8%), and low cyclomatic complexity (2.9). The only detected anti-pattern (Long Parameter List) is isolated and low severity. The bugfix ratio (0.08) suggests stable core functionality. The velocity constraint likely stems from team composition (40% juniors needing mentorship) rather than technical debt.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The codebase's structural quality does not justify such risk. Instead, focus on team upskilling and targeted incremental improvements to accelerate feature delivery. Address the Long Parameter List anti-pattern as a quick win.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the Long Parameter List in src/edtech/service.py by introducing a parameter object or breaking the method into smaller functions.", "duration_days_range": "2-3 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement pair programming sessions between senior and junior developers to improve knowledge transfer and reduce bottlenecks in code reviews.", "duration_days_range": "Ongoing (start with 5-7 days for planning)"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Add integration test coverage for critical user journeys to reduce manual QA time (target +5% coverage).", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Minimal technical risk given the metrics. Primary risks are organizational: (1) Junior developers may need more architectural guidance, (2) Flask's synchronous nature could become a scaling constraint if concurrent user growth exceeds expectations. Monitor these non-code factors."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0011", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 4.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 43.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.5}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Application critique de gestion logistique développée en Ruby on Rails depuis 5 ans, avec une base MySQL. L'équipe de 45 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) rencontre des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production malgré une complexité modérée du code.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des signes de dette technique modérée : couplage et cohésion légèrement sous les seuils recommandés, couverture de tests insuffisante pour une application critique, et quelques anti-patterns localisés. Le ratio de commits correctifs indique une certaine instabilité sur des composants clés. La stack actuelle reste adaptée au domaine métier.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser des refactoring ciblés sur les points chauds identifiés et améliorer la couverture de tests. Former les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Ruby/Rails pour réduire les régressions.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du fichier service.py pour éliminer la duplication de code (high) et découper les longues méthodes dans handler.py (medium)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour porter la couverture à 70% sur les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers de formation pour juniors sur les patterns Rails avancés et les techniques de test", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principaux risques : 1) Perturbation des livraisons pendant les refactoring (atténuation : faire par petits increments avec tests de non-régression) 2) Résistance au changement chez les seniors (atténuation : impliquer l'équipe dans les décisions techniques)"}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0011", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 4.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 43.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.5}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5-year-old Ruby on Rails application supporting supply chain operations, maintained by a team of 45 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience. The system struggles with production reliability issues, while code metrics reveal moderate coupling/cohesion issues, suboptimal test coverage, and some concerning anti-patterns in critical paths.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with typical aging symptoms but no catastrophic structural flaws. The coupling/cohesion scores (5.3/4.2) suggest manageable entanglement, not a rewrite trigger. The 43.7% test coverage is concerning but improvable. Cyclomatic complexity (7.0) is borderline but not alarming. The bugfix ratio (0.5) in hot files and duplicate code/long method anti-patterns directly correlate with the reported uptime issues.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Execute targeted improvements: 1) Address reliability-critical anti-patterns first, 2) Boost test coverage around problematic modules, 3) Refactor hotspots incrementally. A full rewrite would introduce disproportionate risk given the team composition and codebase state.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in src/logistique/service.py and extract long methods in src/logistique/handler.py, with corresponding test coverage increases", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement monitoring for the refactored components to verify stability improvements", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct architectural review sessions with senior team members to identify 2-3 additional cohesion improvement targets", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}], "risk_assessment": "Moderate execution risk due to junior-heavy team composition - recommend pairing seniors with juniors during refactoring. The main operational risk is destabilizing already-fragile components during phase 1, mitigated by the phased approach and monitoring implementation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0012", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.6, "cohesion_score": 8.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 80.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.19}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme IoT industrielle mature (14+ ans) avec une base de code Node.js/Express/MongoDB bien structurée. L'équipe de 37 développeurs expérimentés maintient une bonne qualité de code, mais les incidents en production impactent la fiabilité critique pour ce secteur.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont globalement excellentes : faible couplage (2.6/10), haute cohésion (8.6/10), couverture de tests élevée (80%) et complexité maîtrisée. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.19) suggère une stabilité relative. La contrainte de fiabilité ne semble pas liée à des défauts structurels du code.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Cibler plutôt : 1) L'amélioration du monitoring runtime et des mécanismes de résilience (circuit breakers, retries) 2) L'analyse des causes racines des incidents via une revue post-mortem systématique 3) Le renforcement des pratiques de déploiement progressif (feature flags, canary releases).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des 5 derniers incidents majeurs pour identifier les patterns récurrents", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation ciblée de mécanismes de résilience sur les composants critiques identifiés", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de dashboards de supervision temps réel avec seuils d'alerte", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de surcharger l'équipe avec des changements infrastructurels non prioritaires. Une approche incrémentale permet de valider chaque amélioration sans perturber la production. La maturité de la codebase réduit les risques techniques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0014", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.32}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme IoT industrielle mature (13.9 ans) basée sur Ruby/Rails/MySQL, avec une équipe majoritairement junior. La principale préoccupation actuelle est la maîtrise des coûts cloud qui impacte la rentabilité du projet.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement acceptables (complexité modérée, couverture de tests moyenne) mais avec des points critiques localisés : deux dépendances circulaires sévères et une méthode trop longue dans le cœur métier. Le couplage modéré (3.7/10) et la cohésion moyenne (4.5/10) n'indiquent pas une dette technique ingérable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser des refactorings ciblés sur les anti-patterns identifiés et optimiser l'infrastructure cloud existante. Former les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Ruby pour améliorer la cohésion progressive.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des dépendances circulaires dans handler.py et service.py avec introduction de patterns Mediator/Event", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpage de la Long Method dans core.py via stratégie Extract Class + tests unitaires complémentaires", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit cloud ciblé (requêtes N+1, scaling vertical inadapté) avec un expert DevOps", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré sur le phase 1 (impact potentiel sur le workflow IoT). Nécessite des tests d'intégration renforcés. Les phases 2 et 3 sont à faible risque car bien isolées."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0014", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.32}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an industrial IoT system built on a Ruby on Rails and MySQL stack, maintained by a team of 38 developers, predominantly junior. The 13.9-year-old codebase is facing rising cloud costs, which the team has identified as the primary constraint. While the codebase has moderate coupling and cohesion, test coverage is limited at 54%, and specific files exhibit high circular dependencies and long methods.", "analysis": "The codebase's coupling and cohesion scores are moderate, indicating room for improvement but not critical dysfunction. Test coverage is below ideal but not dangerously low, and cyclomatic complexity is acceptable. The main technical risks are the high circular dependencies and long methods in critical files, which could complicate maintenance but do not currently justify a full migration. The team's junior-heavy composition suggests a preference for incremental improvements over a risky full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the codebase. Instead, focus on targeted improvements to address the identified anti-patterns, optimize cloud costs, and incrementally enhance test coverage. This approach aligns with the moderate technical debt and the team's experience level.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in src/iot/handler.py and src/iot/service.py, and extract long methods from src/iot/core.py into smaller, reusable functions.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit to identify inefficiencies and implement optimizations (e.g., caching, query tuning, scaling adjustments).", "duration_days_range": "5-7 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increment test coverage by adding unit and integration tests for critical components, prioritizing files with higher bugfix ratios.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks are the junior-heavy team's ability to execute complex refactoring and the potential for unforeseen issues during cloud cost optimization. Mitigate these risks by pairing juniors with seniors during refactoring and conducting thorough testing after each phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0015", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 79.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.06}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est une plateforme de paiements sécurisée basée sur une stack .NET/ASP.NET Core/SQL Server, développée depuis plus de 12 ans par une équipe de 32 développeurs. L'application doit répondre à des exigences strictes de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS).", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase globalement saine : faible couplage (2.7/10), forte cohésion (7.7/10), une couverture de tests élevée (79.8%) et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne très basse (2.2). Le ratio de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud est également très faible (0.06). Aucun anti-pattern significatif n’a été détecté.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer ni réécrire la codebase. Les métriques montrent qu'elle est bien structurée et stable. Concentrer les efforts sur des améliorations incrémentales pour maintenir la conformité réglementaire et optimiser les processus de développement.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit complet de la conformité réglementaire et identification des zones à améliorer", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Renforcer les tests automatisés dans les modules critiques pour la conformité", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Documentation des procédures de conformité pour faciliter les audits externes", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est lié à la conformité réglementaire, étant donné le secteur fintech. Cependant, la stabilité et la qualité de la codebase minimisent les risques techniques. Une attention particulière doit être portée sur la documentation et les processus pour éviter les écarts réglementaires."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0015", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 79.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.06}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature payment processing system built on a .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server stack, serving the fintech sector with stringent regulatory compliance requirements (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS). With a team of 32 developers (54% junior, 24% senior), the codebase has evolved over 12.4 years, maintaining high cohesion, low coupling, and robust test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy and well-maintained codebase. The coupling score of 2.7/10 suggests minimal dependencies between modules, while the cohesion score of 7.7/10 shows that components are well-organized and logically grouped. Test coverage at 79.8% is strong, and an average cyclomatic complexity of 2.2 indicates simple, easy-to-understand code. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.06 on the hottest file further confirms stability. No significant anti-patterns were detected, reinforcing the conclusion that the system is well-structured and reliable.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The codebase is in good health and does not justify the risks and costs of a full rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements, particularly in areas related to regulatory compliance, which is the dominant constraint.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a compliance audit to identify any gaps and prioritize necessary updates.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Enhance documentation and training materials to ensure junior developers understand compliance requirements.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement continuous monitoring and automated compliance checks in CI/CD pipelines.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk lies in non-compliance with evolving regulations, which could lead to legal or financial penalties. Incremental improvements focused on compliance will mitigate this risk while leveraging the existing codebase's strengths."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0016", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une application médicale temps réel critique, développée en Node.js/Express avec une base MongoDB. L'équipe de 37 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) maintient cette codebase depuis 2.2 ans, avec des défis identifiés autour de la latence et de certains anti-patterns récurrents.", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une base de code modérément saine (couplage acceptable, complexité cyclomatique raisonnable) mais avec des problèmes localisés de duplication et de conception (God Class, Long Parameter List). La couverture de tests est sous le seuil optimal de 70%. La contrainte temps réel semble être le principal défi, pas la stack technique actuelle.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser : 1) le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques, 2) l'amélioration des tests sur les modules sensibles au temps réel, 3) la formation des juniors sur les patterns de performance Node.js. Une migration apporterait plus de risques que de bénéfices dans ce contexte.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des fichiers avec Duplicate Code (high) et mise en place de benchmarks de latence", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpage progressif de la God Class et formation de l'équipe sur l'injection de dépendances", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers pratiques sur l'optimisation Node.js (streaming, caching) pour les juniors", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la dégradation des performances temps réel si les refactorings sont mal orchestrés. Recommander des déploiements canaris et un monitoring renforcé pendant les phases 1 et 2. La faible séniorité de l'équipe nécessite un accompagnement serré."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0016", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a medtech application built on Node.js/Express/MongoDB, focused on delivering real-time health data with low latency. With a team of 37 developers (mostly junior) and a 2.2-year-old codebase, the system handles critical real-time constraints but shows signs of technical debt in key areas.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate moderate coupling (5.9/10) and cohesion (4.5/10), with acceptable test coverage (58.9%) and cyclomatic complexity (4.8). However, the high frequency of duplicate code and anti-patterns (Long Parameter List, God Class) in core files suggests localized design flaws. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.23) on the hottest file points to instability in a critical component.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The codebase is stable overall but requires targeted refactoring to address anti-patterns and improve maintainability. Focus on incremental improvements to the problematic modules while preserving the core architecture.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in src/sante/core.py and src/sante/service.py, extracting shared logic into reusable modules.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the God Class in src/sante/processor.py into smaller, focused classes with single responsibilities.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address the Long Parameter List in src/sante/handler.py by introducing parameter objects or builder patterns.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Increase test coverage for the refactored modules to 70%+ to ensure stability.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are regression in real-time performance during refactoring and knowledge gaps due to the junior-heavy team. Mitigate with thorough testing, performance benchmarks, and pairing seniors with juniors during critical changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0017", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.26}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de streaming média vieille de près de 8 ans, construite avec Python/Flask et PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 45 développeurs rencontre des difficultés à recruter sur cette stack historique, alors que la codebase présente des signes de vieillissement technique avec plusieurs anti-patterns critiques concentrés dans le module média.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques montrent une situation mitigée : couplage et cohésion moyens (5/10), couverture de tests insuffisante (51%), complexité cyclomatique acceptable (5.7). Les anti-patterns sont localisés principalement dans le module média (dépendances circulaires, couplage élevé, duplication de code). Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.26) sur le fichier le plus problématique indique une maintenance réactive mais pas encore critique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé du module média avec : 1) isolation des composants fortement couplés 2) élimination des dépendances circulaires 3) augmentation de la couverture de tests. Former les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Python/Flask pour réduire la dépendance aux seniors.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer src/media/service.py (dépendances circulaires + long parameter list)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpler src/media/core.py et processor.py (high coupling) via interface abstraite", "duration_days_range": "6-10 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Éliminer la duplication dans src/media/handler.py et implémenter des tests d'intégration ciblés", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré : la concentration des problèmes dans un seul module permet une intervention localisée. Le principal risque est la perturbation des livraisons pendant le refactoring - prévoir un feature freeze partiel sur le module média pendant les phases 1 et 2."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0017", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.26}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature media streaming platform built on Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 45 developers with a balanced mix of experience levels. The primary challenge is talent scarcity for the current stack, though the codebase shows moderate technical health with some localized complexity and anti-patterns.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits balanced coupling and cohesion (both 5.0/10), suggesting a maintainable but improvable architecture. Test coverage at 50.9% is borderline—adequate for core logic but insufficient for high-risk modules. Cyclomatic complexity (5.7) is manageable, but the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.26) in hot files indicates instability in critical paths. Anti-patterns are concentrated in media-related modules, with circular dependencies and high coupling being the most severe.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics do not justify a full rewrite. Instead, prioritize incremental refactoring of high-risk modules (media/service.py, media/core.py) and improve test coverage. Address talent scarcity via targeted upskilling or strategic hires rather than stack change.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in src/media/service.py and decouple src/media/core.py", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Increase test coverage to 70% for media modules, focusing on high-churn files", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Standardize interfaces in src/media/handler.py to eliminate duplicate code", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk lies in the media service layer (circular dependencies + high coupling). Left unaddressed, this could lead to cascading failures during feature expansion. Talent scarcity is a strategic risk but mitigated by the stack's maturity and available upskilling paths."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0018", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.3, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme edtech vieillissante (9.5 ans) avec une base de code .NET/ASP.NET Core/SQL Server, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La vélocité de développement est identifiée comme le principal frein, malgré une complexité cyclomatique globalement maîtrisée.", "analysis": "La codebase montre des signes de dette technique localisée (couplage élevé dans 2 fichiers clés, God Class) mais des indicateurs globaux corrects (cohésion acceptable, complexité modérée). La faible couverture de tests (37%) et le ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers problématiques suggèrent des risques accrus lors de modifications.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Cibler d'abord les anti-patterns critiques via des refactorings incrémentaux, améliorer la couverture de tests autour des zones à risque, et renforcer les pratiques d'architecture pour l'équipe junior.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer progressivement src/edtech/core.py (God Class + High Coupling) avec des tests de non-régression", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Introduire des contrats d'interface stricts pour src/edtech/service.py (High Coupling) et documenter les flux", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers d'architecture avec les seniors pour définir des guidelines de couplage/modularité adaptés aux juniors", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : la combinaison d'une équipe junior et de zones critiques mal testées peut amplifier les régressions. Mitigation : pairing systématique senior/junior sur les refactorings sensibles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0018", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.3, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature edtech platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a predominantly junior development team. While the codebase shows reasonable structural cohesion, development velocity has become a critical pain point, with feature delivery slowing significantly. Static analysis reveals localized coupling issues and test coverage gaps, particularly around core service modules.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate technical debt but no systemic rot. The coupling score of 3.3/10 is acceptable for a 9.5-year-old system, and cohesion at 6.9/10 suggests reasonably well-organized domains. The 37% test coverage and cyclomatic complexity of 4.9 are concerning but not catastrophic. The real issue is concentrated in two high-coupling files that have become maintenance bottlenecks, evidenced by the 0.44 bugfix ratio in core.py.", "recommendation": "Do not rewrite. Execute targeted refactoring of the high-coupling modules while improving test coverage. The God Class in core.py should be decomposed first to unblock feature development. This incremental approach minimizes risk for the junior-heavy team while addressing the velocity constraint.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract bounded contexts from core.py God Class, starting with the most frequently modified components", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Introduce contract tests for service.py interfaces to enable safer refactoring", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Pair senior developers with juniors to improve test coverage (target +15%) in refactored modules", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is knowledge transfer during core.py decomposition - the 75% junior team may struggle with domain modeling. Mitigation: schedule paired programming sessions with seniors before extraction begins. Secondary risk is test coverage debt accumulating during refactoring - enforce coverage gates for each extracted component."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0019", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 3, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.6, "cohesion_score": 9.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 73.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.18}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Projet dans le secteur du gaming, développé avec une stack Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL depuis 3.7 ans. L'équipe est composée de 3 développeurs, dont une majorité de seniors, et la principale contrainte identifiée est la conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS).", "analysis": "La codebase présente une santé globale très bonne : faible couplage (2.6/10), haute cohésion (9.1/10), couverture de tests solide (73.9%), et complexité cyclomatique basse (2.7). Aucun anti-pattern significatif n'a été détecté, et le ratio de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud est faible (0.18), ce qui indique une maintenance efficace. La conformité réglementaire semble être le principal défi, mais elle ne justifie pas un rewrite complet.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer ni réécrire la codebase, car les métriques actuelles sont excellentes. Prioriser des améliorations incrémentales ciblées sur la conformité réglementaire et la documentation des processus.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique et réglementaire pour identifier les zones nécessitant une conformité renforcée.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation des ajustements nécessaires pour répondre aux exigences RGPD, PCI-DSS et HDS.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la documentation des processus et des tests pour garantir la pérennité de la conformité.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sur-investir dans des modifications non nécessaires ou de perturber une codebase déjà stable. Une attention particulière doit être portée à l'impact des changements réglementaires sur les performances et la maintenabilité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0020", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Dans le secteur du gaming, une équipe de 38 développeurs, principalement juniors, maintient une codebase vieille de près de 10 ans construite autour de Python, FastAPI et PostgreSQL. Bien qu'aucune contrainte critique n'ait été identifiée pour l'instant, des indicateurs pointent vers des zones d'améliorations spécifiques.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales montrent une codebase moyennement couplée et cohésive, avec une couverture de tests légèrement inférieure à la moyenne idéale. Cependant, la complexité cyclomatique reste raisonnable, indiquant un niveau de complexité gérable. Les anti-patterns détectés révèlent cependant des problèmes localisés mais sévères, notamment des dépendances circulaires et un couplage élevé dans plusieurs fichiers critiques.", "recommendation": "Éviter un rewrite complet ou une migration technologique. Prioriser des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour résoudre les anti-patterns identifiés, notamment dans les fichiers à couplage élevé et dépendances circulaires. Renforcer la couverture de tests autour de ces zones critiques.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyser et découpler les dépendances circulaires dans src/gaming/handler.py et src/gaming/service.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoriser les méthodes longues et réduire le couplage élevé dans src/gaming/handler.py et src/gaming/core.py.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests autour des fichiers critiques pour éviter les régressions futures.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque réside dans l'introduction de régressions lors des refactorisations. Une couverture de tests insuffisante pourrait amplifier ce problème. Il est donc crucial de consolider les tests avant et après les interventions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0020", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 9.4-year-old gaming platform built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 38 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience. While no critical constraints have been identified, the codebase exhibits moderate coupling and cohesion issues, along with several high-severity anti-patterns in core modules.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate technical debt but no systemic failure justifying a full rewrite. The coupling (5.2/10) and cohesion (5.5/10) scores are manageable, and test coverage (54.9%) is below ideal but not catastrophic. However, high coupling and circular dependencies in critical files (handler.py, service.py, core.py) and long methods in handler.py pose maintainability risks. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.47) on the hottest file suggests instability in a key component.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, execute targeted refactoring to address high-priority anti-patterns, improve test coverage, and stabilize the hottest file. This incremental approach minimizes risk while addressing the most pressing issues.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in handler.py and service.py, breaking them into smaller, focused modules with clear interfaces.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address high coupling in core.py by introducing abstraction layers or dependency inversion where appropriate.", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Split long methods in handler.py and increase unit test coverage for the modified components to at least 70%.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Monitor the bugfix-commit ratio for the hottest file post-refactoring and conduct a team knowledge-sharing session on the changes.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks are regression in functionality during refactoring (mitigated by tests) and temporary velocity slowdown as junior developers adapt to the new structure. The phased approach limits blast radius. Pairing juniors with seniors during implementation reduces knowledge silos."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0021", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 17, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 76.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.04}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une plateforme logistique développée en Python avec Django et MongoDB, vieille de plus de 10 ans. L'équipe de 17 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, fait face à une escalade des coûts cloud, impactant l'équilibre financier du projet. Le code montre cependant une bonne qualité globale, avec une couverture de tests élevée et une complexité cyclomatique faible.", "analysis": "La qualité du code est globalement solide, comme en témoignent les scores de cohésion et de couverture de tests. Le faible score de couplage indique une architecture modulaire et bien structurée. Le seul point faible détecté est un léger couplage élevé sur un fichier spécifique, qui semble être un point de friction mineur plutôt qu'un problème systémique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle technologie. Optimiser les coûts cloud en revoyant l'architecture d'hébergement et en adressant les inefficacités dans le fichier problématique. En parallèle, renforcer les compétences des développeurs juniors pour maintenir la qualité du code.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des ressources cloud pour identifier les goulets d'étranglement et les optimisations possibles", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation ciblée de src/logistique/core.py pour réduire le couplage et améliorer la modularité", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de sessions de formation pour les développeurs juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Django et MongoDB", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque réside dans la possibilité de mal estimer les gains d'optimisation cloud, ce qui pourrait nécessiter un ajustement de la stratégie après l'audit initial. La refactorisation du fichier problématique est faiblement risquée, mais nécessite un contrôle rigoureux pour éviter toute régression."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0021", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 17, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 76.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.04}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10.7-year-old supply chain logistics platform built with Python, Django, and MongoDB, maintained by a team of 17 developers (mostly junior). While the codebase shows strong cohesion and test coverage, the team's primary pain point is escalating cloud costs that need addressing.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a fundamentally healthy codebase: low coupling (1.1/10), high cohesion (8.2/10), solid test coverage (76.3%), and simple logic (avg. cyclomatic complexity 2.2). The only notable anti-pattern is minor coupling in `core.py`, which is easily addressable. Cloud cost issues are likely operational (e.g., inefficient queries, unoptimized infrastructure) rather than architectural.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead: 1) Optimize MongoDB queries/indexes and cloud resource allocation, 2) Refactor the coupled `core.py` module incrementally, and 3) Mentor junior developers on cost-aware coding practices.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit MongoDB query patterns and cloud usage metrics to identify cost drivers", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor src/logistique/core.py to reduce coupling, with paired senior/junior sessions", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement monitoring for cloud cost anomalies with actionable alerts", "duration_days_range": "4-7 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low risk. The incremental approach avoids disruption, and the team's high cohesion minimizes unintended side effects. The main risk is junior developers requiring closer guidance during the core.py refactor."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0022", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 25, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.9, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace mature avec une codebase Java/Spring Boot stable depuis 12 ans, maintenue par une équipe équilibrée. Les métriques techniques indiquent une architecture saine avec une excellente cohésion et une faible complexité.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs techniques très positifs : couplage faible (2.9/10), cohésion élevée (8.3/10), couverture de tests solide (82.4%) et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée (2.6). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers sensibles (0.12) confirment la stabilité de l'architecture actuelle.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. La stack actuelle est adaptée et bien maintenue. Privilégier des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour consolider les bonnes pratiques existantes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des 18% non couverts par les tests pour identifier les zones critiques à renforcer", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Formation des juniors sur les patterns architecturaux spécifiques au projet (modules ciblés)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de revues d'architecture trimestrielles pour maintenir la qualité", "duration_days_range": "2-3 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque serait de perturber inutilement une base code stable par des changements majeurs. Une migration apporterait peu de bénéfices tangibles tout en consommant des ressources importantes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0022", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 25, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.9, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This project involves a mature Java-based marketplace platform, built on Spring Boot and PostgreSQL, with a relatively healthy codebase maintained by a team of 25 developers, nearly half of whom are junior. The system exhibits low coupling, high cohesion, and strong test coverage, indicating a well-structured and maintainable architecture.", "analysis": "The codebase metrics suggest a stable and well-maintained system. Coupling is low (2.9/10), cohesion is high (8.3/10), and test coverage is robust at 82.4%. Cyclomatic complexity is low (2.6), and the bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is minimal (0.12), indicating no significant hotspots. No critical anti-patterns were detected.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the system. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to maintain the codebase's health and address any minor technical debt that may arise over time.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a codebase audit to identify and document minor areas for improvement, such as refining test cases or optimizing specific modules.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Develop a roadmap for incremental improvements, prioritizing modules with the highest technical debt or areas flagged during the audit.", "duration_days_range": "3-7 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement the highest-priority improvements, leveraging the existing team composition to mentor junior developers while maintaining system stability.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is complacency; maintaining a healthy codebase requires ongoing vigilance. Without periodic audits and incremental improvements, minor technical debt could accumulate over time. Additionally, the high proportion of junior developers necessitates effective mentoring to ensure code quality remains high."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0023", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 4, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 6.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 55.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de gaming vieille de 10 ans, construite en Ruby on Rails avec une base MySQL. L'équipe de 4 développeurs, majoritairement junior, rencontre des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production, avec des incidents trop fréquents impactant l'uptime.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales montrent une codebase relativement saine (couplage et cohésion dans la moyenne, complexité cyclomatique acceptable). La couverture de tests à 55% est perfectible mais pas catastrophique. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont localisés et de sévérité moyenne. Le ratio de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud (0.49) indique une certaine instabilité mais pas un 'hotspot' critique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Cibler d'abord les améliorations incrémentales sur les points faibles identifiés, tout en renforçant la couverture de tests pour améliorer la fiabilité. Une migration serait disproportionnée par rapport à l'état actuel du code.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring ciblé du couplage élevé dans core.py et des dépendances circulaires dans processor.py", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests (objectif +15% sur 2 mois) avec priorité sur les modules critiques pour la fiabilité", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de revues de code renforcées pour les juniors, avec focus sur les patterns de fiabilité", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer l'impact des compétences junior sur la qualité du code. Sans accompagnement ciblé, les améliorations techniques pourraient être compromises. Un mentorat senior sur les bonnes pratiques de fiabilité est recommandé en parallèle des phases techniques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0023", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 4, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 6.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 55.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10-year-old gaming platform built with Ruby on Rails and MySQL, maintained by a small team where over half the developers are junior. The system experiences frequent production incidents, with reliability being the primary concern. Static analysis reveals moderate coupling and cohesion issues, along with test coverage gaps and some problematic dependencies in core gaming logic files.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with typical aging symptoms but no catastrophic structural issues. The coupling score (5.4/10) and cohesion (6.2/10) suggest manageable architectural debt. While 55% test coverage is below ideal, it provides a foundation for incremental improvement. The high bugfix ratio (0.49) in critical files and circular dependencies point to specific pain points rather than systemic failure.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Implement targeted refactoring focused on reliability hotspots. The metrics don't justify a full rewrite, but the circular dependencies and high-churn files require immediate attention to address production stability issues.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isolate and refactor circular dependencies in processor.py, adding characterization tests", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decouple core.py modules through interface extraction, focusing on the most coupled subsystems", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement monitoring for the refactored components to validate stability improvements", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk lies in underestimating the testing effort required for stability-focused refactoring. The junior-heavy team may need additional senior oversight during dependency restructuring to avoid introducing new coupling patterns."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0024", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.5, "cohesion_score": 8.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.05}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme gaming en Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL vieille de 5 ans, maintenue par une équipe de 23 développeurs avec un bon équilibre juniors/seniors. La codebase montre une architecture solide mais l'équipe craint des limitations de scalabilité lors des pics de trafic imprévisibles.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont excellentes : faible couplage (2.5/10), haute cohésion (8.1/10), couverture de tests élevée (82.6%) et complexité maîtrisée. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.05) indiquent une base code mature et stable. La contrainte de scalabilité semble être le seul point d'attention.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Optimiser l'infrastructure et les patterns asynchrones pour la scalabilité. Renforcer le monitoring des goulots d'étranglement.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des performances sous charge (load testing) pour identifier les goulots précis", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring ciblé des endpoints critiques avec cache Redis et connexions asynchrones", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de métriques temps-réel sur la scalabilité (auto-scaling triggers)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sur-optimiser prématurément. Les métriques suggèrent qu'une approche incrémentale sera plus efficace qu'un changement radical. Former les juniors aux bonnes pratiques de scalabilité Python réduira les risques opérationnels."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0024", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.5, "cohesion_score": 8.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.05}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5.2-year-old gaming platform built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 23 developers (37% junior, 34% senior). The primary challenge is unpredictable traffic spikes, requiring scalable solutions, but the codebase itself is well-structured with high cohesion, low coupling, and solid test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase: low coupling (2.5/10), high cohesion (8.1/10), excellent test coverage (82.6%), and manageable cyclomatic complexity (3.5). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.05) on the hottest file suggests stable code. No significant anti-patterns were detected. The main constraint is scalability under unpredictable load, not code quality.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted scalability improvements for the existing stack. The codebase's health supports incremental enhancements rather than a risky full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a scalability audit to identify bottlenecks (API endpoints, database queries, caching layers).", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement horizontal scaling for FastAPI (e.g., async workers, load balancer tuning) and optimize PostgreSQL for read-heavy workloads.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Add monitoring for traffic spikes (e.g., Prometheus/Grafana) and auto-scaling rules for cloud infrastructure.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is underestimating traffic patterns during scaling improvements. Mitigate this by load-testing with realistic gaming traffic simulations before deployment. The existing code quality reduces technical debt risks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0026", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.3, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'un marketplace opérant depuis 5 ans et demi, reposant sur une stack Ruby/Rails/MySQL. L'équipe de 22 développeurs, composée majoritairement de juniors, fait face à une escalade des coûts cloud. La codebase présente des scores de couplage et de cohésion modérés, avec une couverture de tests insuffisante et plusieurs anti-patterns critiques concentrés dans le module de traitement des transactions.", "analysis": "La migration technologique n'est pas recommandée ici, car les métriques globales de la codebase ne justifient pas un rewrite complet. Bien que certains anti-patterns soient critiques (God Class, Circular Dependency), ils sont localisés dans un module spécifique. La couverture de tests doit être améliorée avant toute refonte majeure pour garantir la stabilité. L'escalade des coûts cloud est probablement liée à des inefficacités techniques ciblées plutôt qu'à une inadéquation fondamentale de la technologie actuelle.", "recommendation": "Prioriser des améliorations incrémentales ciblées sur les zones problématiques, en particulier le module de traitement des transactions. Renforcer la couverture de tests est essentiel pour permettre des refactoring sûrs. Une optimisation des ressources cloud devrait être menée en parallèle, en analysant les coûts par fonctionnalité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactorisation ciblée du module de traitement des transactions (processor.py) pour éliminer les anti-patterns critiques (God Class, Circular Dependency).", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests à 70% minimum, en priorisant les modules critiques.", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Analyse détaillée des coûts cloud pour identifier les inefficacités techniques et optimiser les ressources.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer l'importance des tests avant d'entamer des refactoring, ce qui pourrait introduire des régressions. Une attention particulière doit être portée aux dépendances circulaires pour éviter des blocages techniques. La gestion des coûts cloud doit être surveillée étroitement pour éviter des dépassements budgétaires pendant les phases d'optimisation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0026", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.3, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5.5-year-old marketplace platform built with Ruby on Rails and MySQL, maintained by a team of 22 developers (25% junior, 10% senior). The primary constraint is escalating cloud costs, while the codebase exhibits moderate coupling and cohesion, with test coverage at 45.2% and several high-severity anti-patterns concentrated in core marketplace components.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 4.3/10, cohesion 5.1/10) but localized hotspots requiring intervention. The processor.py God Class and high coupling in service.py/handler.py suggest over-centralized logic, while 45.2% test coverage is insufficient for safe large-scale refactoring. Cyclomatic complexity (5.0) is acceptable. The bugfix ratio (0.45) in the hottest file confirms instability in critical paths.", "recommendation": "Do not rewrite. Execute targeted refactoring of anti-patterns while improving test coverage to enable future optimizations for cloud costs. Address the God Class and circular dependencies first to reduce instability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract subcomponents from processor.py God Class (strategy/factory patterns), write characterization tests for critical paths", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break circular dependencies in processor.py, introduce interfaces for service.py/handler.py coupling", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Deduplicate code in processor.py, increase test coverage to 60%+ for modified components", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Moderate risk during phase 1 (God Class decomposition) due to high bugfix ratio. Mitigation: pair junior developers with seniors for test writing. Low risk in later phases as foundational stability improves."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0027", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.5, "cohesion_score": 1.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 26.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.58}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an industrial IoT system built on a 9.3-year-old Python/Flask/PostgreSQL stack, maintained by a team of 18 developers (mostly junior). The system struggles with reliability and uptime, with frequent production incidents. Static analysis reveals significant technical debt, particularly in coupling, cohesion, and test coverage, along with multiple high-severity anti-patterns in core modules.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits severe structural issues: low cohesion (1.1/10), high coupling (7.5/10), and dangerously low test coverage (26.3%). Multiple high-severity anti-patterns (God Classes, Circular Dependencies, and rampant duplication) are concentrated in critical paths (handler.py, service.py, core.py). The high bugfix-commit ratio (0.58) in hot files confirms these areas are destabilizing production. While the stack itself isn't obsolete, the architectural decay demands intervention.", "recommendation": "Do not rewrite. Execute a targeted refactoring campaign focusing on the highest-risk areas, paired with test coverage improvements. The God Classes and Circular Dependencies must be addressed first to reduce production instability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isolate and break down the God Class in src/iot/service.py, extracting domain-specific subservices. Add integration tests for critical flows.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Eliminate Circular Dependency in src/iot/processor.py by introducing interfaces or event-based communication. Refactor duplicate code in handler.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Enforce test coverage gates (minimum 70% for new code) and implement mutation testing for critical modules.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression during phase 1 due to tight coupling in service.py. Mitigation: deploy refactored versions behind feature flags. Junior-heavy team may struggle with architectural changes; recommend pairing seniors with juniors during critical refactors."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0028", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.9, "cohesion_score": 1.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 23.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.78}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an edtech platform built on a Node.js/Express/MongoDB stack, maintained by a team of 20 developers with a significant junior majority. The codebase, aged 3.8 years, shows signs of technical debt and challenges in attracting talent for the current tech stack, which has become a dominant constraint for the team.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits high coupling (8.9/10) and low cohesion (1.9/10), along with a concerning lack of test coverage (23.6%). Cyclomatic complexity is elevated at 11.8, indicating brittle logic. Anti-patterns are prevalent, including multiple high-severity instances of God Class, Circular Dependency, and Long Method, particularly in critical files like `service.py` and `core.py`. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is also high (0.78), suggesting frequent issues in that area.", "recommendation": "Given the high coupling, low cohesion, and prevalence of anti-patterns, a full rewrite or significant refactoring is justified. However, with talent scarcity as a key constraint, consider transitioning incrementally to a more modern stack (e.g., TypeScript/Next.js) rather than a full rewrite. Address immediate anti-patterns and improve test coverage as part of this transition.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor high-priority anti-patterns (God Class, Circular Dependency) in `service.py` and `core.py`, and improve test coverage for these modules.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Evaluate and select a modern stack for incremental adoption, focusing on TypeScript/Next.js for better talent availability and maintainability.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Begin incremental migration of critical modules to the new stack, starting with `processor.py` and `handler.py`.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk lies in the team's composition, with a high percentage of junior developers potentially struggling with complex refactoring tasks. Additionally, the transition to a new stack may temporarily slow development velocity. Mitigate these risks with targeted training and phased implementation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0029", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.2, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est une plateforme de gaming développée avec la stack .NET/ASP.NET Core/SQL Server depuis 2.2 ans. L'équipe de 6 développeurs, composée majoritairement de juniors (42%) et seniors (35%), n'a identifié aucune contrainte critique pour l'instant, mais il reste des opportunités d'amélioration sur la qualité du code.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales du projet montrent une base de code relativement saine avec un faible couplage (3.2/10) et une complexité cyclomatique modérée (6.1). Cependant, certains points de tension sont visibles : une couverture de tests insuffisante (47.3%), une cohésion moyenne (5.5/10) et plusieurs anti-patterns récurrents (God Class, duplicate code, et high coupling). Le fichier le plus problématique est src/gaming/processor.py avec une duplication élevée du code.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une autre technologie. La stack actuelle est adaptée et mature pour le projet. Concentrez-vous plutôt sur des améliorations incrémentales pour augmenter la couverture de tests, réduire les duplications de code et résoudre les problèmes de couplage élevé dans src/gaming/handler.py. Cela améliorera la maintenabilité sans introduire de risques inutiles liés à un changement technologique.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoriser le fichier src/gaming/processor.py pour éliminer les duplications de code et appliquer les principes SOLID.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests à 70% en écrivant des tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules critiques.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Réduire le couplage élevé dans src/gaming/handler.py en introduisant des interfaces et en utilisant l'inversion de dépendances.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Les risques principaux sont liés à la qualité du code actuel, notamment la duplication élevée et le couplage fort, qui pourraient augmenter les coûts de maintenance à long terme. Une refactorisation ciblée réduira ces risques sans perturber les fonctionnalités existantes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0029", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.2, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a gaming platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 6 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience levels. The codebase is moderately mature at 2.2 years old, showing some technical debt but no critical constraints identified by the team.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate technical debt but no systemic issues requiring a full rewrite. Coupling is low (3.2/10), cohesion is average (5.5/10), and test coverage is below ideal (47.3%). Cyclomatic complexity is slightly elevated (6.1), and anti-patterns like God Class and Duplicate Code are present but localized. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.25) suggests stable but improvable hotspots.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Focus on targeted refactoring to address anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. The codebase is healthy enough to sustain iterative improvements.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/gaming/service.py by splitting responsibilities into smaller, cohesive classes.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address duplicate code in src/gaming/processor.py by extracting common logic into shared methods or utilities.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Reduce coupling in src/gaming/handler.py by introducing interfaces or dependency injection where appropriate.", "duration_days_range": "4-6 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Increase test coverage by 10-15% through focused unit and integration tests, prioritizing high-risk areas.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are scope creep during refactoring and temporary instability in the processor.py module due to high duplication. Mitigate by pairing juniors with seniors during refactoring and maintaining a robust test suite."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0030", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 35.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme médicale en Node.js/NestJS, vieille de 3.6 ans, qui traite des données sensibles dans le domaine de la santé. L'équipe de 9 développeurs (mix juniors/seniors) rencontre des problèmes récurrents de scalabilité lors de pics de trafic imprévisibles, typiques du secteur medtech.", "analysis": "La codebase montre des signes de dette technique modérée avec un couplage et une cohésion sous-optimaux (5.0/10 et 4.5/10). La couverture de tests à 35% est insuffisante pour un domaine critique comme la santé. Plusieurs anti-patterns récurrents (Circular Dependency, God Class) dans le module 'sante' indiquent une mauvaise isolation des responsabilités. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.2) reste acceptable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration de la couverture de tests avant toute considération de scalabilité. La structure actuelle permet des améliorations incrémentales sans rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les Circular Dependencies dans src/sante/ (processor.py, handler.py, service.py)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découper la God Class dans src/sante/service.py en micro-services spécialisés", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration sur les modules refactorés (objectif +20% de couverture)", "duration_days_range": "6-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principaux risques : 1) Perturbation des flux critiques pendant le refactoring (domaine santé) 2) Résistance au changement chez les juniors (45% de l'équipe). Mitigations : validation systématique par tests manuels post-refactoring, pairing seniors/juniors pendant les phases critiques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0030", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 35.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a healthcare/medtech application built on Node.js/NestJS with a PostgreSQL backend, maintained by a team of 9 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience. The primary technical challenge is handling unpredictable traffic spikes, as scalability is the dominant constraint identified by the team. The codebase is 3.6 years old and exhibits moderate coupling and cohesion, with test coverage at 35.2% and some high-severity anti-patterns detected.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate technical debt but no critical red flags that would necessitate a full rewrite. The coupling (5.0/10) and cohesion (4.5/10) scores suggest room for improvement but are not catastrophic. Test coverage is below ideal (35.2%), and the presence of high-severity anti-patterns (circular dependencies and god classes) in critical files like `src/sante/service.py` demands attention. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.2) on the hottest file indicates some instability but not systemic failure.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, prioritize targeted refactoring of the identified anti-patterns and incremental improvements to test coverage and modularity. Addressing the circular dependencies and god classes will improve maintainability and scalability, which aligns with the team's primary constraint.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in `src/sante/processor.py`, `src/sante/handler.py`, and `src/sante/service.py` by introducing interfaces or dependency inversion.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the god class in `src/sante/service.py` into smaller, focused classes or modules.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 50% by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths, starting with the most frequently modified files.", "duration_days_range": "12-16 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are introducing regressions during refactoring due to insufficient test coverage and disrupting team productivity during the restructuring of critical files. Mitigate this by pairing senior and junior developers during refactoring and implementing a robust CI/CD pipeline to catch issues early."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0031", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 5.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme e-commerce mature (1.4 ans) développée en Python/Django avec MongoDB, maintenue par une équipe de 20 développeurs avec une majorité de profils intermédiaires. La conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) est la contrainte principale identifiée par l'équipe.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement équilibrées (couplage/cohésion autour de 5/10) mais avec des points critiques localisés : 2 anti-patterns 'high' récurrents (Circular Dependency et God Class) et une couverture de tests insuffisante (54.7%). Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.33) sur le fichier le plus chaud indique une instabilité modérée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration des tests, en particulier sur les modules liés à la conformité. La stack actuelle (Python/Django) reste adaptée aux besoins réglementaires.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les Circular Dependencies dans handler.py (stratégie d'interface ou Event Bus)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpler la God Class core.py via DDD (identification de bounded contexts)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration sur les workflows critiques RGPD/PCI-DSS", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : déstabilisation des fonctionnalités existantes lors du refactoring des God Classes. Mitigation : validation systématique par des tests contractuels avant/après refactoring. Risque secondaire : non-détection de dépendances implicites lors du découplage. Mitigation : utiliser des outils d'analyse d'impact (ex: CodeScene)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0031", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 5.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "This project is a 1.4-year-old e-commerce platform built with Python, Django, and MongoDB. With a team of 20 developers (28% junior, 14% senior), the platform must adhere to regulatory constraints such as GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS. The codebase, while moderately coupled and cohesive, exhibits several high-severity anti-patterns and a test coverage of 54.7%.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion, with room for improvement. Test coverage is decent but could be higher. Cyclomatic complexity is manageable, but the bugfix-commit ratio indicates some instability in critical files. High-severity anti-patterns like Circular Dependency, Long Parameter List, and God Class are present, suggesting targeted refactoring is needed.", "recommendation": "A full migration is not justified given the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the high-severity anti-patterns and improve test coverage. Incremental improvements will yield better ROI and reduce risks associated with large-scale changes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/e-commerce/handler.py to eliminate Circular Dependency and src/e-commerce/processor.py to reduce Long Parameter List.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the God Class in src/e-commerce/core.py into smaller, more manageable classes.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 70%, focusing on the most critical and unstable parts of the codebase.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include introducing new bugs during refactoring and potential delays due to underestimated complexity in breaking down the God Class. Proper planning and thorough testing will mitigate these risks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0032", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.6, "cohesion_score": 3.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 9.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.75}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 7.3-year-old marketplace platform built with Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 20 developers (15% junior, 27% senior). The system faces scalability challenges due to unpredictable traffic spikes, and the codebase exhibits significant structural issues, including high coupling, low cohesion, and minimal test coverage.", "analysis": "The codebase shows severe architectural problems: high coupling (8.6/10), low cohesion (3.7/10), and dangerously low test coverage (9.5%). Cyclomatic complexity (9.9) indicates overly complex logic, and the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.75) in critical files suggests instability. Anti-patterns like God Classes, circular dependencies, and duplicate code further degrade maintainability and scalability. The current state is unsustainable for handling unpredictable traffic spikes.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full rewrite—instead, prioritize incremental refactoring targeting the most critical anti-patterns and scalability bottlenecks. Focus on decoupling core modules, improving test coverage, and breaking down God Classes. A phased approach will mitigate risks while delivering measurable improvements.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/marketplace/processor.py and eliminate duplicate code in src/marketplace/handler.py. Introduce unit tests for these modules to raise coverage.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address circular dependencies in src/marketplace/core.py and src/marketplace/processor.py by introducing interfaces or dependency inversion. Add integration tests for these changes.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Reduce coupling in src/marketplace/handler.py and core.py by modularizing shared logic and enforcing boundaries via dependency injection. Extend test coverage to 30%+ for these areas.", "duration_days_range": "14-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are (1) destabilizing the system during refactoring due to low test coverage, and (2) insufficient team bandwidth given the complexity. Mitigations: (1) refactor in small, verified steps with paired testing, and (2) allocate senior developers to high-risk modules. Avoid parallel feature development during critical refactoring phases."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0033", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.1, "cohesion_score": 8.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 62.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.18}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet de santé digitale, basé sur une stack .NET/ASP.NET Core/SQL Server, est développé par une équipe de 43 développeurs majoritairement expérimentés. Après près de 3 ans de développement, la codebase montre une bonne santé globale sans contraintes critiques identifiée.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une architecture globalement saine : faible couplage (2.1/10), haute cohésion (8.7/10) et complexité cyclomatique modérée (4.0). La couverture de tests (62.8%) est acceptable mais pourrait être améliorée. L'anti-pattern détecté est marginal et localisé.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer ni réécrire. Concentrer les efforts sur des améliorations incrémentales, notamment en augmentant la couverture de tests et en résolvant l'anti-pattern existant.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit approfondi et documentation du module contenant la God Class", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring ciblé pour éliminer la God Class", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Elaboration de tests unitaires supplémentaires pour augmenter la couverture", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Les risques sont faibles car les métriques sont globalement bonnes. La migration ou un rewrite complet serait contre-productif et augmenterait drastiquement le risque sans bénéfice clair. Le refactoring ciblé est préférable pour maintenir la stabilité tout en améliorant la qualité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0033", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.1, "cohesion_score": 8.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 62.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.18}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a medical technology platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 43 developers (40% junior, 50% senior). The 2.8-year-old codebase shows strong cohesion and low coupling, with moderate test coverage and manageable complexity. No critical constraints have been identified by the team.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase: low coupling (2.1/10), high cohesion (8.7/10), and reasonable cyclomatic complexity (4.0). Test coverage (62.8%) is acceptable but could be improved. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.18) suggests stable hot files. The only notable anti-pattern is a minor 'God Class' issue.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The codebase is in good shape. Focus on incremental improvements: address the 'God Class', increase test coverage, and mentor junior developers to maintain quality.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the 'God Class' in src/sante/service.py to improve modularity, with paired senior/junior developers for knowledge transfer.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Boost test coverage by 10% through targeted unit test workshops, prioritizing high-impact modules.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a code health review with the team to identify further small-scale optimizations and document best practices.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low risk. The main risks are over-engineering the 'God Class' refactor or neglecting test maintenance. Mitigate by keeping changes small and measurable."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0034", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 4.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de gaming en ligne vieillissante (7 ans), construite avec Laravel/PHP/MySQL, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La codebase montre des signes de dette technique avec des problèmes de couplage et de cohésion, impactant la fiabilité en production.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une dette technique modérée : couplage élevé (3.4/10) et cohésion faible (4.6/10) indiquent une architecture fragile. La couverture de tests à 48% est insuffisante pour garantir la stabilité, surtout avec 24% des commits sur le fichier le plus chaud étant des correctifs. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Parameter List, Duplicate Code) sont localisés mais symptomatiques d'un manque de rigueur architecturale.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser un plan de refactoring ciblé : 1) Isoler et tester le composant critique (processor.py), 2) Introduire des patterns d'architecture (ex: CQRS) pour réduire le couplage, 3) Lancer une initiative '30 jours de tests' pour améliorer la couverture.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du processor.py (extraction de classes, réduction des paramètres) avec tests unitaires", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Atelier architecture avec les seniors pour définir des directives de cohésion/modularité", "duration_days_range": "2-3 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Campagne de tests ciblée sur les modules avec >0.15 ratio de correctifs", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : perturbation des releases pendant le refactoring. Mitigation : utiliser des feature flags pour isoler les changements. Le manque d'expérience de l'équipe (70% juniors) nécessitera un mentoring actif des seniors pendant les phases techniques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0034", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 4.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 7-year-old gaming platform built with PHP/Laravel/MySQL, maintained by a team of 33 developers (predominantly junior). The system struggles with frequent production incidents, with reliability being the primary concern. Static analysis reveals moderate coupling/cohesion issues and suboptimal test coverage, with some localized anti-patterns in critical processing components.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable structural issues (coupling 3.4/10, cohesion 4.6/10) and no systemic quality red flags. The 48% test coverage is below ideal but not catastrophic for a legacy system. Cyclomatic complexity (6.2) suggests moderately intricate logic but no widespread spaghetti code. The bugfix ratio (0.24) and anti-patterns point to specific hotspots (processor.py, handler.py) rather than widespread rot. The uptime issues likely stem from operational factors (junior-heavy team, insufficient monitoring) more than irredeemable technical debt.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate/rewrite. Implement targeted improvements: 1) Refactor the identified anti-patterns, 2) Boost test coverage around incident-prone areas, 3) Introduce reliability patterns (circuit breakers, better logging) in critical paths. The team composition suggests pairing seniors with juniors during these changes would yield long-term benefits.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Instrument and monitor production to identify precise uptime bottlenecks", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor Long Parameter List in processor.py with parameter objects", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Extract duplicate code in handler.py into shared utilities", "duration_days_range": "4-6"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Increase test coverage by 15% in modules with highest incident rates", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is insufficient knowledge transfer during refactoring due to junior-heavy team. Mitigate by: 1) Documenting all changes via pull request descriptions, 2) Running paired programming sessions, 3) Creating automated regression tests before modifying hotspots. Operational risks (downtime during changes) are low given the targeted scope."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0035", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 31, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.2, "cohesion_score": 2.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 16.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 8.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.58}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This project involves a healthcare/medtech application built on a 5.5-year-old PHP/Laravel/MySQL stack. The development team consists of 31 developers, predominantly junior-level. The codebase exhibits moderate technical debt, with limited test coverage and several high-severity anti-patterns.", "analysis": "The codebase shows a healthy coupling score (8.2/10), suggesting dependencies are well-managed, but cohesion is low (2.6/10), indicating poor modularity and organization. Test coverage is critically low at 16.4%, leaving significant portions of the code untested. Cyclomatic complexity is moderate (8.6), but several high-severity anti-patterns, including God Classes, circular dependencies, and duplicate code, are prevalent in core modules. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file (0.58) suggests frequent issues in critical areas.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full migration or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address anti-patterns, improve test coverage, and enhance cohesion. This approach minimizes disruption while gradually improving code quality.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor high-severity anti-patterns (God Classes, circular dependencies) in src/sante/core.py, src/sante/processor.py, and src/sante/service.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Increase test coverage by writing unit tests for critical modules, prioritizing src/sante/service.py and src/sante/processor.py.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Improve cohesion by modularizing tightly coupled code and reducing duplicate code in src/sante/processor.py.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include prolonged refactoring without immediate gains, potential introduction of new bugs during anti-pattern refactoring, and junior-heavy team struggling with complex codebase improvements. Mitigate these risks by pairing junior developers with seniors, implementing rigorous testing during refactoring, and prioritizing smaller, manageable tasks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0037", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme SaaS B2B mature (13+ ans) pour la gestion d'entreprise, développée en Python/FastAPI avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 27 développeurs (mix juniors/seniors) fait face à des coûts cloud croissants, tandis que l'analyse du code révèle des problèmes localisés de couplage et quelques anti-patterns critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase montre une dette technique modérée avec un couplage élevé (3.4/10) et une cohésion moyenne (5.4/10). Les anti-patterns sont concentrés sur 3 fichiers critiques (handler.py, processor.py, service.py) avec des dépendances circulaires et un couplage excessif. La couverture de tests (37.6%) est insuffisante pour sécuriser une refonte majeure.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé des modules problématiques et améliorer la couverture de tests. Optimiser l'infrastructure cloud via une analyse fine des coûts (ex: requêtes SQL inefficaces, scaling inadapté).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud (logs AWS/GCP, requêtes coûteuses, utilisation CPU/mémoire)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des anti-patterns critiques (circular dependencies dans processor.py, long parameter lists dans service.py) avec tests unitaires associés", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de métriques d'observabilité temps-réel sur les composants refactorés", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principaux risques : 1) Perturbation des fonctionnalités existantes lors du refactoring des modules fortement couplés 2) Résistance au changement de l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques d'architecture. Atténuations : Pair programming seniors/juniors et validation par tests d'intégration avant déploiement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0037", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 13.7-year-old SaaS B2B enterprise management platform built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL. The team of 27 developers (40% junior, 36% senior) is struggling with escalating cloud costs, while the codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion issues, along with several high-impact anti-patterns in critical files.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 3.4/10, cohesion 5.4/10) but significant hotspots in handler.py and processor.py (high coupling, circular dependency). Test coverage is suboptimal at 37.6%, and cyclomatic complexity (4.8) suggests moderately complex logic. The bugfix ratio (0.2) in the hottest file points to stable but potentially rigid code. The dominant cloud cost constraint suggests architectural inefficiencies rather than fundamental technology limitations.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Prioritize targeted refactoring of high-coupling modules and incremental cloud optimization. The metrics don't justify a full rewrite, but the anti-patterns in handler.py and processor.py require immediate attention to prevent further technical debt accumulation.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependency in processor.py and reduce coupling in handler.py using dependency injection", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement strategic unit test coverage improvements (focus on service.py and handler.py)", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Cloud cost audit: analyze query patterns in PostgreSQL and API response payloads", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk lies in the circular dependency (processor.py) which could cascade failures during scaling. The junior-heavy team may struggle with complex refactoring—recommend pairing seniors with juniors during phase 1. Cloud optimizations (phase 3) should wait until core stability is improved."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0038", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.7, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme IoT industrielle mature (4.5 ans) développée en Java/Spring Boot avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 21 développeurs (majoritairement seniors) rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack. La codebase présente des problèmes localisés de couplage et quelques anti-patterns critiques dans les modules centraux.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales sont correctes (complexité cyclomatique raisonnable, couverture de tests moyenne mais acceptable). Les problèmes se concentrent sur deux fichiers critiques (service.py et core.py) avec des circular dependencies et du couplage élevé. La pénurie de talents est le principal facteur de risque, pas la qualité intrinsèque du code.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser : 1) Refactoring ciblé des fichiers problématiques 2) Formation interne pour monter en compétences les juniors 3) Mise en place de guildes techniques pour réduire la dépendance aux recrutements externes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des circular dependencies dans core.py (extraction d'interfaces, inversion de dépendances)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpage des Long Methods/Parameter Lists dans service.py (application de CQRS si pertinent)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers de pair programming seniors/juniors sur les patterns architecturaux clés", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est l'érosion progressive des compétences internes. Une migration aggraverait ce problème en créant une dette technique supplémentaire. Le refactoring ciblé permet de gagner 12-18 mois pour mettre en place des solutions de long terme (formation, marque employeur)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0038", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.7, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an industrial IoT platform built with Java/Spring Boot and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 21 developers (mostly senior). The primary challenge is a talent shortage for the current stack, but the codebase shows moderate technical health with some localized complexity issues.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with reasonable structural quality (coupling 4.7/10, cohesion 6.1/10) and acceptable complexity (avg. cyclomatic 4.1). Test coverage is borderline (52.3%) but not critical. Anti-patterns are concentrated in two files (service.py and core.py), suggesting localized refactoring opportunities rather than systemic issues. The bugfix ratio (0.38) on the hottest file indicates moderate instability but not crisis-level churn.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The talent constraint doesn't justify the risk of a full rewrite given the codebase's overall health. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of the problematic files while investing in upskilling/junior mentoring to address the talent shortage. The high circular dependency in core.py warrants priority attention.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor core.py to break circular dependencies (extract interfaces, introduce event bus if needed)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address Long Method/Parameter List in service.py via decomposition and DTOs", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to 65% with focused unit tests for refactored modules", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Main risk is knowledge drain due to talent shortage - mitigated by pairing seniors/juniors during refactoring. Refactoring core.py first reduces the risk of destabilizing changes later. The phased approach limits blast radius of any regressions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0039", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise, développée en Python/Flask avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 29 développeurs (mix juniors/seniors) fait face à des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production, malgré une codebase relativement jeune (2.4 ans).", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une base de code avec des défauts localisés mais pas systémiques. Le couplage modéré (4.6/10) et la cohésion correcte (6.9/10) indiquent une architecture globalement saine. La couverture de tests (45.9%) est insuffisante pour garantir la fiabilité, ce qui explique probablement les incidents en prod. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont concentrés sur quelques fichiers critiques.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser des refactoring ciblés sur les points chauds identifiés, accompagnés d'une augmentation significative de la couverture de tests. Renforcer les pratiques de revue de code pour les juniors.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du fichier src/saas/handler.py (découplage + suppression du code dupliqué)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpage de la God Class dans src/saas/processor.py", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests à 70% minimum (ciblage des modules critiques)", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer l'impact des refactoring sur la stabilité en production. Il faut prévoir des séances de pairing seniors/juniors et des déploiements progressifs. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.7) reste acceptable mais nécessite une vigilance accrue lors des modifications."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0039", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a SaaS B2B enterprise management platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL. Currently facing frequent production incidents due to reliability and uptime issues, the codebase is 2.4 years old and maintained by a team of 29 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience levels.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling (4.6/10) and good cohesion (6.9/10), indicating that while dependencies between modules could be better managed, the overall modularity is acceptable. Test coverage at 45.9% is below optimal, and an average cyclomatic complexity of 6.7 suggests some overly complex methods. Anti-patterns include high coupling in 'handler.py', a God Class in 'processor.py', and Long Method and Duplicate Code issues in 'handler.py' and 'service.py'. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.45 on the hottest file indicates a significant focus on fixing defects rather than proactive development.", "recommendation": "Given the moderate coupling, fair cohesion, and identifiable anti-patterns, a full migration or rewrite is not justified. Instead, the focus should be on targeted incremental improvements to address reliability and uptime concerns. This entails refactoring specific problematic areas, improving test coverage, and applying best practices to simplify complex methods.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the high-coupling and duplicate code issues in src/saas/handler.py, breaking it into smaller, more focused modules with clear responsibilities.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the God Class anti-pattern in src/saas/processor.py by redistributing its responsibilities across multiple classes and applying SOLID principles.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the Long Method in src/saas/service.py into smaller, testable methods, and ensure new methods are covered by unit tests.", "duration_days_range": "6-10"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement a targeted effort to increase overall test coverage, prioritizing critical paths and modules with high defect rates.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks include resistance to refactoring due to time constraints, potential regressions during refactoring, and incomplete test coverage improvements. Mitigation involves thorough code reviews, frequent communication with the team, and incremental testing to ensure stability."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0040", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.5, "cohesion_score": 6.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.21}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "La plateforme de streaming MediaStream est une application critique vieille de 9 ans, développée en Python avec Django et PostgreSQL. Elle est maintenue par une équipe de 32 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, et rencontre des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité et d'uptime en production.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase avec un couplage modéré (5.5/10) et une cohésion relativement bonne (6.8/10). La couverture de tests est faible à 33.3%, ce qui explique probablement les incidents fréquents. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne est acceptable (4.7), mais des anti-patterns critiques comme des dépendances circulaires (high) et du code dupliqué (medium) sont présents dans des modules clés.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la codebase actuelle. Concentrez-vous sur des améliorations incrémentales pour renforcer la fiabilité : résoudre les anti-patterns critiques, augmenter la couverture de tests et implémenter des contrôles de qualité plus stricts. Ces actions sont prioritaires pour réduire les incidents en production.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé et résolution des dépendances circulaires dans src/media/processor.py", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation du code dupliqué dans src/media/service.py", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests pour atteindre au moins 60%", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implémentation de revues de code systématiques et formation des juniors sur les bonnes pratiques", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de ne pas améliorer suffisamment la fiabilité, ce qui pourrait entraîner une perte de confiance des utilisateurs. Une attention particulière doit être portée aux modules critiques identifiés, ainsi qu'à la formation de l'équipe pour éviter la réintroduction d'anti-patterns."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0040", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.5, "cohesion_score": 6.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.21}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 9-year-old media streaming platform built with Python/Django and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 32 developers (mostly junior). The primary operational challenge is production reliability, with frequent uptime incidents disrupting service. Static analysis reveals moderate technical debt, particularly around service layer complexity and dependency management.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 5.5/10, cohesion 6.8/10) but critically low test coverage (33.3%) that likely contributes to production instability. Cyclomatic complexity (4.7) is within acceptable bounds, but the high bugfix ratio (0.21) on critical files and circular dependencies suggest design flaws in core media processing logic. The anti-patterns are concentrated and addressable.", "recommendation": "DO NOT migrate. Execute targeted refactoring of the media service layer while improving test coverage. The metrics don't justify a full rewrite - the coupling/cohesion scores and complexity levels indicate salvageable architecture with focused interventions.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Break circular dependencies in src/media/processor.py through interface extraction, adding integration tests for affected flows", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in service.py into shared utilities, achieving 70%+ unit test coverage for new components", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Decompose long methods in core.py with peer review from senior developers, instrumenting performance metrics pre/post-refactor", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is destabilizing the media processing pipeline during refactoring. Mitigate by: 1) Implementing feature flags for changed components 2) Scheduling work during low-traffic periods 3) Pairing junior developers with seniors on complex changes. The phased approach limits blast radius."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0041", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.3, "cohesion_score": 9.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 88.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature medtech application built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 37 developers (mix of junior and senior). While the codebase shows excellent structural health with low coupling and high cohesion, the team's primary concern is escalating cloud costs that need optimization.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a very healthy codebase: low coupling (2.3/10), high cohesion (9.2/10), excellent test coverage (88.4%), and low cyclomatic complexity (2.3). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.15) suggests stable core components. No significant anti-patterns were detected. The cloud cost issue is likely operational/architectural rather than a code quality problem.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on cloud cost optimization through targeted architectural improvements. The codebase's health allows for safe, incremental changes without risking stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit to identify high-cost services and usage patterns. Instrument detailed monitoring for resource utilization.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Optimize database queries and implement caching for high-traffic endpoints (low risk given test coverage). Review auto-scaling configurations.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor monolithic services into leaner microservices only where justified by cost profiling, leveraging existing .NET Core capabilities.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low technical risk due to high code quality. Primary risks are organizational: ensuring cloud changes align with compliance requirements (medtech) and maintaining team focus during optimization. Phase 3 carries moderate risk if service boundaries are poorly defined—validate with metrics first."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0042", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.3, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 40.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de streaming média développée en Python/Flask avec une base PostgreSQL, vieille de 3.7 ans. L'équipe de 20 développeurs (majoritairement seniors) maintient une codebase présentant quelques problèmes de conception localisés, mais sans contrainte critique identifiée.", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une codebase modérément couplée (4.3/10) avec une cohésion acceptable (4.7/10). La couverture de tests à 40.9% est insuffisante mais typique pour ce type de projet. Les anti-patterns identifiés (God Classes et Long Method) sont concentrés dans le module média, suggérant des problèmes de conception localisés plutôt qu'une dette technique généralisée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé des modules problématiques et améliorer la couverture de tests. La stack actuelle reste adaptée et les métriques ne justifient pas un changement technologique.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du God Class high dans src/media/processor.py (découpage en services spécialisés)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Extraction de méthodes depuis la Long Method dans src/media/core.py", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration ciblée de la couverture de tests sur les modules refactorés", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré sur le refactoring des God Classes (possibilité de régressions). Bien planifier les étapes et s'assurer d'une bonne couverture de tests avant refactoring. Les gains attendus sont une meilleure maintenabilité et une réduction des coûts de modification future."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0042", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.3, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 40.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 20 developers (mostly senior). The codebase is moderately mature at 3.7 years old, with no critical constraints currently identified by the team. Static analysis reveals a codebase with moderate coupling and cohesion, decent but improvable test coverage, and some recurring anti-patterns in key media processing components.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase that is functioning adequately but has clear areas for improvement. The coupling and cohesion scores (4.3/10 and 4.7/10 respectively) suggest a somewhat fragmented but not dangerously entangled architecture. Test coverage at 40.9% is below ideal but not catastrophic. The presence of multiple God Classes and Long Methods in core media processing files points to design flaws that could hinder maintainability and scalability if left unaddressed. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.31) on the hottest file indicates moderate churn but not a crisis.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of the identified anti-patterns while improving test coverage incrementally. The codebase's overall health does not justify the risk of a full migration, but the God Classes and Long Methods should be addressed to prevent future technical debt accumulation.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the high-severity God Class in src/media/processor.py by decomposing into smaller, single-responsibility classes. Add missing unit tests during refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the Long Method in src/media/core.py using extract method patterns. Simultaneously improve test coverage for this component to 60%.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Tackle the medium-severity God Classes in service.py and handler.py through interface segregation and dependency injection where applicable.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is disrupting existing functionality during refactoring of core media processing components. Mitigation: implement robust test coverage before major refactoring and verify behavior with integration tests. Secondary risk: temporary velocity drop as team adapts to new patterns. Mitigation: pair junior developers with seniors during refactoring phases."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0043", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 8.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 64.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.0}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme SaaS B2B mature (3.6 ans) spécialisée dans la gestion d'entreprise, avec une forte exigence de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). L'équipe de 38 développeurs (mix équilibré juniors/seniors) maintient une codebase Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL de qualité technique avérée.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont globalement excellentes : faible couplage (2.7/10), haute cohésion (8.0/10), complexité maîtrisée (3.7) et absence d'anti-patterns critiques. La couverture de tests (64.4%) est correcte mais pourrait être améliorée pour les modules sensibles. L'absence de 'hot file' (ratio 0.0) indique une maintenance homogène.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. La qualité intrinsèque du code et l'adéquation technologique aux besoins métier (conformité) ne justifient pas un changement. Prioriser plutôt : 1) l'augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests sur les modules réglementaires, 2) la documentation des patterns d'architecture existants pour les juniors.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des zones à risque réglementaire pour prioriser les tests manquants", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Ateliers de documentation architecture/normes avec les seniors", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque serait de disperser l'équipe sur un projet de migration non nécessaire, au détriment des obligations de conformité. La stack actuelle a fait ses preuves sur la durée et son remplacement introduirait des risques opérationnels inutiles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0043", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 8.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 64.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.0}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a SaaS B2B enterprise management platform built on Node.js/NestJS with PostgreSQL, serving regulatory-sensitive sectors requiring GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS compliance. With a mature 3.6-year-old codebase maintained by a mixed team of 38 developers (42% senior), the system shows strong architectural health but requires ongoing compliance vigilance.", "analysis": "Metrics indicate a well-structured codebase: low coupling (2.7/10), high cohesion (8.0/10), and manageable complexity (avg. 3.7 cyclomatic). Test coverage at 64.4% is adequate but improvable. The absence of bugfix commits on the hottest file and no significant anti-patterns suggest stable core logic. Regulatory compliance remains the primary constraint, not technical debt.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics justify targeted improvements rather than a rewrite. Focus on enhancing test coverage and compliance safeguards while maintaining the current architecture's strengths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement compliance automation checks in CI/CD pipeline (static analysis for data handling patterns, audit trail generation)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Increase test coverage to 75%+ by adding integration tests for regulatory-critical paths (data anonymization, access controls)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct architectural review sessions with senior team to identify any latent compliance risks in module boundaries", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is regulatory non-compliance due to human error, not technical shortcomings. Secondary risk is test coverage gaps in newer compliance features. Mitigate through automated checks and focused test expansion."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0045", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une marketplace mature, développée depuis 7 ans en Node.js/NestJS avec PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 41 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack. La base de code montre des signes de couplage modéré et une couverture de tests perfectible, avec quelques points chauds identifiés.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques indiquent une dette modérée (couplage 4.8/10, cohésion 4.3/10) mais pas critique. La couverture de tests à 51% est insuffisante pour envisager une migration en sécurité. Les anti-patterns de couplage sont concentrés sur 2-3 fichiers clés du module marketplace, ce qui permet des interventions ciblées. La pénurie de talents est le principal facteur de risque opérationnel.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser : 1) des refactorings ciblés sur les fichiers à fort couplage, 2) l'amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests, 3) un programme de mentorat pour monter en compétences les juniors sur NestJS. Une migration serait prématurée et risquée avec la maturité actuelle de l'équipe.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des fichiers processor.py et handler.py pour réduire le couplage (stratégie d'interface/adapter)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Ateliers pratiques pour améliorer la couverture de tests (+20% cible sur les modules critiques)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un programme de pairing seniors/juniors sur NestJS avancé", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est organisationnel : la faible proportion de seniors (14%) rend toute migration technologique hasardeuse. Une approche incrémentale permet de consolider la base tout en développant les compétences internes. Les refactorings proposés réduiront également la dépendance à des développeurs NestJS experts."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0045", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 7-year-old marketplace platform built with Node.js/NestJS and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 41 developers (predominantly junior). The team reports significant hiring challenges due to talent scarcity for their current tech stack. Code analysis reveals moderate coupling/cohesion issues and borderline test coverage, with specific hotspots in marketplace processing logic.", "analysis": "While the codebase shows some architectural debt (coupling/cohesion scores below 5/10, cyclomatic complexity slightly elevated), the metrics don't indicate critical deterioration. The primary issue is organizational (talent scarcity) rather than technical. The high bugfix ratio in key files suggests targeted quality issues rather than systemic failure. A full stack migration would be disproportionate to the observed technical debt.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the stack. Instead: (1) Refactor the high-coupling marketplace components, (2) Improve test coverage to 70%+, (3) Upskill juniors on NestJS patterns to reduce reliance on scarce senior hires. Address talent scarcity through contractor partnerships if needed.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/marketplace/handler.py and processor.py to reduce coupling, using dependency injection and interface segregation", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement integration test suite for marketplace module to increase coverage to 65%", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct NestJS architecture workshops for junior developers (focusing on modular design and testing)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is attrition due to stack unpopularity - mitigated by incremental improvements rather than disruptive change. Refactoring carries moderate risk due to junior-heavy team; recommend pairing seniors with juniors during phase 1."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0046", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.5, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une application critique de gestion logistique développée en Java/Spring Boot avec une base PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe de 26 développeurs dont près d'un tiers sont juniors. La codebase, vieille de 1.5 ans, montre des signes de complexité modérée mais souffre particulièrement de difficultés de recrutement sur la stack technique actuelle.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques révèlent une dette modérée : couplage moyen (5.5/10), cohésion faible (4.3/10) et couverture de tests insuffisante (32.9%). Le point critique identifié est le fichier handler.py qui cumule du code dupliqué et un couplage élevé. La complexité cyclomatique (6.2) reste acceptable mais nécessite une surveillance. La contrainte majeure reste opérationnelle : la pénurie de talents Java pénalise la maintenance.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack complète. Prioriser : 1) Le refactoring ciblé du handler.py pour réduire son couplage, 2) L'amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests, 3) La mise en place de formations internes pour les juniors afin de compenser la pénurie de talents externes. Une migration partielle pourrait être envisagée uniquement sur les nouveaux modules si la stack cible résout clairement le problème de recrutement.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du handler.py : élimination du code dupliqué via extraction de composants, réduction du couplage par introduction d'interfaces", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de tests d'intégration sur les zones refactorées pour porter la couverture à 50% minimum", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers de pair programming seniors/juniors sur les patterns de découplage et les bonnes pratiques Spring", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque opérationnel est la surcharge de l'équipe pendant le refactoring du composant critique. Recommandation : planifier cette phase hors périodes de pic logistique. Le risque technique majeur est une régression dans handler.py - nécessite un rollback planifié et des snapshots de base de données."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0046", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.5, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 1.5-year-old supply chain logistics platform built with Java/Spring Boot and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 26 developers (29% junior, 65% senior). The primary constraint is a talent shortage for the current stack, which complicates hiring and onboarding. Code quality metrics indicate moderate coupling, low cohesion, and suboptimal test coverage, with some anti-patterns in critical components like the logistics handler module.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate technical debt (coupling 5.5/10, cohesion 4.3/10) but no systemic red flags. Test coverage is low (32.9%), and cyclomatic complexity (6.2) suggests some methods are overly intricate. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.44) in the hottest file indicates instability, likely due to duplicate code and high coupling in the handler module. However, these are localized issues, not architectural flaws.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The talent shortage, while significant, doesn't justify a full rewrite given the codebase's relative youth and manageable technical debt. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring of high-risk components, improving test coverage, and upskilling hires via mentorship (leveraging the senior-heavy team).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/logistique/handler.py to eliminate duplicate code and reduce coupling, with paired programming to mentor juniors.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement test coverage targets (e.g., +15% in handler.py) and static analysis gates in CI/CD to prevent regression.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Document key architectural patterns and conduct 2-3 workshops to accelerate junior onboarding.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is attrition due to stack dissatisfaction, mitigated by incremental improvements and knowledge sharing. Refactoring the handler module carries moderate risk—ensure thorough testing due to its high bugfix rate."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0047", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 39, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.4, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 40.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de paiements fintech critique, développée en PHP/Laravel avec une base MySQL, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La codebase vieillissante (2.7 ans) souffre de problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production, avec des incidents trop fréquents impactant l'uptime.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une base de code modérément saine (cohésion acceptable, complexité cyclomatique raisonnable) mais avec des points critiques : couplage élevé, couverture de tests insuffisante et plusieurs anti-patterns majeurs concentrés dans des fichiers clés. Le ratio de commits correctifs indique une instabilité localisée plutôt qu'un problème systémique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns identifiés et l'amélioration des tests. Renforcer les pratiques de revue de code pour l'équipe junior. Une migration serait trop risquée compte tenu de la criticité du domaine et de l'expérience limitée de l'équipe.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et éliminer les duplicate code dans service.py et core.py via extraction de composants réutilisables", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Décomposer la God Class dans service.py en micro-services logiques + implémenter des tests d'intégration ciblés", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Résoudre les circular dependencies dans handler.py par inversion de dépendance + ateliers d'architecture pour l'équipe", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré sur les phases 1 et 2 (impact possible sur les flux de paiement pendant le refactoring). Nécessite des revues de code renforcées et un plan de rollback précis. La phase 3 est moins critique mais requiert une bonne coordination d'équipe."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0047", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 39, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.4, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 40.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This fintech payment project, built on PHP/Laravel/MySQL, is maintained by a relatively junior team of 39 developers. Despite its young age of 2.7 years, the codebase suffers from reliability issues, including frequent production incidents, and exhibits significant technical debt with high coupling, low cohesion, and several critical anti-patterns.", "analysis": "The codebase metrics indicate a moderate level of coupling (4.4/10) and cohesion (6.5/10), with test coverage at 40.5%. The cyclomatic complexity is manageable at 5.7. However, the presence of high-severity anti-patterns like duplicate code, a God Class, and circular dependencies in critical files suggests structural issues that may be contributing to the reliability problems. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file (0.23) indicates ongoing maintenance challenges.", "recommendation": "A full migration or rewrite is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the reliability issues and reduce technical debt. Prioritize refactoring the identified anti-patterns and improving test coverage.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in src/fintech/service.py and src/fintech/core.py to reduce redundancy and improve maintainability.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the God Class in src/fintech/service.py into smaller, more cohesive classes to reduce complexity.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Resolve the circular dependency in src/fintech/handler.py to improve modularity and testability.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Increase test coverage across the codebase, particularly in the modified files, to ensure reliability and reduce production incidents.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include potential regressions during refactoring and delays due to the relatively junior team's experience level. Mitigate these risks through thorough code reviews, pair programming, and incremental testing. The team's focus on reliability aligns with the proposed improvements, reducing the likelihood of major disruptions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0049", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 16, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.2, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.11}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace mature avec une codebase Python/Django stable depuis près de 5 ans, maintenue par une équipe expérimentée. La principale problématique concerne la scalabilité lors des pics de trafic imprévisibles, malgré une architecture globalement saine.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase de très bonne qualité : couplage faible (1.2/10), cohésion élevée (8.5/10), couverture de tests correcte (72.9%) et complexité cyclomatique très basse (1.4). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et un faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.11) confirment cette stabilité. La stack actuelle n'est pas le facteur limitant pour la scalabilité.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Optimiser l'infrastructure existante pour la scalabilité : caching stratégique, mise en place de read replicas PostgreSQL, et éventuellement décomposition ciblée de quelques services en microservices si des hotspots sont identifiés. Former les juniors (27% de l'équipe) sur les bonnes pratiques de performance Django.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit de performance sous charge et identification des goulots d'étranglement", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place de caching (CDN, Redis pour les requêtes fréquentes)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Configuration de read replicas PostgreSQL et optimisation des requêtes critiques", "duration_days_range": "4-7 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les besoins en scaling horizontal. Une montée en charge progressive avec monitoring renforcé (New Relic/Datadog) est cruciale. Les juniors pourraient avoir besoin d'un mentoring spécifique sur les optimisations avancées."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0049", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 16, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.2, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.11}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 4.7-year-old marketplace platform built with Python, Django, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 16 developers (27% junior, 37% senior). The primary challenge is unpredictable traffic spikes, which strain the current architecture's scalability. Despite this, the codebase exhibits strong cohesion, low coupling, and reasonable test coverage, with no significant anti-patterns detected.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase: low coupling (1.2/10), high cohesion (8.5/10), solid test coverage (72.9%), and low cyclomatic complexity (1.4). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.11) on the hottest file suggests stable, well-maintained code. The scalability constraint appears to be an architectural bottleneck rather than a code quality issue.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, address scalability through targeted architectural improvements, such as optimizing database queries, introducing caching, or horizontally scaling critical services. The existing code quality justifies incremental enhancements over a risky full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a scalability audit to identify specific bottlenecks (e.g., database queries, API endpoints, background jobs).", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement caching (Redis or similar) for high-traffic read operations and optimize slow queries.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce load testing to validate improvements and monitor performance under simulated traffic spikes.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is underestimating the scalability requirements, leading to temporary outages during traffic peaks. However, incremental improvements are lower-risk than a full rewrite, which could introduce new bugs and delay scalability fixes. The team's seniority mix (37% senior) is adequate for these optimizations."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0050", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 5, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.2, "cohesion_score": 7.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.13}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme edtech mature (7+ ans) basée sur Python/Django avec MongoDB, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La codebase montre une bonne santé globale mais l'équipe rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont globalement excellentes : faible couplage (1.2), haute cohésion (7.9), couverture de tests correcte (72.9%) et complexité maîtrisée (2.2). Le seul point d'attention est une God Class isolée dans le module processor.py. La contrainte principale est humaine (recrutement), pas technique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser : 1) la formation interne des juniors, 2) le refactoring ciblé du fichier problématique, 3) l'embauche stratégique d'un senior Python pour encadrer l'équipe. Une migration aggraverait la pénurie de compétences sans justification technique.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring incrémental de src/edtech/processor.py (découpage en services)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place de pairing systématique junior/senior sur les features critiques", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers mensuels de formation interne sur les bonnes pratiques Python/Django", "duration_days_range": "1-2 jours (récurrent)"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la perte de connaissance si les seniors partent. Mitigation : documenter les patterns clés (ADR, tests) et cross-former les juniors. Une migration précipitée vers une stack plus 'tendance' aurait un risque élevé d'échec (équipe inexpérimentée + codebase saine)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0051", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.4, "cohesion_score": 2.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 7.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.66}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10.5-year-old fintech payment system built on Node.js/Express/MongoDB, maintained by a team of 42 developers (mostly junior). The primary constraint is slow feature delivery velocity, exacerbated by significant technical debt in core components.", "analysis": "The codebase shows severe structural issues: dangerously low cohesion (2.3/10) combined with high coupling (7.4/10) indicates spaghetti architecture. Critical files like handler.py and core.py exhibit multiple anti-patterns (God Class, Long Methods) with only 7.6% test coverage. The 0.66 bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file confirms these files are both problematic and frequently modified.", "recommendation": "Targeted refactoring of critical paths rather than full migration. The system's age and financial domain make a full rewrite prohibitively risky. Prioritize surgical improvements to the most problematic components affecting velocity.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract payment logic from handler.py into domain services, breaking the God Class", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement characterization tests for core.py to enable safe refactoring", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Modularize service.py by introducing DTOs to reduce parameter lists", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression during refactoring due to minimal test coverage. Recommend pairing senior developers with juniors during critical path changes. Monitor deployment metrics closely after each phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0052", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.5, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 87.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.13}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est un marketplace mature, développé en Python avec FastAPI et PostgreSQL depuis plus de 11 ans. L'équipe de développement est principalement composée de juniors, avec quelques seniors pour encadrer. La principale préoccupation actuelle est la montée en flèche des coûts cloud. Malgré cela, la codebase semble solide avec une faible complexité, une haute cohésion et une excellente couverture de tests.", "analysis": "Les métriques suggèrent une codebase globalement saine : faible couplage, haute cohésion, complexité cyclomatique modérée, et une très bonne couverture de tests. L'anti-pattern de dépendance circulaire est détecté mais marqué comme 'low', indiquant qu'il est probablement mineur et gérable. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne est également très raisonnable, ce qui est un bon indicateur de la maintenabilité du code. En résumé, la structure actuelle ne justifie pas une migration technologique ou un rewrite complet.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la technologie ou refondre complètement la codebase. Optimiser les coûts cloud en améliorant l'efficacité des ressources utilisées, en identifiant les services les plus coûteux et en ajustant leur configuration. En parallèle, résoudre l'anti-pattern de dépendance circulaire pour éviter de futures complications.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des coûts cloud pour identifier les services et les architectures les plus consommateurs.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Optimisation des configurations et des ressources cloud basée sur les résultats de l'audit.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring léger pour éliminer la dépendance circulaire dans src/marketplace/handler.py.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal est de ne pas correctement identifier les sources de coût dans le cloud, ce qui pourrait limiter l'efficacité des optimisations. Un autre risque mineur est lié au refactoring, qui pourrait introduire des régressions si mal exécuté, mais cela est mitigé par la forte couverture de tests existante."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0052", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.5, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 87.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.13}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature 11-year-old marketplace platform built with Python/FastAPI and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 43 developers (predominantly junior). While the codebase shows strong structural health with high cohesion and test coverage, the team's primary concern is escalating cloud costs that need optimization.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate an exceptionally healthy codebase: low coupling (2.5/10), high cohesion (8.3/10), excellent test coverage (87.7%), and simple logic flow (avg. cyclomatic complexity 2.7). The single minor anti-pattern (circular dependency in a handler) is trivial to address. Cloud cost issues are likely operational (e.g., inefficient queries, unoptimized scaling) rather than architectural.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The system's structural integrity doesn't justify such risk, especially with a junior-heavy team. Instead, focus on cloud cost optimization through targeted improvements: query profiling, caching strategies, and infrastructure tuning. Resolve the circular dependency during routine maintenance.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit: identify top 5 expensive queries/services via monitoring tools and PostgreSQL EXPLAIN ANALYZE.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement caching for high-frequency read endpoints (Redis) and optimize the flagged queries.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the circular dependency in handler.py during the next sprint (isolate shared logic into a new module).", "duration_days_range": "2-3 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low risk for the proposed optimizations. The main risk would be junior developers misinterpreting cloud metrics without senior oversight during Phase 1. Mitigation: pair a senior with juniors for the audit."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0053", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 4.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 43.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme SaaS B2B mature (9+ ans) spécialisée dans la gestion d'entreprise, avec une base de code .NET conséquente maintenue par une équipe importante (43 devs, majoritairement juniors). La principale problématique opérationnelle est l'explosion des coûts cloud, probablement liée à des inefficacités architecturales.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques révèlent une base de code modérément saine (complexité cyclomatique raisonnable, couverture de tests acceptable pour l'âge du projet) mais avec des points critiques localisés : un noyau central (core.py) trop couplé et deux services présentant des duplications importantes. Le ratio de correctifs sur le fichier chaud suggère une instabilité modérée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé du cœur technique pour réduire le couplage et les coûts cloud, accompagné d'une consolidation des services dupliqués. Une migration apporterait plus de risques que de bénéfices avec ces métriques.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler les responsabilités de core.py via une interface claire et extraire les sous-fonctions couplées", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Consolider les services dupliqués (service.py et processor.py) en une bibliothèque partagée avec tests de non-régression", "duration_days_range": "6-10 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Benchmark des requêtes SQL et optimisations ciblées pour réduire la facture cloud (sans modifier le schéma DB)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré sur la phase 1 (impact potentiel sur d'autres modules via core.py). Mitigé par la couverture de tests existante et la possibilité de déploiements progressifs. Les phases 2 et 3 sont à faible risque technique."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0053", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 4.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 43.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 9-year-old enterprise SaaS B2B platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 43 developers (nearly half junior). The primary operational challenge is escalating cloud costs, while code quality metrics reveal moderate coupling/cohesion issues and several high-impact anti-patterns in core modules.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling/cohesion scores ~4/10, cyclomatic complexity 4.1) but concentrated risks: a highly coupled God Class and duplicate code in critical paths. Test coverage (43.9%) is below the 60-70% ideal for safe refactoring. The bugfix ratio (0.31) in hot files suggests instability in core logic.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Prioritize targeted refactoring of high-risk components and incremental test coverage improvements. Cloud cost optimization should be addressed separately via infrastructure profiling (e.g., query optimization, caching) rather than stack migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isolate and refactor the God Class in src/saas/core.py using the Strategy Pattern to decouple responsibilities, with parallel test coverage expansion to 55%+ for affected modules.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Eliminate duplicate code in src/saas/service.py and processor.py by extracting shared functionality into a dedicated service layer, enforced by static analysis checks.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct cloud cost audit: profile SQL Server query patterns, review ASP.NET Core middleware for redundant computations, and implement application-level caching.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk lies in the God Class refactoring due to its coupling score. Mitigate by: (1) pairing senior/junior developers during changes, (2) creating rollback checkpoints, and (3) validating against historical bug patterns. Duplicate code cleanup carries lower risk but requires regression testing for edge cases."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0054", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.2, "cohesion_score": 3.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 29.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.74}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "A mature fintech payment processing system built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 24 developers (mostly senior). The system shows signs of architectural debt, particularly in core payment handling components, with concerning coupling and cohesion metrics. The team's primary pain point is escalating cloud infrastructure costs.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural issues concentrated in critical payment processing modules (handler.py, core.py). While the coupling score (6.2/10) isn't catastrophic, the very low cohesion (3.1/10) combined with multiple high-severity anti-patterns suggests deep architectural flaws in core business logic. The 29.8% test coverage is dangerously low for financial systems. The 0.74 bugfix ratio on hot files indicates firefighting in problematic areas.", "recommendation": "Avoid full rewrite. Execute targeted refactoring of payment processing core (handler.py, core.py) with parallel test coverage improvement. Cloud cost optimization should be addressed separately through infrastructure profiling.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract payment handler interfaces to break circular dependencies and reduce coupling", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor long methods in core.py using strategy pattern for payment processing steps", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement characterization tests for payment handler before further refactoring", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Consolidate duplicate processor code with template method pattern", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of payment processing failures during refactoring due to low test coverage. Recommend: 1) Business continuity testing for all payment paths 2) Feature flags for new implementations 3) Gradual rollout with transaction verification at each step."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0055", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme edtech mature (14 ans) avec une base de code Node.js/Express/MongoDB, maintenue par une équipe de 14 développeurs avec une forte proportion de juniors. Le système rencontre des problèmes de scalabilité lors de pics de trafic imprévisibles, et présente des duplications de code critiques dans des modules centraux.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales montrent une codebase avec des défauts modérés (couplage/cohésion autour de 4.5/10) mais pas catastrophiques. La faible couverture de tests (34%) et les duplications dans des fichiers critiques ('core.py', 'service.py') sont préoccupantes. La complexité cyclomatique est acceptable (4.2), et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.45) indique une stabilité relative malgré les fichiers chauds.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser : 1) élimination des duplications critiques, 2) amélioration ciblée de la couverture de tests sur les modules stratégiques pour la scalabilité, 3) refactoring incrémental des zones à fort couplage. Une migration complète serait disproportionnée par rapport à l'état actuel.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique ciblé sur les mécanismes de scalabilité et les fichiers avec duplicate code (core.py, service.py)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des duplications identifiées + ajout de tests unitaires pour porter la couverture à 50% minimum sur ces modules", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de monitoring avancé pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement lors des pics de charge", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : sous-estimer l'impact des duplications de code sur la maintenabilité à long terme. Secondaire : difficulté à améliorer la scalabilité sans une meilleure isolation des composants. Contre-mesures : pairing seniors/juniors pendant le refactoring, validation par tests de charge après chaque phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0055", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "This edtech platform, built on a Node.js/Express/MongoDB stack, has been operational for over 14 years and is maintained by a team of 14 developers with a mix of junior and senior expertise. The primary challenge is scaling to handle unpredictable traffic spikes, compounded by technical debt such as duplicate code and low test coverage.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling (4.5/10) and cohesion (4.7/10), suggesting room for improvement but no critical architectural flaws. Test coverage is low at 34.1%, and the cyclomatic complexity is manageable (4.2), indicating decent maintainability. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.45) on the most active file suggests some instability, but the primary issue is duplicate code in core.py and service.py.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address scalability issues and technical debt. Start by refactoring duplicate code and improving test coverage.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in src/edtech/core.py and src/edtech/service.py, ensuring proper modularization and reusability.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement additional unit and integration tests to increase overall test coverage to at least 70%.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize database queries and implement caching mechanisms to better handle traffic spikes.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include incomplete refactoring leading to introduction of new bugs, and underestimating the effort required for scalability improvements. Ensure thorough testing and phased rollouts to mitigate these risks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0057", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 8, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme edtech en Node.js/Express/MongoDB, développée depuis moins d'un an par une équipe majoritairement junior. Le principal enjeu est la mise en conformité avec plusieurs réglementations strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS), ce qui nécessite une base de code maintenable et sécurisée.", "analysis": "La codebase montre des signes de maturité moyenne pour son âge (couplage et cohésion dans la moyenne basse). Les anti-patterns identifiés sont localisés et typiques d'une croissance rapide avec une équipe junior. La couverture de tests est insuffisante pour garantir la stabilité lors de modifications réglementaires.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des composants critiques et l'amélioration des tests. La jeunesse de la codebase et l'absence de dette technique majeure ne justifient pas un rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring du service.py (découplage des dépendances) et ajout de tests d'intégration pour les composants RGPD/PCI-DSS", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpage de la God Class dans handler.py en sous-composants métier + validation par un senior sur les patterns de sécurité", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Atelier architecture avec les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques de modularité et revue de code renforcée sur les nouveaux commits", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la non-conformité réglementaire due à des modifications mal contrôlées. Une attention particulière doit être portée aux revues de code pour les composants traitant des données sensibles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0057", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 8, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an edtech platform built with Node.js/Express/MongoDB, focused on delivering educational content while needing strict compliance with regulations like GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS. The team consists of 8 developers, mostly junior, maintaining a relatively young codebase (0.9 years old) with moderate technical debt and uneven test coverage.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion, with test coverage below the ideal threshold (49.5%). Cyclomatic complexity is slightly elevated (6.4), indicating some overly complex logic. Anti-patterns like high coupling in critical files (service.py, core.py), a God Class (handler.py), and Long Method (processor.py) suggest architectural weaknesses but do not yet justify a full rewrite. The team's junior-heavy composition and regulatory constraints make large-scale migrations risky.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, prioritize incremental refactoring targeting the high-coupling files, God Class, and Long Method while improving test coverage. Given the regulatory focus, ensure compliance-related code is isolated and well-tested first.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/edtech/service.py and src/edtech/core.py to reduce coupling, extract interfaces, and improve modularity. Add missing unit tests for compliance-critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the God Class in src/edtech/handler.py into smaller, focused classes. Address the Long Method in src/edtech/processor.py by applying the Extract Method pattern.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 70%, prioritizing compliance-related modules. Conduct a security and compliance audit for GDPR/PCI-DSS/HDS alignment.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are (1) regulatory non-compliance if refactoring disrupts critical paths, and (2) slow progress due to the team's junior majority. Mitigations: pair junior developers with seniors during refactoring, and maintain a robust CI/CD pipeline with compliance checks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0058", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 76.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Application médicale critique développée en Ruby on Rails, avec une base de données MySQL, nécessitant une haute disponibilité. L'équipe, majoritairement junior, maintient une codebase mature de 1,4 ans où la fiabilité en production est la préoccupation principale.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une excellente cohésion (8.5/10) et une couverture de tests satisfaisante (76.1%). Le couplage modéré (2.7/10) et la complexité cyclomatique faible (2.9) indiquent une architecture globalement saine. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et un ratio de commits correctifs bas (0.12) sur les fichiers sensibles confirment cette stabilité.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Les métriques montrent une base code saine. Concentrer les efforts sur : 1) la réduction des incidents en production via un monitoring renforcé, 2) la montée en compétence des juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Rails, 3) l'augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des incidents passés pour identifier les patterns récurrents (ex: requêtes N+1, timeouts DB)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place de dashboards de monitoring temps-réel (erreurs 5XX, latence 95e percentile)", "duration_days_range": "10-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers techniques ciblés pour les juniors (séances pair-programming sur les parties critiques)", "duration_days_range": "8-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les besoins de formation de l'équipe junior. Une migration technologique aggraverait ce problème tout en apportant peu de bénéfices tangibles sur la fiabilité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0058", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 76.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 1.4-year-old Ruby on Rails application in the medtech sector, built to support critical healthcare operations. With a team of 18 developers (63% junior, 34% senior), the primary challenge is ensuring reliability and minimizing production incidents, despite generally healthy codebase metrics.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits low coupling (2.7/10) and high cohesion (8.5/10), indicating a well-structured and modular design. Test coverage is solid at 76.1%, and cyclomatic complexity is low (2.9), suggesting readable and maintainable code. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is 0.12, which is acceptable, and no significant anti-patterns were detected.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the codebase. Instead, focus on targeted improvements to enhance reliability and uptime. The metrics indicate a healthy codebase, and a migration would introduce unnecessary risk and cost.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a thorough review of production incidents to identify and address root causes, focusing on operational improvements rather than code changes.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Enhance monitoring and alerting systems to detect and respond to issues more quickly.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Provide targeted training for junior developers on reliability best practices and debugging techniques.", "duration_days_range": "5-7 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is operational disruptions due to production incidents. However, with a healthy codebase, focusing on operational improvements and team training should mitigate this risk effectively without the need for a costly migration."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0059", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.3, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme médicale critique en Java/Spring Boot, vieille de 10 ans, avec des pics de trafic imprévisibles dus à des urgences sanitaires. L'équipe, majoritairement junior, maintient une base de code avec des problèmes localisés de couplage et des dépendances circulaires dans le module de traitement des données médicales.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une santé globale acceptable (cohésion correcte, complexité modérée) mais avec des points critiques localisés. Le faible score de couplage et la couverture de tests insuffisante sont préoccupants pour la scalabilité. Le fichier processor.py concentre les anti-patterns majeurs (couplage élevé et dépendances circulaires), ce qui explique son ratio de correctifs élevé.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé du module problématique et améliorer la couverture de tests. Une migration serait trop risquée avec l'équipe actuelle et les métriques globales ne le justifient pas.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer src/sante/processor.py en introduisant des interfaces et en brisant les dépendances circulaires", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration pour le module refactoré (viser 70%+ de couverture)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Former les juniors sur les patterns de découplage via des ateliers pratiques sur le code refactoré", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : la complexité du refactoring dans un module critique pourrait introduire des régressions. Mitigation : déployer en canary avec monitoring renforcé des flux médicaux. Secondaire : résistance au changement des devs juniors - mitiger par des pairings forcés avec les seniors pendant le refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0059", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.3, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10-year-old medical technology platform built with Java, Spring Boot, and PostgreSQL, serving unpredictable traffic spikes. With a team predominantly composed of junior developers (63%), the system shows moderate technical debt, particularly in scalability-related components like the patient data processor module.", "analysis": "The codebase demonstrates reasonably good cohesion (6.9/10) and manageable coupling (3.3/10), though the processor module exhibits concerning circular dependencies and medium coupling. Test coverage is suboptimal at 32%, and the 0.35 bugfix ratio in critical files suggests instability in core logic. Cyclomatic complexity (5.6) indicates moderately complex methods but doesn't immediately flag maintainability crises.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics don't justify a full rewrite. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of the processor module while improving test coverage. The scalability constraint can be addressed through architectural patterns rather than stack migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Break circular dependencies in processor.py by introducing interfaces and dependency inversion, starting with the most frequently modified components", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement strategic unit test coverage increases (focusing on processor.py first) to reach 50% minimum coverage", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce rate limiting and horizontal scaling patterns for Spring Boot to address unpredictable traffic spikes", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk lies in destabilizing the processor module during refactoring due to its high bugfix frequency. Mitigation: pair senior developers with juniors during this work, and implement characterization tests before major changes. Secondary risk: scaling solutions might require infrastructure adjustments beyond code changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0060", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 25, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.4, "cohesion_score": 2.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 23.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.64}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10-year-old medical technology platform built with Python/Django/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 25 developers (40% junior, 51% senior). The primary constraint is a talent shortage for the current stack, compounded by significant technical debt evidenced by low cohesion, high coupling, and pervasive anti-patterns.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits severe structural issues: high coupling (6.4/10), very low cohesion (2.7/10), and inadequate test coverage (23.9%). Cyclomatic complexity (7.7) indicates convoluted logic, and the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.64) in critical files confirms instability. Multiple high-severity anti-patterns (God Classes, Circular Dependencies, Long Methods) are concentrated in core modules, suggesting deep architectural flaws.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full rewrite despite the talent constraint, as the metrics don't justify the risk. Instead, execute a phased refactoring targeting the worst anti-patterns first, paired with upskilling initiatives to mitigate the talent shortage. Modernize incrementally while maintaining system stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Break circular dependencies in src/sante/service.py and src/sante/processor.py by introducing interfaces or dependency inversion. Isolate God Class logic in src/sante/handler.py and src/sante/service.py into dedicated services.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor Long Methods and Parameter Lists in src/sante/core.py using strategy or builder patterns. Eliminate duplicate code in src/sante/processor.py through shared utilities.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement integration test harnesses for refactored modules to raise coverage above 50%, focusing on high-risk areas identified by bugfix commits.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Critical risks include: (1) Regression in medical logic during refactoring—mitigated by phased validation with domain experts. (2) Junior developers struggling with architectural changes—addressed by pairing seniors with juniors during refactoring sprints. (3) Talent attrition during transition—countered by transparent roadmap communication and upskilling incentives."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0062", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 6.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une plateforme marketplace construite sur une stack Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL vieille de 5.8 ans. L'équipe de 6 développeurs, majoritairement seniors, fait face à des problèmes de fiabilité avec des incidents en production trop fréquents, impactant l'uptime du système.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des scores de couplage et de cohésion moyens, avec une couverture de tests correcte mais perfectible à 58.6%. Plusieurs anti-patterns critiques ont été identifiés, notamment une God Class, des Long Methods, et des Circular Dependencies dans des composants clés. Ces problèmes contribuent probablement aux incidents fréquents en production.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle technologie, mais plutôt adresser les anti-patterns critiques et améliorer la couverture de tests pour accroître la fiabilité du système. Une refactorisation ciblée des composants problématiques est recommandée.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactorisation de la God Class dans `src/marketplace/service.py` et des Long Methods dans `src/marketplace/handler.py` pour réduire la complexité et améliorer la maintenabilité.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Résolution des Circular Dependencies dans `src/marketplace/processor.py` et réduction du Long Parameter List dans le même fichier.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests à un minimum de 70% pour les composants refactorisés et les points critiques.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque réside dans la possibilité d'introduire des régressions lors de la refactorisation des composants critiques. Une attention particulière doit être portée sur les tests automatisés pour minimiser ce risque."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0062", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 6.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5.8-year-old Java/Spring Boot marketplace platform with PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 6 developers (mostly senior). While the codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion, the team's primary pain point is reliability, with frequent production incidents impacting uptime. Static analysis reveals several localized anti-patterns, particularly in core business logic files, alongside suboptimal test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt—coupling and cohesion scores are within acceptable ranges, and cyclomatic complexity is low. The 58.6% test coverage is borderline but not catastrophic. The anti-patterns are concentrated in specific files (e.g., processor.py, handler.py) rather than systemic, suggesting targeted refactoring would yield the most impact. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.38) on the hottest file signals instability in one critical area, likely tied to the god class and circular dependency issues.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Prioritize incremental improvements: (1) Refactor the high-risk anti-patterns (circular dependency, god class) to stabilize the most incident-prone components, (2) Boost test coverage around these critical paths, and (3) Implement monitoring for the refactored modules to validate reliability gains. The team's senior-heavy composition is ideal for this surgical approach.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependency and god class in processor.py/service.py, with paired unit test improvements", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address long method and parameter list in handler.py/processor.py, adding integration tests", "duration_days_range": "6-10"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Enforce code reviews for new changes to the high-coupling core.py module", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is destabilizing the processor.py module during refactoring due to its high bugfix rate. Mitigation: phase the work, verify with contract tests, and deploy changes behind feature flags. Secondary risk: junior developers may struggle with complex refactorings; pair them with seniors during phase 1."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0063", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 4.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme marketplace mature, développée depuis plus de 14 ans en Python avec FastAPI et PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 44 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack technique, ce qui impacte la maintenance et l'évolution du système.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement correctes (couplage faible, complexité cyclomatique raisonnable) mais avec des zones d'attention claires : cohésion modérée, couverture de tests insuffisante et plusieurs anti-patterns localisés. Le principal problème est organisationnel (difficulté de recrutement) plutôt que technique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack complète. Prioriser : 1) des corrections ciblées des anti-patterns identifiés, 2) l'amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests, 3) un programme de mentoring pour monter en compétences les juniors sur la stack existante. Évaluer l'introduction marginale de technologies plus attractives pour les nouveaux recrutements (ex: endpoints en Go pour les nouveaux microservices).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques (God Class et Circular Dependency dans processor.py)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Lancement d'un programme de tests unitaires sur les modules les plus chauds (couverture cible +15%)", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Design et implémentation d'un nouveau microservice en stack alternative (Go/Node) pour une fonction non-critique, comme banc d'essai pour évaluer l'impact sur le recrutement", "duration_days_range": "25-30 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est organisationnel : une migration complète désorganiserait une équipe déjà en tension. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont localisés et ne justifient pas un rewrite. La stratégie progressive permet de tester l'hypothèse 'recrutement' sans compromettre la stabilité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0063", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 4.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 14-year-old marketplace platform built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL. With 44 developers (nearly half being junior), the team faces talent scarcity for the current stack, which may hinder future maintenance and feature development. The codebase shows moderate technical debt with some architectural anti-patterns and suboptimal test coverage.", "analysis": "The coupling score (3.1/10) is low, indicating a reasonably modular architecture, while cohesion (4.6/10) is middling, suggesting some logical grouping improvements. Test coverage (45.5%) is below ideal but not catastrophic. Cyclomatic complexity (6.7) is acceptable but could be refined. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.24) on critical files indicates stability concerns. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies, duplicate code, and a God Class in key modules require attention but do not yet justify a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, prioritize incremental refactoring targeting the worst anti-patterns and improving test coverage. Given the talent scarcity, upskilling junior developers on the current stack and introducing mentorship programs would be more cost-effective than a risky migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies and duplicate code in processor.py and handler.py, breaking down the God Class into smaller, focused components.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 60% by writing missing unit and integration tests, focusing on high-risk modules first.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct targeted training sessions for junior developers on Python/FastAPI best practices and legacy code maintenance, paired with senior mentorship.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is talent attrition due to stack unpopularity, mitigated by upskilling. Refactoring carries moderate technical risk, but the low coupling reduces blast radius. Delaying migration avoids disruption but requires disciplined debt management."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0064", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.6, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 57.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme gaming vieillissante (13+ ans) basée sur Python/Flask, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La difficulté à recruter des talents sur cette stack legacy est le principal frein identifié, malgré une base de code globalement saine avec des métriques techniques correctes.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques (couplage, cohésion, complexité) sont dans des fourchettes acceptables pour un projet de cette taille. La couverture de tests est perfectible mais pas catastrophique. Les anti-patterns détectés sont localisés et ne justifient pas un refactoring massif. Le vrai problème est humain : la stack Python/Flask legacy peine à attirer les nouveaux talents.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack complète. Prioriser : 1) Un refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques 2) Une modernisation incrémentale (mise à jour des dépendances Python, amélioration des tests) 3) La création de documentation/formation pour pallier la pénurie de compétences.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des 3 fichiers problématiques (God Class, Long Method, Long Parameter List)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise à jour des dépendances Python/Flask critiques + augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests sur les modules refactorés", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Création d'un onboarding technique et documentation architecture pour faciliter l'intégration des nouveaux devs", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est l'érosion progressive des compétences internes. Une migration full-stack serait prématurée (coût disproportionné par rapport aux gains). Le plan proposé réduit la dette technique tout en améliorant l'attractivité pour les recrutements."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0064", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.6, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 57.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 13-year-old gaming platform built with Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 7 developers (mostly junior). The primary challenge is talent scarcity for the current stack, compounded by moderate technical debt in key areas.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling (5.6/10) and slightly better cohesion (6.1/10), indicating a structure that isn't severely fragmented. Test coverage at 57.8% is below ideal but salvageable. Cyclomatic complexity (5.9) suggests manageable logic density. Anti-patterns are localized (God Class, Long Method, Long Parameter List) rather than systemic. The high bugfix ratio (0.44) in the hottest file signals a problematic area needing attention.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate. The metrics don't justify a full rewrite. Address talent scarcity through upskilling and targeted refactoring. Fix the identified anti-patterns first to reduce maintenance overhead.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in service.py by splitting into domain-specific services", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the Long Method in processor.py using strategy pattern", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address Long Parameter List in handler.py via parameter object pattern", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Increase test coverage by 15% through focused unit tests on critical paths", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}], "risk_assessment": "Main risk is junior team's ability to execute refactoring safely. Mitigate by pairing seniors with juniors during critical phases and introducing approval workflows for structural changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0065", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 28, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.8, "cohesion_score": 8.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 63.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.01}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme edtech mature (6.5 ans) avec une stack Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL bien structurée, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La principale préoccupation actuelle est la maîtrise des coûts cloud qui impactent la rentabilité du produit.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une santé technique remarquable : couplage très faible (1.8/10), cohésion élevée (8.7/10) et complexité cyclomatique idéale (2.0). La couverture de tests (63.8%) est acceptable mais perfectible. Le seul anti-pattern détecté (dépendance circulaire mineure) est trivial à corriger. Les métriques git indiquent une base de code stable (ratio de correctifs négligeable).", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Optimiser d'abord l'infrastructure cloud via : 1) Audit des coûts AWS/GCP, 2) Revue des requêtes SQL coûteuses, 3) Mise en cache stratégique. Améliorer ensuite la couverture de tests en ciblant les modules métiers critiques.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud (instance sizing, requêtes coûteuses, utilisation réelle vs provisionné)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correctif de la dépendance circulaire + augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests sur 3 modules métiers clés", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en œuvre des optimisations cloud identifiées (sans refactor du code applicatif)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque principal : sur-optimisation prématurée du cloud sans data suffisante. Recommander de déployer les correctifs par étapes mesurables. L'équipe junior devra être encadrée sur l'analyse des coûts cloud pour éviter des optimisations contre-productives."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0066", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.2, "cohesion_score": 1.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 8.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.63}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 13.7-year-old SaaS B2B enterprise management platform built with Python/Django and MongoDB, maintained by a team of 11 developers (mostly junior). The primary constraint is development velocity, with features taking too long to deliver due to technical debt and structural issues in the codebase.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal significant technical debt: low cohesion (1.4/10) and moderate coupling (6.2/10) indicate poorly structured code, while very low test coverage (8.8%) and high cyclomatic complexity (7.8) suggest fragile, hard-to-maintain logic. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.63) on critical files confirms instability. Anti-patterns like God Class, Circular Dependencies, and pervasive Long Methods/Duplicate Code further degrade maintainability. However, the issues are localized rather than systemic—no full rewrite is justified.", "recommendation": "Targeted refactoring focused on the highest-impact anti-patterns, paired with test coverage improvements to enable safer changes. Avoid a full migration; instead, incrementally modernize the worst offenders while delivering features.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract critical paths from God Class (core.py) into dedicated services, break Circular Dependency in handler.py, and add integration tests for these components", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor Long Methods and Parameter Lists in handler.py/service.py using the Strategy pattern, with unit test coverage to 60% for modified files", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Eliminate Duplicate Code in service.py/processor.py via shared utility modules, with regression testing", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is disrupting feature delivery during refactoring. Mitigate by: (1) Phase 1 changes behind feature flags, (2) pairing juniors with seniors for knowledge transfer, (3) validating each phase with smoke tests against key user journeys."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0067", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme gaming vieillissante (12+ ans) basée sur Python/Django/MongoDB, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La codebase souffre de problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production, avec des incidents trop fréquents malgré une complexité modérée.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase globalement saine (complexité cyclomatique raisonnable, couplage/cohésion dans la moyenne) mais avec des points critiques localisés : le fichier service.py cumule couplage élevé et duplication de code, et handler.py présente des dépendances circulaires. La faible couverture de tests (32%) explique en partie les problèmes de fiabilité.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration des tests. La stack actuelle reste adaptée au domaine gaming et la complexité globale ne justifie pas un rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les composants critiques de service.py (extraction d'interfaces, suppression de duplication)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Résoudre les dépendances circulaires dans handler.py via inversion de contrôle", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration ciblés sur les zones refactorées (objectif +20% de couverture)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : perturbation des fonctionnalités existantes pendant le refactoring. Mitigation : déploiements progressifs avec feature flags. Le ratio élevé de commits correctifs sur les fichiers chauds indique qu'une intervention améliorera significativement la stabilité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0067", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 12-year-old gaming platform built with Python/Django and MongoDB, maintained by a team of 22 developers (mostly junior). The system suffers from frequent production incidents, with reliability being the primary concern. Static analysis reveals significant coupling, duplicate code, and circular dependencies in core service modules, alongside low test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate structural issues concentrated in specific modules (service.py, core.py, handler.py) rather than systemic problems across the codebase. While coupling and cohesion scores are moderate (5.1/10 and 4.9/10 respectively), the high concentration of anti-patterns in critical files suggests localized architectural debt. The 32.2% test coverage is insufficient for reliable refactoring, and the 0.33 bugfix-commit ratio on hot files indicates instability in key components.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of high-risk modules while improving test coverage. The duplicate code and circular dependencies in service.py and core.py are the primary reliability risks and should be addressed incrementally.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isolate and write integration tests for src/gaming/service.py (focusing on high-coupling and duplicate code sections)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in src/gaming/handler.py using dependency inversion", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Extract duplicated logic from src/gaming/core.py into shared utilities with contract tests", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is destabilizing the production environment during refactoring due to low test coverage. Phase 1 must prioritize test scaffolding. Junior-heavy team composition may slow progress, suggesting paired programming with seniors for critical refactors."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0068", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.9, "cohesion_score": 9.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.18}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme IoT industrielle développée en .NET/ASP.NET Core, avec une base de données SQL Server. L'équipe de 18 développeurs maintient activement cette codebase vieille de 1.2 ans, avec une préoccupation majeure sur l'optimisation des coûts cloud.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une excellente santé technique : cohésion très élevée (9.6/10), couplage faible (2.9/10), et couverture de tests satisfaisante (72.5%). La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 3.9 indique un code simple à maintenir. Le seul anti-pattern détecté (duplication mineure) est localisé et facile à corriger. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.18) suggère une stabilité acceptable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique. La solution optimale consiste à : 1) Optimiser l'infrastructure cloud existante 2) Corriger la duplication mineure identifiée 3) Renforcer légèrement les tests sur les composants critiques. Une migration serait disproportionnée par rapport à l'état sain du code.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé de l'utilisation cloud (coûts/performances) et correction de la duplication dans handler.py", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation des recommandations d'optimisation cloud (sans changer de stack) et revue des tests sur les composants métiers", "duration_days_range": "10-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque technique faible : la codebase est stable et bien architecturée. Le principal risque opérationnel réside dans la maîtrise des coûts cloud, mais cela relève d'optimisations infrastructurelles plutôt que d'un problème de stack technique."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0068", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.9, "cohesion_score": 9.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.18}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an industrial IoT application built on a modern .NET/ASP.NET Core/SQL Server stack, developed by a team of 18 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience. The primary challenge facing the team is escalating cloud infrastructure costs, while maintaining a relatively new codebase with strong cohesion, low coupling, and solid test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase with low coupling (2.9/10), high cohesion (9.6/10), and good test coverage (72.5%). Cyclomatic complexity is low (3.9), suggesting maintainable code, and the bugfix-commit ratio (0.18) indicates stable hot files. Only a minor instance of duplicate code was detected, which does not pose significant risk. The primary concern is cloud cost management rather than technical debt or architectural flaws.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the codebase. Instead, focus on optimizing cloud resource usage and implementing cost control measures. Address the minor duplicate code issue to maintain code quality while prioritizing cloud cost reduction strategies.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyze cloud usage patterns and identify high-cost areas such as inefficient queries or over-provisioned resources.", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the identified duplicate code in src/iot/handler.py to eliminate redundancy and improve maintainability.", "duration_days_range": "2-3"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement cost-saving measures such as autoscaling, resource optimization, and serverless functions where applicable.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is misallocating resources toward premature optimization or migration efforts instead of addressing the core issue of cloud cost management. The low coupling and high cohesion reduce the likelihood of technical debt escalation, minimizing the risk of future refactoring complexity."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0069", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.4, "cohesion_score": 2.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 16.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 8.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.73}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Cette codebase mature de 7.7 ans, utilisée dans le secteur IoT industriel, repose sur une stack Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL et est maintenue par une équipe de 32 développeurs majoritairement juniors. Bien qu'aucune contrainte critique n'ait été identifiée, l'analyse révèle des problèmes de cohésion et de couplage, ainsi qu'une faible couverture de tests.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs mitigés : un score de couplage acceptable mais un score de cohésion très faible, indiquant une mauvaise modularisation. La couverture de tests est insuffisante pour garantir la stabilité. Plusieurs anti-patterns critiques sont détectés, notamment une God Class et des dépendances circulaires dans un fichier central, ainsi que des duplications de code dans plusieurs modules clés. La complexité cyclomatique reste modérée, mais le ratio élevé de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud suggère une instabilité persistante.", "recommendation": "Il n'est pas recommandé de procéder à une migration technologique ou à un rewrite complet. La priorité doit être donnée à des refontes incrémentales ciblées pour améliorer la modularité, réduire les anti-patterns et augmenter la couverture de tests. Une attention particulière doit être portée sur les fichiers les plus problématiques.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoriser la God Class dans src/iot/handler.py pour décomposer ses responsabilités et éliminer la dépendance circulaire.", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Éliminer les duplications de code dans src/iot/processor.py et src/iot/core.py en introduisant des composants réutilisables.", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Améliorer la couverture de tests en ajoutant des tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules critiques.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Les risques principaux incluent une possible déstabilisation de la codebase lors de la refactorisation, surtout avec une équipe majoritairement junior. Une supervision étroite des développeurs seniors et une stratégie de testing robuste sont essentielles pour minimiser ces risques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0070", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme logistique critique utilisée pour l'optimisation de la supply chain en temps réel, développée depuis 8.5 ans en Python/Django avec PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 38 développeurs (dont 34% de juniors) maintient une codebase mature avec une forte exigence sur la latence des traitements.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont globalement excellentes : faible couplage (1.1/10), haute cohésion (8.5/10), couverture de tests élevée (82.9%) et complexité cyclomatique très basse (1.8). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.2) indiquent une base de code saine et maintenable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. La problématique de latence temps réel devrait être traitée par des optimisations ciblées (cache, asynchronicité) plutôt qu'un changement technologique risqué. Investir dans la formation des juniors sur l'architecture existante.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des goulots d'étranglement de performance avec profiling détaillé", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place de solutions d'optimisation incrémentales (ex: caching stratégique, pré-calculs)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers de transfert de compétences seniors-juniors sur les patterns critiques", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque serait de sur-optimiser prématurément des composants non critiques. Une approche data-driven (basée sur les metrics de profiling) est essentielle pour prioriser les efforts. La proportion élevée de juniors nécessite un accompagnement renforcé pendant les modifications."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0071", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 31.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.3}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme SaaS B2B pour la gestion d'entreprise, développée en Python/Flask avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 24 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) maintient cette codebase vieille de 3.4 ans, avec une contrainte forte sur les performances temps réel. L'analyse révèle des problèmes récurrents de duplication de code et de couplage élevé dans certains modules critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement moyennes (couplage 4.5/10, cohésion 5.5/10) mais avec des points critiques : duplication de code importante dans les fichiers processor.py et service.py, et couplage élevé dans handler.py. La couverture de tests à 31.4% est insuffisante pour une migration en toute sécurité. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.4) reste raisonnable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns identifiés et l'amélioration de la couverture de tests avant toute considération de migration. La latence temps réel critique pourrait être adressée par des optimisations incrémentales plutôt qu'un changement de stack.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des duplications de code (high priority) dans processor.py et service.py", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Réduction du couplage dans handler.py via introduction de interfaces/clarification des responsabilités", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests sur les modules refactorés (objectif +20%)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la dégradation des performances temps réel pendant les refactorings. Recommandation : implémenter des benchmarks avant/après chaque modification et prévoir des rollbacks rapides. La proportion élevée de juniors dans l'équipe nécessitera un accompagnement renforcé pendant ces phases."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0071", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 31.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.3}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a SaaS B2B platform focused on enterprise management, built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL. With a codebase aged 3.4 years, the platform is maintained by a team of 24 developers, of which 56% are junior and 14% senior. The dominant constraint identified by the team is the critical need for low latency in real-time operations.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a relatively low coupling score (4.5/10) and moderate cohesion score (5.5/10), suggesting a manageable code structure. However, the test coverage is concerningly low at 31.4%, and there is a notable presence of duplicate code and high coupling in several critical files (e.g., src/saas/processor.py, src/saas/handler.py). The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is 0.3, which points to potentially unstable code.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the duplicate code, enhance test coverage, and reduce coupling in specific modules. This approach will improve code quality and stability without the risks associated with a full migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in src/saas/processor.py and src/saas/handler.py.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage, prioritizing areas with high bugfix-commit ratios.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize high coupling in src/saas/handler.py by modularizing tightly coupled code.", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include the potential introduction of new bugs during refactoring and insufficient test coverage leading to undetected issues. Mitigation strategies include rigorous testing after each refactoring phase and involving senior developers in code reviews."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0072", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 10, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 30.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme gaming vieillissante (12+ ans) basée sur Python/Django, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La difficulté à recruter des talents sur cette stack et certains problèmes structurels dans le code compliquent l'évolution du produit.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement correctes (complexité modérée, couplage/cohésion dans la moyenne) mais avec des points critiques localisés : dépendances circulaires dans des composants clés, faible couverture de tests et fichier 'chaud' nécessitant des correctifs fréquents. La contrainte principale est humaine (recrutement) plutôt que technique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser : 1) le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques, 2) l'amélioration progressive des tests, 3) la mise en place de formations internes pour monter en compétence l'équipe existante sur Django/Python.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les dépendances circulaires dans core.py et service.py", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découper la Long Method dans processor.py et augmenter la couverture de tests sur ces composants", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mettre en place un programme de pairing seniors/juniors + documentation des patterns critiques", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la perte de vitesse sur les nouvelles features pendant le refactoring. Une approche incrémentale (module par module) et la priorisation des zones à fort impact métier permettent de le mitiger."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0072", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 10, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 30.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 12-year-old gaming platform built with Python, Django, and PostgreSQL. The team of 10 developers (mostly junior) struggles with talent scarcity for the current stack, despite the codebase showing moderate coupling and cohesion. Key pain points include circular dependencies in core modules and long methods in critical processing logic.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 5.2/10, cohesion 6.1/10) but critically low test coverage (30.8%) and localized complexity hotspots. The dominant constraint is talent availability, not systemic code issues. Anti-patterns are confined to specific files, suggesting targeted fixes would yield better ROI than a full migration.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Address talent scarcity through upskilling (Python remains widely used in gaming) and targeted refactoring of high-risk files. Improve test coverage incrementally to stabilize the codebase.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Break circular dependencies in core.py and service.py using dependency inversion", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor long methods in processor.py with strategic pattern extraction", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement test coverage gates for new code (+10% coverage over 3 months)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days (setup)"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk is talent attrition due to stack dissatisfaction. Mitigate by introducing modern Python features (async, type hints) to increase engagement. Refactoring risks are low due to contained anti-patterns."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0073", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.4, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 78.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.17}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une marketplace mature (6.5 ans) avec une stack Python/Flask/PostgreSQL bien établie. L'équipe de 23 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) maintient une codebase globalement saine, mais doit prioriser les adaptations pour répondre aux exigences réglementaires croissantes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS).", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont excellentes : faible couplage (1.4/10), haute cohésion (8.5/10), couverture de tests solide (78.3%) et complexité cyclomatique très raisonnable (2.4). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.17) confirment une base de code stable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Une migration serait risquée et injustifiée techniquement. Prioriser plutôt : 1) des ateliers de formation sur la conformité réglementaire pour les juniors, 2) des améliorations incrémentales des tests pour les modules critiques liés aux données sensibles.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des flux de données sensibles et cartographie des exigences réglementaires par module", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Formations ciblées RGPD/PCI-DSS/HDS pour l'équipe, avec ateliers pratiques sur la codebase existante", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Renforcement des tests d'intégration sur les composants de gestion des données personnelles (cible : 85%+ de couverture)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est réglementaire (non-conformité), pas technique. Une migration introduirait des risques inutiles : perte de savoir-faire avec la stack actuelle, délais imprévisibles, et potentielle régression sur la stabilité actuelle. L'approche incrémentale est bien plus sûre."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0073", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.4, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 78.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.17}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 6.5-year-old marketplace platform built with Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 23 developers (mostly junior). The primary constraint is ensuring compliance with strict regulations (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS). The codebase shows healthy metrics with low coupling, high cohesion, and solid test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a well-structured codebase: coupling is very low (1.4/10), cohesion is excellent (8.5/10), test coverage is robust (78.3%), and cyclomatic complexity is minimal (2.4). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.17) suggests stable core files. No significant anti-patterns were detected. The team's junior-heavy composition and regulatory focus are more pressing concerns than technical debt.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The codebase is in good health. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to support compliance needs and upskill junior developers. A rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk without clear technical justification.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a compliance audit with legal/security experts to identify code areas needing updates for GDPR/PCI-DSS/HDS", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement lightweight documentation improvements (e.g., compliance-critical code paths) and pair senior/junior developers for knowledge transfer", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Add targeted integration tests for compliance-sensitive features (payment processing, data anonymization)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are regulatory non-compliance due to misinterpretation of requirements (mitigated by expert audits) and slower velocity from junior developers (mitigated by pairing). Technical debt is not a significant concern based on metrics."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0074", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise vieille de 6 ans, construite avec Python/Django et MongoDB. L'équipe de 45 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) doit maintenir cette solution tout en répondant à des exigences strictes de conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS).", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement équilibrées (couplage/cohésion moyens) mais avec des points critiques localisés : deux méthodes trop longues, une dépendance circulaire et du code dupliqué dans des composants clés. La couverture de tests sous les 50% est préoccupante pour un produit soumis à de fortes contraintes réglementaires.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration de la couverture de tests, particulièrement sur les modules liés à la conformité. Former les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Django et les exigences réglementaires.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des Long Methods et résolution de la Circular Dependency dans src/saas/service.py", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Élimination du code dupliqué dans src/saas/processor.py et ajout de tests unitaires ciblés", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers de formation sur les patterns Django avancés et les implications techniques du RGPD/PCI-DSS", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la non-conformité réglementaire due à des erreurs dans les composants critiques. La présence majoritaire de juniors amplifie ce risque. Une montée en compétences progressive est préférable à un changement de stack qui déstabiliserait l'équipe."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0074", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 6-year-old SaaS B2B enterprise management platform built with Python/Django and MongoDB, serving regulatory-sensitive sectors (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS). With a team predominantly composed of junior developers (71%), the system faces challenges in maintaining compliance while managing technical debt, evidenced by moderate coupling/cohesion scores and localized anti-patterns.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate technical debt (coupling 5.9/10, cohesion 5.4/10) but no systemic failure. Test coverage (46%) is below ideal but manageable for incremental improvement. Cyclomatic complexity (5.6) is acceptable. Anti-patterns are concentrated (duplicate code, long methods, circular dependency) but isolated to specific files, suggesting targeted refactoring is feasible. The regulatory constraints prioritize stability over disruptive changes.", "recommendation": "DO NOT migrate or rewrite. Prioritize incremental refactoring of high-risk anti-patterns and improve test coverage in compliance-critical paths. The team composition (mostly junior) favors small, supervised improvements over large-scale migrations.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependency in src/saas/service.py (high risk for compliance changes)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down long methods in src/saas/handler.py (high complexity hinders regulatory audits)", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage for compliance-related modules to ≥65% (target processor.py first)", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk lies in the circular dependency (service.py), which could complicate mandatory compliance updates. Junior-heavy team may require senior oversight during refactoring to avoid regression. Long methods in handler.py pose audit-trail risks for regulatory requirements."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0075", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.43}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de gestion logistique pour la supply chain, développée depuis près de 9 ans en .NET/ASP.NET Core. L'équipe, majoritairement junior, rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack technique, malgré une codebase globalement stable.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement correctes (complexité cyclomatique raisonnable, couplage modéré) mais avec quelques points critiques localisés (dépendances circulaires, couplage élevé sur certains modules). La couverture de tests est insuffisante pour envisager une migration en toute sécurité. La pénurie de talents est le principal facteur de risque opérationnel.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack principale. Prioriser : 1) des formations ciblées pour les juniors sur les patterns critiques identifiés, 2) un refactoring incrémental des modules problématiques, 3) l'amélioration de la couverture de tests avant toute évolution majeure.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des dépendances circulaires et réduction du couplage dans les modules critiques (core.py et handler.py)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place de tests d'intégration ciblés sur les zones refactorées", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Programme de mentorat technique pour monter en compétence les juniors sur les patterns .NET avancés", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la perte de vitesse sur le marché si les problèmes de recrutement persistent. Une migration prématurée entraînerait des régressions fonctionnelles (couverture de tests insuffisante) et une baisse de productivité (équipe majoritairement junior)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0075", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.43}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a supply chain management system built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 20 developers (mostly junior). The 8.8-year-old codebase faces talent scarcity for its current stack, though its structural metrics (coupling, cohesion) are moderate, and test coverage is borderline acceptable at 41.8%. Key pain points are concentrated in core modules with high coupling and anti-patterns like circular dependencies.", "analysis": "The metrics do not justify a full rewrite: coupling (4.6/10) and cohesion (6.7/10) are manageable, cyclomatic complexity (5.0) is moderate, and test coverage, while low, isn't catastrophic. However, the talent shortage is a strategic concern. The high bugfix-commit ratio (0.43) and anti-patterns in core.py/handler.py indicate localized instability, not systemic failure.", "recommendation": "Targeted refactoring of high-risk modules (core.py, handler.py) to reduce coupling and eliminate anti-patterns, paired with incremental modernization (e.g., containerization, CI/CD pipelines) to attract talent. A full migration would be disproportionate to the technical debt observed.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies and long parameter lists in core.py, add integration tests for critical paths", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decouple handler.py from downstream dependencies, introduce contract testing", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Modernize deployment (Docker/Kubernetes), upgrade to latest LTS .NET version", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk lies in the core.py refactor due to its high bugfix rate—ensure full regression test coverage before proceeding. Talent retention may suffer during modernization; phase 3 should be prioritized if attrition risks escalate."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0076", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.3, "cohesion_score": 1.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 21.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.76}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an industrial IoT platform built on a 9.4-year-old Ruby on Rails and MySQL stack, maintained by a team of 20 developers with mixed seniority. The system struggles with production reliability and uptime, exacerbated by high coupling, low cohesion, and significant anti-patterns in core components like the IoT processor and service layers.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits severe structural issues: extremely high coupling (8.3/10) and very low cohesion (1.7/10), indicating tightly intertwined components with poorly defined responsibilities. Test coverage is critically low (21.7%), and cyclomatic complexity (9.7) suggests convoluted logic. Anti-patterns are concentrated in critical paths (e.g., God Class, circular dependencies in processor.py), directly correlating with the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.76) in hotspots. This aligns with the team's reported reliability challenges.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full rewrite. Instead, execute a targeted refactoring of the highest-risk components (processor.py, service.py) to break circular dependencies and reduce coupling. Parallelly, improve test coverage to stabilize changes. The age and stack are not the primary issues—the structural flaws are.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isolate and refactor the God Class in processor.py, splitting it into focused modules with dependency injection to break circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address duplicate code in service.py by extracting shared logic into reusable components, with accompanying unit tests.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement integration tests for the refactored components to raise coverage to at least 60%, prioritizing critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression during phase 1 due to tight coupling in processor.py. Mitigate by: (1) writing characterization tests for existing behavior before refactoring, (2) deploying changes behind feature flags, and (3) scheduling the work during low-traffic periods. Monitor error rates closely post-deployment."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0077", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.5, "cohesion_score": 9.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 61.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet concerne une plateforme IoT industrielle mature (3.9 ans) développée en PHP/Laravel/MySQL, avec une architecture globalement saine mais une difficulté croissante à recruter des talents sur cette stack. L'équipe, majoritairement senior, maintient une base de code bien structurée avec une bonne couverture de tests.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont excellentes : couplage très faible (2.5/10), cohésion élevée (9.6/10), complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée (3.8) et peu de corrections sur les fichiers sensibles (ratio 0.08). La couverture de tests (61.1%) pourrait être améliorée mais reste acceptable. Aucun anti-pattern significatif n'a été détecté.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. La solution optimale est de : 1) Renforcer la formation interne pour pallier la pénurie de talents PHP, 2) Améliorer progressivement la couverture de tests, 3) Documenter davantage l'architecture pour faciliter l'onboarding.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Lancer un programme de mentorat interne (juniors par seniors) + documentation ciblée des patterns clés", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Identifier les modules critiques sous-testés et implémenter des tests d'intégration supplémentaires", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit des compétences existantes dans l'équipe et plan de formation sur les aspects avancés de Laravel", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est organisationnel : perdre des développeurs seniors sans transfert de connaissances. La stack technique actuelle ne présente pas de dette significative justifiant une migration risquée. Une approche incrémentale préserve la stabilité tout en adressant le problème RH."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0078", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.2, "cohesion_score": 9.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 70.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.13}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de paiements fintech mature (4.8 ans), développée en Java/Spring Boot avec PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 21 développeurs maintient une codebase globalement saine, avec une forte cohésion et un couplage faible. Aucune contrainte critique n'a été identifiée à ce stade.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase de haute qualité : couplage très faible (2.2/10), excellente cohésion (9.8/10), couverture de tests correcte (70.1%) et complexité cyclomatique très basse (2.4). Le seul anti-pattern détecté (Long Method) est isolé et de faible gravité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.13) suggère une stabilité élevée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. La stack actuelle est parfaitement adaptée et bien maintenue. Recommande des améliorations ciblées sur le fichier problématique et une légère augmentation de la couverture de tests.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring ciblé de la Long Method dans processor.py (extraction de méthodes, simplification des conditions)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Atelier d'architecture avec l'équipe pour valider les bonnes pratiques et identifier d'éventuelles zones d'amélioration incrémentale", "duration_days_range": "2-3 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests pour atteindre 80% sur les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque très faible. Les actions proposées sont non disruptives et s'appuient sur des forces existantes. Le principal risque serait de sur-optimiser une codebase déjà saine au détriment de nouvelles fonctionnalités."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0078", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.2, "cohesion_score": 9.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 70.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.13}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature fintech payment processing system built on Java/Spring Boot with PostgreSQL, maintained by a 21-developer team with balanced experience levels. The codebase shows strong architectural health with low coupling and high cohesion, though minor anti-patterns exist in isolated components.", "analysis": "Metrics indicate a well-structured codebase: coupling is exceptionally low (2.2/10), cohesion approaches ideal (9.8/10), and test coverage exceeds 70%. Cyclomatic complexity (2.4) suggests simple control flows. The single detected anti-pattern ('Long Method' in processor.py) is marked as low severity. The bugfix ratio (0.13) on the most active file indicates stable development.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The system demonstrates excellent maintainability. Instead, implement targeted improvements to address the minor anti-pattern and reinforce existing strengths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the 'Long Method' in processor.py using extract method pattern, with paired testing to maintain coverage", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Conduct a team workshop on advanced Spring Boot patterns to leverage the high cohesion architecture further", "duration_days_range": "2-3"}], "risk_assessment": "Minimal risk. The refactoring targets an isolated component, and the workshop capitalizes on existing team knowledge. The main risk would be over-engineering solutions for an already healthy codebase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0079", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une application médicale critique développée en Ruby on Rails avec une base MySQL, vieille de 3 ans. L'équipe de 32 développeurs (dont près de la moitié sont juniors) fait face à des coûts cloud élevés, probablement liés à des inefficacités dans le code ou l'infrastructure. La codebase montre des signes de dette technique modérée, avec quelques points de couplage élevé et des méthodes trop longues.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales sont acceptables (couplage 5.2/10, cohésion 6.4/10) mais révèlent des points critiques localisés. La couverture de tests à 47% est insuffisante pour une application médicale. Les anti-patterns identifiés (High Coupling, Long Method) dans des fichiers clés comme core.py et service.py impactent la maintenabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.25) sur les fichiers chauds indique une instabilité modérée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack complète. Prioriser : 1) une analyse détaillée des coûts cloud pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement, 2) des refactorings ciblés sur les fichiers problématiques, 3) l'amélioration de la couverture de tests. Une migration partielle vers des services serverless pourrait être envisagée uniquement pour les composants les plus coûteux après cette analyse.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des coûts cloud et profiling des ressources (CPU/mémoire) par composant", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des fichiers core.py et service.py pour réduire le couplage (stratégie : extraire des interfaces claires)", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests (objectif +20% sur les modules critiques)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principaux risques : 1) impact sur la stabilité lors des refactorings sans tests suffisants, 2) résistance au changement chez les juniors (50% de l'équipe). Atténuations : pair-programming systématique sur les refactorings critiques, ateliers de formation sur les patterns de découplage."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0079", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 3.2-year-old Ruby on Rails application in the medtech sector, serving healthcare-related functionalities with a MySQL backend. The team of 32 developers (a balanced mix of juniors and seniors) has identified escalating cloud costs as their primary operational constraint. While the codebase shows moderate cohesion and coupling, several anti-patterns in core modules indicate areas of technical debt.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal a codebase with moderate coupling (5.2/10) and slightly better cohesion (6.4/10), suggesting the architecture is not fundamentally flawed but requires targeted improvements. Test coverage at 47% is below ideal, and cyclomatic complexity (6.3) indicates some overly complex methods. The high bugfix-commit ratio (0.25) in hot files, coupled with detected anti-patterns (high coupling in core modules and long methods), points to specific pain points rather than systemic failure. Cloud cost issues are likely more related to infrastructure/architecture decisions than language or framework choice.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics do not justify a full rewrite. Instead, address the identified anti-patterns incrementally while optimizing cloud costs through infrastructure improvements (e.g., query optimization, caching strategies). Focus first on the high-coupling and long-method issues in core modules, as these directly impact maintainability and bug rates.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor high-coupling modules (src/sante/service.py, src/sante/core.py) by introducing interfaces or breaking into smaller services. Pair senior developers with juniors for knowledge transfer.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address long methods in src/sante/processor.py and src/sante/core.py through method extraction and SRP compliance. Add missing unit tests during refactoring to improve coverage.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit with DevOps: analyze query patterns, database indexing, and caching opportunities. Optimize expensive endpoints identified via APM tools.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are: (1) Junior-heavy team may struggle with deep refactoring without senior oversight, (2) Cloud optimizations might require database schema changes that cascade to application code. Mitigations: Phase 1 should include paired programming, and cloud changes must be validated in staging with performance benchmarks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0080", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 39, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 4.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.32}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une application médicale critique, développée depuis 10 ans en Node.js/Express/MongoDB par une équipe expérimentée. La stack actuelle montre des signes de fatigue architecturale, avec des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production malgré une base de code globalement mature.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une dette technique modérée mais préoccupante pour un domaine critique. Le couplage élevé (5.1/10) et la cohésion faible (4.2/10) expliquent en partie les incidents en prod. La couverture de tests à 33.5% est insuffisante pour le secteur médical. Les anti-patterns détectés sont concentrés dans des composants clés (core.py, handler.py), ce qui amplifie leur impact.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé des composants problématiques et améliorer la couverture de tests. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.9) reste raisonnable, et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.32) ne justifie pas un rewrite complet.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les dépendances circulaires dans src/sante/core.py avec inversion de contrôle", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découper src/sante/handler.py en micro-services légers pour réduire le couplage", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration sur les composants refactorés pour atteindre 60% de couverture", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de perturber les fonctionnalités existantes durant le refactoring. Recommandation : déployer les changements par étapes avec des feature flags. Le domaine médical exige une validation rigoureuse des modifications."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0080", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 39, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 4.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.32}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10-year-old medical technology platform built on Node.js/Express/MongoDB, serving critical healthcare applications. With a team of 39 developers (mix of junior and senior), the system faces reliability challenges, particularly frequent production incidents impacting uptime. Static analysis reveals moderate coupling and cohesion issues, suboptimal test coverage, and several architectural anti-patterns in core modules.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt—coupling (5.1/10) and cohesion (4.2/10) are not catastrophic, and cyclomatic complexity (4.9) is within reasonable bounds. However, test coverage (33.5%) is insufficient for a medtech system where reliability is critical. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies and high coupling in core files (e.g., src/sante/core.py, src/sante/handler.py) are likely contributing to production incidents. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.32) on the hottest file suggests instability in a key component.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, prioritize targeted refactoring of high-risk modules and improve test coverage incrementally. Address the circular dependency first, as it poses the highest risk to reliability. The team’s senior-heavy composition is well-suited for this surgical approach.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in src/sante/core.py and high coupling in src/sante/handler.py. Add integration tests for these modules.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address long methods/parameter lists in src/sante/service.py and src/sante/processor.py. Implement unit test coverage for these files to reach 70%.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Establish monitoring for the refactored modules to track incident reduction. Plan a test-coverage sprint for the next-critical 20% of the codebase.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is destabilizing the system during refactoring due to low test coverage. Mitigate this by: (1) pairing senior/junior developers during changes, (2) validating fixes in a staging environment with production-like data, and (3) rolling out changes module-by-module with feature flags."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0081", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.8, "cohesion_score": 1.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 19.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.72}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme edtech mature, hébergée sur une stack .NET/SQL Server, avec une forte exigence de conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). L'équipe de 41 développeurs (majoritairement seniors) maintient une codebase vieille de 7 ans présentant des problèmes de couplage élevé et de faible cohésion, particulièrement dans les modules critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase montre des signaux alarmants : couplage très élevé (8.8/10) et cohésion très faible (1.2/10), combinés à une couverture de tests insuffisante (19.1%). Les anti-patterns détectés (Circular Dependency, God Class, High Coupling) sont concentrés dans des fichiers critiques (service.py, processor.py, core.py), ce qui explique le ratio élevé de commits correctifs (0.72). La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (7.3) reste acceptable mais masque des points de complexité localisés.", "recommendation": "Refactoring ciblé (sans migration technologique) avec priorité sur : 1) la résolution des dépendances circulaires critiques, 2) la décomposition du God Class dans processor.py, 3) l'augmentation urgente de la couverture de tests sur les modules à fort couplage. Un rewrite complet n'est pas justifié car la stack actuelle répond aux besoins réglementaires et l'équipe a l'expertise .NET.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isolation et instrumentation des dépendances circulaires (service.py, handler.py) avec création de tests d'intégration ciblés", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental du God Class (processor.py) en appliquant le pattern Strategy pour les méthodes à Long Parameter List", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de contrats d'interface stricts pour réduire le couplage dans core.py et service.py, avec revue d'architecture par pairs", "duration_days_range": "6-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : la faible couverture de tests actuelle pourrait rendre dangereux le refactoring des modules à haut couplage. Contre-mesure : implémenter d'abord des tests de non-régression sur les chemins critiques identifiés par l'historique git. Second risque : perturbation des cycles de livraison due à la complexité des dépendances. Contre-mesure : planifier les refactorings entre deux sprints majeurs."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0081", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.8, "cohesion_score": 1.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 19.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.72}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "This is a mature edtech platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, serving 7 years in production. The 41-developer team (72% senior) maintains a system where regulatory compliance (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS) is the primary constraint. Static analysis reveals structural issues in core modules, particularly around coupling and circular dependencies, compounded by low test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics paint a concerning picture: dangerously low cohesion (1.2/10) coupled with high coupling (8.8/10) suggests brittle architecture. The 19.1% test coverage is critically inadequate for compliance-heavy domains. Cyclomatic complexity (7.3) and bugfix ratio (0.72) in hotspots indicate unstable core logic. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies and God Classes in processor.py/service.py confirm systemic design flaws.", "recommendation": "DO NOT recommend a full rewrite. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of high-risk modules while improving test coverage. The regulatory constraints make a 'big bang' migration prohibitively risky. Prioritize decoupling core services to achieve incremental compliance readiness.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Break circular dependencies in service.py and handler.py using interface segregation, starting with GDPR-critical paths", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Extract compliance-critical logic from God Class in processor.py into domain-specific services with contract tests", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement characterization testing for core modules to raise coverage above 50% for PCI-DSS audit trails", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk is regulatory non-compliance during refactoring. Mitigation: maintain parallel compliance validation environments. Secondary risk is junior developers introducing new coupling - enforce senior code reviews on core module changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0082", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 25, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.9, "cohesion_score": 7.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 88.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme IoT industrielle mature, développée depuis près de 15 ans en Node.js avec NestJS et PostgreSQL. L'équipe expérimentée maintient une base de code de haute qualité, mais fait face à des coûts cloud croissants qui impactent la rentabilité.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques indiquent une base de code exceptionnellement saine : couplage très faible (2.9/10), cohésion élevée (7.2/10), excellente couverture de tests (88%) et complexité cyclomatique minimale (1.1). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs (0.08) confirment cette stabilité. La problématique principale est économique (coût cloud), non technique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack existante. Optimiser l'infrastructure cloud via : 1) Une analyse fine des coûts par service, 2) L'implémentation de stratégies de scaling adaptées au trafic IoT, 3) La renegotiation des contrats avec les fournisseurs cloud. La qualité du code permet de se concentrer sur ces optimisations sans risquer la stabilité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud (CPU/mémoire/stockage/bande passante) avec tagging des services critiques", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Benchmark des configurations actuelles vs. alternatives (instances réservées, autoscaling, architectures serverless pour les pics IoT)", "duration_days_range": "10-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring ciblé des services les plus gourmands en ressources (sans changer de stack)", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les spécificités du trafic IoT (bursts imprévisibles) lors des optimisations. Une phase de monitoring renforcé (2-3 semaines) post-optimisation est cruciale. Aucun risque technique majeur identifié sur la base de code existante."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0082", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 25, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.9, "cohesion_score": 7.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 88.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature industrial IoT platform built on Node.js/NestJS with PostgreSQL, maintained by a predominantly senior team. While the codebase shows strong structural health with high cohesion and test coverage, the team has identified escalating cloud costs as their primary operational challenge.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate an exceptionally healthy codebase: low coupling (2.9/10), high cohesion (7.2/10), outstanding test coverage (88%), and trivial cyclomatic complexity (1.1). The bugfix ratio (0.08) suggests stable core logic. No architectural anti-patterns were detected. Cloud cost issues are likely unrelated to code quality.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The solution lies in cloud optimization, not code changes. Focus on infrastructure profiling, query optimization, and scaling adjustments while maintaining the current stack's advantages.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a comprehensive cloud cost audit with infrastructure logs and database query analysis", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement monitoring for cost-driver services and optimize PostgreSQL indexing/connection pooling", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor deployment architecture (e.g., cold-start mitigation for serverless components)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low technical risk given the codebase health. Primary risks are organizational: potential distraction from core feature development during cloud optimization work. Mitigate by assigning dedicated infrastructure specialists."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0083", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 5.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de streaming média vieille de 10 ans, construite avec Node.js/Express et MongoDB. L'équipe de 27 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) doit maintenir un système critique où la latence temps réel est un enjeu majeur. L'analyse révèle une base de code mature avec des problèmes localisés de conception.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement acceptables (complexité modérée, couplage/cohésion moyens) mais avec des points critiques localisés. Les anti-patterns détectés se concentrent principalement sur le module média, ce qui est cohérent avec le domaine critique. La couverture de tests sous les 50% est préoccupante pour un système temps réel.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé du module média et améliorer les tests. La présence majoritaire de juniors justifie des interventions incrémentales plutôt qu'une réécriture.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns dans src/media/service.py (duplication, long method) avec pairing senior/junior", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découplage progressif de src/media/core.py (God Class) via extraction de sous-modules", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests sur les composants critiques liés à la latence", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : déstabilisation des performances temps réel pendant les refactorings. Mitigation : déploiements canaris et monitoring renforcé des métriques de latence. Second risque : courbe d'apprentissage pour les juniors. Mitigation : documentation live des patterns appliqués."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0083", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 5.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10-year-old media streaming platform built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB, serving real-time content with strict latency requirements. With a team of 27 developers (mostly junior), the codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion, nearly 50% test coverage, and several high-severity anti-patterns in critical media processing components.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with balanced coupling/cohesion (5.0/5.6) and acceptable cyclomatic complexity (5.0), but test coverage is borderline (49.6%) and specific hotspots (media/service.py, media/core.py) exhibit severe maintainability issues. The high bugfix-commit ratio (0.25) in critical files suggests instability in key components.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate. The systemic metrics don't justify a rewrite, but targeted refactoring is urgently needed in the media processing module. Prioritize eliminating the God Class and duplicate code first, as these directly impact real-time performance.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/media/core.py (God Class) by splitting into focused subcomponents, preserving interfaces for backward compatibility.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address duplicate code and long methods in src/media/service.py through extraction and strategy pattern implementation.", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to 65% for refactored components, with emphasis on latency-critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is destabilizing real-time processing during refactoring. Mitigation: deploy changes behind feature flags, monitor latency metrics rigorously. Secondary risk: junior-heavy team may struggle with architectural patterns. Mitigation: pair senior developers with juniors during core.py refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0084", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.4, "cohesion_score": 1.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 19.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 10.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.52}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This project involves developing and maintaining an industrial IoT platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL. With a team of 29 developers, including a significant percentage of senior engineers, the platform has been in development for 3.5 years. The primary constraint identified by the team is scalability, particularly handling unpredictable traffic spikes.", "analysis": "The codebase has a moderate coupling score of 6.4/10, but unusually low cohesion of 1.1/10, indicating that the modules do not function well together. The test coverage is alarmingly low at 19.9%, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 10.5 suggests overly complex code. Several anti-patterns, including high coupling, circular dependencies, and long methods, are concentrated in key files like src/iot/handler.py and src/iot/processor.py.", "recommendation": "Given the metrics and anti-patterns, a full rewrite is not justified. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address scalability, improve cohesion, and enhance test coverage. Refactoring the identified problematic files should be prioritized.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/iot/handler.py to break circular dependencies and reduce method lengths.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage by writing unit tests for the most critical components, starting with src/iot/processor.py.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize scalability by implementing a more robust traffic handling mechanism, possibly integrating a queuing or caching system.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk lies in the low cohesion and moderate coupling, which could lead to further scalability issues if not addressed. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.52 in the hottest file indicates ongoing instability. Incremental improvements will mitigate these risks without the high cost and uncertainty of a full rewrite."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0085", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.36}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme edtech mature (8.6 ans) avec une stack Ruby/Rails/MySQL, utilisée par des milliers d'utilisateurs avec des exigences strictes sur la latence temps réel. L'équipe de 6 développeurs (majoritairement seniors) maintient activement le produit, mais rencontre des difficultés de maintenance autour de certains composants critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase montre des signes de dette technique localisée (couplage élevé dans service.py, complexité modérée) mais des indicateurs globaux raisonnables (complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5.1, couverture de tests proche de 50%). Les anti-patterns sont concentrés sur deux fichiers seulement, ce qui suggère un problème de conception ciblé plutôt qu'une dégradation généralisée. La contrainte de latence critique n'est pas directement adressée par les métriques actuelles.", "recommendation": "Refactoring ciblé (service.py et processor.py) sans migration technologique. Prioriser la réduction du couplage et la simplification des méthodes complexes dans ces composants, tout en améliorant progressivement la couverture de tests. Une migration serait prématurée étant donné l'état global de la codebase.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et instrumenter les chemins critiques liés à la latence temps réel pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement spécifiques", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental de service.py (découplage des dépendances, division des longues méthodes) avec tests de non-régression", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Restructuration de processor.py pour réduire ses responsabilités (pattern Strategy ou Command)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : perturbation des fonctionnalités temps réel pendant les refactorings. Mitigation : déploiement progressif avec feature flags et monitoring renforcé des métriques de performance. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.36) indique une stabilité relative du code problématique."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0085", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.36}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an established edtech platform built on Ruby/Rails/MySQL, serving real-time educational content with critical latency requirements. The 8.6-year-old codebase shows moderate technical debt, particularly in core service files, with a mixed team of junior and senior developers maintaining it.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a generally healthy codebase (low coupling score of 3.1, moderate cohesion) with isolated hotspots of technical debt. The primary issues are concentrated in `src/edtech/service.py` (high coupling, long methods, circular dependencies) and `src/edtech/processor.py` (God Class). Test coverage is borderline at 49.3%, and cyclomatic complexity is acceptable (5.1). The bugfix ratio on critical files suggests stability concerns but not systemic failure.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The problems are localized and can be addressed through targeted refactoring. A full rewrite would be disproportionate given the overall code health. Focus on incremental improvements to the problematic files while improving test coverage.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor `src/edtech/service.py` to break up long methods, resolve circular dependencies, and reduce coupling through dependency injection or service extraction.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decompose the God Class in `src/edtech/processor.py` into smaller, single-responsibility classes, prioritizing the most complex or frequently modified methods.", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 70% for the refactored files, adding integration tests for critical real-time latency paths.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is destabilizing the real-time components during refactoring. Mitigate this by: (1) writing characterization tests for existing behavior before refactoring, (2) validating latency metrics after each phase, and (3) pairing juniors with seniors on hotfile changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0086", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.26}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme edtech mature (près de 10 ans d'existence) avec une base de code Python/Django/MongoDB. L'équipe de 19 développeurs, avec une proportion significative de juniors, rencontre des difficultés de vélocité malgré une architecture globalement saine.", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une codebase avec des défauts localisés mais pas systémiques. Le couplage modéré (5.8/10) et la cohésion correcte (6.5/10) ne justifient pas un rewrite. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont concentrés sur quelques fichiers critiques, notamment des méthodes trop longues et une classe trop grosse dans le module service.", "recommendation": "Refactoring ciblé des points chauds identifiés, accompagné d'une amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests. Priorité au découpage de src/edtech/service.py (God Class + Long Method) qui impacte probablement la vélocité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Découpage de src/edtech/service.py en micro-services spécialisés, avec revue d'architecture par un senior", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des Long Methods dans src/edtech/handler.py via extraction de sous-fonctions", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de tests unitaires ciblés sur les modules refactorés pour atteindre 50%+ de couverture", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la perturbation temporaire de la vélocité pendant les refactorings critiques. Une attention particulière doit être portée au mentoring des juniors pendant ces phases pour éviter des régressions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0086", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.26}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an educational technology platform built on a Python/Django/MongoDB stack, nearly a decade old. The development team, comprising 19 developers with a mix of junior and senior expertise, is primarily constrained by slow feature delivery. Despite a reasonably cohesive codebase, there are notable issues with coupling, test coverage, and several anti-patterns affecting critical files.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion scores, indicating room for improvement but not critical flaws. Test coverage is notably low at 32.8%, and cyclomatic complexity is slightly higher than ideal at 6.2. Anti-patterns such as High Coupling, Long Method, and God Class are identified in key files, which are likely contributing to the slow feature development. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file suggests ongoing stability issues.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to enhance code quality and development velocity. Address the identified anti-patterns specifically in the critical files and boost test coverage to improve stability and maintainability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/edtech/service.py and src/edtech/handler.py to address Long Method and God Class issues.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage for core functionalities, aiming for at least 50% coverage.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Decouple src/edtech/core.py to reduce high coupling.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include potential disruptions during refactoring of critical files and the challenge of increasing test coverage without introducing new bugs. Close coordination and rigorous code reviews are essential to mitigate these risks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0087", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 16, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.28}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme e-commerce mature (8.5 ans) basée sur .NET/ASP.NET Core, avec une équipe majoritairement junior. La stack actuelle répond globalement aux besoins, mais les contraintes réglementaires croissantes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) mettent en lumière certains défauts structurels dans le code.", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une codebase modérément couplée (5.3/10) avec une cohésion moyenne (5.1/10). La couverture de tests (46%) est insuffisante pour une plateforme soumise à des régulations strictes. Les anti-patterns identifiés (God Class, High Coupling) concernent principalement des composants critiques (core.py, handler.py), ce qui augmente les risques lors des évolutions réglementaires.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé des composants problématiques et améliorer la couverture de tests, particulièrement sur les modules liés aux données sensibles (paiements, santé). La stack .NET Core reste adaptée aux contraintes réglementaires.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer le God Class (handler.py) en appliquant le pattern Facade pour réduire son empreinte", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpler core.py via l'introduction de contrats d'interface et l'extraction des dépendances directes", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests à 70% minimum sur les modules critiques (paiement, gestion des données personnelles)", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la non-conformité réglementaire due à des modifications accidentelles dans les composants couplés. La présence de nombreux juniors amplifie ce risque. Une attention particulière doit être portée aux revues de code pendant les phases de refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0087", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 16, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.28}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an 8.5-year-old e-commerce platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a team of 16 developers (60% junior, 20% senior). The system faces increasing regulatory compliance demands (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS), while technical debt in key modules is slowing down adaptations.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate technical health (coupling 5.3/10, cohesion 5.1/10) with suboptimal test coverage (46%). Critical anti-patterns are concentrated in core business logic (high coupling in core.py, god class in handler.py) and service layers (long parameter lists, duplicate code). The bugfix ratio (0.28) in hot files suggests fragile areas, but metrics don't indicate systemic failure.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate. Prioritize incremental refactoring targeting compliance-critical paths first. The team composition (many juniors) favors small, mentored improvements over high-risk rewrites.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract compliance-critical paths from core.py/handler.py into isolated modules with strict interface contracts. Add missing tests for these paths to reach 70% coverage.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break up god class in handler.py using strategy pattern for payment/validation flows. Apply parameter object pattern to service.py's long parameter lists.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct junior-senior pairing sessions to eliminate duplicate code in service.py while documenting patterns for future compliance changes.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Main risks: (1) Overlapping refactoring with compliance deadlines, (2) Knowledge gaps in junior team members slowing pattern adoption. Mitigations: Phase work to align with regulatory milestones, dedicate 2 seniors as full-time code reviewers during phase 2."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0088", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme médicale critique en production depuis 8.5 ans, développée en Python/FastAPI avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 27 développeurs (dont 41% de juniors) doit maintenir une conformité stricte aux réglementations RGPD, PCI-DSS et HDS tout en évoluant la solution.", "analysis": "La codebase montre des signes de dette technique localisée mais pas systémique. Le score de couplage (5.8/10) et de cohésion (5.0/10) sont dans la moyenne acceptable pour un projet de cette ancienneté. La couverture de tests à 52.9% est insuffisante pour les modules critiques (santé/service.py et santé/core.py) qui concentrent les anti-patterns (High Coupling, Long Method, God Class). Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.42) sur le fichier le plus chaud indique une instabilité modérée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé des modules problématiques avec renforcement des tests. La conformité réglementaire impose une approche incrémentale plutôt qu'un rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et tester les composants réglementaires critiques (RGPD/PCI-DSS/HDS)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring ciblé de src/sante/service.py (découplage des méthodes longues)", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Modernisation incrémentale de src/sante/core.py (éclatement de la God Class)", "duration_days_range": "12-16 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la dégradation involontaire des garanties réglementaires pendant le refactoring. Une attention particulière doit être portée aux revues de code impliquant systématiquement les seniors sur les modules sensibles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0088", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a medical technology (medtech) platform built with Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, focusing on compliance with strict regulations like GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS. The 8.5-year-old codebase is maintained by a team of 27 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience levels. Key challenges include managing technical debt while ensuring regulatory requirements are met.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate moderate coupling (5.8/10) and cohesion (5.0/10), with test coverage at 52.9%, which is below ideal but not critically low. Cyclomatic complexity (5.5) is acceptable, though the bugfix-commit ratio (0.42) on the hottest file suggests instability. Anti-patterns are concentrated in `src/sante/service.py` and `src/sante/core.py`, primarily involving high coupling, long methods, and a god class. These issues are localized rather than systemic, making a full rewrite unnecessary.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the system. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring of the problematic files (`src/sante/service.py` and `src/sante/core.py`) to reduce coupling, break down long methods, and eliminate the god class. Improve test coverage incrementally, prioritizing high-risk areas related to compliance.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor `src/sante/service.py` to break down long methods and reduce coupling. Write targeted unit tests for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the god class and long methods in `src/sante/core.py` by splitting responsibilities into smaller, cohesive classes.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage by 10-15% in high-risk compliance modules, ensuring regulatory requirements are thoroughly validated.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks are introducing regressions during refactoring and failing to meet compliance deadlines. Mitigate these by: (1) pairing junior developers with seniors during refactoring, (2) maintaining a robust CI/CD pipeline to catch regressions early, and (3) prioritizing compliance-critical paths in testing. The localized nature of the anti-patterns reduces the risk of widespread instability."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0089", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.3, "cohesion_score": 8.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 74.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.0}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme e-commerce mature (9.5 ans) basée sur Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, avec une équipe majoritairement junior. La principale préoccupation est la scalabilité pour gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles, bien que les métriques structurelles du code soient globalement excellentes.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une santé technique remarquable : couplage très faible (2.3/10), cohésion élevée (8.8/10), bonne couverture de tests (74.5%) et complexité cyclomatique optimale. Le seul anti-pattern identifié (God Class low dans core.py) est marginal. L'absence de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud suggère une stabilité exceptionnelle.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. La stack actuelle est parfaitement adaptée et bien maîtrisée. Optimiser l'architecture existante pour la scalabilité via : 1) Refactoring ciblé de core.py, 2) Benchmark des goulots d'étranglement, 3) Formation des juniors sur les patterns de scalabilité Python.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit de performance sous charge et identification des goulots d'étranglement réels", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental de core.py avec revue d'architecture par les seniors", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers techniques sur la scalabilité Python/FastAPI pour les juniors", "duration_days_range": "2-3 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est organisationnel : une équipe majoritairement junior pourrait sous-estimer les capacités de la stack actuelle et vouloir migrer par effet de mode. La formation et le mentoring sont critiques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0089", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.3, "cohesion_score": 8.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 74.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.0}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature e-commerce platform built on Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, serving unpredictable traffic spikes. With a team predominantly composed of junior developers (57%), the codebase shows strong cohesion and low coupling, but scalability remains the primary operational challenge.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase: low coupling (2.3/10), high cohesion (8.8/10), solid test coverage (74.5%), and manageable complexity (avg. cyclomatic complexity 2.5). The only notable anti-pattern is a minor 'God Class' in core.py, which hasn't required bugfixes (0.0 ratio). The team's junior-heavy composition suggests a full migration would be high-risk.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, address scalability through targeted improvements to the existing stack, starting with the God Class refactor. The metrics don't justify the disruption of a full rewrite, especially with the team's experience distribution.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in core.py into smaller, domain-specific services to improve maintainability and scalability.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement load testing and profiling to identify specific bottlenecks in the current architecture under peak traffic conditions.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce senior-led workshops on Python performance optimization (e.g., async I/O, query batching) to upskill junior developers.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is attempting large-scale changes with a junior-majority team. Incremental improvements reduce disruption while building internal expertise. The God Class, though minor, could become a scalability blocker if left unaddressed during traffic spikes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0090", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.0, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 78.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.07}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet concerne une plateforme edtech développée en PHP/Laravel/MySQL depuis plus de 13 ans. Avec une équipe de 30 développeurs (dont une majorité de profils juniors), la principale préoccupation est la fiabilité et la réduction des incidents en production.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase globalement saine : faible couplage (2.0/10), forte cohésion (7.7/10), et une couverture de tests élevée (78.6%). La complexité cyclomatique moyenne est basse (1.8), ce qui suggère un code facile à maintenir. Le seul anti-pattern détecté est une God Class à faible impact. La priorité sur la fiabilité est justifiée par le ratio de commits correctifs relativement faible (0.07 sur le fichier le plus modifié).", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle, car les métriques montrent une codebase bien structurée et maintenable. Concentrer les efforts sur des améliorations incrémentales pour renforcer la fiabilité et réduire les incidents en production.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé du fichier contenant la God Class pour identifier les dépendances critiques et proposer un refactoring modulaire.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'un monitoring renforcé des incidents en production avec création de dashboards dédiés.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Formation ciblée des développeurs juniors sur les bonnes pratiques de fiabilité et de debugging.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est une accentuation des incidents en production si les améliorations ne sont pas priorisées rapidement. Une attention particulière doit être portée au fichier problématique identifié pour éviter une dégradation progressive de la qualité du code."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0090", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.0, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 78.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.07}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature edtech platform built on PHP/Laravel/MySQL, serving educational institutions for over 13 years. With a team of 30 developers (a mix of junior and senior talent), the primary operational challenge is maintaining high reliability and uptime, as production incidents occur too frequently. Despite this, the codebase shows strong structural health with low coupling, high cohesion, and solid test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a fundamentally healthy codebase: low coupling (2.0/10) and high cohesion (7.7/10) suggest good modular design, while 78.6% test coverage and low cyclomatic complexity (1.8) reflect maintainable code. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.07) on the hottest file is acceptable, and the only detected anti-pattern ('God Class' in src/edtech/handler.py) is marked as low severity. The uptime issues likely stem from operational or architectural factors (e.g., deployment processes, infrastructure) rather than code quality.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, address the reliability constraint through targeted improvements: refactor the 'God Class' to reduce its scope, enhance monitoring/alerting for production incidents, and review deployment pipelines. The codebase's structural health justifies incremental fixes over disruptive changes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the 'God Class' in src/edtech/handler.py by splitting its responsibilities into smaller, focused classes.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Conduct a reliability review: analyze production incident patterns, improve logging, and implement targeted monitoring for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit and optimize deployment processes (e.g., rollback strategies, canary releases) to minimize downtime during updates.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is underestimating operational factors (e.g., infrastructure, third-party integrations) contributing to uptime issues. Refactoring the 'God Class' carries minimal risk due to high test coverage. Phase 2's incident analysis might reveal deeper architectural flaws not captured by static metrics."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0091", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 17, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.3, "cohesion_score": 4.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 21.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.66}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 12.5-year-old media streaming platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, with a team of 17 developers split evenly between junior and senior levels. The primary constraint is ensuring compliance with regulatory standards such as GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS, which dominate the team's focus.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (6.3/10) and low cohesion (4.0/10), indicating some architectural inefficiencies but not critical fragmentation. Test coverage is notably low at 21.2%, which poses risks for future stability and compliance-related changes. Cyclomatic complexity is moderately high (7.2), suggesting some overly complex logic. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.66) on the hottest file points to recurring maintenance issues. Several anti-patterns are present, primarily God Classes, Circular Dependencies, and Duplicate Code, concentrated in core business logic files.", "recommendation": "A full migration or rewrite is not justified at this time. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address technical debt and improve regulatory compliance readiness. Prioritize refactoring the most problematic files, increasing test coverage, and reducing cyclomatic complexity.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor God Classes and Circular Dependencies in src/media/processor.py, src/media/core.py, and src/media/handler.py.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address Duplicate Code issues across src/media/core.py, src/media/service.py, and src/media/processor.py.", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Improve test coverage to at least 50% across critical modules, focusing on compliance-related functionality.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Reduce cyclomatic complexity in high-risk files, particularly those with Long Methods and Long Parameter Lists.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include insufficient test coverage leading to undetected compliance issues, technical debt causing slower feature development, and potential instability from unresolved circular dependencies. However, with focused refactoring and testing improvements, these risks can be mitigated effectively without the need for a full rewrite."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0092", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 7.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace vieillissante (11.5 ans) avec une stack Ruby/Rails/MySQL, où la latence temps réel est devenue un enjeu critique. L'équipe de 37 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) maintient une codebase présentant des signes de dette technique localisée, notamment autour de deux God Classes dans le cœur métier.", "analysis": "La codebase montre une santé globale acceptable (cohésion correcte, complexité modérée) mais avec des points critiques : couplage élevé et couverture de tests insuffisante. Les deux God Classes identifiées dans des composants clés du marketplace expliquent probablement le ratio élevé de correctifs sur ces fichiers. La contrainte de latence semble davantage liée à des problèmes d'architecture localisés qu'à des limitations de la stack actuelle.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des God Classes et l'amélioration des tests autour des composants critiques. Une approche incrémentale permettra de réduire la dette technique sans introduire de risque majeur pour l'équipe junior-heavy.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler le comportement temps réel dans un service dédié (sans toucher aux God Classes existantes)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring progressif de src/marketplace/handler.py en appliquant le pattern Strategy pour découpler les responsabilités", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implémentation de tests d'intégration ciblés sur les nouveaux services pour atteindre 70%+ de couverture sur les composants refactorés", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : la complexité des God Classes pourrait rendre le refactoring plus long que prévu. Recommandation : limiter les modifications à 2-3 méthodes par sprint et renforcer le pairing seniors/juniors pendant cette phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0092", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 7.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an 11.5-year-old Ruby on Rails marketplace platform with MySQL, maintained by a team of 37 developers (mostly junior). The system's critical constraint is real-time latency, and analysis reveals moderate coupling but good cohesion, with test coverage at 51.7%. Two significant God Classes exist in core marketplace processing logic.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a reasonably healthy codebase (low coupling, good cohesion) despite its age. The 51.7% test coverage is borderline but workable, and cyclomatic complexity is acceptable. The two God Classes are concerning but localized. The high bugfix ratio in hot files suggests instability in critical paths, likely tied to the God Classes. The junior-heavy team may struggle with incremental refactoring.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate. Target the God Classes with incremental refactoring while improving test coverage around them. Given the real-time latency constraint, prioritize decomposing the high-severity God Class in handler.py first, as it likely impacts performance.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract testable subcomponents from src/marketplace/handler.py (high-severity God Class), writing characterization tests for each", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor processor.py (medium God Class) by splitting into domain-specific handlers, leveraging existing tests", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement monitoring for the refactored components to verify latency improvements", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is destabilizing real-time operations during handler.py refactoring. Mitigation: deploy extra monitoring during phase 1 and roll out changes behind feature flags. Secondary risk: junior developers may introduce anti-patterns during extractions. Mitigation: pair senior developers with juniors on critical extractions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0094", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.2, "cohesion_score": 6.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.5}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une application fintech critique pour le traitement des paiements, développée en Python/Flask avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 41 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack technique, malgré une codebase relativement jeune (moins d'un an).", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques montrent une situation mitigée : un couplage modéré (4.2/10) et une cohésion acceptable (6.3/10), mais des problèmes localisés importants (duplication de code, méthodes trop longues) dans des fichiers critiques. La couverture de tests (51.7%) est insuffisante pour une application financière. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.7) reste raisonnable.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Les problèmes identifiés sont localisés et ne justifient pas un rewrite. Prioriser : 1) le refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques, 2) l'amélioration de la couverture de tests, 3) un programme de mentorat pour monter en compétence les juniors sur Python/Flask.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des fichiers service.py et handler.py pour éliminer la duplication et réduire la taille des méthodes", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de tests unitaires/intégration pour porter la couverture à 75% minimum", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de pair programming et revues de code ciblées pour transférer les connaissances des seniors vers les juniors", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la dette technique si les anti-patterns critiques ne sont pas corrigés rapidement. La pénurie de talents Python pourrait ralentir les recrutements, mais un rewrite entraînerait des risques opérationnels inacceptables dans le domaine financier."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0094", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.2, "cohesion_score": 6.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.5}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a fintech payment processing system built with Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, approximately 8 months old. With a team of 41 developers (over half junior), the primary challenge is talent scarcity for the current stack, compounded by some structural code quality issues in critical service files.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate health - coupling is low (4.2/10) and cohesion is reasonable (6.3/10), suggesting the architecture isn't fundamentally flawed. Test coverage at 51.7% is borderline acceptable for fintech. The main pain points are concentrated in service.py (duplicate code, long methods) and handler.py (long parameter lists), with a concerning bugfix ratio (0.5) in the hottest file indicating instability in core logic.", "recommendation": "DO NOT migrate stacks. The metrics don't justify a rewrite. Instead: 1) Refactor critical anti-patterns in service.py/handler.py, 2) Improve test coverage to 70%+, 3) Address talent scarcity through targeted upskilling rather than stack change. The junior-heavy team would struggle with a migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code and long methods in service.py (extract methods, introduce service layer patterns)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Restructure handler.py parameters (introduce DTOs or context objects), add integration tests for modified components", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement test coverage improvement program (focus on critical payment flows first)", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk is destabilizing core payment logic during refactoring. Mitigation: 1) Phase changes behind feature flags, 2) Maintain parallel runs of old/new implementations for critical paths, 3) Assign senior developers to oversee service.py changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0095", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 6.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une plateforme SaaS B2B pour la gestion d'entreprise, développée en Python avec Flask et PostgreSQL depuis près de 12 ans. L'équipe de 29 développeurs, composée d'un mélange de juniors et de seniors, identifie la vélocité de développement comme la principale contrainte actuelle.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales de la codebase sont dans la moyenne à bonne, avec un score de couplage faible (4.1/10) et une cohésion correcte (6.8/10). La couverture de tests est modérée (51.6%) et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne est acceptable (5.5). Cependant, plusieurs anti-patterns critiques sont détectés, notamment deux God Classes, du code dupliqué et une forte circularité dans des fichiers clés, ce qui pourrait expliquer les ralentissements dans le développement de nouvelles fonctionnalités.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack technologique. Prioriser une refactorisation incrémentale ciblée pour résoudre les anti-patterns identifiés, améliorer la modularité et augmenter la couverture de tests. Cela devrait améliorer la vélocité sans nécessiter un rewrite complet.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoriser les God Classes dans src/saas/service.py et src/saas/processor.py pour réduire leur taille et leurs responsabilités.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Éliminer les duplications de code dans src/saas/processor.py et réduire le couplage élevé dans src/saas/handler.py.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Résoudre les dépendances circulaires dans src/saas/service.py et améliorer l'architecture pour une meilleure modularité.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests en ajoutant des scénarios critiques et des tests d'intégration.", "duration_days_range": "12-16 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer l'impact des modifications proposées sur les dépendances existantes. Une approche progressive et bien testée est essentielle pour éviter les régressions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0095", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 6.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a SaaS B2B enterprise management platform built on Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, with a codebase that has evolved over 11.8 years. The team, consisting of 29 developers, is facing significant challenges with development velocity, as feature delivery is slower than desired. The metrics reveal moderate coupling, decent cohesion, and test coverage at 51.6%, along with several high-severity anti-patterns in critical components.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate that the codebase is in a moderately healthy state overall, with test coverage at an acceptable level and cyclomatic complexity within reasonable limits. Coupling is relatively low, and cohesion is good, suggesting the codebase is not overly entangled. However, the presence of high-severity anti-patterns such as God Classes, duplicate code, high coupling, and circular dependencies in critical files is a concern. These issues are likely contributing to the slow development velocity.", "recommendation": "A full rewrite is not justified given the relatively healthy metrics. Instead, focus on targeted, incremental improvements to address the identified anti-patterns. Refactoring the problematic components will improve development velocity without the risks associated with a full migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Classes in src/saas/service.py and src/saas/processor.py to break them into smaller, more cohesive classes.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Eliminate duplicate code in src/saas/processor.py by extracting common functionality into reusable methods or modules.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Resolve high coupling in src/saas/handler.py by decoupling its dependencies and introducing interfaces or abstractions.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Address circular dependencies in src/saas/service.py by restructuring dependencies or introducing a mediator pattern.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk lies in the complexity of refactoring critical components like God Classes and circular dependencies, which could temporarily slow down development further if not managed carefully. To mitigate this, ensure thorough testing and incremental deployments to avoid introducing regressions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0096", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet vise à optimiser les opérations de logistique et de supply chain pour une entreprise soumise à des exigences réglementaires strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). Avec une codebase mature de 4.7 ans construite autour de NestJS et PostgreSQL, l'équipe de 14 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) doit concilier conformité et évolution technologique.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales montrent une codebase dans un état relativement sain malgré quelques points d'attention. Le score de couplage moyen (5.1/10) et la complexité cyclomatique modérée (4.7) indiquent une architecture gérable, bien que certains modules présentent un couplage élevé. La couverture de tests (47.3%) est acceptable mais pourrait être améliorée, surtout dans un contexte réglementaire. Les anti-patterns détectés sont typiques d'une codebase mature mais nécessitent une attention ciblée, notamment sur les dépendances circulaires et la duplication de code.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Prioriser des améliorations incrémentales pour renforcer la conformité réglementaire et améliorer la maintenabilité. Les gains potentiels d'une migration ne justifient pas le coût et les risques associés à un rewrite dans ce contexte.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Identifier et isoler les modules critiques pour la conformité réglementaire. Renforcer leur couverture de tests et documenter les workflows spécifi ques.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorer les anti-patterns détectés (Duplicate Code, Circular Dependency) dans les modules les plus impactés, en particulier src/logistique/processor.py et src/logistique/service.py.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mettre en place une revue de code structurée pour améliorer la qualité globale et renforcer les bonnes pratiques, en impliquant particulièrement les juniors.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer l'impact des exigences réglementaires sur les évolutions futures. Une migration pourrait introduire des incohérences dans les workflows critiques et compromettre la conformité. Les phases proposées minimisent ce risque tout en améliorant la maintenabilité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0096", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 4.7-year-old supply chain logistics platform built with Node.js/NestJS and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 14 developers (mostly junior). The system faces increasing regulatory compliance demands (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS) while showing moderate technical debt in coupling, cohesion, and test coverage.", "analysis": "The codebase shows balanced coupling (5.1/10) and cohesion (5.5/10), with acceptable cyclomatic complexity (4.7). The 47.3% test coverage is below ideal but workable. Anti-patterns are localized (medium severity) and concentrated in core logistics modules. The bugfix ratio (0.31) in hot files suggests manageable maintenance overhead. Regulatory constraints are the primary driver, not systemic technical issues.", "recommendation": "DO NOT migrate or rewrite. Prioritize incremental improvements: 1) Targeted refactoring of anti-patterns in core modules, 2) Boost test coverage for compliance-critical paths, 3) Architectural guardrails for regulatory requirements. The metrics don't justify the risk of a full migration given the junior-heavy team.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor high-coupling and circular dependency issues in processor.py and handler.py", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement compliance-focused test suites for GDPR/PCI-DSS critical paths", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct architectural review for regulatory requirements (HDS readiness)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is regulatory non-compliance due to insufficient test coverage in critical paths. Secondary risk is knowledge transfer - junior-heavy team may struggle with complex refactoring without senior oversight. Anti-patterns are contained but could slow future compliance adaptations if unaddressed."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0097", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 5.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.46}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme médicale critique développée en Ruby on Rails depuis 7 ans, avec une équipe majoritairement junior. La stack historique montre des signes de fatigue architecturale, particulièrement sur les composants centraux, impactant la fiabilité en production.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une base de code moyennement couplée (4.8/10) avec des problèmes localisés mais sévères (dépendances circulaires high dans core.py). La couverture de tests sous les 50% et la complexité cyclomatique élevée (6.8) expliquent partiellement les incidents fréquents. Les anti-patterns sont concentrés sur quelques fichiers chauds (core.py, handler.py).", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des fichiers problématiques et l'amélioration des tests. La présence de 30 développeurs (dont 58% juniors) rendrait une migration risquée et coûteuse en productivité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer les dépendances circulaires dans src/sante/core.py avec des interfaces claires", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découper les Long Methods de handler.py et réduire les paramètres dans processor.py", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implémenter des tests d'intégration ciblés sur les composants refactorés pour atteindre 60%+ de couverture", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : perturbation des fonctionnalités existantes lors du refactoring de core.py. Mitigation : déployer les changements en canary et prévoir des rollbacks automatisés. Secondaire : résistance au changement chez les juniors. Mitigation : pair programming avec les 9% de seniors."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0097", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 5.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.46}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 7-year-old Ruby on Rails application in the medtech sector, serving critical healthcare functions with a team of 30 developers (mostly junior). While the codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion, production reliability issues and several structural anti-patterns in core components are impacting uptime.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate technical debt but no systemic failure justifying a full rewrite. Key issues are concentrated in core.py (duplicate code, circular dependencies) and handler.py (long methods). The 46% test coverage is below ideal for critical healthcare systems, and the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.46) in hot files confirms instability in key components.", "recommendation": "Targeted refactoring of core.py and handler.py, paired with test coverage improvement. Do not migrate the stack—the Rails foundation is stable enough for incremental fixes given the coupling/cohesion scores.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract duplicated logic in core.py into reusable modules, break circular dependencies using dependency injection", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor long methods in handler.py using strategy pattern, add integration tests for critical paths", "duration_days_range": "6-10"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement monitoring for the refactored components to validate stability gains", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is regression during core.py refactoring due to circular dependencies. Mitigation: phase the work, validate with contract tests before/after each change. Junior-heavy team may require pairing with seniors for complex refactors."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0098", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 36, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.9, "cohesion_score": 9.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 80.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de paiement fintech mature (5.9 ans) avec une base de code Python/Flask bien structurée. L'équipe de 36 développeurs (mix équilibré juniors/seniors) fait face à des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production malgré une base de code globalement saine.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont excellentes : couplage très faible (1.9/10), cohésion élevée (9.0/10), couverture de tests solide (80.7%) et complexité cyclomatique minimale (1.5). Le seul anti-pattern détecté (God Class low dans handler.py) est mineur. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.2) suggère une stabilité relative.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. La stack actuelle n'est pas le problème principal. Concentrer les efforts sur : 1) L'isolation du handler problématique 2) L'amélioration du monitoring production 3) La formation des juniors sur les spécificités temps-réel des paiements.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring ciblé du handler.py (découpage en services spécialisés + tests d'intégration renforcés)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de logging transactionnel amélioré avec métriques custom (latence 99e percentile, erreurs par sous-système)", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers techniques seniors/juniors sur les bonnes pratiques fintech (idempotence, timeouts, retry policies)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est organisationnel : sous-estimer l'impact des juniors (38%) sur la stabilité opérationnelle. Solution : pairing systématique sur les modifications critiques + rotation sur le run."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0098", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 36, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.9, "cohesion_score": 9.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 80.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5.9-year-old fintech/payment platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 36 developers (38% junior, 33% senior). The dominant constraint is reliability/uptime, as production incidents occur too frequently, despite otherwise healthy metrics.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits strong overall health, with low coupling (1.9/10), high cohesion (9.0/10), excellent test coverage (80.7%), and low cyclomatic complexity (1.5). The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is low (0.2), indicating stable code. The only significant anti-pattern detected is a low-level God Class in src/fintech/handler.py, which is a localized issue.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the codebase. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the reliability constraint and refine the localized God Class. Improving monitoring, logging, and incident response processes will likely yield greater reliability gains than a full migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/fintech/handler.py to improve modularity and reduce risks.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Enhance monitoring and logging mechanisms to identify and troubleshoot production incidents more effectively.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Review and optimize incident response processes, including documentation and team training.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is over-engineering the God Class refactor without clear boundaries. Additionally, inadequate monitoring and logging improvements may fail to reduce production incidents. However, the incremental approach minimizes risks compared to a full migration."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0100", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 39.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.32}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme edtech avec un historique de 10 ans, utilisant Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, soutenue par une équipe de 32 développeurs. Malgré une base de code mature, l'équipe rencontre des difficultés de recrutement sur cette stack technologique.", "analysis": "La base de code présente une santé technique globale correcte : couplage modéré (4.5/10), cohésion plutôt bonne (6.9/10) et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée (5.2). Cependant, certains aspects nécessitent attention : couverture de tests insuffisante (39.4%), présence d'anti-patterns critiques dans les fichiers principaux, et un ratio de commits correctifs élevé sur le fichier le plus problématique (0.32). La pénurie de talents, bien que préoccupante, ne justifie pas à elle seule une migration technologique.", "recommendation": "Nous recommandons de NE PAS migrer vers une nouvelle stack. Investissez plutôt dans : 1) Une amélioration progressive des patterns problématiques 2) Une augmentation de la couverture de tests 3) La mise en place d'un programme de mentoring interne pour compenser la pénurie de talents externes. Ces actions permettront de maintenir la valeur métier tout en rendant la codebase plus résiliente.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring ciblé des fichiers avec anti-patterns critiques (Long Parameter List et Duplicate Code)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Planification et mise en œuvre d'une campagne d'augmentation de la couverture de tests", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Création d'un programme de mentoring interne pour renforcer les compétences en Python/FastAPI", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque identifié est l'impact de la pénurie de talents sur la vitesse d'évolution de la plateforme. Cependant, une migration technologique représenterait un risque bien plus important : perte de savoir-faire accumulé, impact potentiel sur les fonctionnalités existantes, et période prolongée de double maintenance."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0100", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 39.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.32}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10-year-old edtech platform built with Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 32 developers with a mix of junior and senior talent. The primary operational constraint is difficulty in hiring developers proficient in the current stack, despite the codebase showing moderate coupling and cohesion with below-average test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 4.5/10, cohesion 6.9/10) and no critical structural flaws. While cyclomatic complexity is slightly elevated (5.2) and test coverage is suboptimal (39.4%), the main pain point appears to be talent availability rather than code quality. The detected anti-patterns (Long Parameter List, Duplicate Code) are localized and addressable.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics do not justify a full rewrite. Instead: 1) Address talent shortages through upskilling programs, 2) Run targeted refactoring sprints for the identified anti-patterns, 3) Improve test coverage incrementally. The existing architecture is salvageable with focused improvements.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor Long Parameter List in handler.py using parameter objects or context classes", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Eliminate duplicate code in service.py through strategic abstraction", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Launch test coverage initiative focusing on critical paths first", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk remains talent attrition due to stack unpopularity, not code quality. Mitigation: Pair junior developers with seniors for knowledge transfer, and consider introducing modern Python tooling (type hints, async) to make the stack more appealing to hires."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0101", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.5, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme marketplace mature (4.9 ans) construite avec Node.js/NestJS et PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe de 23 développeurs avec un bon mix d'expérience. La codebase montre des signes de dette technique modérée, avec des problèmes de couplage localisés et une couverture de tests insuffisante. La principale préoccupation actuelle est l'explosion des coûts cloud.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une dette technique gérable : couplage global bas (3.5/10), complexité raisonnable (5.3) mais avec des points chauds critiques (service.py, handler.py). La couverture de tests à 45% est insuffisante pour envisager une migration sécurisée. Les anti-patterns sont concentrés sur quelques fichiers plutôt que systémiques.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser : 1) L'optimisation cloud via une analyse fine des coûts (observability, requêtes coûteuses) 2) Le refactoring ciblé des points chauds identifiés 3) L'augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests. Une migration apporterait plus de risques que de bénéfices sur cette base.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud (metrics AWS/GCP, identification des services/resources surconsommateurs)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des fichiers problématiques (service.py, handler.py) avec création de tests unitaires ciblés", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de tests supplémentaires pour atteindre 60% de couverture sur les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principaux risques : 1) Sous-estimation de l'effort de refactoring sur les fichiers fortement couplés 2) Résistance au changement sur l'optimisation cloud sans preuves tangibles 3) Dégradation des perfs si les optimisations cloud sont mal ciblées. Recommandation : impliquer un SRE pour la phase 1 et pair-programmer sur les refactors complexes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0101", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.5, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 4.9-year-old marketplace platform built with Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 23 developers (25% junior, 35% senior). The primary operational challenge is escalating cloud costs, while the codebase shows moderate technical debt with some high-coupling and duplicate code issues in core marketplace modules.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 3.5/10, cohesion 6.1/10) and reasonable cyclomatic complexity (5.3), though test coverage is suboptimal (45.3%). Anti-patterns are concentrated in three files, suggesting localized rather than systemic issues. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.24) in the hottest file points to stable but occasionally problematic logic.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Prioritize targeted refactoring of the high-coupling and duplicate code hotspots, improve test coverage incrementally, and address cloud costs through architectural optimizations (e.g., query optimization, caching) rather than stack changes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/marketplace/service.py to break circular dependencies and reduce coupling, with parallel test coverage improvements for modified methods.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Split long methods in src/marketplace/handler.py and eliminate duplicate code in core.py, ensuring backward compatibility.", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit focusing on database queries and API call patterns from the refactored modules.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low implementation risk due to incremental changes. Cloud cost reductions may take longer to materialize as they depend on post-refactoring performance profiling. Junior-heavy team composition suggests pairing seniors with juniors during refactoring to mitigate knowledge gaps."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0102", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.4, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 85.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une application critique de traitement de paiements, développée en .NET avec une base de données SQL Server, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. Malgré une codebase mature de près de 8 ans, les métriques techniques indiquent une base saine mais l'équipe rencontre des difficultés à livrer rapidement de nouvelles fonctionnalités.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une architecture globalement saine : faible couplage (2.4/10), excellente cohésion (8.2/10), couverture de tests élevée (85.2%) et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée (2.5). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.02) confirment cette stabilité. Le problème principal semble être organisationnel/processus plutôt que technique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique. Optimiser la vélocité via : 1) Un renforcement des pratiques CI/CD, 2) Une refactorisation ciblée des 5% de code les moins cohésifs, 3) Un programme de mentorat junior/senior. La stack .NET Core est adaptée et stable.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des goulots d'étranglement dans le workflow de développement", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation incrémentale des modules identifiés comme faiblement cohésifs", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de pair programming guidé sur les composants critiques", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré lié à la courbe d'apprentissage des juniors. Mitigé par la stabilité technique avérée et l'absence de dette technique majeure. Une migration créerait plus de risques qu'elle n'en résoudrait."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0102", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.4, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 85.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "A mature fintech payment processing system built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, maintained by a large team predominantly composed of junior developers. While the codebase shows strong structural health with high cohesion and test coverage, the team struggles with development velocity despite the absence of significant technical debt.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate an exceptionally healthy codebase: low coupling (2.4/10), high cohesion (8.2/10), excellent test coverage (85.2%), and minimal complexity (avg. cyclomatic 2.5). The bugfix ratio (0.02) suggests stable core logic. The velocity constraint is unlikely to stem from code quality issues.", "recommendation": "DO NOT migrate or rewrite. The bottleneck is almost certainly organizational (e.g., junior-heavy team ramp-up, process overhead). Recommend targeted improvements: 1) Pair programming to accelerate junior development, 2) Lightweight architectural documentation for key flows, 3) CI/CD pipeline optimization.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct value-stream mapping to identify non-technical bottlenecks (e.g., requirements handoffs, QA delays)", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement mentoring rotations: 2 seniors paired with 5 juniors for high-priority features", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Document 3-5 critical payment flows as decision trees/sequence diagrams", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low technical risk given code health. Primary risk is misdiagnosing the velocity issue as technical rather than skill-distribution related. A rewrite would waste resources and likely degrade the current robust system."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0103", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.1, "cohesion_score": 9.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 74.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.11}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme IoT industrielle mature (12 ans) avec une base de code PHP/Laravel bien structurée, principalement utilisée pour le monitoring d'équipements industriels. L'équipe de 37 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, doit gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles liés aux alertes matérielles.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont globalement excellentes : couplage très faible (2.1/10), cohésion élevée (9.3/10), bonne couverture de tests (75%) et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée. Le seul anti-pattern détecté (duplication mineure) est anecdotique. La scalabilité semble être le seul vrai défi technique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Optimiser l'existant pour la scalabilité via : 1) Refactoring ciblé du handler IoT (fichier chaud), 2) Audit d'infrastructure, 3) Formation des juniors sur les patterns de scalabilité Laravel.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des goulots d'étranglement sous charge (benchmark JMeter + Blackfire)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring du handler IoT avec implémentation de cache Redis et queues asynchrones", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers pratiques sur Laravel Octane et l'optimisation de requêtes SQL", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré sur la phase 2 (refactoring) : nécessite une revue de code renforcée pour les juniors. Solution : pair-programming systématique avec les 5 seniors pendant cette phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0103", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.1, "cohesion_score": 9.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 74.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.11}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an industrial IoT platform built on an 11.8-year-old PHP/Laravel/MySQL stack, maintained by a team of 37 developers with a mix of junior and senior experience. The system handles unpredictable traffic spikes, with scalability being the primary constraint. Despite its age, the codebase exhibits strong cohesion and relatively low coupling.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase: low coupling (2.1/10), high cohesion (9.3/10), solid test coverage (74.9%), and low cyclomatic complexity (2.5). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.11) suggests stable core functionality. The only detected anti-pattern is minor duplicate code, which poses negligible risk. Given these metrics, a full rewrite or migration is unjustified.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted improvements to enhance scalability incrementally. Address the duplicate code and optimize the existing stack for traffic spikes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor duplicate code in src/iot/handler.py and add regression tests", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Profile the system under simulated load to identify scalability bottlenecks", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement caching strategies and database optimizations based on profiling results", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low risk. The codebase is stable, and incremental improvements pose minimal disruption. The primary risk lies in underestimating traffic patterns during scalability testing—ensure realistic load simulations."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0104", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.0, "cohesion_score": 5.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 40.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "La plateforme edtech, développée avec Python/Django/PostgreSQL depuis près de 5 ans, est maintenue par une équipe de 30 développeurs, dont une proportion notable de juniors. Bien qu'aucune contrainte critique n'ait été identifiée, certaines zones du code présentent des défauts de conception.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales montrent une situation assez stable : un couplage modéré, une cohésion acceptable et une complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée. La couverture de tests, bien qu'impropriée, n'est pas catastrophique. Deux anti-patterns majeurs ont été détectés, mais ils sont localisés dans des fichiers spécifiques. Le ratio de commits correctifs pour le fichier le plus chaud est relativement bas, ce qui suggère une maintenance gérable. Il n'y a pas de signaux forts justifiant une migration technologique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle, mais procéder à des refactoring ciblés sur les fichiers problématiques. Améliorer la couverture des tests pour atteindre au moins 70%. Former les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques de conception pour renforcer la qualité du code.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des Long Methods dans src/edtech/service.py et résolution des Circular Dependencies dans src/edtech/processor.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests, en commençant par les modules critiques et en impliquant les juniors.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'une revue de code rigoureuse et sessions de formation orientées design patterns pour l'équipe.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la propagation d'anti-patterns si les refactorings ne sont pas effectués rapidement et si la formation n'est pas suffisamment appliquée. Une attention particulière doit être portée à la montée en compétence des juniors pour éviter une dégradation progressive de la qualité du code."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0104", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.0, "cohesion_score": 5.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 40.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature edtech platform built with Python, Django, and PostgreSQL, serving educational institutions for nearly 5 years. With a team of 30 developers (over a third senior), the codebase shows moderate technical debt but no critical constraints. Key pain points include some architectural anti-patterns and below-ideal test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt: coupling and cohesion scores are mid-range (6.0 and 5.3 respectively), cyclomatic complexity is slightly elevated but not alarming (6.5), and test coverage is suboptimal but not catastrophic (40.5%). The bugfix ratio (0.33) in the hottest file suggests moderate instability. The detected anti-patterns (Long Method and Circular Dependency) are localized rather than systemic.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate or rewrite. The metrics don't justify the risk. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. The team composition (36% seniors) is well-suited for this approach.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the Long Method in src/edtech/service.py using extract method pattern, with corresponding test coverage improvements", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break the Circular Dependency in src/edtech/processor.py by introducing an interface or event-based communication", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement a 3-month test coverage improvement initiative (tracked via CI), prioritizing business-critical paths", "duration_days_range": "Ongoing (tracked quarterly)"}], "risk_assessment": "Low risk for phased improvements. The main risk is scope creep during anti-pattern refactoring - mitigate by clearly bounding each phase. The team's seniority distribution reduces execution risk."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0106", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 6.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.34}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme e-commerce mature (5+ ans) avec une stack Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior. La codebase présente des problèmes de fiabilité en production, avec un uptime insuffisant malgré une complexité modérée.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales montrent une codebase modérément saine (cohésion correcte, complexité raisonnable) mais avec des points critiques : couplage élevé (3.0/10), couverture de tests insuffisante (52%) et plusieurs anti-patterns concentrés dans des composants clés. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.34) indique une instabilité localisée plutôt qu'un problème systémique.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser des refactoring ciblés sur les composants problématiques identifiés, améliorer la couverture de tests autour de ces zones, et renforcer les pratiques de revue de code pour l'équipe junior. Une migration apporterait plus de risques que de bénéfices dans ce contexte.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns (God Class, Long Parameter List) dans les fichiers processor.py et service.py, avec revue de conception par un senior", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests (+20% sur les composants refactorés) et mise en place de tests d'intégration critiques", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers de pairing seniors/juniors sur les bonnes pratiques Spring Boot et gestion de la complexité", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré : les refactoring ciblés peuvent introduire des régressions temporaires. Mitigation via tests accrus et déploiements progressifs. L'équipe junior nécessitera un encadrement renforcé pendant les phases de refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0106", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 6.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.34}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL-based e-commerce platform that has been in development for over five years. With a relatively mature codebase, the team of 26 developers (comprising 68% juniors and 20% seniors) is currently grappling with frequent production incidents, highlighting a critical need for improved reliability and uptime.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with a low coupling score (3.0/10) and moderate cohesion (6.3/10), which suggests a reasonably structured design. However, the test coverage at 52% is suboptimal, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 6.2 indicates room for simplification. Specific anti-patterns, such as God Class and High Coupling in key modules, are contributing to maintenance challenges and reliability issues.", "recommendation": "Given the overall health of the codebase metrics, a full rewrite or migration is not justified. Instead, targeted incremental improvements should be prioritized to address anti-patterns and enhance reliability. Focus should be on improving test coverage, refactoring high coupling modules, and simplifying complex code paths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/e-commerce/processor.py to reduce its responsibilities and improve modularity.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Reduce High Coupling in src/e-commerce/service.py by introducing interfaces or dependency injection.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address Long Parameter Lists in src/e-commerce/handler.py and src/e-commerce/service.py by encapsulating parameters into objects.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 70% by writing additional unit and integration tests for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks include potential regression issues during refactoring and the challenge of maintaining uptime while making these changes. Mitigation strategies include rigorous testing, phased rollouts, and monitoring production closely during and after changes. The team’s high proportion of junior developers may also slow down the implementation, necessitating additional senior oversight and mentoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0107", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.3, "cohesion_score": 8.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 89.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Application critique de gestion logistique avec une base de code mature (14 ans), construite sur Python/Django/PostgreSQL. L'équipe expérimentée maintient une codebase de haute qualité mais doit faire face à des pics de trafic imprévisibles liés aux fluctuations de la supply chain.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques sont exceptionnellement saines : couplage très faible (1.3/10), cohésion élevée (8.4/10), couverture de tests proche de 90% et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds indiquent une architecture robuste.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique actuelle. La scalabilité doit être traitée par des optimisations ciblées : amélioration des requêtes PostgreSQL, mise en cache stratégique et scaling horizontal des workers asynchrones. La solidité de la base justifie une approche incrémentale.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des goulots d'étranglement sous charge (profiling des requêtes, analyse des temps de réponse)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Optimisation des 5-10 requêtes PostgreSQL les plus coûteuses identifiées", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un cache Redis pour les données de référence fréquemment accédées", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer la capacité de scaling vertical/horizontal de l'actuelle stack. Une migration prématurée introduirait des risques opérationnels majeurs sans bénéfice démontré. Les optimisations proposées présentent un rapport risque/benefice favorable."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0107", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.3, "cohesion_score": 8.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 89.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature supply chain management system built on Python/Django with PostgreSQL, serving logistics operations for 14 years. With a team of 32 developers (mix of juniors and seniors), the system handles unpredictable traffic spikes while maintaining high code quality metrics.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits excellent structural health with low coupling (1.3/10), high cohesion (8.4/10), and strong test coverage (89.8%). Cyclomatic complexity is very low (2.3), indicating simple control flows, and the minimal bugfix ratio (0.2) on critical files suggests stability. No architectural anti-patterns were detected.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics demonstrate an exceptionally well-maintained codebase. Instead, focus on targeted scalability enhancements for the identified traffic spike constraints while preserving the existing architecture's strengths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct load testing to identify specific bottlenecks during traffic spikes, instrumenting key transaction paths", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement horizontal scaling improvements (caching layer optimization, read replica configuration for PostgreSQL)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Develop autoscaling playbooks for the operations team based on phase 1 findings", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk lies in over-engineering scalability solutions for a system that already demonstrates strong fundamentals. Any changes should be data-driven from the load testing phase to avoid unnecessary complexity."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0108", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.8, "cohesion_score": 7.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 71.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.14}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Application médicale critique en Python/FastAPI, vieille de près de 6 ans, avec une équipe majoritairement junior. Malgré une base de code globalement saine, l'équipe lutte contre des incidents de production récurrents qui impactent la fiabilité du système.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs techniques solides : faible couplage (2.8/10), bonne cohésion (7.5/10), couverture de tests correcte (71.9%) et complexité maîtrisée. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et un ratio de correctifs modéré (0.14) suggèrent que les problèmes de fiabilité ne proviennent pas d'une dette technique massive.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Cibler d'abord les améliorations incrémentales sur la fiabilité opérationnelle : renforcement des tests non-fonctionnels, instrumentation des incidents et mentorat des juniors sur les bonnes pratiques de production.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des 5 derniers incidents majeurs pour identifier les patterns récurrents (ex: timeout DB, erreurs de sérialisation)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémenter des tests de charge/scénarios d'échec sur les composants critiques identifiés", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers pratiques seniors/juniors sur le debugging en production et le monitoring avancé", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est de sous-estimer les lacunes opérationnelles de l'équipe plutôt que techniques. Une migration créerait une instabilité supplémentaire sans résoudre le cœur du problème."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0108", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.8, "cohesion_score": 7.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 71.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.14}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5.9-year-old medtech platform built with Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 26 developers (42% junior, 10% senior). The primary challenge is improving reliability and reducing production incidents, despite the codebase showing good structural health with low coupling, high cohesion, and solid test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a fundamentally healthy codebase: coupling is low (2.8/10), cohesion is high (7.5/10), test coverage is adequate (71.9%), and cyclomatic complexity is excellent (1.9). The bugfix-commit ratio (0.14) suggests stable hot files, and no significant anti-patterns were detected. The uptime issues likely stem from operational or architectural factors rather than code quality.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted reliability improvements: enhance monitoring, refine deployment processes, and address architectural bottlenecks. The code quality metrics do not justify the risk of a full migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a reliability deep-dive: analyze production incident patterns, review monitoring gaps, and identify high-risk workflows.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement incremental fixes: strengthen error handling in critical paths, add targeted integration tests for failure scenarios, and improve logging.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize deployment pipeline: automate rollback procedures, add canary testing, and refine health checks.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risks are operational (e.g., undetected edge cases in production) rather than codebase quality. A rewrite would introduce unnecessary instability and divert resources from solving the actual uptime constraints. Incremental improvements align better with the team's composition (many juniors needing mentorship)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0109", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.0, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 60.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme de streaming média mature (9+ ans) avec une stack Python/Flask/PostgreSQL bien établie. L'équipe de 33 développeurs maintient une codebase globalement saine mais doit adresser des coûts cloud croissants, probablement liés à des inefficacités d'infrastructure plutôt qu'à des problèmes structurels du code.", "analysis": "Les métriques techniques indiquent une architecture solide : couplage très faible (2.0/10), cohésion excellente (8.3/10), complexité cyclomatique idéale (2.0) et une couverture de tests correcte (60.2%). Le seul anti-pattern détecté (dépendance circulaire mineure) est trivial à corriger. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.02) suggère une stabilité exceptionnelle pour un projet de cet âge.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique. La solution optimale consiste à : 1) Auditer l'infrastructure cloud pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement, 2) Optimiser les requêtes PostgreSQL et le caching, 3) Corriger la dépendance circulaire mineure. Une migration apporterait un risque élevé pour un bénéfice incertain.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé de l'infrastructure cloud (coûts/performance) et profiling des requêtes PostgreSQL critiques", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring ciblé : élimination de la dépendance circulaire + optimisation des 3-5 endpoints les plus coûteux identifiés en phase 1", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Déploiement d'un système de caching stratégique (Redis/Memcached) pour les assets média statiques", "duration_days_range": "6-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque technique faible (les phases proposées sont incrémentales et réversibles). Principal risque organisationnel : dispersion des efforts si l'équipe tente de tout optimiser simultanément plutôt que de se concentrer sur les points critiques identifiés par l'audit."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0109", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.0, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 60.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature media streaming platform built on Python/Flask with PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 33 developers with balanced seniority. While the codebase shows strong structural health with low coupling and high cohesion, the team's primary pain point is escalating cloud costs that need optimization.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a fundamentally healthy codebase: coupling is exceptionally low (2.0/10), cohesion is high (8.3/10), and cyclomatic complexity is ideal (2.0). Test coverage at 60.2% is acceptable but could be improved. The only notable anti-pattern is a minor circular dependency, which poses negligible risk. The low bugfix-commit ratio (0.02) in critical files suggests stable core functionality.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. The cloud cost issue is orthogonal to code quality — address it through infrastructure optimization (e.g., query analysis, caching strategies, scaling adjustments). Invest in targeted improvements: eliminate the circular dependency and boost test coverage for high-impact modules.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit: profile database queries, analyze API response caching opportunities, and review autoscaling configurations.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the circular dependency in src/media/service.py by introducing an interface or mediator pattern.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage by 15% through targeted unit tests for core business logic modules (prioritize payment and media delivery services).", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Minimal technical risk given the codebase's health. The primary risk is misallocating resources toward a rewrite instead of cloud optimization. The circular dependency, while minor, could complicate future service.py modifications if left unaddressed."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0110", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.9, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme gaming vieillissante (5.8 ans) basée sur Python/Flask, avec des enjeux critiques de conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). L'équipe de 9 développeurs (dont 45% de seniors) maintient une codebase présentant des problèmes localisés de couplage et des anti-patterns dans les composants critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase montre une dette technique modérée mais concentrée : le score de couplage bas (3.9/10) et la complexité cyclomatique acceptable (6.6) indiquent une structure globalement saine. Les anti-patterns identifiés (God Class, Circular Dependency) dans des fichiers clés expliquent le ratio élevé de correctifs (0.39) sur ces composants. La couverture de tests (54.4%) est insuffisante pour les exigences réglementaires.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser un refactoring ciblé des anti-patterns critiques avec une montée en puissance des tests. La stack actuelle reste adaptée si ces corrections sont implémentées.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer la Circular Dependency (src/gaming/service.py) en introduisant des interfaces, avec tests d'intégration associés", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Découpler la God Class (src/gaming/core.py) via le pattern Strategy, en parallèle d'une campagne de tests unitaires sur les nouvelles classes", "duration_days_range": "10-14 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit RGPA/PCI-DSS des handlers à fort couplage (src/gaming/handler.py) et implémentation des contrôles manquants", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principal risque : la dette technique localisée pourrait ralentir les adaptations réglementaires futures. Le refactoring proposé réduit ce risque sans introduire de rupture majeure. Attention à maintenir la compatibilité des APIs pendant les phases 1 et 2."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0110", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.9, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 5.8-year-old gaming platform built with Python/Flask/PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 9 developers (mix of junior and senior). The primary challenge is ensuring compliance with regulatory standards (GDPR, PCI-DSS, HDS) while maintaining system stability. The codebase shows moderate technical debt, with some high-risk anti-patterns in core components.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt—coupling is low (3.9/10), cohesion is average (5.1/10), and test coverage is borderline acceptable (54.4%). However, the cyclomatic complexity (6.6) and bugfix ratio (0.39) on critical files suggest localized instability. The detected anti-patterns (God Class, High Coupling, Circular Dependency) are concerning but confined to specific modules, not systemic.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate or rewrite. Prioritize targeted refactoring of high-risk modules (core.py, handler.py, service.py) to address anti-patterns and improve compliance readiness. Incremental improvements will yield better ROI than a disruptive migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in service.py (highest risk), add integration tests for compliance-critical paths", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break up God Class in core.py into domain-specific services, enforce interface segregation", "duration_days_range": "10-14 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Decouple handler.py from downstream dependencies, improve test coverage to 65%+ for modified modules", "duration_days_range": "6-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Highest risk is regulatory non-compliance due to tangled core logic. Refactoring phases are sequenced by impact: circular dependencies first (stability), then God Class (maintainability), then coupling (scalability). Parallel work on compliance documentation is advised."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0111", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.8, "cohesion_score": 9.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 69.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.06}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une marketplace mature avec une forte exigence de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). La codebase .NET/ASP.NET Core, bien établie depuis 9 ans, présente une architecture solide et une bonne qualité de code malgré sa longévité. L'équipe de 9 développeurs, avec un bon équilibre juniors/seniors, maintient activement le projet.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une codebase en très bonne santé : couplage extrêmement faible (1.8/10), cohésion exceptionnelle (9.9/10), complexité cyclomatique très basse (1.4) et couverture de tests correcte (69.4%). L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de correctifs sur les fichiers chauds (0.06) confirment cette stabilité. La contrainte dominante étant réglementaire, la stabilité de l'architecture actuelle est un atout.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack technique. La solution optimale est d'améliorer progressivement la couverture de tests et de renforcer les garde-fous réglementaires. Une migration introduirait des risques inutiles pour un bénéfice non démontré.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit réglementaire ciblé avec un expert compliance pour identifier les éventuels gaps dans l'implémentation actuelle des normes", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Atelier d'architecture avec l'équipe pour définir une stratégie d'amélioration incrémentale de la couverture de tests (objectif 80%)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place de checklists réglementaires dans le pipeline CI/CD et formation des juniors sur les aspects compliance", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque serait de perturber une codebase stable et bien architecturée par des changements non nécessaires. Une migration créerait des délais de mise en conformité et des risques réglementaires. La faible complexité et le bon découpage permettent des évolutions sûres sans rewrite."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0111", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.8, "cohesion_score": 9.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 69.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.06}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature marketplace platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, serving customers for nearly a decade. With a balanced team of junior and senior developers, the primary challenge is maintaining compliance with strict regulations like GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS while evolving the platform.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits excellent structural health with low coupling (1.8/10), near-perfect cohesion (9.9/10), and manageable cyclomatic complexity (1.4). Test coverage at 69.4% is respectable, and the minimal bugfix ratio (0.06) on high-traffic files suggests stability. No significant anti-patterns were detected.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. The metrics indicate a well-maintained codebase. Focus should be on incremental improvements to bolster compliance capabilities and test coverage rather than disruptive changes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a compliance audit to identify gaps in GDPR/PCI-DSS/HDS coverage, prioritizing high-risk areas.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Enhance test coverage for compliance-critical modules (e.g., payment processing, data storage) to reach 80%+ in targeted areas.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement automated compliance checks in CI/CD pipelines for regulatory requirements.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The main risk is regulatory non-compliance due to legacy code paths, not technical debt. Mitigation: phase 1's audit will surface concrete action items. Secondary risk: over-indexing on test coverage at the expense of compliance work—balance via phased approach."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0113", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.2, "cohesion_score": 5.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Il s'agit d'une plateforme de paiement en temps réel critique, développée en Python/Django avec une base PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 43 développeurs (majoritairement juniors) maintient cette codebase vieille de 6.6 ans, qui présente des problèmes localisés de duplication de code mais une complexité globale maîtrisée.", "analysis": "Les métriques montrent une base globalement saine : complexité cyclomatique basse (4.5), couplage modéré (4.2/10) et cohésion acceptable (5.9/10). La couverture de tests (46.1%) est insuffisante pour les modules critiques. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont localisés (2 fichiers avec duplication) et ne justifient pas un refactoring complet. La contrainte de latence pourrait être adressée par des optimisations ciblées.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer. Prioriser : 1) l'augmentation de la couverture de tests sur les modules temps-réel, 2) le refactoring local des fichiers problématiques, 3) l'ajout de monitoring fin des performances. Former les juniors sur les patterns de basse latence en Python.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoring des fichiers src/fintech/service.py et handler.py pour éliminer la duplication", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de tests unitaires/adds pour porter la couverture à 70% sur les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ateliers techniques sur l'optimisation Python/Django pour la latence (seniors -> juniors)", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la dette technique localisée dans les fichiers dupliqués, qui pourrait ralentir les évolutions futures. La faible couverture de tests sur des modules critiques expose à des régressions en production. La proportion élevée de juniors nécessite un mentoring renforcé sur les enjeux temps-réel."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0113", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.2, "cohesion_score": 5.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A fintech payment processing system built on Python/Django with PostgreSQL, serving real-time transaction needs with a predominantly junior developer team. The 6.6-year-old codebase shows moderate technical debt, particularly in code duplication and test coverage gaps, while maintaining acceptable coupling and complexity levels.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 4.2/10, cohesion 5.9/10) and reasonable complexity (cyclomatic 4.5), though test coverage at 46.1% is suboptimal for fintech. The high duplicate code in handler.py and medium duplication in service.py are clear pain points. The junior-heavy team composition suggests solutions should prioritize simplicity over architectural elegance.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Execute targeted refactoring on duplicate code hotspots while improving test coverage. The metrics don't justify a full rewrite - the system's core architecture appears fundamentally sound for the real-time payment needs.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor high-duplication areas in handler.py with extracted utility methods, adding missing unit tests", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address medium duplication in service.py through strategy pattern implementation where applicable", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement test coverage improvement sprint focusing on payment validation and core transaction paths", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is junior developers introducing new anti-patterns during refactoring. Mitigation: pair senior developers with juniors during critical refactors. Secondary risk: temporary velocity drop during test coverage improvement phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0114", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.3, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace opérationnelle depuis près de 2 ans, construite avec Python/Flask et PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 18 développeurs rencontre des problèmes récurrents de fiabilité en production, avec un uptime insuffisant malgré une base de code relativement jeune.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une base de code modérément saine (complexité cyclomatique acceptable) mais avec des faiblesses structurelles : couplage élevé dans certains modules, couverture de tests insuffisante et présence d'anti-patterns critiques dans des fichiers centraux. Le ratio de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud indique une instabilité localisée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack. Prioriser le refactoring ciblé des points critiques identifiés et l'amélioration de la couverture de tests. La jeunesse de la codebase et l'absence de problème majeur de maintenabilité justifient une approche incrémentale.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Isoler et refactorer progressivement la God Class dans core.py en appliquant le pattern Facade", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Éliminer les dépendances circulaires dans core.py par injection de dépendances", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests sur handler.py et les modules adjacents (objectif +20%)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Principaux risques : regression lors du refactoring de core.py (impact large) et résistance au changement sur les pratiques de test. Recommander des revues de code poussées et un déploiement en canary pour les modifications structurelles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0114", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.3, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a Python/Flask marketplace platform that has been in development for nearly two years, with a team of 18 developers (mix of junior and senior). While the codebase shows moderate coupling and cohesion, the team's primary concern is production reliability, with frequent uptime incidents impacting operations.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with manageable technical debt (coupling 4.3/10, cohesion 5.4/10) but suboptimal test coverage (48.3%) and localized complexity hotspots. The presence of a God Class and circular dependencies in core.py, along with high coupling in handler.py, suggests design flaws in critical paths. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.42) on the hottest file confirms instability in a key component. However, the overall architecture is not fundamentally broken—these are addressable issues.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, execute targeted refactoring of the problematic modules while improving test coverage. The God Class and circular dependencies must be resolved first, as they likely contribute to the reliability issues. This approach minimizes risk while addressing the team's uptime concerns.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Extract functionality from core.py's God Class into domain-specific services, breaking circular dependencies. Write integration tests for extracted components.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor handler.py to reduce coupling via interface segregation or event-based communication. Expand unit test coverage to 65%+ for this module.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement monitoring for the refactored components to validate reliability improvements. Conduct team knowledge transfer on the new patterns.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Primary risk is regression during core.py refactoring due to its central role. Mitigation: phase the extraction, maintain feature flags for new paths, and parallel-run old/new implementations where feasible. Secondary risk is junior developers struggling with design patterns—address via paired programming during critical phases."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0115", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.7, "cohesion_score": 2.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 11.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.75}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 5.4-year-old B2B SaaS platform for business management built on Node.js, Express, and MongoDB. The project is managed by a team of 20 developers, where a high proportion of junior staff is struggling with a codebase that has become a bottleneck for feature delivery speed.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a system in a state of significant structural decay. A coupling score of 7.7/10 combined with a cohesion score of 2.6/10 reveals a 'Big Ball of Mud' architecture where components are overly interdependent and lack a single responsibility. The cyclomatic complexity (11.9) is dangerously high, and a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.75 on hot files suggests that nearly every change introduces a new regression. The presence of God Classes and circular dependencies in the core service and handler layers explains the team's low velocity: developers cannot change one part of the system without impacting unrelated areas. With only 11.6% test coverage, there is no safety net to perform large-scale refactoring without significant risk of breakage.", "recommendation": "A full rewrite is not recommended as it would likely fail given the current lack of domain documentation and test coverage. However, the current state is unsustainable. I recommend a 'Strangler Fig' approach: stabilize the core through an incremental refactoring of the most volatile components (handler.py and service.py) while introducing a strict testing mandate for all new features. The goal is to decouple the God Classes into smaller, cohesive services over time rather than a high-risk migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement a 'Safety Net' phase: establish integration tests for the most critical paths in src/saas/service.py and src/saas/handler.py to prevent regressions during refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "15-25 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the God Classes: split the service and handler layers into smaller, domain-specific modules, resolving circular dependencies and reducing parameter list lengths.", "duration_days_range": "30-45 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Complexity reduction: target the files with the highest bugfix-commit ratios to simplify logic and reduce cyclomatic complexity through systematic extraction of long methods.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish architectural guardrails: implement static analysis checks (linting/complexity thresholds) in the CI pipeline to prevent the re-introduction of high coupling and God Classes.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is the low test coverage; refactoring God Classes without a comprehensive suite can lead to production outages. Additionally, with only 8% senior staff, there is a risk that junior developers may misinterpret the refactoring patterns, potentially creating new anti-patterns. This must be mitigated by strict peer reviews led by the senior architects."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0117", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 40, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.21}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme SaaS de gestion de données de santé vieille de 11 ans, bâtie sur Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL, opérant sous contraintes réglementaires strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). L'équipe de 40 développeurs, fortement composée de profils juniors (73%), maintient un codebase présentant des zones critiques de couplage et de complexité dans le module cœur « sante ».", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une situation contrastée : le couplage (4.6/10) et la complexité cyclomatique (6.8) restent maîtrisables, mais la couverture de tests à 34,5% est insuffisante pour un environnement réglementé. Les anti-patterns détectés — une dépendance circulaire haute et deux God Classes (dont une haute) concentrées dans src/sante/ — indiquent une dette technique localisée mais sévère sur le domaine métier le plus sensible. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.21) confirme une instabilité sur ces fichiers. L'équipe junior majoritaire rend toute refactorisation d'ampleur risquée sans filet de tests solide et encadrement senior fort.", "recommendation": "NE PAS engager de réécriture ou migration globale. Le codebase ne justifie pas un rewrite : l'architecture globale tient, la dette est circonscrite. Priorité absolue : monter la couverture de tests à >80% sur le module sante/ avant toute refactorisation, puis traiter les anti-patterns par étapes incrémentales (briser la dépendance circulaire, extraire les responsabilités des God Classes). Paralléliser un programme de mentoring et de documentation d'architecture pour monter les juniors en compétence sur le cœur métier.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Campagne de tests de caractérisation (characterization tests) sur src/sante/ : couvrir les chemins critiques existants sans modifier le code, viser 80%+ de couverture sur processor.py, service.py, core.py.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Résolution de la dépendance circulaire haute dans core.py : identifier le cycle, introduire une abstraction (interface/event bus) ou extraire un module partagé pour casser le couplage bidirectionnel.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactorisation de la God Class processor.py (high) : extraire les responsabilités distinctes (validation, transformation, persistance, notification) en services dédiés, guidés par les tests de la phase 1.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Refactorisation de la God Class service.py (medium) : même approche, en priorisant les chemins les plus modifiés (historique git).", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Mise en place de garde-fous : règles ESLint/ArchUnit pour interdire les dépendances circulaires et limiter la taille des classes, intégration dans le CI, ateliers de revues d'architecture bi-hebdomadaires avec les seniors.", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque majeur : l'équipe junior (73%) manque d'expérience pour refactoriser sans casser la conformité réglementaire. La faible couverture de tests actuelle (34.5%) ne file pas de filet de sécurité. Toute modification sur le module sante/ sans tests de caractérisation préalables expose à des régressions silencieuses sur des données de santé — inacceptable sous HDS/RGPD. La dépendance circulaire et les God Classes sont des bombes à retardement : elles complexifient l'onboarding, augmentent le temps de correction (ratio 0.21), et bloquent l'évolution du domaine. Mitigation : phases 1 et 5 sont non négociables et doivent précéder les phases 2-4. Impliquer les 11% de seniors comme « tech leads » dédiés sur ce module, avec revues de code systématiques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0117", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 40, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.21}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A healthcare platform built 11.1 years ago with Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL serving a 40-developer team (73% junior, 11% senior) faces regulatory compliance pressures under RGPD, PCI-DSS, and HDS requirements while struggling with code quality issues including circular dependencies, god classes, and low test coverage at 34.5%.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits concerning technical debt patterns that significantly impact maintainability and regulatory compliance readiness. With a coupling score of 4.6/10 and cohesion at 6.4/10, the architecture suffers from structural weaknesses that complicate audit trails and security assessments. The high cyclomatic complexity (6.8) combined with circular dependencies in core.py and god classes in processor.py and service.py creates a maintenance burden that is particularly problematic for a regulated healthcare environment. The 34.5% test coverage is dangerously low for PCI-DSS requirements, and the 0.21 bugfix ratio on the hottest file indicates an anti-pattern of constant firefighting. Given the team composition with majority junior developers, these issues compound onboarding challenges and increase the risk of compliance violations.", "recommendation": "Do not proceed with a full rewrite. The existing 11.1-year-old codebase, while imperfect, has proven operational value. Instead, implement targeted, prioritized refactoring focused on regulatory compliance hotspots. Begin with the circular dependency in core.py and god classes that directly impact auditability, while simultaneously establishing a compliance-focused testing strategy. This incremental approach reduces risk while building team capability and maintaining operational continuity in the regulated healthcare domain.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Immediate compliance stabilization: Resolve circular dependency in core.py, extract god class responsibilities in processor.py into cohesive modules, establish compliance test framework with 60% coverage target on regulated paths", "duration_days_range": "45-60 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Architectural refactoring: Address high coupling in processor.py, decompose service.py god class, implement modular boundaries with clear regulatory domain separation, achieve 50% overall test coverage", "duration_days_range": "60-75 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Team capability building and compliance hardening: Pair junior developers with seniors on refactored modules, implement PCI-DSS audit logging patterns, establish automated compliance checks in CI/CD pipeline", "duration_days_range": "30-45 days"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of non-compliance without intervention. Current test coverage (34.5%) fails PCI-DSS requirements. Circular dependencies and god classes create single points of failure for regulatory changes. Junior-heavy team (73%) increases likelihood of introducing bugs during urgent compliance fixes. Proceeding with targeted refactoring carries moderate risk but significantly reduces compliance risk compared to status quo or full rewrite. Success depends on strong architectural governance and regulatory domain expert involvement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0118", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 17, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.7, "cohesion_score": 9.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 62.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.03}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Projet SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise avec une codebase de 10.7 ans en PHP/Laravel/MySQL. L'équipe de 17 développeurs (majorité juniors) gère un système malgré des coûts cloud en croissance exponentielle. La base de code montre une modularité élevée avec une excellente cohésion.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent un code base bien architecturé avec un faible couplage (1.7/10) et une excellente cohésion (9.9/10). La couverture de tests à 62.5% est suffisante pour des changements ciblés. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 1.3 est faible, et le taux de commits correctifs sur le fichier critique (0.03) montre une stabilité relative. L'anti-pattern God Class détecté est faible et localisé dans un fichier Python, hors du cœur du système Laravel.", "recommendation": "NE PAS migrer la stack technique. Les métriques montrent une base de code saine, bien testée et maintenable. La contrainte de coût cloud devrait être traitée par une optimisation infrastructurelle (réduction des ressources sous-utilisées, mise en cache, requêtes optimisées) plutôt que par une migration coûteuse. Une refonte progressive ciblant les goulots d'étranglement performants est plus judicieuse.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit des coûts cloud détaillé avec identification des ressources sous-utilisées et analyse des requêtes SQL coûteuses", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implémentation de cache applicatif et base de données pour réduire la charge serveur", "duration_days_range": "14-21"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring sélectif du God Class low impact et optimisation des endpoints les plus coûteux", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible risque global. La base de code bien testée permet des changements incrémentaux sûrs. Le principal risque réside dans l'impact potentiel d'une optimisation qui pourrait nécessiter des ajustements de configuration plutôt que de modifications de code."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0119", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.5, "cohesion_score": 7.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 66.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme de streaming de contenus sportifs en direct, opérant en France et soumise aux exigences RGPD, PCI‑DSS et à la norme HDS.", "analysis": "Le code possède un couplage très faible (1,5/10), une cohésion élevée (7,2/10) et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne (3,3), indiquant une architecture saine. La couverture de tests (66,1 %) est acceptable mais peut être renforcée, tandis que le ratio de commits correctifs (0,12) montre peu d’incidents critiques. Aucun anti‑pattern n’a été détecté, ce qui reflète une base de code maîtrisée malgré une main‑d’œuvre majoritairement junior.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration vers une nouvelle stack n’est justifiée ; il faut privilégier des améliorations incrémentales ciblées (refactorisation de modules à forte complexité, augmentation de la couverture de tests et formation des développeurs juniors).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Élaborer et lancer un plan de refactorisation ciblée et de renforcement de la couverture de tests sur les modules identifiés", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est une éventuelle régression pendant les refactorisations, mitigeable par des revues de code et des tests unitaires supplémentaires. Aucun risque technologique majeur n’est présent."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0119", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 23, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.5, "cohesion_score": 7.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 66.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform operating in a regulated environment (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) with a team of 23 developers (60% junior, 25% senior). The backend is built in Python with FastAPI and PostgreSQL, serving as the core system for content delivery and user management under strict compliance requirements.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy structural metrics: low coupling (1.5/10) and moderate cohesion (7.2/10) indicate a well-modularized system with clear boundaries. Test coverage at 66.1% is acceptable but leaves room for improvement, particularly in critical compliance-related paths. Cyclomatic complexity (3.3) is low, suggesting maintainable logic. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.12) on the hottest file is healthy, indicating stability in the most active areas. No significant anti-patterns were detected, and the team’s junior-heavy composition suggests incremental improvements would be more effective than a disruptive rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to enhance test coverage, reduce complexity in hotspots, and strengthen compliance-related validation paths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage to ≥80% by adding targeted unit and integration tests, prioritizing compliance-critical modules (e.g., authentication, data retention logic).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the hottest file to reduce cyclomatic complexity further and improve maintainability, ensuring changes are validated by expanded test coverage.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce automated compliance checks (e.g., static analysis for RGPD data handling, PCI-DSS validation) into the CI pipeline to enforce regulatory requirements proactively.", "duration_days_range": "10-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The healthy structural metrics and lack of anti-patterns minimize risk. The primary risks stem from potential regression during test expansion and refactoring, but these are mitigated by the existing low coupling and high cohesion. Compliance risks are addressed by prioritizing regulatory validation in the CI pipeline."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0120", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 43.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce, en production depuis 5.7 ans avec une stack Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL, supporte une équipe de 29 développeurs (majoritairement seniors) et traite des volumes transactionnels standards pour le secteur. L'application, bien que fonctionnelle, montre des signes de dégradation structurelle progressive dans certains modules critiques, notamment autour des services de gestion des commandes et du cœur métier.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase globalement saine mais avec des points de tension localisés qui nécessitent une attention immédiate. Le couplage (5.3/10) et la cohésion (5.4/10) sont dans une zone acceptable pour un projet de cette maturité, mais les anti-patterns détectés (dépendances circulaires et couplage élevé dans core.py et service.py) créent des risques de régression à long terme. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.6) reste dans une fourchette gérable, et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.23) suggère une stabilité opérationnelle correcte. La couverture de tests (43.9%) est le point le plus préoccupant, mais elle n'est pas rédhibitoire pour des améliorations incrémentales.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée à ce stade. Les problèmes identifiés sont ciblés et peuvent être résolus par des refactorings incrémentaux combinés à un renforcement de la couverture de tests. Une approche de 'strangler fig pattern' serait contre-productive ici, car la stack actuelle est parfaitement adaptée au domaine métier et maîtrisée par l'équipe. L'accent doit être mis sur la réduction des anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration de la testabilité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Résolution des anti-patterns critiques : suppression des dépendances circulaires dans core.py et service.py, et réduction du couplage élevé dans core.py via l'application du principe de responsabilité unique.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests : cibler les modules critiques (core.py et service.py) avec une approche TDD pour atteindre un seuil minimal de 60% sur ces fichiers, en priorisant les cas d'usage métier.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit de la complexité cyclomatique : identifier les fonctions/méthodes avec une complexité > 10 et les décomposer, en parallèle d'une revue des paramètres longs dans service.py.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place de garde-fous : ajouter des hooks Git pour bloquer les commits introduisant des dépendances circulaires ou une complexité cyclomatique excessive, et former l'équipe aux bonnes pratiques de modularité.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global modéré si les phases sont exécutées dans l'ordre proposé. Le principal risque réside dans une tentative de résoudre tous les problèmes simultanément, ce qui pourrait introduire des régressions. La priorisation des anti-patterns critiques (dépendances circulaires et couplage élevé) limite les risques de blocage majeur. Aucun risque de migration technologique n'est à considérer, car la stack actuelle est adaptée et maîtrisée par l'équipe."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0120", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 43.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This e-commerce platform, built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL over 5.7 years, supports a team of 29 developers (with a senior-heavy distribution). The system operates under no immediate critical constraints, serving as the backbone for the company’s online retail operations with a focus on scalability and maintainability.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with coupling and cohesion scores around 5.3-5.4/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe degradation. Test coverage at 43.9% is suboptimal and suggests a need for stronger regression safety nets. Cyclomatic complexity at 6.6 is acceptable but could benefit from refactoring to reduce maintenance friction. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies (high in service.py, medium in core.py) and long parameter lists (medium in service.py) are present but localized, while high coupling in core.py is a concern. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.23 on the hottest file is manageable but warrants attention to prevent technical debt accumulation.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the absence of critical constraints and the overall moderate health of the codebase. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most impactful anti-patterns and bolster test coverage. This approach will yield measurable benefits with lower risk and shorter feedback loops.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies and high coupling in core.py and service.py to reduce technical debt and improve maintainability. Prioritize breaking cycles and simplifying parameter lists.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally increase test coverage to at least 60% by adding targeted unit and integration tests for critical paths, particularly around the refactored modules.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address cyclomatic complexity hotspots by breaking down complex functions into smaller, more manageable units. Implement static analysis checks to enforce complexity thresholds moving forward.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce automated quality gates (e.g., SonarQube) to monitor coupling, cohesion, and test coverage trends. Conduct a retrospective to refine the refactoring strategy based on observed outcomes.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The absence of critical constraints mitigates migration risks, but the localized anti-patterns and suboptimal test coverage introduce potential for regression if refactoring is not carefully managed. Incremental improvements reduce risk by limiting blast radius and allowing for continuous validation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0121", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 31, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.4, "cohesion_score": 3.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 8.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.81}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 1.9-year-old medtech platform built in Python with FastAPI and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 31 developers (80% junior) with a critical scalability constraint due to unpredictable traffic spikes. The codebase must reliably handle sensitive health data while evolving under high pressure for rapid feature delivery.", "analysis": "The codebase shows concerning structural health despite its young age. The cohesion score (3.4/10) is alarmingly low, indicating poor module separation and high interdependency. Coupling (6.4/10) is elevated but not catastrophic, suggesting some modular boundaries exist. Test coverage (8%) is dangerously low and will severely hinder safe refactoring. Cyclomatic complexity (7.3) is moderate but concentrated in anti-pattern hotspots like 'sante/service.py' and 'sante/processor.py'. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.81) on the hottest file reveals a maintenance burden that will worsen as traffic grows. Multiple God Classes and Long Methods across core modules indicate design erosion under delivery pressure.", "recommendation": "Do NOT perform a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the critical scalability constraint and structural decay. The current stack (Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL) is appropriate for the domain, and a rewrite would delay addressing the real issues: poor test coverage, high coupling, and design anti-patterns.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement comprehensive test coverage for critical paths, starting with the hottest files (sante/service.py, sante/processor.py) and core modules. Parallelize this with the extraction of Long Methods into smaller, focused functions/classes.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor God Classes in sante/core.py, sante/handler.py, and sante/processor.py by splitting them into smaller, single-responsibility components. Introduce dependency injection to reduce coupling in core modules.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address scalability bottlenecks by introducing caching layers (Redis) for predictable traffic spikes and optimizing database queries in PostgreSQL. Implement horizontal scaling strategies for FastAPI endpoints.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish automated code quality gates (SonarQube or similar) and team-wide refactoring workshops to prevent regression. Introduce pair programming for critical modules to improve knowledge sharing among junior developers.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of production incidents if refactoring is attempted without sufficient test coverage. The team's junior-heavy composition increases the risk of introducing new bugs during structural changes. Scalability improvements may be delayed by the time required to stabilize the codebase. However, these risks are manageable with disciplined incremental delivery and strong code review practices."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0122", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.3, "cohesion_score": 8.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 78.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.1}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built over 7 years with a Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL stack. It serves as the core backend for content delivery and user management, currently facing talent scarcity due to the niche expertise required for its technology choices. The system powers a growing user base with stable performance but struggles to attract developers familiar with its aging stack.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits strong internal quality with a low coupling score (1.3/10) and high cohesion (8.8/10), indicating a well-structured architecture. Test coverage at 78.5% is healthy for a mature system, and cyclomatic complexity (2.9) remains low, suggesting maintainable code. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.1) on the hottest file is excellent, indicating stability. Only one low-severity anti-pattern (God Class) was detected, which is easily addressable without systemic impact.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, implement targeted incremental improvements to address the talent scarcity constraint while preserving the system's stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/media/core.py to reduce complexity and improve maintainability, while introducing clear interfaces to facilitate knowledge transfer.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Expand test coverage to 85%+ by adding missing unit and integration tests for critical paths, improving confidence for future changes.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Document key architectural decisions and module interactions in a lightweight ADR format to ease onboarding for new developers.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Gradually introduce modern Python practices (e.g., type hints, async patterns) in non-critical modules to modernize the codebase incrementally.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The existing architecture is sound, and changes are localized. The primary risk is disruption to ongoing feature development during refactoring, which can be mitigated by strict code review and incremental rollouts."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0123", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 59.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet MedTech, en production depuis près de 10 ans, gère des fonctionnalités critiques pour le secteur de la santé avec une stack Java/Spring Boot et PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 44 développeurs, majoritairement junior, fait face à des défis de vélocité pour livrer de nouvelles fonctionnalités, malgré une base de code mature et des contraintes réglementaires strictes.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase globalement saine mais avec des points de friction majeurs : un couplage modéré (5.4/10) et une cohésion perfectible (6.4/10) qui impactent la maintenabilité. La couverture de tests à 59.7% est insuffisante pour une application critique en santé, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.3) suggère des fonctions difficiles à maintenir. Les anti-patterns détectés (notamment des listes de paramètres trop longues et du code dupliqué) sont des sources probables de bugs et de ralentissements. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.31) indique une stabilité relative, mais les problèmes structurels actuels expliquent la lenteur des livraisons.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. En revanche, une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns et l'amélioration de la testabilité est recommandée. L'objectif doit être d'augmenter la vélocité sans prendre de risque sur la stabilité du système, cruciale dans le secteur santé.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi pour prioriser les modules les plus impactés par les anti-patterns (handler.py, service.py, core.py) et identifier les dépendances critiques.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correction des anti-patterns identifiés (refactoring des Long Parameter List et élimination du Duplicate Code) avec ajout de tests unitaires pour les modules concernés.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests (objectif : +20% en 3 mois) en ciblant les fonctions à haute complexité cyclomatique, avec revue de code systématique.", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'outils de monitoring (SonarQube, JaCoCo) et de pipelines CI/CD optimisés pour réduire le temps de feedback et accélérer les livraisons.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal est la perturbation des fonctionnalités critiques pendant les phases de refactoring. Une approche incrémentale avec des tests renforcés et des rollbacks rapides est essentielle. Le manque de seniors dans l'équipe pourrait ralentir la mise en œuvre, mais les corrections ciblées limitent l'exposition aux risques. Une migration progressive et documentée est préférable à un big-bang."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0123", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.4, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 59.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 9.6-year-old medtech application built with Java/Spring Boot and PostgreSQL, serving a healthcare sector where regulatory and patient-safety constraints demand rapid yet reliable feature delivery. The team of 44 developers (77% junior) faces slow feature delivery despite a mature codebase, prompting an analysis of technical debt and delivery bottlenecks.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with coupling (5.4/10) and cohesion (6.4/10) scores indicating room for improvement but not alarming levels. Test coverage at 59.7% is suboptimal and likely contributes to slower bug resolution, as evidenced by a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.31 on the hottest file. Cyclomatic complexity (6.3) is acceptable but could be reduced in critical paths. Anti-patterns like Long Parameter List (high/medium) and Duplicate Code (medium) are localized and actionable, suggesting technical debt rather than systemic decay.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full rewrite. Instead, implement targeted refactoring to address the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. The current metrics do not justify a high-risk, high-cost migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address anti-patterns: refactor Long Parameter List in src/sante/handler.py, src/sante/service.py, and src/sante/core.py, and eliminate Duplicate Code in src/sante/handler.py. Introduce parameter objects and extract methods to reduce complexity.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage by adding unit and integration tests for the refactored modules, prioritizing the hottest file. Aim to increase coverage incrementally while maintaining existing functionality.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce lightweight architectural improvements, such as modularizing tightly coupled components and introducing facade patterns to reduce coupling. Pair senior developers with juniors to accelerate knowledge transfer.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The refactoring is localized and reversible, with clear anti-patterns to target. The junior-heavy team may slow progress, but pairing with seniors mitigates risk. No migration risk, as the recommendation avoids a full rewrite."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0124", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 5.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 59.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.48}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise en production depuis 11.6 ans, reposant sur une stack Python/Flask/PostgreSQL. Il est soumis à des exigences strictes de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) et est maintenu par une équipe de 20 développeurs majoritairement juniors. La codebase, bien que mature, présente des défis de maintenabilité liés à sa croissance organique et à l'évolution des besoins métiers.", "analysis": "La codebase affiche des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de cet âge : couplage et cohésion modérés (5.8/10 et 5.7/10), complexité cyclomatique moyenne maîtrisée (5.2), et couverture de tests à 59.5% — un niveau acceptable pour une application métier où les tests end-to-end sont critiques. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.48) suggère une stabilité relative, bien que perfectible. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method et Circular Dependencies) sont ciblés et localisés, ce qui limite leur impact systémique. L'enjeu principal n'est pas l'architecture globale, mais la dette technique accumulée dans des zones spécifiques, aggravée par la proportion élevée de juniors dans l'équipe.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique complète n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. En revanche, une refonte ciblée des composants identifiés comme problématiques (notamment src/saas/service.py et les circular dependencies dans src/saas/handler.py) permettrait d'améliorer significativement la maintenabilité sans prendre les risques d'un rewrite massif. L'accent doit être mis sur la réduction de la dette technique incrémentale, couplée à un renforcement des bonnes pratiques (revues de code, tests automatisés) pour accompagner l'équipe junior. La conformité réglementaire doit rester un fil rouge dans toutes les modifications.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des composants critiques (service.py, handler.py) pour prioriser les refactoring et identifier les dépendances cachées. Définition d'un plan de découplage progressif avec des interfaces claires.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental du Long Method dans service.py, avec découpage en fonctions plus petites et introduction de tests unitaires pour valider le comportement. Migration progressive vers une architecture plus modulaire (ex: séparation des responsabilités entre services métiers et handlers).", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Résolution des Circular Dependencies dans handler.py via l'introduction d'interfaces ou de classes abstraites. Mise en place de mécanismes de mocking pour faciliter les tests et réduire les dépendances directes.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Renforcement de la couverture de tests (cible : +15%) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration, en ciblant les zones refactorées. Formation de l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques de test et de découplage.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Mise en place d'outils de monitoring (ex: SonarQube, CodeClimate) pour suivre l'évolution des métriques (couplage, complexité) et détecter les régressions. Revue trimestrielle des anti-patterns restants.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal est l'accumulation de dette technique si les refactorings ne sont pas priorisés ou si l'équipe junior n'est pas accompagnée. Un risque secondaire est la perturbation des fonctionnalités critiques pendant les modifications, atténué par une approche incrémentale et des tests renforcés. La conformité réglementaire doit être vérifiée à chaque étape pour éviter des non-conformités temporaires. Aucun risque majeur de migration complète (ex: réécriture en Go ou Node.js) n'est identifié, car les métriques ne justifient pas un tel changement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0124", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 5.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 59.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.48}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 11.6-year-old SaaS B2B application for business management, built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL. It operates under strict regulatory constraints (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) and is maintained by a team of 20 developers, predominantly junior (78%). The system requires continuous compliance with evolving data protection and security standards while supporting core business functionalities for enterprise clients.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with coupling and cohesion scores around 5.8/10 and 5.7/10, respectively. While not alarmingly high, these scores indicate room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage at 59.5% is suboptimal but not critically low, suggesting a need for expanded test suites to improve reliability, especially in critical regulatory paths. Cyclomatic complexity of 5.2 is acceptable but indicates potential for simplification in some areas. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.48 on the hottest file suggests frequent reactive fixes, which may correlate with the detected anti-patterns. The presence of high-severity 'Long Method' and medium-severity 'Circular Dependency' anti-patterns in critical files (src/saas/service.py and src/saas/handler.py) is concerning, as these directly impact maintainability and increase the risk of regulatory non-compliance due to error-prone changes.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full technology migration at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical structural and quality issues. The current stack (Python/Flask/PostgreSQL) is well-suited for the regulatory constraints and team skillset, and a full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk without clear justification. Prioritize refactoring the anti-patterns in the hottest files to reduce complexity and improve testability, while gradually expanding test coverage to strengthen compliance-related paths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the 'Long Method' in src/saas/service.py and resolve circular dependencies in src/saas/handler.py to reduce complexity and improve maintainability. Implement targeted unit and integration tests for the refactored modules to ensure behavioral consistency.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Expand test coverage to at least 70% by adding tests for critical regulatory paths (e.g., data handling, audit logging) and high-risk business logic. Introduce automated security and compliance checks in the CI pipeline to catch regressions early.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement modularization improvements to reduce coupling and improve cohesion, particularly in areas with high interaction between modules. Introduce clear interfaces and dependency injection patterns to minimize circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a regulatory compliance audit of the refactored codebase to ensure all changes meet RGPD, PCI-DSS, and HDS requirements. Update documentation and training materials for the team to reflect the new structural patterns.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The primary risks stem from the current anti-patterns and low test coverage, which could lead to compliance violations or production incidents if left unaddressed. However, the incremental approach mitigates the high risk associated with a full rewrite. The team's junior-heavy composition may slow down refactoring efforts, but pairing senior developers with juniors can mitigate this. The regulatory constraints add complexity, but the targeted improvements are designed to address these risks directly without disrupting the existing compliance posture."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0125", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.48}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est un marketplace en croissance développé en Ruby on Rails avec une base de données MySQL, lancé il y a 18 mois. L'équipe de 14 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, maintient une plateforme transactionnelle où la stabilité et l'évolutivité sont critiques pour l'expérience utilisateur et la rentabilité. La stack actuelle répond aux besoins fonctionnels mais montre des signes de complexité croissante dans certains modules centraux.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une base de code globalement saine avec des indicateurs techniques modérés : couplage et cohésion dans une fourchette acceptable (3.7/10 et 4.7/10), et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 4.0 qui reste dans des limites gérables. La couverture de tests à 45.8% est le point le plus préoccupant, mais pas critique en soi. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method, Long Parameter List) sont localisés et de gravité moyenne, sans impact systémique apparent. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.48 suggère une stabilité relative malgré la proportion importante de juniors dans l'équipe. Aucune contrainte critique n'a été identifiée, ce qui indique que la stack actuelle n'est pas un frein à la croissance.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée à ce stade. Les métriques ne montrent pas de blocage majeur nécessitant un changement radical de stack. L'approche recommandée est une amélioration incrémentale ciblée sur les points faibles identifiés, combinée à un renforcement des pratiques de test et de revue de code pour améliorer la maintenabilité à long terme.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Renforcement de la couverture de tests via l'ajout de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules critiques, en priorisant les zones à forte complexité cyclomatique. Mise en place d'un processus de revue de code systématique pour les modifications impactant les fichiers identifiés comme problématiques.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation des anti-patterns détectés (Long Method, Long Parameter List) dans les fichiers marketplace/handler.py, marketplace/core.py et marketplace/service.py. Cette phase inclut une documentation des changements et une validation par les tests existants.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la cohésion et réduction du couplage dans les modules centraux en appliquant des principes de conception orientée objet (SOLID) et en introduisant des interfaces pour les dépendances critiques. Formation de l'équipe sur ces bonnes pratiques.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal réside dans l'augmentation de la dette technique si les améliorations incrémentales ne sont pas menées à bien. Cependant, ce risque est modéré car les anti-patterns sont localisés et la stack actuelle reste fonctionnelle. Le risque de migration vers une nouvelle stack serait élevé compte tenu de la proportion de juniors dans l'équipe et de l'absence de contrainte critique. La stratégie proposée minimise les perturbations tout en renforçant la base technique de manière durable."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0125", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.48}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 1.8-year-old Ruby on Rails marketplace platform with a team of 14 developers (72% junior, 6% senior) running on MySQL. The system currently operates without critical constraints but shows early signs of technical debt in method complexity and test coverage gaps.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (3.7/10) and cohesion (4.7/10), indicating room for improvement but not alarming structural issues. Test coverage at 45.8% is suboptimal but not catastrophic, especially given the project's age. Cyclomatic complexity (4.0) is acceptable, though the presence of medium anti-patterns (Long Method, Long Parameter List) suggests some hotspots. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.48) implies a manageable defect rate. The team's junior-heavy composition may benefit from targeted refactoring rather than a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the detected anti-patterns and boost test coverage. A full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk given the project's age and current metrics.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor identified anti-patterns (Long Method, Long Parameter List) in the hottest files to improve maintainability and reduce future defect risk.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally increase test coverage from 45.8% to at least 60% by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce automated code quality checks (e.g., RuboCop) to enforce consistency and prevent regression of anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The project is young with no critical constraints, but the junior-heavy team may struggle with deeper refactoring without guidance. Incremental improvements mitigate risks while building team capability."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0126", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.0, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme SaaS éducative en Node.js/Express avec base MongoDB, utilisée par 120 000 utilisateurs mensuels. L'application propose des parcours pédagogiques personnalisés, des outils de collaboration en temps réel et des tableaux de bord analytiques pour les enseignants. L'équipe technique de 45 développeurs gère un codebase vieillissant de 5,4 ans, avec une croissance continue des coûts d'infrastructure cloud qui impacte la rentabilité du produit.", "analysis": "Le codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour une application de cette taille : couplage modéré (4/10) et cohésion acceptable (6,9/10) suggèrent une architecture maintenable malgré son âge. La couverture de tests à 52% est insuffisante mais pas critique, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5,3 reste dans une plage gérable pour une équipe majoritairement junior. Les anti-patterns détectés (dépendances circulaires, méthodes longues) sont concentrés dans quelques fichiers centraux (handler.py, service.py, core.py) et ne semblent pas systématiques. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0,39 indique une stabilité relative du code malgré les évolutions fonctionnelles.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour réduire les coûts cloud et renforcer la maintenabilité. Une refonte complète serait contre-productive compte tenu du niveau de couplage acceptable et de la maturité de l'équipe. Les gains seraient marginaux comparés aux risques d'une migration mal planifiée.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des 3 fichiers problématiques (handler.py, service.py, core.py) pour identifier les causes racines des anti-patterns et prioriser les corrections", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'un plan de tests automatisés progressif pour atteindre 70% de couverture sur les modules critiques, avec intégration dans le pipeline CI/CD", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes MongoDB et refactoring des endpoints Express pour réduire la consommation cloud, avec monitoring des gains avant/après", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation des développeurs juniors aux bonnes pratiques (dépendances circulaires, méthodes courtes) via des ateliers pratiques et des revues de code systématiques", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour les phases 1 et 4 (actions internes). Risque modéré pour la phase 2 (tests) si la couverture actuelle est trop faible, nécessitant une approche progressive. Risque élevé pour la phase 3 (optimisation cloud) si les gains ne sont pas mesurables rapidement - un échec pourrait justifier une analyse plus poussée des patterns de consommation cloud avant toute action."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0126", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.0, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "An edtech platform built over 5 years with a Node.js/Express/MongoDB stack, serving 45 developers (60% junior, 11% senior). The system faces rising cloud costs as the primary operational constraint while maintaining moderate code health metrics and several structural anti-patterns that hinder maintainability and scalability.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 4.0/10 and cohesion at 6.9/10, indicating room for improvement but not critical failure. Test coverage at 52% is suboptimal but not disastrous for an established system, while cyclomatic complexity at 5.3 remains within acceptable bounds. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.39 suggests the hottest file requires attention but isn't in crisis mode. The detected anti-patterns (circular dependencies in handler.py and service.py, long parameter list in handler.py, and high method length in core.py) are concerning but localized to specific modules rather than systemic.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the overall moderate health of the codebase. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage. This approach will reduce cloud costs by optimizing inefficient code paths while minimizing risk and preserving business continuity.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address circular dependencies in handler.py and service.py by introducing dependency injection and breaking up tightly coupled modules. Fix the long parameter list in handler.py through parameter object pattern. Extract the high-complexity method in core.py into smaller, focused functions.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted test coverage improvements, prioritizing the most critical paths and the previously identified hot file. Use mutation testing to validate test effectiveness.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize cloud resource usage by profiling application performance, identifying inefficient queries or operations, and implementing caching or query optimization where applicable.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish monitoring and alerting for cloud cost anomalies and code health metrics. Implement a lightweight governance process to prevent regression of anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The refactoring approach targets specific pain points without requiring a full rewrite, reducing the risk of introducing new defects. The primary risk lies in the complexity of circular dependency resolution, which may require careful coordination across teams. Cloud cost optimization carries minimal risk but requires thorough testing to avoid performance degradation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0127", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace mature en Python/Django avec une base de code de 8,7 ans, supportant une équipe de 42 développeurs. La plateforme souffre d'une vélocité de développement ralentie par des problèmes structurels récurrents malgré une stack techno stable et éprouvée.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs mitigés : le couplage (5,8/10) et la cohésion (4,4/10) sont dans une zone acceptable mais perfectibles, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4,7) et le ratio de commits correctifs (0,49) révèlent une instabilité modérée. Les anti-patterns identifiés (dépendances circulaires, couplage élevé, méthodes longues) sont concentrés dans des zones critiques (core.py, service.py), ce qui explique partiellement la baisse de vélocité. La couverture de tests (52,4%) est insuffisante pour garantir des refactoring en toute sécurité.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. L'approche recommandée est une stratégie d'amélioration incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns identifiés, combinée à un renforcement de la couverture de tests. Cette voie permet de réduire les frictions de développement sans prendre les risques d'un rewrite complet.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Décomposition des dépendances circulaires dans core.py via une analyse des responsabilités et extraction de modules dédiés (ex: séparation des concerns entre services métiers et logique core).", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des méthodes longues dans service.py avec application du principe Single Responsibility et découpage en fonctions plus petites. Mise en place de tests unitaires pour valider chaque extrait.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests (objectif : +20%) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration, en priorisant les modules les plus instables (core.py, service.py).", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des processus de CI/CD pour réduire le temps de feedback des tests (ex: parallélisation, exécution sélective des tests critiques).", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré : les améliorations incrémentales ciblées limitent l'exposition aux bugs, mais nécessitent une discipline collective (revues de code strictes, tests obligatoires). Le principal risque est une sous-estimation de l'effort de découplage si les dépendances circulaires sont plus profondes que prévu. Une approche itérative avec des revues intermédiaires permet de mitiger ce risque."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0127", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature Python/Django/PostgreSQL marketplace platform with an 8.7-year history, serving a team of 42 developers (mix of junior and senior). The primary business constraint is slow feature delivery, prompting an evaluation of the codebase's maintainability and architectural health to identify bottlenecks in development velocity.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (5.8/10) and cohesion (4.4/10), which are not alarmingly high but indicate room for improvement in modularity. Test coverage at 52.4% is concerning, as it suggests insufficient safety nets for refactoring. Cyclomatic complexity (4.7) is acceptable but could benefit from reduction in critical paths. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.49) on the hottest file signals fragility in core components. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies and high coupling in `core.py` are structural issues that directly impede development velocity by making changes risky and time-consuming.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the dominant constraint (slow feature delivery) by reducing fragility in the core components and improving test coverage. These changes will yield faster, safer iterations without the overhead of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address structural anti-patterns in `core.py` by breaking circular dependencies and reducing coupling through modularization. Introduce dependency injection or facade patterns to isolate changes.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage incrementally, prioritizing critical paths in `core.py` and `service.py`. Aim to raise coverage to at least 70% in these modules to enable safer refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor `service.py` to reduce method length and complexity, splitting long methods into smaller, single-responsibility functions. Introduce intermediate abstractions where needed.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement CI/CD pipeline improvements to automate testing and deployment, reducing manual bottlenecks in the release process.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks are related to the fragility of `core.py` during refactoring, which could introduce regressions if not handled carefully. Mitigation includes incremental changes, extensive testing, and feature flags for new implementations. The team's size and mix of experience are sufficient to execute these improvements, provided adequate code reviews and pair programming are enforced."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0128", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 9.9, "cohesion_score": 3.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 17.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 8.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.72}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a logistics and supply chain management system built with PHP/Laravel and MySQL, serving a team of six developers with a mix of junior and senior experience. The system has evolved over 11 years, and the team is currently facing challenges with escalating cloud costs, which they identify as the dominant constraint on further growth and scalability.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural issues that undermine maintainability and increase operational costs. The coupling score of 9.9/10 and cohesion score of 3.7/10 indicate a highly interdependent system with poor separation of concerns, making changes risky and expensive. The low test coverage (17.3%) and high cyclomatic complexity (8.9) further exacerbate the risk of introducing regressions during modifications. Anti-patterns such as long parameter lists and long methods in critical files (e.g., src/logistique/service.py and src/logistique/core.py) compound the technical debt, leading to a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.72 in the hottest file—suggesting frequent firefighting rather than sustainable development. These metrics collectively point to a system that is difficult to extend, costly to operate, and prone to instability.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, the focus should be on targeted refactoring to address the most critical structural issues. The primary goal is to reduce coupling and improve cohesion in the core logistics modules, which will directly help mitigate cloud cost overruns by enabling more efficient resource usage and reducing the risk of costly failures. Incremental improvements, such as breaking down long methods, reducing parameter lists, and introducing modular boundaries, will yield measurable benefits without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a detailed architectural assessment to identify the top 3-5 hotspots contributing most to cloud cost overruns and technical debt. Focus on the files with high coupling (e.g., src/logistique/service.py and src/logistique/core.py) and prioritize refactoring candidates based on their impact on system stability and operational costs.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement modular boundaries in the core logistics modules by extracting cohesive components from the highly coupled files. Start with the file exhibiting the highest bugfix-commit ratio (src/logistique/service.py) to reduce the immediate risk of regressions. Introduce interfaces and dependency injection to lower coupling and improve testability.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor long methods and reduce parameter lists in the identified hotspots. Break down methods into smaller, single-responsibility units and introduce value objects or data transfer objects to encapsulate parameter lists. Pair this work with incremental test coverage improvements to ensure changes are safe and maintainable.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement observability and cost monitoring improvements to provide visibility into cloud resource usage patterns. Use this data to guide further refactoring efforts and validate the impact of architectural changes on cloud costs.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The risk of proceeding with incremental refactoring is moderate but manageable. The team's junior-heavy composition may slow progress, but pairing senior developers with juniors can mitigate this. The absence of automated tests increases the risk of regressions, so refactoring must be done cautiously and in small increments, with manual testing and rollback plans in place. The dominant constraint—cloud costs—will likely improve as coupling and cohesion issues are addressed, but the timeline for measurable cost reductions depends on the depth of the refactoring. A full rewrite would carry significantly higher risk due to the team's inexperience with such projects and the potential for introducing new, unknown issues."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0130", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.5, "cohesion_score": 2.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 9.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.68}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, with a codebase of 6.1 years. The team of 19 developers (74% senior, 21% junior) maintains a codebase that has grown organically, with no critical constraints currently identified but notable technical debt in cohesion, coupling, and test coverage.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural issues despite being operational. The coupling score (7.5/10) and cohesion score (2.1/10) indicate a system where components are overly interdependent and responsibilities are poorly separated. Test coverage at 9.7% is critically low, and the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.68) on the hottest file suggests frequent firefighting. Anti-patterns such as circular dependencies, god classes, and duplicate code are actively degrading maintainability. While the team is experienced, the combination of low cohesion, high coupling, and minimal test coverage poses a growing risk to stability and scalability.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on incremental refactoring to address the most damaging anti-patterns and improve structural quality. The primary goal should be to reduce coupling, improve cohesion, and introduce meaningful test coverage to stabilize the system. This approach will mitigate risks while delivering tangible improvements without the overhead of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address critical anti-patterns and structural issues in the most problematic files (handler.py, core.py, processor.py, service.py). Prioritize breaking circular dependencies, reducing god classes, and eliminating duplicate code. Introduce targeted unit tests for high-risk areas to prevent regression.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor core modules to improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Introduce design patterns (e.g., Strategy, Factory) where appropriate to decouple components. Gradually expand test coverage to at least 30% for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement architectural improvements to enforce better separation of concerns. Introduce interfaces and dependency injection to reduce tight coupling. Establish coding standards and automated checks to prevent recurrence of anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "High. The current state of the codebase is fragile, with frequent bugfixes and low test coverage. Refactoring carries the risk of introducing regressions, but the alternative—continuing with the current structure—risks further degradation and technical debt accumulation. Mitigation strategies include incremental changes, comprehensive testing, and close monitoring of system behavior during refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0131", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 30, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.6, "cohesion_score": 7.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 77.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise en production depuis 3,4 ans, utilisé par des centaines d'entreprises clientes. La stack technique repose sur Ruby on Rails et MySQL, avec une exigence forte de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) qui impacte directement l'architecture et les processus de développement. L'équipe de 30 développeurs, majoritairement expérimentée, maintient une base de code en croissance constante tout en garantissant la stabilité opérationnelle.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une base de code saine et bien structurée : un couplage faible (2,6/10) suggère une architecture modulaire avec des dépendances maîtrisées, tandis qu'une cohésion élevée (7,4/10) confirme que les composants sont bien alignés sur leurs responsabilités. La couverture de tests à 77,9% est satisfaisante pour un projet de cette taille, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2,0 montre un code simple et maintenable. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le ratio de commits correctifs bas (0,15) renforcent cette impression de maturité technique. La contrainte de conformité, bien que exigeante, est gérable dans l'écosystème actuel sans refonte majeure.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. La stack Ruby/Rails/MySQL, malgré son âge, reste parfaitement adaptée au contexte SaaS B2B avec des exigences de conformité strictes. Les métriques démontrent une base de code maintenable et évolutive, où les gains d'une migration seraient largement compensés par les risques et les coûts. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour renforcer la résilience et la conformité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Renforcer la couverture de tests sur les modules critiques pour la conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS) afin d'atteindre 85%+ sur ces zones. Prioriser les tests d'intégration et de sécurité.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Automatiser les audits de conformité dans le pipeline CI/CD pour détecter précocement les écarts (ex: fuites de données potentielles, configurations non conformes).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimiser les requêtes SQL les plus coûteuses identifiées par le profiling, en collaboration avec les équipes DBA pour réduire la charge sur MySQL.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Documenter les décisions architecturales critiques liées à la conformité (ex: chiffrement des données, gestion des accès) dans un ADR (Architecture Decision Record) partagé.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal réside dans l'accumulation de dette technique non maîtrisée sur le long terme, mais les métriques actuelles ne justifient pas une refonte. Les risques opérationnels d'une migration (downtime, perte de fonctionnalités, courbe d'apprentissage) seraient disproportionnés par rapport aux bénéfices potentiels. La stratégie recommandée minimise les risques tout en améliorant progressivement la qualité et la conformité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0132", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce, vieillissant de 13.8 ans, supporte un trafic critique avec des exigences strictes de latence en temps réel. La stack Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL, maintenue par une équipe majoritairement junior, doit concilier performance et évolutivité tout en gérant une dette technique croissante dans des modules centraux comme le cœur métier et les handlers de requêtes.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase modérément saine malgré son âge : couplage faible (3.0/10) et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée (6.3) suggèrent une architecture globalement stable. Cependant, la cohésion moyenne (6.1/10) et la couverture de tests insuffisante (47.6%) indiquent des risques de régressions lors des modifications. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method, Duplicate Code) sont concentrés dans deux fichiers critiques, ce qui explique le ratio élevé de commits correctifs (0.23) sur ces modules. L'équipe junior majoritaire pourrait amplifier ces problèmes lors des évolutions futures.", "recommendation": "Éviter un rewrite complet coûteux et risqué. Privilégier une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns identifiés, combinée à un renforcement des tests et à une amélioration de la cohésion. Cette approche limite les perturbations tout en réduisant la dette technique de manière mesurable.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyse approfondie des fichiers critiques (core.py, handler.py) pour identifier les duplications et les méthodes trop longues. Définition d'un plan de découpage modulaire avec des interfaces claires.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'une stratégie de tests : augmentation de la couverture sur les modules modifiés (objectif +15%) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration, avec un focus sur les chemins critiques de latence.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns détectés, en commençant par les duplications les plus impactantes. Intégration progressive des changements via des feature flags pour minimiser les risques.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation ciblée pour l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques de découplage et de test, avec des ateliers pratiques sur les modules refactorisés.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Audit post-refactoring pour valider l'impact sur la latence et la stabilité, avec ajustements si nécessaire.", "duration_days_range": "5-7 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré : les anti-patterns sont localisés et la complexité globale reste maîtrisée. Le principal risque réside dans l'exécution du refactoring par une équipe majoritairement junior, d'où l'importance des phases de formation et de validation incrémentale. Une approche trop agressive pourrait introduire des régressions, mais une stratégie progressive et bien encadrée limite ce danger."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0132", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 6.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a long-standing e-commerce platform built on Java/Spring Boot with a PostgreSQL backend, serving a team of 20 developers where the majority are junior. The system operates under a critical real-time latency constraint, requiring consistent performance to support high-traffic transactions and user interactions.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.0/10 and cohesion score of 6.1/10, indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage stands at 47.6%, which is below the threshold for confident refactoring, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 6.3 suggests some areas may be difficult to maintain. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.23 on the hottest file implies a relatively stable but potentially brittle component. Anti-patterns such as long methods and duplicated code in core and handler modules further increase technical debt and risk of regression during changes.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical issues affecting maintainability and performance. The current stack is capable of supporting the real-time latency constraint with proper refactoring and testing discipline.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-impact anti-patterns by splitting long methods and eliminating duplicate code in core.py and handler.py. Introduce modular boundaries to improve cohesion and reduce coupling in the most problematic modules.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Gradually increase test coverage in the refactored modules to at least 60% through incremental test writing. Prioritize unit and integration tests for the hottest files to stabilize the codebase.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce lightweight architectural patterns such as CQRS or event-driven components in isolated areas to improve scalability and maintainability without a full rewrite. Focus on modules with the highest change frequency.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression if refactoring is not accompanied by comprehensive testing. The junior-heavy team may struggle with complex architectural changes without mentorship. However, incremental improvements reduce overall risk compared to a full migration. Real-time latency could be impacted during refactoring if performance testing is not integrated."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0133", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 5.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet medtech, développé en Java/Spring Boot avec une base PostgreSQL, gère des flux de données critiques pour des dispositifs médicaux connectés. Après 4.5 ans de développement par une équipe de 33 personnes (mix juniors/seniors), il alimente en temps réel les tableaux de bord hospitaliers et les alertes de sécurité patient. La contrainte principale reste la stabilité opérationnelle, avec une exigence de disponibilité >99.9% pour les services critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de cette taille et maturité. Le score de couplage à 3.4/10 indique une architecture modulaire acceptable, tandis que la cohésion à 5.8/10 suggère des opportunités d'amélioration dans l'organisation des responsabilités. La couverture de tests à 50.8% est faible mais gérable pour un legacy en santé où les tests d'intégration sont souvent prioritaires. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 4.1 reste dans une fourchette raisonnable pour des services métier. Les anti-patterns détectés (circular dependencies et long parameter lists) sont localisés et gérables sans refonte majeure. Le ratio de commits correctifs à 0.47 montre une stabilité acceptable du code malgré des zones à risque.", "recommendation": "Pas de migration ou rewrite complet justifié. Les métriques ne révèlent pas de problème structurel bloquant. Une approche incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns et l'amélioration de la couverture de tests sera plus efficace et moins risquée. Le projet peut continuer à évoluer en mode maintenance évolutive avec des améliorations ciblées.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Résolution des anti-patterns identifiés : découplage des circular dependencies dans src/sante/service.py et src/sante/processor.py via l'application du principe de dépendance vers les abstractions (DIP) et extraction d'interfaces. Refactorisation des long parameter lists dans src/sante/core.py et src/sante/handler.py via l'encapsulation des paramètres dans des objets dédiés (DTOs).", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests : identification des modules critiques non couverts et création de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les services exposés via des APIs REST. Priorisation des tests pour les endpoints de santé critiques (ex: /api/patient/alerts).", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation de la cohésion : réorganisation des responsabilités dans les modules à faible cohésion via l'extraction de classes dédiées pour les responsabilités transverses (ex: logging, validation). Mise en place de revues de code ciblées pour valider les changements.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour les phases 1 et 3 (changements localisés et réversibles). Risque modéré pour la phase 2 (amélioration de la couverture de tests) si les tests existants sont fragiles ou mal documentés. Stratégie de mitigation : validation progressive via des pull requests et tests de régression automatisés avant déploiement en production. Aucun risque critique identifié pour la stabilité du système."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0133", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.4, "cohesion_score": 5.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 4.5-year-old medtech application built in Java/Spring Boot with PostgreSQL, serving the healthcare sector. It is maintained by a 33-developer team with a mix of junior and senior profiles, and currently operates without critical constraints, focusing on delivering reliable patient and clinical data services.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.4/10 and cohesion at 5.8/10, indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage at 50.8% is suboptimal and suggests incomplete verification of business logic, especially in critical patient data flows. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 4.1 on average, but the presence of circular dependencies (medium in service.py, high in processor.py) and long parameter lists (high in core.py and handler.py) indicates design erosion and potential maintainability risks. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.47 on the hottest file suggests active stabilization but may reflect underlying fragility. Overall, the system is functional but not yet in a state where large-scale change can be risked without prior refactoring.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the detected anti-patterns and improve test coverage. The current architecture, while not pristine, does not justify a full rewrite given the absence of critical constraints and the team’s size and experience.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address circular dependencies and long parameter lists by refactoring core modules (service.py, processor.py, core.py, handler.py) using dependency inversion and parameter object patterns. Introduce automated tests for these modules to prevent regression.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage incrementally, targeting critical patient data paths and high-risk modules. Introduce property-based testing where applicable to increase confidence in edge cases.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the most complex methods to reduce cyclomatic complexity and improve readability. Introduce consistent logging and monitoring to detect stability issues early.", "duration_days_range": "10-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a team workshop to define and enforce coding standards and architectural guidelines, with automated checks in CI to prevent regression of anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The absence of critical constraints reduces immediate risk, but the presence of circular dependencies and low test coverage increases the risk of introducing regressions during refactoring. A phased, incremental approach with strong test coverage and monitoring will mitigate these risks effectively."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0136", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.9, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 87.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.05}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel, en production depuis 5.8 ans avec une stack Python/Django/PostgreSQL, gère le traitement et l'analyse de données issues de capteurs industriels. L'application centralise les flux de données temps réel pour optimiser la maintenance prédictive et la gestion énergétique des infrastructures clientes, avec une équipe de 26 développeurs dont la majorité a une expérience significative sur ce codebase.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une base de code saine et mature : un couplage très faible (1.9/10) suggère une architecture modulaire bien isolée, tandis qu'une cohésion élevée (8.2/10) confirme que les composants sont bien alignés sur leurs responsabilités. La couverture de tests à 87.7% et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 3.0 sont des indicateurs solides de maintenabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.05) montre une stabilité remarquable du code, et l'anti-pattern détecté (duplicate code low) est mineur et localisé. Aucune contrainte critique n'a été identifiée, ce qui est cohérent avec une base de code vieillissante mais bien structurée.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. Le projet présente des caractéristiques d'une codebase mature et bien gérée, avec des métriques qui ne signalent pas de problème structurel majeur. Une approche incrémentale de maintenance et d'amélioration continue est préférable à un changement radical.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Élimination ciblée du duplicate code dans src/iot/processor.py via une refactorisation incrémentale avec tests automatisés", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests dans les modules critiques (objectif : +5%) avec ajout de tests d'intégration pour les flux IoT", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit de sécurité et optimisation des requêtes PostgreSQL pour les volumes de données actuels et futurs", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global faible. Les améliorations proposées sont incrémentales et réversibles, avec des tests automatisés comme filet de sécurité. Aucun risque de blocage majeur n'est identifié, et les changements proposés peuvent être déployés progressivement sans interruption de service."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0137", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 6.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 53.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.27}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Cette application SaaS B2B en .NET/ASP.NET Core, âgée de 9 mois, automatise la gestion financière et opérationnelle pour des PME européennes. Elle est utilisée par 120 clients avec un taux de disponibilité de 99,8%, mais souffre d'une pénurie locale de développeurs maîtrisant la stack .NET moderne, limitant sa capacité d'évolution.", "analysis": "La codebase présente une santé globale acceptable avec des scores de couplage (3.1/10) et de cohésion (6.6/10) modérés, indiquant une architecture ni trop monolithique ni trop dispersée. La couverture de tests à 53,4% est perfectible mais couvre les fonctionnalités critiques. Les anti-patterns de dépendances circulaires (high dans 3 fichiers) sont préoccupants car ils créent des silos techniques et compliquent les évolutions. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.27) suggère une stabilité relative malgré ces problèmes structurels.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique complète n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. L'enjeu principal est la pénurie de talents .NET, mais une refonte radicale introduirait des risques majeurs sans garantie de résolution durable. Une approche incrémentale ciblée sur les dépendances circulaires et l'amélioration des tests serait plus pertinente.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Identifier et documenter toutes les dépendances circulaires avec un outil comme NDepend, puis prioriser leur résolution par impact métier (commencer par les high dans core.py et service.py)", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mettre en place une stratégie de tests automatisés pour les modules critiques (cibler 70% de couverture sur les endpoints API principaux)", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Moderniser progressivement la stack .NET vers .NET 8 en parallèle des corrections structurelles, avec une approche de feature flags pour limiter les risques", "duration_days_range": "30-40"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Former l'équipe aux bonnes pratiques d'architecture modulaire (DDD, CQRS) et documenter les décisions techniques dans un ADR", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque élevé de régression si les dépendances circulaires ne sont pas traitées avec une approche systématique. Le risque de migration technologique est modéré mais justifié par l'alignement avec le marché du travail. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.6) indique un besoin de simplification progressive des fonctions critiques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0137", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 6.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 53.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.27}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 0.9-year-old SaaS B2B application for business management, built on .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server. The team of 19 developers faces a talent shortage in their current stack, prompting an evaluation of potential technology shifts to address recruitment challenges while maintaining system stability and scalability.", "analysis": "The codebase metrics indicate a relatively young but moderately coupled system (3.1/10 coupling score) with acceptable cohesion (6.6/10). Test coverage at 53.4% is suboptimal but not critical for a 0.9-year-old project, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 4.6 suggests manageable code complexity. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.27 on the hottest file is concerning but not alarming. The presence of high and medium circular dependencies in core files (service.py, processor.py, core.py) is a structural issue that could hinder maintainability and scalability over time. The team's talent shortage in the current stack is a valid operational constraint that may justify exploring alternative technologies, but the codebase itself does not exhibit severe decay that would necessitate a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the circular dependencies and improve test coverage. These changes will reduce technical debt and improve maintainability without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite. The talent shortage should be addressed through targeted hiring or upskilling rather than a technology shift, as the current stack's health does not warrant such a drastic step.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependencies in src/saas/service.py, src/saas/processor.py, and src/saas/core.py to break cycles and improve modularity. Introduce interfaces or dependency injection to decouple components.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage from 53.4% to at least 70% by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths. Prioritize high-risk areas identified in the bugfix analysis.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a code review and static analysis session to identify and address additional anti-patterns or technical debt. Document architectural decisions and update the team's coding standards to prevent regressions.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks involve the refactoring of circular dependencies, which could introduce new bugs if not handled carefully. The incremental approach mitigates this risk by allowing for gradual validation. The talent shortage remains an operational risk but is not directly tied to the codebase's health. No migration risks (e.g., data loss, extended downtime) are present since a full rewrite is not recommended."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0138", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.3, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 71.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.05}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise en production depuis 14 ans, reposant sur une stack Python/FastAPI avec PostgreSQL. Il doit gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles tout en supportant une équipe de 41 développeurs, dont près de la moitié sont juniors. La scalabilité est donc un enjeu critique pour la continuité du service et la satisfaction client.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales de la codebase sont saines : un couplage faible (2.3/10) et une cohésion élevée (8.3/10) indiquent une architecture modulaire et bien structurée. La couverture de tests à 71.3% est acceptable pour un projet mature, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2.0 suggère un code lisible et maintenable. Le ratio de commits correctifs très bas (0.05) sur le fichier le plus sollicité confirme une stabilité opérationnelle. Seul un anti-pattern mineur (Long Parameter List) a été détecté, sans impact majeur sur la maintenabilité. L'équipe senior est suffisamment expérimentée pour gérer les évolutions incrémentales sans risque de dégradation architecturale.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. La stack Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL répond aux besoins métiers et techniques, avec une scalabilité maîtrisable via des optimisations ciblées. Une refonte complète serait coûteuse en ressources et risquée sans preuve d'un blocage technique majeur.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Corriger l'anti-pattern Long Parameter List dans src/saas/processor.py en utilisant des objets de transfert de données (DTO) ou des paramètres nommés.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Améliorer la couverture de tests à 85% en ciblant les modules critiques (ex: gestion des pics de trafic) via des tests de charge et des tests unitaires complémentaires.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimiser les requêtes PostgreSQL les plus fréquentes (ex: indexation, requêtes batch) pour réduire la latence lors des pics de trafic, en collaboration avec l'équipe DevOps.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Documenter les bonnes pratiques d'architecture (ex: séparation claire des responsabilités, gestion des dépendances) et former les développeurs juniors pour renforcer la cohésion de l'équipe.", "duration_days_range": "5-7 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible à modéré. Les risques principaux sont liés à une mauvaise priorisation des optimisations (ex: sur-optimisation prématurée) ou à une formation insuffisante des juniors. Aucun risque majeur de blocage technique ou de dégradation de la scalabilité n'est identifié avec les métriques actuelles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0139", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.5}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace en croissance active depuis près de 10 ans, dont l'architecture actuelle en Python/Flask/PostgreSQL supporte des pics de trafic imprévisibles. L'équipe de 45 développeurs, majoritairement junior, fait face à des défis de maintenance liés à une base de code vieillissante et à des anti-patterns structurels qui limitent l'évolutivité et la fiabilité du système.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase avec des métriques globalement saines mais des points de friction critiques. Le couplage (4.8/10) et la cohésion (4.9/10) sont dans une fourchette acceptable, mais les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Circular Dependency, Long Method) et la faible couverture de tests (33.2%) créent des goulots d'étranglement majeurs. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.2) et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.5) confirment une dette technique qui impacte directement la scalabilité. La contrainte de trafic imprévisible est aggravée par ces problèmes structurels.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. En revanche, une refonte ciblée des composants identifiés comme anti-patterns (God Class, Circular Dependency) combinée à une amélioration incrémentale de la couverture de tests est la stratégie la plus efficace. Cela permettra de réduire la dette technique sans perturber l'équipe majoritairement junior, tout en préparant le terrain pour des évolutions futures si nécessaire.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Décomposition des anti-patterns identifiés (God Class dans processor.py, Circular Dependency dans service.py) via des techniques de refactoring incrémental (Extract Class, Dependency Injection).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests via une approche par couches : tests unitaires pour les nouveaux composants, tests d'intégration pour les endpoints critiques, et tests de charge pour valider les pics de trafic.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des endpoints Flask les plus sollicités (notamment dans handler.py) pour réduire la complexité cyclomatique et améliorer la lisibilité. Mise en place de mécanismes de caching ciblés.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Documentation des nouvelles conventions de code et formation de l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques de refactoring et de test. Mise en place d'outils d'analyse statique (SonarQube, Bandit) pour prévenir les régressions.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de code strictes. Le principal risque est la résistance au changement dans une équipe majoritairement junior, mais cela peut être atténué par des ateliers de formation et un accompagnement rapproché. La dette technique accumulée pourrait entraîner des incidents en production si les refactorings sont mal exécutés, d'où l'importance de tests automatisés robustes avant chaque déploiement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0139", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.5}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The Marketplace Platform is a 9.9-year-old Python/Flask application backed by PostgreSQL, serving a team of 45 developers (57% junior, 40% senior). It operates in the marketplace sector, facing unpredictable traffic spikes that challenge its current scalability, while maintaining a codebase with moderate structural integrity but significant technical debt in critical components.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling and cohesion scores (4.8/10 and 4.9/10 respectively), indicating a generally maintainable structure but with room for improvement. Test coverage at 33.2% is low and poses a risk to safe refactoring. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable (4.2), but anti-patterns such as God Class, Long Method, and Circular Dependencies in core modules (processor.py, service.py) are concerning. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.5 on the hottest file suggests active maintenance but potential fragility in high-change areas. The team's junior-heavy composition may struggle with large-scale architectural changes without targeted guidance.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this time. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve test coverage. This approach will reduce immediate scalability risks while building a foundation for future evolution without the high cost and risk of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address critical anti-patterns in core modules: split God Class in processor.py, refactor Long Method in service.py, and resolve Circular Dependency in service.py. Introduce modular boundaries to reduce coupling.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted test coverage improvements (aim for 50%+) in the refactored modules to ensure safe future changes. Prioritize high-bugfix files like src/marketplace/handler.py.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce incremental scalability improvements: implement caching layers, optimize database queries, and introduce async task queues for non-critical paths to handle traffic spikes.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish code quality gates (e.g., SonarQube, custom linters) and pair programming sessions for junior developers to prevent regression. Plan a future architecture review after 6-12 months of stability.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium risk if anti-patterns are not addressed promptly, particularly in the processor.py and service.py modules which are likely performance bottlenecks. Low risk of migration failure since no full rewrite is proposed. Highest risk lies in inadequate test coverage during refactoring, which could introduce regressions. Mitigate by prioritizing test coverage improvements before structural changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0140", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 28, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 10.0, "cohesion_score": 3.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 13.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 10.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.77}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est un système backend critique pour une plateforme de gaming en ligne, gérant des millions de transactions quotidiennes avec des exigences strictes de disponibilité (99.9% d'uptime). Développé initialement en PHP/Laravel, il souffre d'une dette technique accumulée sur 9 ans, avec une équipe majoritairement junior et des incidents récurrents en production qui impactent l'expérience utilisateur et la réputation de l'entreprise.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une base de code profondément dégradée : un couplage extrême (10/10) combiné à une cohésion très faible (3.4/10) indique une architecture spaghetti où les composants sont fortement interdépendants et mal définis. La couverture de tests à 13.6% et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 10.6 confirment un code difficile à maintenir et à tester. Les anti-patterns dominants (dépendances circulaires, classes monolithiques, méthodes trop longues) sont concentrés dans des fichiers centraux comme `handler.py`, `service.py` et `core.py`, ce qui explique les incidents fréquents. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.77 montre que plus de 77% des modifications sont des corrections de bugs, signe d'une instabilité chronique. L'équipe junior majoritaire aggrave la situation : sans refactoring guidé, les nouveaux développeurs perpétuent les mauvaises pratiques.", "recommendation": "Un rewrite complet n'est pas justifié à ce stade. La priorité absolue est de stabiliser la base de code existante via un refactoring incrémental ciblé, combiné à une amélioration des pratiques d'équipe. Les gains seront rapides et mesurables sur la fiabilité sans le risque d'un big-bang. Une migration technologique (ex: vers Node.js ou Go) pourrait être envisagée plus tard, mais uniquement après avoir rétabli une architecture saine et documentée.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des fichiers critiques (handler.py, service.py, core.py) pour identifier les dépendances circulaires et les classes God Object à scinder. Formation de l'équipe sur les principes SOLID et les bonnes pratiques de découplage.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des fichiers prioritaires : extraction de méthodes longues, découplage des dépendances circulaires, et introduction de tests unitaires pour les composants modifiés (objectif : porter la couverture à 25% sur ces fichiers). Mise en place d'un pipeline CI/CD avec analyse statique (SonarQube) et tests automatisés.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la cohésion via la création de modules métiers bien définis (ex: séparation des responsabilités entre gestion des joueurs, transactions, et contenu gaming). Introduction de design patterns adaptés (ex: Strategy pour les algorithmes de scoring, Repository pour l'accès aux données).", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Stabilisation et documentation : rédaction de guides de contribution, mise à jour de l'architecture dans un ADR (Architecture Decision Record), et organisation de revues de code systématiques pour éviter la régression des anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque ÉLEVÉ si le refactoring est mal planifié (ex: modification simultanée de trop de fichiers critiques). Pour le mitiger : limiter les changements à des zones bien délimitées, valider chaque étape par des tests automatisés, et impliquer les seniors dans les revues de code. Le risque principal reste la résistance au changement de l'équipe junior, à contrer par des formations pratiques et des exemples concrets de gains (ex: réduction des bugs post-déploiement)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0141", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 12, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 9.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 89.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.17}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Une plateforme d'apprentissage en ligne en temps réel pour les établissements scolaires, développée en PHP/Laravel avec une base de données MySQL. Le système doit synchroniser instantanément les interactions des élèves et enseignants (quiz, annotations, feedback) avec des exigences strictes de latence inférieure à 200ms pour les opérations critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques saines qui indiquent une architecture mature et bien structurée. Le couplage très faible (3.0/10) et la cohésion excellente (9.7/10) suggèrent une séparation claire des responsabilités et une conception modulaire. La couverture de tests élevée (89.6%) et la complexité cyclomatique minimale (1.4) confirment une base solide avec peu de risques de régression. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le ratio de commits correctifs bas (0.17) sur le fichier le plus sollicité montrent une maintenance efficace. La contrainte de latence critique est gérable dans l'écosystème actuel avec des optimisations ciblées.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données. Une refonte complète serait contre-productive et risquée, compte tenu des métriques excellentes. L'approche incrémentale est préférable pour préserver la stabilité tout en améliorant les performances.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Optimisation de la latence en ciblant les endpoints critiques : mise en cache Redis pour les données fréquemment accédées, optimisation des requêtes N+1 avec Laravel Scout, et révision des indexes MySQL sur les tables de sessions utilisateurs.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la résilience : implémentation d'un circuit breaker pour les appels externes (API de paiement, services tiers) et ajout de métriques de monitoring (Prometheus/Grafana) pour suivre les temps de réponse en temps réel.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Modernisation incrémentale : introduction progressive de PHP 8.2 sur les modules non critiques, avec validation via des tests de performance automatisés. Migration des tâches en arrière-plan vers des workers Laravel Horizon.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global faible à modéré. Les optimisations ciblées minimisent les perturbations, mais nécessitent des tests de charge approfondis en environnement de staging. La modernisation incrémentale de PHP doit être validée par des benchmarks pour éviter toute dégradation des performances. Aucun risque majeur identifié si les phases sont suivies méthodiquement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0141", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 12, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 9.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 89.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.17}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 5.5-year-old edtech platform built with PHP/Laravel and MySQL, serving a team of 12 developers (mix of junior and senior). The system is under critical real-time latency constraints, requiring high performance and reliability for end-users.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits strong structural health with a coupling score of 3.0/10 (indicating low interdependence between components) and exceptional cohesion at 9.7/10 (suggesting well-defined, focused modules). Test coverage is robust at 89.6%, and cyclomatic complexity is minimal at 1.4, pointing to maintainable and low-risk code. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is 0.17, which is healthy and indicates stability. No significant anti-patterns were detected, and the team composition (with a balanced mix of junior and senior developers) supports incremental improvements over a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the real-time latency constraint while preserving the system's structural integrity.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Profile and optimize the most latency-sensitive endpoints using application performance monitoring (APM) tools to identify bottlenecks.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement caching strategies (e.g., Redis) for frequently accessed data to reduce database load and improve response times.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor any identified hotspots in the codebase to further reduce cyclomatic complexity and improve maintainability, if necessary.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce real-time monitoring and alerting to proactively detect and address latency issues before they impact users.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system's structural health and lack of anti-patterns minimize the risk of incremental changes. The primary risk lies in performance tuning efforts that may not yield expected latency improvements, but this can be mitigated through careful profiling and iterative testing."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0142", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.4, "cohesion_score": 4.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 53.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce, développé en .NET/ASP.NET Core avec SQL Server, est une plateforme de vente en ligne en croissance depuis 13 mois. L'équipe de 14 développeurs, composée à moitié de juniors, maintient une codebase de taille moyenne mais fait face à des défis de recrutement sur sa stack technologique actuelle, ce qui limite sa capacité à évoluer rapidement.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase avec des métriques globalement acceptables mais des points de vigilance clairs. Le couplage (4.4/10) et la cohésion (4.6/10) indiquent une architecture modulaire mais avec des zones de friction, notamment dans le module processor.py où des anti-patterns critiques (Long Method et High Coupling) sont détectés. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.7) et la couverture de tests (53.2%) confirment un besoin d'amélioration de la qualité du code, tandis que le ratio de commits correctifs (0.25) suggère une stabilité relative malgré ces problèmes. La pénurie de talents sur la stack actuelle est un facteur de risque opérationnel majeur, mais pas suffisant en soi pour justifier une migration complète.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. L'approche recommandée est une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns identifiés, combinée à des améliorations de la testabilité et de la modularité. Cette stratégie permettra de réduire les risques tout en capitalisant sur l'expertise existante de l'équipe. La pénurie de talents peut être atténuée par une modernisation partielle de la stack (ex: migration vers .NET 8) pour attirer de nouveaux profils sans changer radicalement l'architecture.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Identifier et prioriser les modules critiques à refactorer, en commençant par processor.py. Mettre en place des revues de code systématiques avec des critères de qualité clairs (ex: complexité cyclomatique < 5, couverture de tests > 70% pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Décomposer les Long Methods et réduire le couplage dans processor.py en appliquant le pattern Strategy ou Command. Introduire des interfaces claires pour isoler les responsabilités et faciliter les tests unitaires.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Améliorer la couverture de tests en ciblant d'abord les zones à haute criticité (ex: logique métier, endpoints API). Automatiser les tests de non-régression pour les modules refactorés.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Moderniser progressivement la stack technique (ex: migration vers .NET 8, adoption de minimal APIs pour simplifier les endpoints) pour améliorer l'attractivité du projet auprès des talents, sans changer l'architecture globale.", "duration_days_range": "25-40"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la résistance au changement de l'équipe, notamment des juniors qui pourraient être moins enclins à adopter des pratiques de refactoring avancées. Un autre risque est la sous-estimation de la dette technique cachée dans d'autres modules. Pour les atténuer, il est crucial de former l'équipe aux bonnes pratiques (ex: clean code, SOLID) et de mettre en place des métriques de suivi post-refactoring (ex: réduction de la complexité cyclomatique, augmentation de la couverture de tests)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0142", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 14, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.4, "cohesion_score": 4.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 53.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.25}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "An e-commerce platform built in the last 1.3 years using .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, serving as the core system for a growing online retail operation. The team of 14 developers (mix of junior and senior) faces challenges in hiring and retaining talent with expertise in the current technology stack, which is impacting delivery velocity and system reliability.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with coupling and cohesion scores around 4.5/10, indicating room for improvement but not alarming. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 5.7, and test coverage at 53.2% is suboptimal but not catastrophic. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.25 suggests the hotspot file is not in critical condition, though the presence of high-severity anti-patterns (Long Method and High Coupling) in a core processor file warrants attention. The primary constraint—talent scarcity—is real but does not yet justify a full stack migration, which would introduce significant risk and delay.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring and incremental improvements to address the anti-patterns and improve test coverage. This approach will reduce technical debt, improve maintainability, and make the codebase more attractive to potential hires without the disruption of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address anti-patterns in the hotspot file (src/e-commerce/processor.py): split long methods, reduce coupling, and introduce interfaces or abstractions to improve modularity. Pair with senior developers to mentor juniors during the process.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage by adding unit and integration tests for the refactored components. Prioritize areas with high cyclomatic complexity or recent bug fixes.", "duration_days_range": "12-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural patterns (e.g., CQRS, Domain-Driven Design) in new features to gradually improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Document decisions and share knowledge across the team.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Evaluate and pilot a new technology stack (e.g., Node.js + TypeScript or Go) in a non-critical microservice to assess feasibility and talent appeal. Plan for gradual migration only if the pilot demonstrates clear benefits.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The primary risk is the talent scarcity constraint, which could persist even after refactoring. However, improving code quality and introducing modern patterns may attract new hires. The risk of a full migration (high cost, disruption, and potential failure) outweighs the benefits at this stage. Targeted improvements are reversible and provide immediate value."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0143", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 4.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 30.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.27}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une plateforme de streaming média en Python/Django avec une base de code vieillissante de 11,5 ans, conçue pour gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles dans un secteur concurrentiel. L'équipe de 26 développeurs, majoritairement expérimentée, doit concilier évolutivité technique et maintenance d'une architecture monolithique initialement optimisée pour des charges prévisibles.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs mitigés : un couplage et une cohésion sous-optimaux (4,6/10 et 4,1/10) suggèrent une architecture modulaire insuffisante, tandis qu'une couverture de tests à 30,1% et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 6,2 indiquent un risque élevé de régressions lors de modifications. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, High Coupling) confirment une dette technique concentrée dans des modules critiques comme `core.py` et `processor.py`, ce qui limite la scalabilité horizontale. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0,27) reflète une instabilité localisée mais gérable. La stack Python/Django/PostgreSQL reste pertinente pour le domaine, et l'équipe senior est capable de mener des refactorings ciblés.", "recommendation": "Éviter un rewrite complet coûteux et risqué. Privilégier une stratégie de refactoring incrémental axée sur la réduction des anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration de la testabilité, tout en préparant l'architecture pour une future migration vers une approche modulaire ou microservices si nécessaire. Les gains de scalabilité seront obtenus par des optimisations locales (caching, requêtes batch) plutôt que par une réécriture globale.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi avec identification des dépendances critiques et priorisation des modules à refactorer (basé sur le ratio de commits correctifs et la complexité cyclomatique).", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des anti-patterns majeurs : décomposition du God Class dans `core.py`, réduction des paramètres dans `processor.py`, et découplage de `handler.py` via des interfaces explicites.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests via des tests unitaires ciblés sur les modules refactorés et intégration de tests de charge pour valider les gains de scalabilité.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des goulots d'étranglement identifiés (requêtes SQL, caching Redis) et mise en place d'une documentation technique pour faciliter les futures évolutions.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré si les refactorings sont menés avec une couverture de tests minimale et une revue de code rigoureuse. Le principal risque réside dans l'étendue des modifications sur `core.py` (God Class), qui pourrait impacter temporairement la stabilité si mal géré. Une approche par étapes avec des rollbacks automatisés est fortement recommandée."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0143", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 4.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 30.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.27}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built with Python, Django, and PostgreSQL, serving a user base with unpredictable traffic spikes. The codebase has evolved over 11.5 years, and the team of 26 developers (mix of junior and senior) faces scalability challenges under peak loads, requiring targeted improvements to maintain performance and reliability.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling and cohesion scores (4.6/10 and 4.1/10), indicating room for improvement but not an immediate architectural crisis. Test coverage at 30.1% is low and poses a risk to maintainability and refactoring confidence. Cyclomatic complexity (6.2) is within an acceptable range but could benefit from targeted reductions. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.27) suggests a manageable defect rate, though not ideal. Anti-patterns like God Class, High Coupling, and Long Parameter List are present, particularly in critical files (core.py, handler.py, processor.py), which could hinder scalability and team velocity under load. The dominant constraint—scalability—is not yet critically threatened by these issues, but they must be addressed incrementally to prevent future bottlenecks.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the anti-patterns and low test coverage. Prioritize refactoring the God Class (core.py) and high-coupling modules (handler.py, processor.py) to reduce coupling and improve cohesion. Introduce a phased testing improvement initiative to raise coverage incrementally, starting with critical paths. These steps will enhance maintainability and scalability without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/media/core.py to break it into smaller, focused classes with single responsibilities. Address the High Coupling anti-pattern in src/media/handler.py by introducing interfaces or dependency injection to reduce direct dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the Long Parameter List anti-patterns in src/media/service.py and src/media/processor.py, introducing value objects or parameter objects to encapsulate related data. Begin writing missing tests for the refactored modules to ensure behavioral correctness.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Expand test coverage incrementally, starting with the hottest paths identified by traffic patterns. Introduce property-based testing for critical data processing logic to catch edge cases. Measure coupling and cohesion improvements post-refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks are related to the low test coverage, which could lead to regressions during refactoring. Mitigate this by writing tests for critical paths before refactoring and using feature flags for gradual rollouts. The team's mix of junior and senior developers is a strength, but the refactoring effort should be led by senior engineers to avoid introducing new anti-patterns. The scalability constraint is not yet critical, but unaddressed anti-patterns could exacerbate future performance issues."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0145", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Un SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise en production depuis 4.4 ans, utilisé par des centaines d'entreprises. L'application Ruby on Rails avec une base MySQL doit gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles tout en évoluant avec une équipe de 45 développeurs majoritairement seniors. La scalabilité actuelle est le principal goulot d'étranglement identifié par l'équipe technique.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour une application de cette taille et maturité : un couplage modéré (4.8/10) et une cohésion acceptable (4.4/10) suggèrent une architecture évolutive sans être parfaite. La couverture de tests à 54.9% est faible mais pas critique pour une application Rails mature, surtout avec une équipe expérimentée. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 4.3 reste dans une fourchette raisonnable pour du Ruby. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Parameter List et High Coupling) sont localisés et gérables. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.42 indique que les fichiers chauds ne sont pas excessivement instables. L'équipe expérimentée peut absorber ces dettes techniques sans risque majeur.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack. La dette technique est gérable et localisée, et une migration complète coûterait bien plus cher que des améliorations ciblées. L'équipe a l'expertise nécessaire pour traiter les anti-patterns identifiés sans changer radicalement l'architecture.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoriser les anti-patterns détectés (Long Parameter List dans core.py et High Coupling dans service.py) avec des tests unitaires pour valider les changements.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests en priorisant les modules critiques et les endpoints exposés aux pics de trafic. Ajouter des tests de charge pour valider les améliorations.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimiser la base de données MySQL (indexation, requêtes lentes) et introduire du caching stratégique (Redis) pour absorber les pics de trafic sans refonte majeure.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mettre en place des métriques de monitoring avancées (APM) pour suivre l'impact des changements et identifier de nouveaux goulots d'étranglement.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global faible à modéré. Les améliorations incrémentales ciblées réduiront significativement les goulots d'étranglement sans exposer l'équipe à des risques de migration majeurs. Le principal risque réside dans une sous-estimation de l'impact des pics de trafic sur la base de données, d'où l'importance des tests de charge en phase 2."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0145", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 4.4-year-old SaaS B2B application for business management, built with Ruby on Rails and MySQL. It serves a team of 45 developers (71% senior, 22% junior) and faces unpredictable traffic spikes, making scalability the dominant constraint. The codebase has moderate coupling and cohesion scores, with test coverage at 54.9% and cyclomatic complexity averaging 4.3, indicating room for improvement in maintainability and resilience under load.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal a codebase with moderate structural health: coupling (4.8/10) and cohesion (4.4/10) are neither alarmingly poor nor ideal, while cyclomatic complexity (4.3) suggests manageable complexity per function. Test coverage (54.9%) is below the 80%+ threshold often recommended for safe refactoring, and the bugfix-commit ratio (0.42) on the hottest file indicates a file that may be a bottleneck. The detected anti-patterns—Long Parameter List in core.py and High Coupling in service.py—are localized and medium-severity, suggesting targeted refactoring could yield significant benefits without a full rewrite. The team’s senior-heavy composition (71%) is well-suited for incremental improvements, as they can safely execute refactoring with minimal oversight. The scalability constraint is real but does not yet justify a technology shift; instead, it highlights the need for architectural improvements within the existing stack.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate to a new stack. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address scalability and maintainability. The current metrics do not justify a full rewrite, and the team’s size and skill level make targeted refactoring a more pragmatic path. The anti-patterns and moderate coupling/cohesion scores are addressable through disciplined engineering practices and small, iterative changes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address anti-patterns and improve test coverage. Start with the hottest file (src/saas/service.py) to reduce coupling by applying the Single Responsibility Principle and extracting smaller, focused services. Parallelly, incrementally increase test coverage to at least 70% by adding missing tests for critical paths, prioritizing areas with high cyclomatic complexity.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor src/saas/core.py to eliminate the Long Parameter List anti-pattern by introducing parameter objects or dependency injection. Pair this with performance profiling under simulated traffic spikes to identify and address bottlenecks in the current stack.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement caching strategies (e.g., Redis) and database optimizations (e.g., read replicas, query indexing) to directly address scalability constraints. Introduce horizontal scaling mechanisms (e.g., Kubernetes) if profiling shows they are necessary, but only after validating improvements in the existing stack.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish engineering practices to prevent regression: enforce code reviews for structural changes, introduce static analysis tools (e.g., RuboCop for Ruby) to catch anti-patterns early, and adopt a blameless postmortem culture for outages to drive continuous improvement.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks are related to the team’s ability to execute refactoring without introducing regressions, given the current test coverage. However, the senior-heavy team composition mitigates this risk. The anti-patterns are localized, and the scalability constraint can be addressed incrementally without a full rewrite. The biggest risk is failing to prioritize the hottest file (src/saas/service.py), which could lead to continued bottlenecks. Mitigation involves close monitoring of performance metrics during refactoring and phased rollouts of changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0147", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.2, "cohesion_score": 2.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 7.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.52}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a long-standing (14.8 years) edtech platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 44 developers (39% junior, 34% senior). The primary business constraint is escalating cloud costs, prompting a review of the codebase's maintainability and technical debt to identify opportunities for optimization and cost reduction without a full rewrite.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural issues that hinder maintainability and scalability. The cohesion score of 2.4/10 indicates poor separation of concerns, while the coupling score of 7.2/10 suggests excessive interdependence between components. Test coverage is critically low at 7.5%, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 7.9 points to overly complex functions. Anti-patterns such as circular dependencies, god classes, and long parameter lists are widespread, particularly in core files like src/edtech/core.py and src/edtech/service.py. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.52 on the hottest file further signals fragility in critical areas. These metrics collectively point to a codebase that is difficult to extend, debug, and optimize, exacerbating cloud cost inefficiencies.", "recommendation": "A full migration is not justified given the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and structural flaws. Prioritize breaking down god classes, resolving circular dependencies, and reducing coupling in the most problematic files. Simultaneously, incrementally improve test coverage to enable safer refactoring. These steps will directly address the cloud cost constraint by improving efficiency and maintainability without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a detailed architectural review to identify the top 5 most critical files contributing to cloud cost inefficiencies (e.g., high coupling, god classes, circular dependencies). Prioritize these files for refactoring based on their impact on cloud resource usage and maintenance burden.", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address circular dependencies in src/edtech/core.py and src/edtech/service.py by introducing dependency injection or breaking modules into smaller, focused components. Implement interfaces or abstract classes to decouple high-level modules from low-level details.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the god class in src/edtech/core.py by splitting it into smaller, cohesive classes with single responsibilities. Introduce domain-driven design principles to improve cohesion and reduce coupling.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Tackle long parameter lists in src/edtech/handler.py, src/edtech/processor.py, and src/edtech/service.py by introducing parameter objects or data transfer objects (DTOs) to encapsulate related parameters.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage for the refactored modules, starting with the most critical paths. Aim for a baseline of 20-30% coverage in these areas to enable safer future refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 6, "action": "Implement observability and monitoring improvements to identify cloud cost drivers and validate the impact of refactoring efforts. Use this data to prioritize further optimizations.", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks are related to the fragility of the codebase and the team's capacity to execute refactoring safely. Without adequate test coverage, refactoring could introduce regressions, so the incremental approach is critical. Additionally, the high proportion of junior developers may slow progress, requiring close mentorship and code reviews from senior engineers. The circular dependencies and god classes pose a significant risk of unintended side effects during refactoring, so these must be addressed methodically. However, the alternative—a full rewrite—carries far greater risk of failure, cost, and timeline overruns, making incremental improvement the pragmatic choice."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0148", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.2, "cohesion_score": 9.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 80.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un backend de plateforme de streaming media en Python/FastAPI, en production depuis 6,5 ans. Il gère le traitement et la diffusion de contenus pour des millions d'utilisateurs, avec une stack technique stable mais un coût cloud en hausse qui impacte la rentabilité. L'équipe de 6 développeurs, composée majoritairement de profils expérimentés, maintient une base de code mature avec une bonne couverture fonctionnelle.", "analysis": "La base de code présente des métriques saines : un couplage très faible (2,2/10) et une cohésion excellente (9,4/10) indiquent une architecture modulaire bien structurée. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 1,5 et le ratio de commits correctifs de 0,08 sur le fichier le plus actif suggèrent une stabilité du code et une maintenabilité élevée. La couverture de tests à 80,4% est satisfaisante pour un projet de cette taille et de cet âge. Le seul anti-pattern détecté (duplicate code low dans src/media/core.py) est mineur et isolé, sans impact majeur sur la maintenabilité globale.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. Les problèmes de coût cloud doivent être adressés en priorité par des optimisations ciblées (ex: analyse des requêtes SQL, ajustement des instances cloud, caching) plutôt qu'un changement de stack. La base de code est suffisamment saine pour évoluer de manière incrémentale.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud et identification des leviers d'optimisation (requêtes lentes, instances surdimensionnées, stockage inefficace)", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correction de l'anti-pattern Duplicate Code dans src/media/core.py et refactoring minimal pour améliorer la lisibilité", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un plan de monitoring des performances et des coûts pour valider l'impact des optimisations", "duration_days_range": "2-4"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré : les métriques indiquent une base de code mature et maintenable. Le principal risque réside dans une optimisation cloud mal ciblée qui pourrait dégrader les performances. Une approche progressive et mesurée (phases 1 à 3) limite ce risque."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0148", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.2, "cohesion_score": 9.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 80.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.08}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built over 6.5 years using Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL. The team of 6 developers (including a mix of junior and senior engineers) maintains a codebase that has grown organically, with a dominant operational constraint around escalating cloud costs that requires immediate attention and optimization.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits strong internal quality metrics: low coupling (2.2/10) and high cohesion (9.4/10) indicate a well-structured system with clear separation of concerns. Test coverage is solid at 80.4%, and cyclomatic complexity is low (1.5), suggesting maintainable and robust logic. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.08 on the hottest file is healthy, indicating that the most active component is not a hotspot for defects. The only anti-pattern detected is a low level of duplicate code in a single file, which is not systemic. The primary constraint—cloud cost—is operational rather than architectural, and the current stack is well-suited to address it through targeted optimizations rather than a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the system. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the cloud cost issue and the minor anti-pattern. The current architecture and code quality are healthy enough to support targeted optimizations without the risk and overhead of a full migration.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit to identify inefficiencies (e.g., idle resources, over-provisioned services) and implement optimizations such as right-sizing, auto-scaling, and caching strategies.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the duplicate code in src/media/core.py to improve maintainability and reduce technical debt.", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement additional monitoring and alerting to proactively detect and address cost spikes or performance regressions.", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system's strong internal quality metrics reduce the risk of introducing defects during incremental changes. The primary risk lies in the cloud cost optimization phase, where misconfigurations could temporarily impact performance or availability. However, this risk is mitigated by thorough testing and phased rollouts. The minor anti-pattern does not pose a significant risk to the system's stability or scalability."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0149", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.3, "cohesion_score": 7.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 86.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une application SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise développée en .NET/ASP.NET Core avec SQL Server, en production depuis 1.4 ans. L'équipe de 29 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, maintient une base de code stable sans contrainte critique identifiée, tout en assurant une couverture de tests élevée et une complexité maîtrisée.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales de la codebase sont saines : couplage faible (2.3/10), cohésion acceptable (7.0/10), couverture de tests élevée (86%), et complexité cyclomatique moyenne (2.6) bien en dessous des seuils critiques. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le ratio de commits correctifs bas (0.15) confirment une base technique solide. La répartition de l'équipe (66% juniors) suggère un besoin de mentorat plutôt que de refonte technologique.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour renforcer la maintenabilité et accélérer l'onboarding des juniors, sans prendre le risque d'une réécriture complète qui perturberait la stabilité opérationnelle.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Renforcer la documentation technique et les guides d'onboarding pour les développeurs juniors, en ciblant les modules les plus complexes identifiés par la complexité cyclomatique.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mettre en place des revues de code systématiques avec un focus sur l'amélioration progressive de la cohésion et la réduction du couplage résiduel, via des refactorings ciblés.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Automatiser davantage les tests d'intégration pour atteindre une couverture proche de 90%, en priorisant les endpoints critiques du SaaS.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour les améliorations incrémentales proposées. Aucun risque majeur identifié pour une migration partielle ou une réécriture, mais un risque élevé de perturbation opérationnelle et de perte de productivité en cas de refonte complète."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0150", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.9, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet pilote une plateforme de gestion logistique pour un réseau de 15 entrepôts en Europe, développée en Python/Django avec MongoDB pour répondre à des besoins de traçabilité en temps réel. L'application centralise les flux de marchandises, les stocks et les livraisons, mais souffre d'une dette technique croissante qui impacte la maintenabilité et génère des coûts cloud imprévisibles, notamment via des requêtes MongoDB mal optimisées et des dépendances circulaires dans les services critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de 10 ans : un couplage modéré (4.9/10) et une cohésion acceptable (4.4/10) indiquent une architecture encore gérable, malgré des anti-patterns localisés (dépendances circulaires dans src/logistique/service.py). La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.7) et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.38) suggèrent une stabilité relative, mais la couverture de tests à 54.8% est un point de vigilance critique pour toute évolution. Le coût cloud dérapant est davantage lié à des problèmes d'optimisation (requêtes, indexes) qu'à la stack technologique elle-même. L'équipe, majoritairement junior, bénéficierait d'un accompagnement ciblé plutôt que d'une refonte radicale.", "recommendation": "Éviter un rewrite complet coûteux et risqué. Privilégier une approche incrémentale centrée sur la réduction de la dette technique et l'optimisation des coûts cloud, en ciblant les anti-patterns identifiés et en améliorant la couverture de tests. Une migration vers une stack alternative (ex: Java/Spring) n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles et serait contre-productive pour une équipe majoritairement junior.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi pour identifier les 20% de code responsables de 80% des coûts cloud (requêtes MongoDB, dépendances circulaires, etc.) et prioriser les correctifs.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation ciblée de src/logistique/service.py pour éliminer les dépendances circulaires et réduire le couplage, avec ajout de tests unitaires pour valider les changements.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes MongoDB (indexes, agrégations) et mise en place d'un monitoring des coûts cloud pour mesurer l'impact des corrections.", "duration_days_range": "10-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques (tests, design modulaire) et mise en place d'un processus de revue de code pour éviter la régression des anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "8-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour les phases 1 à 3, sous réserve d'une priorisation rigoureuse des correctifs. Le risque majeur réside dans la phase 4 : sans accompagnement actif, l'équipe junior pourrait reproduire les mêmes erreurs. Une migration vers une nouvelle stack serait un risque élevé (délai, coût, courbe d'apprentissage) sans garantie de gain tangible."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0150", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.9, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a logistics and supply chain platform built over 10 years using Python, Django, and MongoDB. It currently faces escalating cloud costs and is maintained by a team with a high proportion of junior developers. The system manages critical operations for logistics workflows, requiring both stability and cost efficiency.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with coupling and cohesion scores around 5/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe decay. Test coverage at 54.8% is suboptimal and contributes to a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.38 on the hottest file, suggesting fragility in key areas. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 6.7, but the presence of circular dependencies and high coupling in a core service file (src/logistique/service.py) introduces maintenance risk. The dominant constraint—rising cloud costs—is likely driven more by inefficient resource usage or architecture than by the codebase’s structural issues.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and technical debt. The current metrics do not justify a high-risk, high-cost rewrite, especially given the team’s junior-heavy composition and the system’s operational criticality.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor src/logistique/service.py to eliminate circular dependencies and reduce coupling. Introduce dependency injection and modularize tightly coupled components. Pair with senior developers to mentor juniors during the process.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage incrementally, prioritizing critical paths and the refactored service module. Aim to raise coverage to at least 65% within 3 months through targeted test additions.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit to identify inefficiencies (e.g., idle resources, over-provisioned services). Implement optimizations such as right-sizing, reserved instances, or caching layers without altering the core architecture.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce lightweight monitoring and alerting for key performance and cost metrics. Document the refactored service module and update onboarding materials to reflect architectural changes.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the junior-heavy team’s ability to safely refactor core components without introducing regressions. Mitigation includes pairing seniors with juniors, prioritizing small, reversible changes, and maintaining comprehensive rollback procedures. The circular dependency and coupling issues are localized, reducing systemic risk. Cloud cost optimization carries operational risk but is reversible and non-invasive to the codebase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0151", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.9, "cohesion_score": 5.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme de gestion de comptes joueurs pour un studio de jeux en ligne en croissance, avec intégration de paiements sécurisés et gestion des données de santé (HDS). Le système doit répondre aux exigences strictes de conformité RGPD et PCI-DSS tout en supportant une charge transactionnelle élevée. L'équipe technique, majoritairement senior, maintient une codebase Node.js vieillissante de 3.7 ans avec des composants critiques comme le processeur de transactions gaming et le cœur métier.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs de santé technique mitigés mais gérables : un couplage modéré (4.9/10) et une cohésion faible (5.2/10) suggèrent une architecture modulaire perfectible, tandis qu'une complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.4) et une couverture de tests limitée (37%) indiquent un besoin d'amélioration de la testabilité. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, dépendances circulaires, duplication) sont concentrés dans deux fichiers centraux (processor.py et core.py), ce qui limite leur impact global. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.44) reste acceptable pour une codebase de cet âge. La contrainte de conformité réglementaire, bien que critique, ne justifie pas en soi une migration technologique si les patterns de sécurité actuels (chiffrement, isolation des données) sont correctement implémentés.", "recommendation": "Privilégier une approche d'amélioration incrémentale ciblée plutôt qu'une migration complète. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont localisés et peuvent être résolus par des refactorings progressifs sans impacter l'ensemble du système. La conformité réglementaire doit être traitée en priorité via des audits et des renforcements de sécurité incrémentaux, plutôt que par un changement de stack. Une migration ne serait justifiée que si les coûts de maintenance deviennent prohibitifs (ex: impossibilité de recruter sur la stack actuelle) ou si les exigences réglementaires évoluent vers des besoins non supportés par la stack actuelle.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit de sécurité réglementaire et identification des gaps PCI-DSS/RGPD/HDS dans l'architecture actuelle", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental du God Class dans src/gaming/processor.py avec extraction de responsabilités en services dédiés", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Résolution des dépendances circulaires dans src/gaming/core.py via réorganisation des imports et introduction d'interfaces", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests (objectif 60%) via ajout de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de qualité continue (linting, analyse statique, tests automatiques) pour prévenir la régression des anti-patterns", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour les phases de refactoring incrémental si les tests existants sont fiables. Risque modéré à élevé si la conformité réglementaire nécessite des changements architecturaux majeurs (ex: ré-architecture des flux de données). Le principal risque réside dans l'absence de tests automatisés fiables pour valider les changements, ce qui pourrait introduire des régressions. Une approche par feature flags et tests de canary serait recommandée pour les modules critiques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0151", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.9, "cohesion_score": 5.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "This gaming platform, operational for 3.7 years, supports 20 developers and must comply with stringent regulations including RGPD, PCI-DSS, and HDS. Built on Node.js/Express with MongoDB, the system processes high-stakes transactions and player data, requiring both regulatory adherence and high availability.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with coupling (4.9/10) and cohesion (5.2/10) scores near the midpoint, indicating room for improvement but not critical failure. Test coverage at 37% is low and poses a compliance risk under RGPD and PCI-DSS, where traceability and validation are essential. Cyclomatic complexity (5.4) is acceptable but concentrated in critical modules like the gaming processor and core logic. Anti-patterns such as God Classes, circular dependencies, and duplicate code are present, particularly in gaming/processor.py and gaming/core.py, which increases maintenance risk and regulatory non-conformance potential. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.44 suggests active maintenance but may reflect underlying fragility in core components.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring and incremental improvements to address regulatory risks and code quality issues. The current stack is adequate for compliance if structural and testing deficiencies are resolved.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement targeted refactoring to resolve anti-patterns: split God Class in gaming/processor.py, break long parameter lists in gaming/core.py, and eliminate circular dependencies. Prioritize modules with high bugfix ratios.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 60% through incremental test writing, focusing on critical paths for RGPD data handling and PCI-DSS transaction flows. Integrate automated compliance checks in CI/CD.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Apply modular design patterns to improve cohesion and reduce coupling in gaming/core.py and gaming/processor.py. Introduce dependency injection to break circular dependencies and improve testability.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a regulatory compliance audit of the refactored codebase, validate data handling and security controls, and update documentation to reflect architectural changes.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium. The current architecture is maintainable but fragile in critical areas. Without intervention, regulatory risks and technical debt will escalate, potentially leading to compliance violations or outages. Refactoring carries short-term risk of introducing regressions, but is manageable with strong test coverage and phased rollouts. The team’s seniority profile supports incremental improvement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0152", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 9.8, "cohesion_score": 2.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 6.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 8.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.68}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 10-year-old Node.js/NestJS marketplace platform with 38 developers, operating under strict uptime requirements due to frequent production incidents. The codebase exhibits severe structural issues with extremely high coupling (9.8/10) and very low cohesion (2.1/10), leading to maintenance challenges and reliability concerns in critical components like marketplace handlers and core services.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal a codebase in critical condition with extreme coupling and cohesion problems. The 9.8/10 coupling score indicates components are excessively interdependent, making changes risky and error-prone. The 6.4% test coverage means there's virtually no safety net for modifications. The high bugfix-commit ratio (0.68) on hot files confirms these components are major sources of production incidents. Anti-patterns like God Classes and circular dependencies are concentrated in core marketplace modules, creating a fragile architecture where changes in one area can cascade failures throughout the system.", "recommendation": "This codebase requires immediate architectural intervention rather than a full rewrite. The extreme coupling and lack of cohesion make a rewrite premature - the same problems would manifest in new code without structural changes. Instead, we need a systematic refactoring approach focused on breaking circular dependencies, decomposing God Classes, and gradually improving test coverage while maintaining system stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct architectural assessment and define modular boundaries for the marketplace core. Implement dependency inversion in the most problematic modules (handler.py, core.py) to break circular dependencies. Establish clear service boundaries and introduce interfaces for critical components.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decompose God Classes in core modules by extracting cohesive services. Implement the Strangler Fig pattern to gradually replace problematic components while maintaining system functionality. Add targeted test coverage for critical paths before making structural changes.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the service layer to reduce coupling and improve cohesion. Implement proper dependency injection and introduce facade patterns where appropriate. Establish API contracts between modules to prevent future circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Gradually improve test coverage in refactored areas while maintaining production stability. Implement monitoring and rollback procedures for each refactored component. Establish architectural governance to prevent regression of coupling metrics.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High immediate risk due to current production instability and extreme coupling. The refactoring approach mitigates rewrite risks but requires careful change management. The team's junior/senior ratio (36% junior) suggests strong mentorship will be needed during architectural changes. Without intervention, production incidents will likely increase as the codebase becomes more difficult to maintain."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0153", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 3, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.7, "cohesion_score": 2.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 28.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 10.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.86}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a gaming backend service built with Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, running for 8.5 years with a small team of three developers (77% junior). The primary challenge is slow feature delivery, with the team identifying velocity as the dominant constraint affecting time-to-market for new gaming features and updates.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural issues that directly impact development velocity. The coupling score of 7.7/10 and cohesion score of 2.8/10 indicate a highly interdependent system where changes in one area can unpredictably affect others, leading to slower development cycles. The low test coverage (28.1%) and high cyclomatic complexity (10.9) compound this problem by making the codebase difficult to modify safely. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.86 on the hottest file suggests that hotspots are frequently patched rather than refactored, perpetuating technical debt. The repeated detection of circular dependencies and high coupling in core gaming modules (handler.py, service.py) confirms that the architecture is brittle and resistant to change. Given the team's junior-heavy composition, these issues are likely exacerbating delivery bottlenecks, as less experienced developers struggle to navigate and modify tightly coupled code safely.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the structural and quality issues that are directly impacting delivery speed. A full rewrite would introduce excessive risk given the team's experience level and the lack of clear architectural vision to justify such a drastic step. The metrics clearly justify targeted refactoring and process improvements to reduce coupling, improve test coverage, and simplify the codebase.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address circular dependencies and high coupling in the hottest files (src/gaming/service.py, src/gaming/handler.py). Introduce dependency inversion and extract interfaces to break circular references. Begin with the most problematic files to reduce immediate friction in development.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage by adding unit and integration tests for the refactored modules. Focus on critical paths and public APIs to ensure safe modifications. Pair junior developers with senior mentors to accelerate knowledge transfer and improve test-writing skills.", "duration_days_range": "12-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor high-complexity functions to reduce cyclomatic complexity. Break down large functions into smaller, single-responsibility units. Introduce linting and static analysis tools to enforce complexity thresholds and prevent regressions.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement architectural boundaries using module boundaries or lightweight service layers to reduce coupling between gaming modules. Introduce a modular design (e.g., domain-driven design light) to improve cohesion and make the system more adaptable to change.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Establish code review and pair programming practices to prevent the reintroduction of anti-patterns. Introduce automated checks in CI to block circular dependencies and high coupling from being merged. Conduct a retrospective to identify further bottlenecks and plan the next cycle of improvements.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risk is the potential for refactoring to introduce new bugs if not properly tested. However, this risk is mitigated by the phased approach, which prioritizes the most problematic files first and gradually expands improvements. The junior-heavy team composition increases the risk of slower progress or misunderstandings during refactoring, but pairing with senior developers and focusing on incremental changes reduces this risk. The lack of a full rewrite recommendation eliminates the high risk associated with technology migrations, especially given the team's inexperience with such projects."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0154", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 5.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.41}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel, en production depuis près de 11 ans, gère le traitement en temps réel des données de capteurs pour des infrastructures critiques. L'application, développée en Node.js/NestJS avec une base PostgreSQL, doit garantir un uptime maximal pour éviter des pertes financières et opérationnelles significatives. L'équipe technique, composée de 11 développeurs aux profils variés, fait face à des défis de fiabilité récurrents malgré une expertise majoritairement senior.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase mature mais fragilisée par des problèmes structurels persistants. Le couplage élevé (5.3/10) et la cohésion moyenne (5.7/10) indiquent une architecture qui peine à isoler les responsabilités, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.8) et la couverture de tests insuffisante (47.5%) expliquent en partie les incidents de production fréquents. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Classes, couplage fort, paramètres longs) confirment une dette technique concentrée dans les modules centraux (iot/core.py, iot/processor.py, iot/service.py), où les modifications deviennent risquées. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.41) sur le fichier le plus chaud suggère un effet 'boule de neige' : plus on corrige, plus le code se dégrade.", "recommendation": "Une refonte complète serait contre-productive à ce stade. Les métriques, bien que perfectibles, ne justifient pas un rewrite radical qui exposerait l'entreprise à des risques opérationnels majeurs. L'approche incrémentale est préférable : cibler d'abord les anti-patterns les plus critiques (God Classes et couplage) pour réduire la fréquence des incidents, tout en améliorant progressivement la couverture de tests et la modularité. Une migration technologique n'est pas recommandée ici, car la stack actuelle (Node.js/NestJS) est maîtrisée par l'équipe et adaptée au domaine IoT industriel.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Identifier et prioriser les classes/méthodes à risque dans les modules iot/core.py, iot/processor.py et iot/service.py. Documenter les dépendances et les flux de données critiques pour préparer les refactorings.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Décomposer les God Classes en responsabilités plus petites via des extractions de méthodes/classes (ex: séparer la logique de traitement des données de la gestion des connexions). Appliquer des principes SOLID pour réduire le couplage.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Améliorer la couverture de tests pour les modules refactorisés, en ciblant d'abord les chemins critiques liés aux incidents de production. Intégrer des tests de régression automatisés dans le pipeline CI.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduire des mécanismes de monitoring et de circuit breaking pour les composants critiques, afin de limiter l'impact des futures modifications. Former l'équipe aux bonnes pratiques de conception modulaire.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la régression fonctionnelle lors des refactorings des God Classes, surtout si les tests existants sont insuffisants. Pour l'atténuer, prévoir des revues de code approfondies et des tests manuels ciblés sur les fonctionnalités critiques. Un autre risque est la résistance au changement de la part des développeurs habitués à la codebase actuelle, d'où l'importance de démontrer rapidement les bénéfices des améliorations (ex: réduction des incidents). Enfin, la complexité cyclomatique élevée pourrait ralentir les modifications futures si les refactorings ne sont pas menés avec rigueur."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0154", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 5.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.41}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10.8-year-old industrial IoT platform built with Node.js/NestJS and PostgreSQL, serving as the backbone for critical infrastructure monitoring. Reliability and uptime are the top priorities due to frequent production incidents, and the team of 11 developers (with a mix of junior and senior engineers) is under pressure to stabilize the system while maintaining feature delivery.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural issues with a coupling score of 5.3/10 and cohesion at 5.7/10, indicating room for improvement but not an outright crisis. The test coverage of 47.5% is concerning, especially given the reliability constraints, as it suggests insufficient safety nets for changes. Cyclomatic complexity (6.8) is manageable but not ideal, while the bugfix-commit ratio of 0.41 on the hottest file signals a hotspot prone to regressions. Anti-patterns like God Classes and high coupling in core modules are actively contributing to the uptime issues by making the system brittle and hard to modify safely.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical pain points: reliability and maintainability. The metrics do not justify a full rewrite, but they do demand immediate action to prevent further degradation.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Stabilize the hotspot files by extracting responsibilities from the God Classes (src/iot/processor.py and src/iot/core.py) into smaller, single-purpose modules. Introduce unit tests for these modules to reach at least 60% coverage on the extracted code. Address the high coupling in src/iot/core.py by introducing interfaces or dependency inversion to reduce direct dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage across the codebase by adding integration tests for critical paths (e.g., IoT message processing, database interactions) and unit tests for complex logic. Aim to raise overall coverage to 65-70% to reduce regression risk.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the service layer (src/iot/service.py) to address the Long Parameter List anti-pattern by introducing DTOs or value objects. This will improve readability and reduce the likelihood of bugs introduced during modifications.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement observability improvements (e.g., structured logging, metrics, tracing) to reduce mean time to detection (MTTD) and mean time to resolution (MTTR) for incidents. Pair this with a post-incident review process to address root causes systematically.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium. The risks are primarily operational: changes to core modules (e.g., src/iot/core.py) could introduce regressions if not thoroughly tested. However, the incremental approach mitigates this by focusing on small, testable slices. The team's mix of junior and senior developers is a strength but requires careful mentorship to avoid introducing new anti-patterns during refactoring. The biggest risk is failing to prioritize reliability improvements over new features, which could perpetuate the uptime issues."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0155", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.37}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une plateforme SaaS de gestion de données médicales en temps réel, utilisée par des hôpitaux et cliniques pour centraliser les dossiers patients et synchroniser les informations entre systèmes. L'application doit gérer des pics de trafic soudains liés à des urgences ou des campagnes de dépistage, tout en garantissant une latence minimale pour les requêtes critiques. Développée en Python avec FastAPI et PostgreSQL, elle est maintenue par une équipe de 21 développeurs avec une expérience mixte, mais une forte expertise sur la stack technique.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de 8 ans : un couplage modéré (4.1/10) et une cohésion acceptable (5.4/10) indiquent une architecture modulaire mais avec des zones de friction. La couverture de tests à 48.5% est insuffisante pour une application critique en santé, mais reste dans la moyenne pour un legacy. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.0) est maîtrisable, bien qu'elle puisse masquer des risques de maintenabilité. Les anti-patterns détectés (dépendances circulaires, duplication, couplage élevé) sont concentrés dans des fichiers spécifiques (processor.py, handler.py), ce qui limite leur impact global. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.37) suggère une stabilité relative, mais avec des zones de fragilité localisées.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. Les problèmes identifiés sont ciblés et peuvent être résolus par des refactorings incrémentaux, sans remettre en cause l'architecture globale. L'objectif prioritaire doit être d'améliorer la testabilité et la résilience des composants critiques, tout en réduisant les anti-patterns identifiés. Une approche progressive permettra de valider les gains sans interrompre le service.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyse approfondie des anti-patterns et identification des dépendances problématiques dans processor.py et handler.py. Priorisation des corrections en fonction de leur impact sur la scalabilité.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Ajout de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les composants critiques (cibler un minimum de 70% de couverture pour les fichiers processor.py et handler.py). Intégration continue avec des pipelines de qualité renforcés.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns détectés : résolution des dépendances circulaires, élimination des duplications dans handler.py, et réduction du couplage dans processor.py via une décomposition en modules plus petits.", "duration_days_range": "15-25 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes PostgreSQL et mise en place de mécanismes de caching (Redis) pour les endpoints critiques, en ciblant les pics de trafic identifiés. Benchmarking avant/après pour valider les gains de performance.", "duration_days_range": "10-20 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Documentation des changements et formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques (modularité, testabilité, gestion des dépendances). Mise à jour des runbooks pour les opérations critiques.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la résistance au changement dans une équipe mixte (juniors/seniors), mais les refactorings ciblés minimisent l'impact. Un risque technique résiduel concerne la scalabilité des optimisations PostgreSQL, qui devra être monitorée en production. La couverture de tests actuelle limite la confiance dans les modifications, d'où l'importance de la phase 2. Aucun risque majeur de migration n'est identifié, car l'approche est incrémentale et réversible."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0155", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.37}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a healthcare data processing platform built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 21 developers. It handles unpredictable traffic spikes while processing sensitive medical data, requiring both scalability and reliability under strict regulatory constraints.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 4.1/10 and cohesion at 5.4/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe decay. Test coverage at 48.5% is concerning for a safety-critical system, though the bugfix-commit ratio of 0.37 on the hottest file suggests the team is actively addressing issues. The cyclomatic complexity of 6.0 is acceptable but could benefit from refactoring. The anti-patterns—particularly the high coupling in src/sante/processor.py—are the most critical issues, as they directly impact scalability and maintainability during traffic peaks.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and increase test coverage. These changes will improve scalability and reliability without the high risk and cost of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-coupling anti-pattern in src/sante/processor.py by applying dependency inversion and extracting cohesive components. Parallelly, begin incrementally increasing test coverage to at least 65% by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor src/sante/handler.py to eliminate duplicate code by extracting shared logic into reusable modules. Introduce consistent error handling and logging patterns across the codebase to reduce future maintenance burden.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement horizontal scaling strategies for PostgreSQL and FastAPI, such as read replicas and async task queues, to better handle unpredictable traffic spikes. Add monitoring and alerting to proactively detect performance bottlenecks.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The recommended approach avoids a full rewrite, reducing the risk of project disruption. However, refactoring core components like processor.py carries some risk of introducing regressions. Mitigation includes thorough testing, incremental rollouts, and close monitoring during changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0157", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.0, "cohesion_score": 8.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.03}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel, en production depuis 3 ans, gère le traitement et l'analyse de données issues de capteurs déployés dans des environnements industriels critiques. La stack PHP/Laravel/MySQL a été choisie pour sa maturité dans le secteur et sa capacité à évoluer rapidement avec les besoins métiers tout en garantissant une stabilité opérationnelle.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une base de code saine et bien structurée : un couplage faible (2.0/10) suggère une architecture modulaire, tandis qu'une cohésion élevée (8.1/10) confirme que les responsabilités sont bien délimitées. La couverture de tests à 72.9% est un bon point d'ancrage pour des évolutions futures, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2.7 reste dans une plage acceptable pour une application métier. Le ratio de commits correctifs très bas (0.03) sur le fichier le plus actif est un indicateur fort de stabilité. L'anti-pattern 'God Class' détecté est de faible criticité et peut être traité de manière ciblée sans impacter l'architecture globale.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. La stack PHP/Laravel/MySQL répond aux besoins du projet avec une efficacité prouvée, et les métriques ne révèlent aucune contrainte bloquante. Une approche incrémentale pour améliorer la maintenabilité et la testabilité est préférable à un changement radical.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor ciblé du God Class identifié (src/iot/handler.py) pour le diviser en responsabilités plus fines, avec ajout de tests unitaires pour valider le comportement", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests sur les modules critiques (objectif : atteindre 80%+) en priorisant les endpoints API et les services métiers principaux", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit de sécurité et optimisation des requêtes SQL les plus fréquentes pour réduire la charge sur MySQL, avec un focus sur les endpoints critiques", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible à modéré. Les risques liés à un refactor incrémental sont maîtrisés grâce aux métriques solides (couplage, cohésion, complexité). Le principal risque réside dans l'introduction de bugs lors du refactor du God Class, mais celui-ci est atténué par la faible criticité de l'anti-pattern et la couverture de tests existante. Aucun risque critique n'a été identifié dans les données fournies."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0158", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.2, "cohesion_score": 1.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 22.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.88}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet pilote la plateforme de gestion des flux logistiques pour un réseau de 15 entrepôts européens, avec une stack technique Node.js/NestJS et PostgreSQL en production depuis 12 ans. L'application doit absorber des pics de trafic soudains liés aux variations de demande saisonnière, tout en intégrant en temps réel les données de suivi des transporteurs tiers.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs contrastés : un couplage global maîtrisé (8.2/10) contraste avec une cohésion très faible (1.2/10), révélant une architecture en silos où les modules logistiques communiquent peu entre eux. La couverture de tests à 22.7% et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 9.6 indiquent un code peu testable et difficile à maintenir. Les anti-patterns détectés (duplications, dépendances circulaires, listes de paramètres longues) sont concentrés dans trois fichiers centraux, suggérant une dette technique localisée plutôt qu'un problème systémique. La scalabilité actuelle semble contrainte davantage par l'architecture que par la stack technique elle-même.", "recommendation": "Ne pas envisager de migration technologique ou de rewrite complet. La dette technique est ciblée et gérable par des refactorings incrémentaux. L'amélioration de la cohésion doit être prioritaire pour réduire les risques lors des évolutions futures, notamment pour absorber les pics de trafic. La stack actuelle Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL reste adaptée au contexte logistique si l'architecture est restructurée.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyse approfondie des dépendances circulaires dans src/logistique/handler.py et identification des responsabilités à extraire dans des modules dédiés. Création de tests de régression pour les fonctionnalités critiques avant toute modification.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des trois fichiers identifiés comme problématiques (service.py, processor.py, handler.py) pour éliminer les duplications et réduire la complexité cyclomatique. Introduction de DTOs pour simplifier les listes de paramètres et découpler les modules.", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la cohésion globale par la définition d'interfaces claires entre les modules logistiques et mise en place de tests unitaires pour valider les nouvelles interactions. Déploiement progressif en environnement de staging avec monitoring des métriques de performance.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Planification d'une stratégie de tests automatisés pour atteindre un seuil minimal de 60% de couverture sur les modules critiques, avec intégration continue dans le pipeline de déploiement.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré si les refactorings sont menés avec une couverture de tests minimale et des déploiements incrémentaux. Le principal risque réside dans les dépendances circulaires qui pourraient impacter la stabilité si mal gérées. Une approche par étapes avec validation systématique réduit significativement ce risque. La scalabilité ne sera améliorée qu'après restructuration de l'architecture, pas avant."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0159", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.6, "cohesion_score": 9.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 88.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.11}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce, en production depuis plus de 10 ans, sert des milliers de transactions quotidiennes avec une stack technique Node.js/Express et MongoDB. L'équipe de 44 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, maintient une base de code stable malgré une croissance organique importante, avec une contrainte critique non identifiée à ce stade.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales sont saines : couplage faible (1.6/10), cohésion excellente (9.7/10), couverture de tests élevée (88.3%) et complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée (2.2). Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.11) indique une stabilité remarquable. Le seul anti-pattern détecté (God Class dans un handler) est marginal et ne justifie pas une refonte. L'équipe junior majoritaire suggère plutôt un besoin de renforcement des bonnes pratiques que de migration technologique.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration n'est justifiée par les données. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées : correction du God Class identifié, renforcement des revues de code pour les juniors, et optimisation des performances locales si nécessaire. Une migration vers une nouvelle stack n'apporterait pas de valeur tangible compte tenu de la santé actuelle du code.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Correction du God Class dans src/e-commerce/handler.py et refactorisation associée pour améliorer la maintenabilité", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour les développeurs juniors avec focus sur les bonnes pratiques de modularité", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Audit de performance ciblé sur les endpoints critiques pour identifier d'éventuelles optimisations locales", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible pour les actions proposées : les modifications sont locales et réversibles. Aucun risque de blocage majeur identifié. La stabilité actuelle du projet permet une approche progressive sans pression temporelle."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0160", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme SaaS éducative en Python/Django/MongoDB pour l'apprentissage personnalisé, utilisée par 50 000 utilisateurs actifs. Le système gère des parcours pédagogiques complexes avec intégration de contenus interactifs et d'outils d'analyse des performances. L'équipe technique maintient une base de code vieillissante mais fonctionnelle, avec une dette technique modérée mais des performances globales stables.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de 8 ans : couplage modéré (5.8/10) et complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.6) indiquent une architecture encore maîtrisable. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.2) suggère une stabilité relative. Cependant, la cohésion faible (4.5/10) et la couverture de tests insuffisante (58.7%) sont des signaux d'alerte majeurs. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method et God Class) confirment une dégradation progressive de la qualité du code, particulièrement dans un fichier critique (src/edtech/service.py). L'équipe expérimentée (59% seniors) est capable de gérer ces défis, mais l'absence de contraintes critiques actuelles permet une approche progressive.", "recommendation": "Ne pas envisager de migration technologique ou de rewrite complet. La stack actuelle répond aux besoins fonctionnels et l'équipe a la maturité pour traiter la dette technique de manière incrémentale. L'objectif prioritaire est d'améliorer la maintenabilité et la fiabilité du code existant avant d'envisager des évolutions majeures.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactoriser les anti-patterns identifiés (Long Method et God Class dans src/edtech/service.py) en appliquant des principes SOLID et en décomposant les responsabilités. Parallellement, augmenter la couverture de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour le module concerné jusqu'à atteindre un seuil minimal de 75%.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Améliorer la cohésion globale du codebase en identifiant et séparant les responsabilités transverses (ex: gestion des parcours pédagogiques, analytics, intégrations externes). Mettre en place des revues de code systématiques pour prévenir la régression de ces métriques.", "duration_days_range": "15-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Déployer une stratégie de tests automatisés progressive (unitaires, d'intégration, E2E) pour atteindre une couverture minimale de 80% sur les modules critiques. Documenter les nouvelles conventions de code et former l'équipe junior aux bonnes pratiques identifiées.", "duration_days_range": "25-40 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de qualité. Le principal risque réside dans une refactorisation trop ambitieuse qui pourrait introduire des bugs. La priorisation des anti-patterns critiques limite ce risque. L'absence de contraintes critiques actuelles permet une approche itérative sans pression temporelle."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0160", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 21, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.2}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is an EdTech platform built over 8 years using Python, Django, and MongoDB, serving a team of 21 developers with a mix of junior and senior talent. The platform has no identified critical constraints but shows signs of architectural strain, particularly in service-layer components where anti-patterns like God Classes and Long Methods have emerged over time.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (5.8/10) and low cohesion (4.5/10), indicating structural issues that could hinder maintainability. While test coverage stands at 58.7%—a reasonable baseline for a mature system—cyclomatic complexity (5.6) and a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.2 on the hottest file suggest localized pain points. The anti-patterns in `src/edtech/service.py` are the most pressing concerns, as they directly impact readability and scalability. The team’s size and skill distribution (34% junior) further justify incremental improvements over a full rewrite, as the latter would introduce disproportionate risk without clear justification from the metrics.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the entire stack. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the God Class and Long Method anti-patterns in `src/edtech/service.py`, paired with incremental improvements to test coverage and cohesion. The current metrics do not warrant a full rewrite, but proactive remediation is necessary to prevent future technical debt accumulation.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor `src/edtech/service.py` to split the God Class into smaller, cohesive components and decompose Long Methods. Introduce unit tests for the refactored sections to improve coverage and validate behavior.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address coupling and cohesion at the architectural level by introducing service boundaries or domain-driven design patterns where appropriate. Prioritize areas with high change frequency or bugfix ratios.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Expand test coverage incrementally, targeting critical paths first. Pair with static analysis tools to enforce coding standards and reduce cyclomatic complexity.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The absence of critical constraints mitigates immediate risk, but the God Class and Long Method anti-patterns pose long-term maintainability challenges. A full rewrite would introduce high risk due to the team’s size and the project’s maturity. Incremental refactoring reduces disruption while addressing the most pressing issues."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0161", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.5, "cohesion_score": 4.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce en Python/FastAPI avec PostgreSQL gère un catalogue de produits et des transactions en ligne pour une marketplace en croissance. L'application doit absorber des pics de trafic imprévisibles tout en maintenant une expérience utilisateur fluide, avec une équipe de 24 développeurs répartis entre juniors et seniors. La base de code, âgée de 1.6 ans, est encore jeune mais montre des signes de complexité croissante dans les modules critiques liés au traitement des commandes et à la gestion des stocks.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une base de code avec des métriques globalement saines pour une application de cette taille et maturité. Le score de couplage à 3.5/10 et de cohésion à 4.8/10 sont acceptables pour un projet en évolution, bien que perfectibles. La couverture de tests à 32.1% est le point le plus critique, mais reste dans la moyenne pour un projet Python récent. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 6.5 est modérée et gérable avec des bonnes pratiques. Les anti-patterns détectés (couplage élevé et dépendances circulaires dans les modules core) sont concentrés dans trois fichiers centraux, ce qui limite leur impact systémique. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.47 suggère une stabilité relative malgré ces problèmes de structure.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack technologique n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. Les problèmes identifiés sont localisés et peuvent être résolus par des refactorings ciblés et une amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests. L'approche incrémentale permettra de réduire les risques tout en améliorant la maintenabilité et la scalabilité de l'application. La priorité doit être donnée à la correction des anti-patterns dans les modules core avant d'envisager des évolutions majeures.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Correction des anti-patterns identifiés dans les modules core (processor.py, handler.py, core.py) : découplage des dépendances circulaires et réduction du couplage élevé. Mise en place de tests unitaires pour ces modules (objectif : porter la couverture de 32.1% à 50% minimum).", "duration_days_range": "25-35 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests globale du projet, avec focus sur les endpoints critiques liés à la scalabilité (gestion des pics de trafic). Intégration de tests de charge pour valider les performances sous charge.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes PostgreSQL et mise en place de mécanismes de cache (Redis) pour les données fréquemment accédées. Revue de l'architecture pour identifier d'éventuels goulots d'étranglement liés à la scalabilité.", "duration_days_range": "15-25 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Documentation des décisions architecturales et formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques identifiées (clean code, tests, scalabilité). Mise en place d'un processus de revue de code renforcé pour prévenir la régression des anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la persistance des anti-patterns dans les modules core, qui pourraient limiter la capacité de l'application à absorber des pics de trafic à long terme. Cependant, leur concentration dans trois fichiers seulement réduit ce risque. Le risque de régression pendant les refactorings est modéré mais maîtrisable avec une couverture de tests accrue. La complexité cyclomatique actuelle ne justifie pas un risque de paralysie du projet. La scalabilité peut être améliorée incrémentalement sans migration complète, ce qui minimise les risques opérationnels."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0161", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.5, "cohesion_score": 4.8, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "An e-commerce platform built in Python with FastAPI and PostgreSQL, designed to handle unpredictable traffic spikes. The codebase is 1.6 years old and maintained by a team of 24 developers, with a primary focus on scalability to accommodate variable load during peak periods.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (3.5/10) and cohesion (4.8/10), indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage is low at 32.1%, which increases the risk of regressions during changes. Cyclomatic complexity is manageable (6.5), but the presence of high and medium coupling in critical files (processor.py, handler.py, core.py) and circular dependencies—particularly in core.py—suggests structural fragility. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.47 on the hottest file signals that maintenance efforts are disproportionately focused on a few components, likely due to tight coupling and poor isolation of responsibilities.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, prioritize targeted refactoring to address the most critical structural issues: high coupling and circular dependencies in core components. Focus on incremental improvements to reduce coupling, improve cohesion, and increase test coverage. These changes will directly enhance maintainability and scalability without the overhead and risk of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor core.py to eliminate circular dependencies and reduce coupling by introducing interfaces or dependency injection. Introduce unit tests for the refactored modules to ensure behavioral integrity.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor processor.py and handler.py to reduce high coupling by splitting responsibilities and introducing clear boundaries between components. Add integration tests to validate interactions between refactored modules.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Gradually improve test coverage by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths, prioritizing areas with high bugfix frequency. Aim to increase coverage to at least 50% over time.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement observability improvements (e.g., logging, metrics) in refactored components to monitor performance and detect scalability bottlenecks early.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the low test coverage and the complexity of refactoring tightly coupled components. However, these risks are mitigated by the incremental approach, which allows for continuous validation and rollback if issues arise. The team's size and experience (16% senior) provide sufficient capacity to execute the refactoring safely. No migration risk is present, as a full rewrite is not recommended."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0162", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.8, "cohesion_score": 2.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 21.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.71}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a core learning platform in the edtech sector, built over 11 years with a Python/Flask/PostgreSQL stack. It serves as the backbone for delivering educational content and user interactions, with a critical operational constraint of maintaining high reliability and uptime due to frequent production incidents.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural and quality issues that directly correlate with the observed uptime problems. The coupling score (7.8/10) and cohesion score (2.2/10) indicate a highly interdependent system with poor separation of concerns, making changes risky and error-prone. Test coverage (21.5%) is critically low, leaving large portions of logic unvalidated and increasing the likelihood of regressions. The presence of multiple high-severity anti-patterns—such as circular dependencies in core modules (processor.py, service.py), a God Class in core.py, and duplicate code—further compounds technical debt. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.71) on the hottest file suggests that maintenance efforts are largely reactive, addressing symptoms rather than root causes. These factors collectively explain the frequent production incidents and point to a system that is difficult to maintain, extend, and operate reliably.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full technology migration at this time. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the root causes of instability. The current stack (Python/Flask/PostgreSQL) is not inherently problematic for the domain, and a rewrite would introduce significant risk without addressing the underlying architectural flaws. A disciplined refactoring and modernization effort will yield better reliability gains with lower risk.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a focused architectural audit to identify the most critical failure points and define a prioritized refactoring backlog. Focus on breaking circular dependencies in processor.py and service.py, and decompose the God Class in core.py into smaller, cohesive components.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted refactoring for the top 3 high-severity anti-patterns identified in Phase 1. Introduce automated tests for the refactored modules to prevent regressions and improve test coverage incrementally.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Gradually expand test coverage across the most critical paths (e.g., user authentication, content delivery, and payment processing) using a risk-based approach. Pair refactoring with test development to ensure stability.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce observability improvements (e.g., structured logging, metrics, and tracing) to reduce mean time to detect (MTTD) and mean time to resolve (MTTR) incidents. Implement gradual rollouts and feature flags to minimize risk during deployments.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Establish a continuous improvement process, including regular code reviews focused on anti-patterns, automated static analysis integration, and team training on clean architecture principles.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of continued instability if no action is taken. Moderate risk of regression during refactoring, mitigated by incremental changes, strong test coverage, and observability improvements. Low risk of technology stack obsolescence in the short to medium term, given the domain stability of Python/Flask/PostgreSQL for edtech applications."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0165", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.9, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.28}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est un marketplace en croissance active, développé en PHP/Laravel avec une base de code de près de 3 ans. L'équipe de 26 développeurs, composée majoritairement de juniors et seniors, fait face à des défis de vélocité avec des fonctionnalités qui prennent trop de temps à être livrées, impactant directement la compétitivité du produit sur un marché dynamique.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales du projet révèlent une situation contrastée : un couplage élevé (3.9/10) et une cohésion moyenne (6.4/10) indiquent une architecture encore fragile, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.9) et les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method, High Coupling) confirment des problèmes de maintenabilité. Cependant, la couverture de tests estimée à 51.4% et un ratio de commits correctifs modéré (0.28) suggèrent que le code reste partiellement testable et que les régressions ne sont pas encore hors de contrôle. L'équipe, bien que jeune, a une expérience suffisante pour gérer des refactorings incrémentaux sans risque majeur.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique complète n'est pas justifiée à ce stade. Les métriques ne montrent pas de dégradation critique (ex : couplage > 7/10, complexité cyclomatique > 15), et le coût d'un rewrite serait disproportionné par rapport aux gains potentiels. L'approche recommandée est une refonte ciblée des composants les plus problématiques, combinée à une amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests et à l'adoption de bonnes pratiques architecturales (ex : séparation claire des responsabilités, réduction des dépendances circulaires).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi pour prioriser les modules critiques à refactorer (ex : processor.py, core.py) et définir des interfaces claires pour réduire le couplage.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorings incrémentaux des méthodes et classes identifiées comme anti-patterns (Long Method, High Coupling), avec ajout de tests unitaires pour chaque modification (objectif : +15% de couverture).", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline CI/CD amélioré avec analyse statique automatisée (ex : PHPStan, Psalm) et revues de code systématiques pour prévenir la régression des anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les principes SOLID et les patterns d'architecture adaptés (ex : CQRS pour les opérations complexes) pour améliorer la cohésion et réduire la complexité cyclomatique.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal est une surcharge de l'équipe pendant les refactorings, surtout si les juniors ne sont pas accompagnés. Cependant, en découpant le travail en petites unités et en impliquant les seniors comme mentors, le risque est maîtrisable. Un risque secondaire est la sous-estimation de la dette technique cachée, mais l'audit initial et les tests automatisés devraient limiter cet impact. Aucune migration n'est prévue, donc le risque de blocage total est nul."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0165", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.9, "cohesion_score": 6.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 51.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.28}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 2.9-year-old marketplace platform built with PHP/Laravel and MySQL, maintained by a team of 26 developers (50% junior, 32% senior). The primary business constraint is slow feature delivery, prompting an evaluation of the codebase's maintainability and technical debt to improve development velocity without compromising stability.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (3.9/10) and cohesion (6.4/10), with cyclomatic complexity averaging 5.9—indicating manageable but non-trivial complexity. Test coverage stands at 51.4%, which is suboptimal but not critically low, and the bugfix-commit ratio (0.28) suggests a moderate level of instability in hotspots. Anti-patterns like Long Method and High Coupling are concentrated in a few files (handler.py, processor.py, core.py), which are likely bottlenecks. The team's junior-heavy composition may exacerbate delivery slowness due to onboarding challenges in a tightly coupled codebase.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the metrics. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. This approach will reduce coupling, enhance cohesion, and streamline feature delivery without the high risk and cost of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address anti-patterns in the hottest files (handler.py, processor.py, core.py) by splitting long methods, reducing parameter lists, and decoupling high-coupling modules. Introduce unit tests for these refactored components to raise coverage toward 70% in the refactored areas.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement modular design patterns (e.g., Command, Strategy) in processor.py and core.py to further reduce coupling. Parallelize this work across sub-teams to maximize velocity gains.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Expand test coverage to 60%+ across the codebase by adding integration and end-to-end tests for critical user journeys. Pair senior developers with juniors to improve code review quality and knowledge sharing.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce lightweight CI/CD improvements (e.g., automated linting, static analysis gates) to catch anti-patterns early and enforce coding standards. Document refactoring decisions and outcomes for future maintainability.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks are temporary delivery slowdowns during refactoring and potential regression if tests are not comprehensive. Mitigate by prioritizing high-impact files, pairing refactoring with test coverage, and using feature flags for gradual rollouts. The junior-heavy team may require additional mentoring during refactoring to avoid introducing new anti-patterns."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0166", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 8.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 84.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 13-year-old SaaS B2B platform in the enterprise management sector, built with Python/Django and MongoDB, serving 43 developers (including 19% junior and 14% senior). The system operates under strict regulatory constraints (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) and requires continuous compliance with evolving standards while maintaining high availability and data integrity for its B2B clients.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy structural metrics: low coupling (2.7/10) indicates modularity, high cohesion (8.9/10) suggests well-organized components, and an average cyclomatic complexity of 2.7 reflects maintainable logic. Test coverage at 84.4% is strong for a mature system, and the bugfix-commit ratio of 0.15 on the hottest file suggests stable core functionality. No significant anti-patterns were detected, and the team size (43 developers) provides sufficient capacity for incremental improvements without requiring a disruptive rewrite. The regulatory compliance constraint is a critical non-functional requirement that would be better addressed through targeted refactoring and architectural safeguards rather than a full migration.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to enhance maintainability and compliance while preserving the existing system's stability and domain knowledge embedded in the codebase.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement targeted refactoring to reduce coupling in high-risk modules (e.g., payment processing, user data handling) while introducing stricter input validation and audit logging to meet compliance requirements. Prioritize files with higher cyclomatic complexity for focused improvements.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Expand test coverage to 90%+ in critical compliance-related modules (e.g., RGPD data deletion workflows, PCI-DSS transaction handling) using property-based testing to validate edge cases. Introduce automated compliance checks in CI/CD pipelines.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Enhance observability by instrumenting key compliance workflows (e.g., data retention, access logging) with structured logging and metrics. Deploy gradual rollouts to production with feature flags to minimize risk.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a regulatory gap analysis to identify gaps between current implementation and latest compliance standards (e.g., updated RGPD guidelines, new PCI-DSS requirements). Prioritize fixes based on risk exposure.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system's healthy metrics and lack of anti-patterns reduce the risk of major failures during incremental changes. Regulatory compliance is the primary risk driver; however, targeted improvements (e.g., stricter validation, audit trails) can mitigate this without requiring a full rewrite. The team's size and experience further lower risk. A full migration would introduce higher risk due to the potential for introducing new bugs in a complex, long-lived codebase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0167", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 53.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.29}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet fintech gère les paiements en temps réel pour des milliers de transactions quotidiennes. Il repose sur une stack Python/Django avec MongoDB, et doit garantir un uptime proche de 99,9% malgré une équipe majoritairement junior. La dette technique accumulée sur 11 ans impacte la fiabilité opérationnelle, avec des incidents récurrents en production.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase vieillissante mais pas encore en état de crise absolue. Le couplage (4.1/10) et la cohésion (4.7/10) sont médiocres mais pas catastrophiques, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.2) reste dans une fourchette gérable. La couverture de tests à 53% est insuffisante mais pas rédhibitoire, surtout pour un projet de cette ancienneté. Les anti-patterns détectés (duplication de code, couplage élevé) sont concentrés dans deux fichiers centraux (core.py et service.py), ce qui limite leur impact global. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.29) suggère des corrections fréquentes mais pas une instabilité chronique.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack serait prématurée et risquée compte tenu de la taille de l'équipe (37 personnes, 70% juniors). Les problèmes identifiés sont localisés et gérables par des refactorings ciblés. L'objectif prioritaire doit être d'améliorer la fiabilité opérationnelle via des améliorations incrémentales, tout en renforçant les pratiques de tests et de revue de code.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des fichiers core.py et service.py pour identifier les points de couplage critiques et les duplications de code à extraire. Priorisation des refactorings en fonction de leur impact sur la fiabilité.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'un plan de couverture de tests progressif : d'abord pour les fonctions critiques identifiées en phase 1, puis extension à l'ensemble du codebase. Intégration de tests de mutation pour valider la qualité des tests existants.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des fonctions les plus problématiques (Long Parameter List, duplication de code) avec revue de code systématique. Introduction de patterns adaptés (ex: Strategy pour les fonctions complexes) pour réduire la complexité.", "duration_days_range": "25-40"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Amélioration des pratiques d'équipe : formation aux bonnes pratiques Python/Django, mise en place de revues de code obligatoires pour les fichiers critiques, et automatisation des tests de performance pour détecter les régressions.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour les phases 1 à 3 si les refactorings sont menés de manière incrémentale et testés systématiquement. Le risque majeur réside dans la phase 2 (couverture de tests) : une augmentation brutale de la couverture pourrait révéler des bugs cachés et impacter la stabilité. La phase 4 dépend fortement de l'adhésion de l'équipe : sans engagement des seniors, les améliorations pourraient être superficielles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0167", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.1, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 53.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.29}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 11.7-year-old fintech payment platform built with Python, Django, and MongoDB, serving as a critical backbone for financial transactions. With a team of 37 developers (70% junior), the system faces reliability challenges due to frequent production incidents, necessitating urgent improvements to maintain uptime and trust in financial operations.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits concerning reliability issues despite its age, with a coupling score of 4.1/10 and cohesion at 4.7/10 indicating structural weaknesses. Test coverage at 53.2% is insufficient for a financial system, and a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.29 on the hottest file suggests recurring instability. Anti-patterns like high duplicate code (especially in core.py and service.py) and long parameter lists exacerbate maintenance challenges. While the team’s junior-heavy composition may contribute to these issues, the metrics clearly point to technical debt rather than a need for a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address reliability and maintainability. The existing stack (Python/Django/MongoDB) is adequate for the domain, and a full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk given the team’s composition and the system’s critical role in payments.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address critical anti-patterns in core.py and service.py: refactor duplicate code, reduce parameter lists, and improve cohesion. Prioritize test coverage expansion to at least 70% for critical paths, with a focus on payment transaction flows.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted reliability improvements: add circuit breakers for external integrations, enhance logging for transaction failures, and introduce automated rollback mechanisms for failed payments.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Gradually introduce architectural improvements: split core.py into smaller, focused modules to reduce coupling, and adopt a layered service architecture to improve cohesion. Pair senior developers with juniors to transfer knowledge.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish continuous reliability monitoring: implement synthetic transaction tests, set up automated incident response playbooks, and conduct regular chaos engineering exercises to proactively identify failure points.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High operational risk due to frequent production incidents, but low technical risk for incremental improvements. A full rewrite would pose significant risk given the team’s junior-heavy composition and the system’s critical financial role. The proposed phased approach mitigates risk by delivering incremental value while addressing the root causes of instability."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0168", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 17, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.2, "cohesion_score": 1.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 27.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 8.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.69}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a supply-chain logistics platform built with Python, Django, and PostgreSQL, serving a 17-developer team that must continuously comply with strict regulatory frameworks such as RGPD, PCI-DSS, and HDS. Over its 5.9-year lifetime, the codebase has accumulated significant structural debt, including multiple God Classes, circular dependencies, and duplicated logic, which now threaten both maintainability and regulatory compliance efforts.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal a codebase that is structurally brittle and difficult to change safely. A coupling score of 6.2/10 and cohesion of 1.6/10 indicate tight interconnections and poor module boundaries, making regression-prone changes likely. Test coverage at 27.7% and a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.69 on the hottest file suggest insufficient safety nets for refactoring. The presence of multiple high-severity anti-patterns—especially God Classes and circular dependencies—further increases the risk of introducing defects during maintenance, which directly conflicts with the regulatory conformance requirement.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration. Instead, prioritize targeted incremental refactoring to address the most critical structural issues that impede regulatory compliance and team velocity. A full rewrite would introduce unacceptable risk given the current lack of test coverage and high coupling, and would not guarantee faster delivery of compliance features.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address the highest-risk anti-patterns: break up God Classes in core.py and handler.py, resolve circular dependencies in processor.py, and reduce duplication in service.py. Introduce targeted unit and integration tests around these modules to reach at least 45% coverage before structural changes.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor service.py to reduce coupling and remove duplicate logic. Introduce modular service layers and dependency injection to improve cohesion and testability. Expand test coverage to 60% in affected areas.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement automated static analysis and linting gates in CI to prevent regression of anti-patterns. Introduce architectural tests to enforce module boundaries and reduce future coupling. Document compliance-relevant interfaces and data flows.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of defect introduction during refactoring due to low test coverage and high coupling. Mitigation relies on phased, incremental changes with strong test coverage gates and continuous monitoring of functional behavior. Without disciplined rollback and observability, regulatory non-conformance risks remain elevated during the refactoring window."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0169", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.9, "cohesion_score": 5.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Un service de streaming média en Node.js/Express avec MongoDB, lancé il y a 9 ans, qui a connu une croissance organique avec une équipe majoritairement junior. Le projet souffre aujourd'hui d'une dette technique accumulée et d'une explosion des coûts cloud, nécessitant une optimisation urgente pour maintenir sa viabilité opérationnelle.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines malgré son âge : un couplage modéré (4.9/10) et une cohésion acceptable (5.2/10) indiquent une architecture encore maintenable. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.4) et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.38) suggèrent une stabilité relative, bien que perfectible. Cependant, la couverture de tests à 37.3% est préoccupante et expose le projet à des régressions. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Circular Dependency, Long Method) sont ciblés et gérables sans refonte majeure. La contrainte cloud n'est pas directement liée à la stack technique mais à l'optimisation des ressources, ce qui peut être adressé sans migration technologique.", "recommendation": "Privilégier une approche incrémentale axée sur la réduction de la dette technique et l'optimisation des coûts, plutôt qu'une migration coûteuse et risquée. Les anti-patterns identifiés doivent être corrigés en priorité pour améliorer la maintenabilité, tandis que la couverture de tests doit être renforcée pour sécuriser les évolutions futures.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud et identification des leviers d'optimisation (instances sous-utilisées, requêtes inefficaces, etc.)", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correction des anti-patterns critiques : refactorisation du God Class dans src/media/service.py, découpage des méthodes longues dans src/media/processor.py, et résolution des dépendances circulaires dans src/media/core.py", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'une stratégie de tests : ajout de tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés sur les modules critiques, avec un objectif progressif de couverture à 60%", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes MongoDB et mise en cache des données fréquentes pour réduire la charge cloud", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Documentation des décisions techniques et formation des développeurs juniors sur les bonnes pratiques identifiées", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de code rigoureuses. Le principal risque réside dans l'absence de tests automatisés avant les refactorisations, qui pourrait introduire des régressions. La dépendance à l'équipe majoritairement junior nécessite un accompagnement pour éviter une accumulation de nouvelles dettes techniques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0169", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.9, "cohesion_score": 5.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 37.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.38}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "A media streaming platform built on Node.js, Express, and MongoDB, serving 33 developers—mostly junior—over 9 years. The system’s cloud cost overruns have become a dominant operational constraint, prompting a review of technical debt and maintainability to improve efficiency and reduce waste.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with coupling (4.9/10) and cohesion (5.2/10) scores indicating room for improvement but not critical decay. Test coverage at 37.3% is low and poses a risk to safe refactoring, especially given the high proportion of junior developers. Cyclomatic complexity (4.4) is acceptable but could rise with continued growth. The presence of anti-patterns—circular dependency, god class, and long method—is concerning and likely contributes to maintenance friction and cloud inefficiency. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.38) suggests that hotspots are being actively addressed, but without structural improvements, these fixes may only be temporary.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage. This will reduce cloud waste by improving code efficiency and maintainability, while building team capability incrementally.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/media/service.py using the Extract Class and Move Method patterns to improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Introduce unit tests (aiming for 60% coverage on this module) to safeguard changes.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Break down the Long Method in src/media/processor.py into smaller, single-responsibility functions. Add integration tests to validate end-to-end behavior of the media processing pipeline.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Resolve the Circular Dependency in src/media/core.py by restructuring imports and introducing interfaces or dependency injection. Pair with senior developers to mentor juniors on modular design principles.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Run a team-wide code review and refactoring workshop to standardize patterns, improve test practices, and reduce future debt. Measure cloud usage before and after to quantify efficiency gains.", "duration_days_range": "5-7"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The main risks are related to low test coverage and junior-heavy team capacity. However, by focusing on small, well-tested refactorings and pairing seniors with juniors, the risks can be mitigated. A full rewrite is not justified given the moderate structural metrics and the high cost of such an effort."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0170", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.2, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un système de gestion de données médicales pour une plateforme de santé en ligne, développé en Python/Flask avec PostgreSQL. Il doit répondre à des exigences strictes de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) tout en évoluant avec une équipe majoritairement junior. La base de code, vieillissante de 3,7 ans, est soumise à une pression constante pour maintenir la sécurité et la performance des traitements de données sensibles.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de cette taille et de ce secteur : couplage et cohésion modérés (4.2/10 et 4.4/10), complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.3) et ratio de commits correctifs acceptable (0.39). La couverture de tests à 47,5% est faible mais gérable dans un contexte réglementaire où la priorité est la stabilité plutôt que la testabilité exhaustive. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method, Duplicate Code, High Coupling, God Class) sont localisés et gérables, sans impact systémique majeur. L'équipe junior nécessite des améliorations de qualité de code incrémentales plutôt qu'une refonte complète.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack. Privilégier une approche de refactoring ciblé et progressif pour améliorer la maintenabilité et la conformité, en corrigeant les anti-patterns identifiés tout en renforçant la couverture de tests. Une migration vers une nouvelle architecture (ex: microservices) serait prématurée et risquée compte tenu du niveau d'expérience de l'équipe et des contraintes réglementaires.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit de conformité et priorisation des corrections réglementaires (ex: isolation des données sensibles, journalisation renforcée).", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns critiques : décomposition du God Class dans core.py, réduction des méthodes longues dans handler.py, et élimination des duplications dans core.py.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests (cibler les modules critiques pour la conformité) et mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour limiter la régression.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques (ex: SOLID, design patterns adaptés au contexte santé) et automatisation des vérifications de qualité via des outils comme SonarQube.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des validations intermédiaires. Le principal risque est la surcharge de l'équipe junior pendant les phases de refactoring, nécessitant un accompagnement actif des seniors. Aucun risque de blocage réglementaire n'est identifié si les corrections sont priorisées correctement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0170", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.2, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a healthcare data processing platform built with Python/Flask and PostgreSQL, designed to handle sensitive patient and payment data while ensuring strict compliance with RGPD, PCI-DSS, and HDS regulations. The team of 33 developers, predominantly junior, has maintained the codebase for 3.7 years, with a strong focus on regulatory adherence but facing challenges in code maintainability and test coverage.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling and cohesion scores (4.2/10 and 4.4/10 respectively), indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage at 47.5% is concerning for a regulated environment where reliability is critical, and the bugfix-commit ratio of 0.39 on the hottest file suggests instability in a key component. Anti-patterns like Long Method, Duplicate Code, High Coupling, and God Class further degrade maintainability and increase the risk of regulatory non-compliance due to potential hidden bugs or data leaks.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and enhance test coverage, particularly in the regulatory-sensitive areas. This approach will reduce immediate risks while building a foundation for future scalability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address the most critical anti-patterns: refactor the Long Method in src/sante/handler.py to improve readability and maintainability, and split the God Class in src/sante/core.py to reduce complexity. Introduce unit tests for the refactored components to ensure no regression.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage by writing missing tests for critical paths, prioritizing areas with high cyclomatic complexity (current average: 6.3). Focus on files with high bugfix-commit ratios to stabilize the most problematic components.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor src/sante/processor.py to reduce high coupling, and eliminate duplicate code in src/sante/core.py. Introduce design patterns (e.g., Strategy or Factory) to improve modularity and make the codebase more adaptable to future regulatory changes.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "High regulatory risk due to low test coverage and unstable hotspots (bugfix-commit ratio of 0.39). Medium technical risk from anti-patterns like God Class and High Coupling, which could lead to hidden bugs or data integrity issues. The junior-heavy team may struggle with complex refactoring, requiring close mentorship and incremental validation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0171", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.5, "cohesion_score": 1.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 24.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.55}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a real-time edtech platform built over 7 years with Python/Django and MongoDB, serving 41 developers (mix of junior and senior). The system must deliver sub-second responses to support live learning experiences, making low-latency a critical non-functional requirement across all user interactions.", "analysis": "The codebase shows severe structural decay: cohesion is critically low (1.1/10), coupling is dangerously high (8.5/10), and test coverage is critically low at 24.6%. The presence of multiple high-severity anti-patterns—including circular dependencies, long methods, duplicate code, and high coupling—indicates a system that is brittle and resistant to change. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.55 on the hottest file suggests that maintenance is reactive and error-prone. While the team size and domain constraints are valid, the technical debt has reached a level where further incremental changes risk introducing regressions and failing to meet real-time latency requirements.", "recommendation": "A targeted incremental refactoring is insufficient given the systemic nature of the issues. A controlled, phased rewrite is justified to restore architectural integrity, improve testability, and meet real-time performance constraints.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Stabilize the current system: freeze new features, implement targeted hotfixes for critical latency paths, and add observability (logging, tracing) to identify real bottlenecks. Begin documenting the core domain model and critical user journeys.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Design a new modular architecture using domain-driven design (DDD) to improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Define bounded contexts, APIs, and data contracts. Set up a new repository with CI/CD and automated testing pipeline.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Incrementally migrate core modules (e.g., user authentication, content delivery, real-time events) using the strangler fig pattern. Each module is rewritten, tested, and deployed behind feature flags. Maintain dual-write during transition.", "duration_days_range": "60-90"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Decommission legacy system, optimize database queries, and fine-tune real-time performance. Conduct load testing to validate sub-second latency under peak load. Finalize documentation and team knowledge transfer.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}], "risk_assessment": "High technical and delivery risk due to the size of the codebase and team unfamiliarity with the new architecture. Risk is mitigated by phased approach, strong observability, and rollback mechanisms. Business risk is high if real-time performance is not met post-migration."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0173", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 9.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.14}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet pilote une plateforme de gestion des flux logistiques pour un réseau de 15 entrepôts européens, développée en Python/Django avec MongoDB comme base de données. L'équipe maintient une application critique pour la supply chain depuis plus d'une décennie, avec une exigence de haute disponibilité et une tolérance limitée aux temps d'arrêt.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une base de code saine et mature : un couplage faible (2.7/10) suggère une architecture modulaire bien structurée, tandis qu'une cohésion élevée (9.0/10) confirme que les composants sont bien alignés sur leurs responsabilités. La couverture de tests à 82.4% est satisfaisante pour un projet de cette envergure, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2.3 reste dans une plage acceptable. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.14 est très bas, signe d'une stabilité opérationnelle remarquable. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs est un indicateur fort de la qualité de la conception. L'équipe, bien que composée majoritairement de juniors, semble avoir su maintenir la qualité du code sur le long terme.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. Les métriques démontrent une base de code robuste et maintenable, avec des indicateurs de qualité qui s'améliorent même après plus d'une décennie de développement. Une migration vers une nouvelle stack ou une réécriture complète serait un risque inutile qui perturberait la productivité sans bénéfice tangible.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Amélioration ciblée de la couverture de tests pour atteindre 90% via des tests d'intégration pour les modules critiques (gestion des stocks, planification des livraisons)", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Renforcement des pratiques DevOps : mise en place de pipelines de déploiement automatisés avec tests de performance pour les scénarios de pic de charge (ex: Black Friday)", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Formation avancée pour les développeurs juniors sur les patterns d'architecture propres à Django (ex: services layer, querysets complexes) pour réduire la dette technique potentielle", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque identifié est la stagnation des compétences : une équipe majoritairement junior pourrait, à terme, ne plus être capable de maintenir une architecture aussi complexe sans supervision senior. Cependant, ce risque est gérable via les phases de formation proposées. Aucun risque technique majeur n'est détecté dans l'état actuel du projet."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0173", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 9.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 82.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.14}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "This is a 11.2-year-old logistics and supply chain application built with Python, Django, and MongoDB, maintained by a team of 22 developers (54% junior, 30% senior). The system operates under no critical constraints and supports core business operations in logistics workflows.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy structural metrics: low coupling (2.7/10) and high cohesion (9.0/10) indicate a well-modularized system with clear separation of concerns. Test coverage stands at 82.4%, which is robust for a mature application, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 2.3 suggests maintainable, straightforward logic. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.14 on the hottest file is low, implying stability in critical areas. No significant anti-patterns were detected, and the team has not identified any pressing constraints. These factors collectively point to a stable, maintainable system that is not suffering from architectural decay.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to sustain maintainability and address minor technical debt. The current metrics justify continued evolution over a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Enhance test coverage in low-coverage modules to reach 85%+ and add targeted integration tests for critical logistics workflows to improve reliability.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the top 3 most complex modules (cyclomatic complexity > 5) to reduce complexity and improve readability, guided by the existing high cohesion.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a team knowledge-sharing session to document high-risk modules and onboarding paths, leveraging the senior developers to mentor juniors on the codebase.", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement lightweight monitoring for coupling hotspots and set up automated alerts for rising complexity or decreasing test coverage.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system is stable and maintainable, but incremental changes carry minimal risk. The primary risk lies in over-scoping improvements or introducing unnecessary complexity during refactoring. A phased, measured approach mitigates this risk effectively."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0175", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 5, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 38.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel gère le traitement de données sensibles issues de capteurs industriels, avec une stack Python/Django/PostgreSQL mature de 10 ans. L'application centralise les flux de données pour des clients soumis à des exigences réglementaires strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS), tout en supportant une équipe majoritairement junior. La conformité réglementaire est la contrainte technique dominante, imposant une rigueur particulière sur la traçabilité et la sécurité des données.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines malgré son âge : un couplage modéré (5.9/10) et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.2) indiquent une architecture encore maintenable. Cependant, la cohésion faible (4.3/10) et la couverture de tests insuffisante (38.3%) révèlent des problèmes structurels majeurs. Les anti-patterns détectés (duplications critiques dans service.py et handler.py, dépendances circulaires dans core.py) sont des sources probables de bugs et de difficultés de maintenance. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.4) suggère une instabilité locale, typique des zones à forte duplication. La contrainte réglementaire impose une priorité absolue à la stabilité et à la testabilité, ce qui rend ces problèmes inacceptables à long terme.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique complète n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. En revanche, une refonte ciblée des modules critiques (service.py, handler.py, core.py) est nécessaire pour éliminer les anti-patterns et améliorer la cohésion. Cette approche incrémentale permettra de répondre aux exigences réglementaires tout en réduisant les risques de régression. La priorité doit être donnée à la stabilisation des zones à haute criticité (fichiers chauds avec ratio correctif élevé) avant toute évolution fonctionnelle.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit réglementaire et identification des exigences critiques pour les modules concernés (service.py, handler.py, core.py). Définition des critères de testabilité et de traçabilité nécessaires à la conformité.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des modules critiques : élimination des duplications dans service.py et handler.py, résolution des dépendances circulaires dans core.py. Mise en place de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les zones modifiées (objectif : +20% de couverture minimum).", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la cohésion globale : restructuration des responsabilités entre modules, introduction de patterns adaptés (ex: DDD léger pour les services IoT) sans changement de stack. Documentation des nouvelles interfaces et des règles de conformité associées.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Déploiement progressif des changements sur un environnement de staging réglementaire, avec validation des critères de conformité. Formation de l'équipe junior sur les nouvelles pratiques et outils de test.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque élevé de régression fonctionnelle si les refactorings ne sont pas accompagnés de tests automatisés stricts. Le profil junior de l'équipe augmente ce risque, nécessitant une revue de code systématique et une documentation exhaustive. Cependant, l'approche incrémentale limite l'exposition globale. La conformité réglementaire pourrait être temporairement impactée pendant les phases 2 et 3 si les exigences ne sont pas intégrées dès la phase 1. Une régression majeure dans les modules critiques (ex: service.py) aurait un impact direct sur la conformité PCI-DSS/HDS."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0175", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 5, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 38.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a decade-old IoT platform built with Python, Django, and PostgreSQL, serving industrial IoT use cases under strict regulatory constraints (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). The team of five developers—with a majority of junior members—maintains a codebase that must continuously comply with evolving regulatory requirements while integrating new device protocols and data pipelines.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 5.9/10 and cohesion at 4.3/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe degradation. Test coverage at 38.3% is low and concerning, especially given the regulatory context where regression risks are high. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 5.2, but the presence of multiple high-impact anti-patterns—particularly duplicate code and circular dependencies—signals technical debt that could hinder maintainability and scalability. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.4 suggests frequent reactive fixes, likely exacerbated by the structural issues. While the stack is stable, the regulatory pressure and team composition (junior-heavy) amplify the risk of introducing compliance gaps during changes.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. The regulatory constraints and team skill mix make a rewrite unjustified at this stage; a measured, risk-aware approach to improving maintainability and reliability is more appropriate.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-impact anti-patterns (duplicate code in src/iot/handler.py and src/iot/service.py, and circular dependency in src/iot/core.py) through targeted refactoring. Pair senior developers with junior team members to ensure knowledge transfer and compliance with coding standards.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement incremental test coverage improvements, starting with critical paths related to regulatory compliance (e.g., data handling, authentication, and audit logging). Use a risk-based approach to prioritize test cases.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce lightweight architectural improvements to reduce coupling, such as modularizing shared logic in src/iot/service.py and handler.py. Introduce dependency injection patterns to mitigate circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish automated compliance checks in the CI pipeline (e.g., static analysis for RGPD/PCI-DSS relevant code paths, test coverage gates). Document refactoring decisions and compliance assumptions for future maintainers.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium to high. The low test coverage and presence of high-impact anti-patterns introduce significant risk during refactoring, particularly in a regulatory context where correctness is critical. However, a full rewrite would pose even greater risks (scope creep, extended compliance gaps, team burnout) given the team’s junior-heavy composition and the project’s age. The proposed phased approach mitigates risk by focusing on incremental, verifiable improvements with built-in compliance safeguards."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0176", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 29, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.0, "cohesion_score": 8.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 63.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.05}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est une plateforme de streaming media en production depuis 8 ans, supportant des pics de trafic imprévisibles dans le secteur concurrentiel des médias. L'application, développée en Node.js/NestJS avec PostgreSQL, sert une base de 29 développeurs majoritairement juniors, avec une contrainte majeure de scalabilité à adresser sans interruption de service.", "analysis": "Les métriques globales du projet sont saines et indiquent une architecture mature : un couplage très faible (2.0/10) et une cohésion élevée (8.0/10) suggèrent une séparation claire des responsabilités, tandis qu'une complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2.5 et un ratio de commits correctifs de 0.05 sur le fichier le plus chaud (0.05 est un seuil acceptable) confirment une base de code maintenable. La couverture de tests à 63.5% est perfectible mais pas critique pour une codebase de cette ancienneté. L'anti-pattern de dépendance circulaire détecté est mineur et isolé (low impact).", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données. Les métriques actuelles montrent une architecture stable et scalable, adaptée aux contraintes de l'équipe et du trafic. Une refonte complète serait un risque majeur pour la stabilité du service et une perte de productivité inutile.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Améliorer la couverture de tests jusqu'à 80% via des tests unitaires ciblés sur les modules critiques (ex: gestion des pics de trafic) et des tests d'intégration pour les endpoints principaux.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Corriger l'anti-pattern de dépendance circulaire dans src/media/processor.py en appliquant une refactorisation incrémentale (ex: inversion de dépendances) et ajouter des tests de régression pour valider le changement.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimiser les mécanismes de scalabilité existants (ex: mise en cache Redis, ajustement des pools de connexions PostgreSQL) en s'appuyant sur les patterns déjà en place, avec des benchmarks avant/après.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Former les développeurs juniors (74% de l'équipe) aux bonnes pratiques d'architecture (ex: SOLID, clean code) via des ateliers pratiques et des revues de code ciblées sur les modules critiques.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal est une dégradation temporaire de la stabilité pendant les phases 1 et 2 (tests et refactoring), mais atténué par les métriques saines du projet. Les phases 3 et 4 sont à faible risque et visent à renforcer la résilience du système. Aucune migration n'est prévue, donc aucun risque de réécriture complète ou de changement de stack."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0177", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.3, "cohesion_score": 1.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 7.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.75}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built on Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, serving a growing user base in the media sector. The codebase has evolved over 7.2 years with a team of 24 developers, predominantly junior, and currently faces maintainability challenges due to high coupling, low cohesion, and minimal test coverage.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal significant structural issues: extreme coupling (8.3/10) paired with very poor cohesion (1.1/10) indicates a system where components are tightly interdependent and poorly organized. Test coverage at 7.9% and high cyclomatic complexity (7.3) suggest fragility in changes, while a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.75 on the hottest file implies frequent firefighting. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies, long parameter lists, and duplicate code are concentrated in the media module, compounding technical debt and slowing delivery.", "recommendation": "A full technology stack migration is not justified at this time. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring within the existing stack to reduce coupling, improve cohesion, and increase test coverage. This will address the root causes of instability and slow delivery without the high risk and cost of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a dependency analysis to identify and break circular dependencies in src/media/service.py and src/media/handler.py. Introduce interfaces or event-driven patterns to decouple components.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor src/media/core.py to reduce long parameter lists by introducing value objects or configuration objects. Apply the Single Responsibility Principle to split large functions.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Eliminate duplicate code in src/media/service.py and src/media/handler.py by extracting shared logic into reusable modules or utility classes. Introduce consistent naming and structure.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage in the media module, starting with critical paths. Introduce unit and integration tests for refactored components to prevent regressions.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Implement code review guidelines and static analysis checks (e.g., ESLint, SonarQube) to enforce modularity and prevent future anti-patterns. Conduct a team workshop on clean architecture principles.", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of continued instability and delivery delays if no action is taken. Moderate risk of regression during refactoring, mitigated by incremental changes and strong test coverage. Low risk of stack migration given the lack of critical constraints and the team's junior-heavy composition."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0178", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 18, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 9.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 70.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel gère des flux de données critiques entre capteurs industriels et plateformes cloud, avec une exigence forte de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). La stack .NET/ASP.NET Core/SQL Server est mature et bien intégrée, mais l'équipe souhaite évaluer la pérennité de l'architecture face aux évolutions réglementaires et technologiques récentes.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une architecture globalement saine : un couplage modéré (2.7/10) suggère une modularité acceptable sans être optimale, tandis qu'une cohésion excellente (9.5/10) indique une bonne séparation des responsabilités. La couverture de tests à 70.7% est correcte pour un projet de cette envergure, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (3.3) reste dans des limites raisonnables. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs et le faible ratio de commits correctifs (0.02) confirment la stabilité du codebase. La contrainte réglementaire, bien que critique, n'impose pas de refonte architecturale mais plutôt des adaptations ciblées.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. Une approche incrémentale est préférable pour renforcer la conformité réglementaire et améliorer la maintenabilité sans prendre les risques d'un rewrite complet. Les améliorations doivent se concentrer sur l'optimisation du couplage et l'augmentation de la couverture de tests, tout en capitalisant sur la stack existante.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit réglementaire détaillé pour identifier les gaps de conformité spécifiques (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) et prioriser les correctifs", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration incrémentale du couplage via une refactorisation ciblée des modules les plus exposés (ex: extraction d'interfaces pour les services critiques)", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests à 85%+ via des tests unitaires et d'intégration, en priorisant les modules réglementairement sensibles", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'outils de monitoring et de reporting pour la conformité réglementaire (ex: logs d'audit automatisés, alertes sur les accès aux données sensibles)", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré pour une approche incrémentale : les métriques actuelles indiquent une base stable, mais les évolutions réglementaires futures pourraient nécessiter des adaptations. Un rewrite complet introduirait des risques majeurs (délais, coûts cachés, perte de savoir-faire) sans garantie de gain proportionnel. L'équipe doit cependant surveiller l'évolution du couplage et de la dette technique à long terme."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0179", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.3, "cohesion_score": 3.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 27.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.61}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme de gestion de tournois en temps réel pour un studio de jeux mobiles en croissance, avec une architecture monolithique Node.js/NestJS sous PostgreSQL. Le système doit absorber des pics de trafic soudains lors de lancements de nouveaux titres ou événements communautaires, tout en maintenant une latence acceptable pour les joueurs. L'équipe technique est expérimentée mais peine à faire évoluer le codebase actuel en raison de problèmes structurels persistants.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase mature mais fragilisée par des anti-patterns structurels majeurs : couplage élevé (7.3/10), cohésion faible (3.7/10) et complexité cyclomatique moyenne à élevée (9.9). La couverture de tests à 27% est préoccupante pour une application critique en termes de scalabilité. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Duplicate Code, Circular Dependency) sont tous concentrés dans des modules centraux (gaming/*), ce qui explique le ratio élevé de commits correctifs (0.61) sur les fichiers chauds. La contrainte de scalabilité n'est pas actuellement bloquée par la stack technique (Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL), mais par la qualité du design. L'équipe senior est capable de mener une refonte incrémentale si guidée.", "recommendation": "Ne pas envisager de migration technologique ou de rewrite complet. La stack actuelle est adaptée au besoin métier et l'équipe a l'expertise nécessaire. La priorité absolue est une refonte architecturale incrémentale ciblant les anti-patterns identifiés, combinée à une amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests. Cette approche permettra d'améliorer la scalabilité sans disruption majeure, tout en capitalisant sur les connaissances existantes de l'équipe.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi avec focus sur les modules gaming/* pour identifier les dépendances critiques et les points d'entrée/sortie du système. Définition d'une stratégie de découplage incrémental avec identification des premières cibles (ex: extraction des handlers dupliqués, refactorisation du God Class processor.py).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de tests automatisés pour les modules critiques, avec augmentation progressive de la couverture (objectif initial : 40% sur les fichiers les plus chauds). Implémentation de mécanismes de monitoring pour les pics de trafic afin de valider l'impact des refactos.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactorisation incrémentale des modules identifiés en phase 1, avec découplage des responsabilités et élimination des anti-patterns (ex: extraction des méthodes longues dans service.py, résolution des circular dependencies dans core.py). Validation des changements via les tests automatisés et monitoring.", "duration_days_range": "30-45"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des performances pour la scalabilité : mise en cache des données fréquentes, optimisation des requêtes PostgreSQL, et préparation pour une éventuelle horizontalisation future (sans migration de stack). Documentation des nouvelles conventions d'architecture.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré de blocage si les dépendances entre modules gaming/* sont trop fortes. Ce risque est atténué par la phase 1 d'audit approfondi. Risque de régression fonctionnelle lors des refactos, couvert par l'augmentation de la couverture de tests. Risque organisationnel : l'équipe devra consacrer 20-30% de son temps à ces refactos pendant 6-9 mois, ce qui peut impacter les fonctionnalités nouvelles. Aucun risque technologique majeur lié à la stack actuelle."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0179", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 37, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 7.3, "cohesion_score": 3.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 27.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.61}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/gaming/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/gaming/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 5.9-year-old gaming platform built with Node.js/NestJS and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 37 developers (with a senior-heavy composition) facing unpredictable traffic spikes. The system powers core gaming features but struggles with scalability under load, compounded by architectural issues like high coupling, low cohesion, and scattered test coverage that hinder maintainability and performance during peak demand.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits significant structural weaknesses that directly threaten its ability to scale under unpredictable gaming traffic. Coupling (7.3/10) and cohesion (3.7/10) scores indicate a tangled architecture where components are overly interdependent and poorly aligned with single responsibilities. Test coverage (27%) is critically low, while cyclomatic complexity (9.9) and the bugfix ratio (0.61) on the hottest file suggest fragile, hard-to-maintain logic. Anti-patterns like God Classes, circular dependencies, and duplicated code across core modules (e.g., processor.py, service.py) amplify technical debt, making incremental changes risky and performance tuning difficult. The team’s senior-heavy makeup is a strength but cannot compensate for systemic design flaws.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted architectural refactoring to reduce coupling, improve cohesion, and incrementally modernize the codebase. The gaming sector’s unpredictable traffic demands a stable, scalable foundation, which cannot be achieved through isolated fixes alone. A phased cleanup of anti-patterns, modular decomposition, and test coverage expansion will yield measurable improvements in maintainability and scalability without the prohibitive cost and risk of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address critical anti-patterns in the hottest files (processor.py, service.py, core.py) by breaking down God Classes, resolving circular dependencies, and deduplicating logic. Introduce modular boundaries (e.g., domain-driven modules for gaming features) to reduce coupling.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage from 27% to at least 50%, prioritizing high-risk modules (e.g., service.py, processor.py) and critical paths (e.g., traffic-handling logic). Pair this with static analysis to enforce complexity thresholds (e.g., cyclomatic complexity < 7).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the most tightly coupled modules to reduce coupling score below 5/10. Introduce event-driven patterns (e.g., message queues) to decouple gaming handlers from core processors, improving scalability under load.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement observability and performance tuning for traffic spikes, including caching layers (e.g., Redis) and horizontal scaling strategies (e.g., containerization). Validate improvements through load testing.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression if anti-patterns are not addressed incrementally. The team’s senior-heavy composition mitigates some risk, but the low test coverage and high complexity make changes brittle. A full rewrite would carry prohibitive risk (e.g., extended downtime, data loss, or feature regression), while a phased refactor spreads risk across smaller, reversible steps. Success hinges on strict adherence to modular boundaries and rigorous testing during each phase."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0180", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel, en production depuis 8,5 ans, gère le traitement de données temps réel pour des capteurs industriels via une stack Java/Spring Boot et PostgreSQL. L'application centralise les flux de données des équipements sur site vers des tableaux de bord analytiques, avec une exigence forte de stabilité opérationnelle et de maîtrise des coûts cloud, notamment en raison de l'augmentation des volumes de données et des pics de traitement non optimisés.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une base de code mature mais avec des signes clairs de dégradation progressive : un couplage élevé (3.7/10) et une cohésion moyenne (5.4/10) indiquent une architecture qui a évolué de manière organique, avec des responsabilités mal délimitées entre composants. La couverture de tests à 48,4% est insuffisante pour garantir la fiabilité des modifications futures, surtout avec une équipe composée à 43% de juniors. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.1) et les anti-patterns détectés (High Coupling dans les handlers, Long Method dans les services) confirment une dette technique qui impacte la maintenabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.35) suggère une instabilité récurrente sur les modules critiques. Cependant, la stack actuelle reste adaptée au domaine (Java/Spring Boot est robuste pour l'IoT industriel) et une migration complète ne serait justifiée que si les coûts cloud étaient directement liés à des inefficacités architecturales majeures — ce qui n'est pas démontré ici.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack, il est préférable de lancer un plan de refactoring ciblé et incrémental pour réduire la dette technique et améliorer l'efficacité cloud. Les gains seront obtenus par une meilleure séparation des responsabilités, une augmentation de la couverture de tests, et une optimisation des modules les plus critiques (handlers et services). Une approche progressive permettra de limiter les risques tout en démontrant rapidement des améliorations mesurables.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des modules à refactorer : identifier les 3-5 composants les plus critiques (basé sur le ratio de commits correctifs et les anti-patterns) et définir des critères de qualité mesurables (couplage cible, couverture de tests minimale par module).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des modules prioritaires : commencer par les handlers avec couplage élevé en appliquant le principe de responsabilité unique (SRP) et en introduisant des interfaces pour réduire les dépendances directes. Parallellement, décomposer les Long Methods dans les services en méthodes plus petites et testables.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests : cibler les modules refactorés avec une couverture minimale de 70%, en priorisant les cas critiques (ex: gestion des erreurs, flux de données temps réel). Intégrer des tests de performance pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement liés aux coûts cloud.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation cloud progressive : analyser les logs et métriques cloud pour identifier les sources de coûts (ex: requêtes SQL inefficaces, sur-allocation de ressources). Appliquer des optimisations ciblées (indexation, mise en cache, scaling horizontal) en parallèle des refactorings.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Documentation et transfert de connaissances : rédiger des guides d'architecture pour les nouveaux développeurs, et organiser des sessions de mentorat pour les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques (ex: SOLID, tests unitaires). Mettre à jour la documentation technique pour refléter les changements.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la résistance au changement dans une équipe déjà en tension (coûts cloud + dette technique). Une approche trop ambitieuse ou mal communiquée pourrait entraîner des blocages. Pour le limiter, il faut : (1) impliquer l'équipe dès la phase 1 via des ateliers de priorisation, (2) montrer des résultats rapides (ex: réduction des commits correctifs après refactoring d'un module), et (3) éviter les changements radicaux qui pourraient dégrader la stabilité. La stack actuelle (Java/Spring Boot) reste un atout pour la stabilité, mais nécessite une discipline accrue en matière de tests et de modularité."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0180", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 48.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Java", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This industrial IoT platform, built over 8.5 years with Java/Spring Boot and PostgreSQL, manages device telemetry and control for a fleet of sensors and actuators. The system faces escalating cloud costs due to inefficient resource usage and architectural decisions that have increased coupling over time. With a team of 42 developers (43% junior), the codebase shows signs of technical debt that complicate maintenance and scalability despite its operational success in production.", "analysis": "The current architecture exhibits moderate coupling (3.7/10) and cohesion (5.4/10), indicating a system that is neither highly tangled nor perfectly modular. Test coverage at 48.4% is suboptimal but not catastrophic, and cyclomatic complexity (5.1) remains within acceptable bounds for maintainability. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.35) on the hottest file suggests frequent reactive fixes, likely exacerbated by the detected anti-patterns: high coupling in critical handlers and a long method in the service layer. These issues are localized and do not indicate systemic architectural failure. The primary constraint—rising cloud costs—is likely driven by inefficient resource allocation or scaling behavior rather than fundamental architectural flaws.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the anti-patterns and improve maintainability. The metrics do not justify a full rewrite, and the team size and junior-heavy composition make large-scale changes risky. Addressing the coupling and cohesion issues will likely reduce cloud costs indirectly by improving efficiency and reducing unnecessary resource usage.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the high-coupling files (src/iot/handler.py and src/iot/service.py) to reduce coupling and split the long method. Introduce clear interfaces and extract smaller, focused methods. Pair senior developers with juniors to ensure knowledge transfer and maintain quality.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted unit and integration tests for the refactored modules to improve test coverage incrementally. Focus on critical paths and the hottest files to reduce the bugfix-commit ratio. Use test-driven development (TDD) where feasible to ensure new code is well-tested.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize cloud resource usage by analyzing and adjusting scaling policies, query performance, and caching strategies. Work with the DevOps team to identify low-hanging fruit for cost reduction without architectural changes.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce lightweight architectural guardrails, such as code reviews focused on coupling and cohesion, and static analysis tools to detect regressions early. Document the refactored modules and update architectural decision records (ADRs) to reflect the changes.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the team's junior-heavy composition and the potential for introducing new bugs during refactoring. Mitigate these by pairing seniors with juniors, using feature flags for gradual rollouts, and ensuring thorough testing. The risk of a full rewrite failure is avoided by pursuing incremental improvements, but there is a risk of scope creep if the team attempts to address too many issues at once. Clear prioritization and governance will be critical."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0181", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 30.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce en PHP/Laravel, vieillissant de plus de 12 ans, supporte un catalogue de produits et des transactions en ligne pour une entreprise soumise à des exigences réglementaires strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). Avec une équipe de 27 développeurs dont un tiers de juniors, la base de code accumule des anti-patterns structurels qui ralentissent les évolutions de conformité et augmentent les risques de non-respect des normes sectorielles.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase mature mais fragilisée par des scores de couplage et cohésion médiocres (5.2/10 et 5.4/10), symptomatiques d'une architecture vieillissante où les responsabilités sont mal délimitées. La couverture de tests à 30.3% et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5.3 confirment un terrain propice aux régressions, particulièrement critique dans un contexte réglementaire où la traçabilité et la stabilité des processus sont impératives. Les anti-patterns détectés (High Coupling, God Class, Duplicate Code) sont concentrés dans des fichiers centraux comme handler.py et core.py, indiquant des goulots d'étranglement techniques plutôt qu'une architecture fondamentalement inadaptée. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.24 reste modéré, suggérant que l'équipe parvient à maintenir le système en l'état malgré ses défauts.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack technologique n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. En revanche, une refonte ciblée des composants critiques identifiés (handler.py, core.py, service.py) est nécessaire pour réduire les risques de non-conformité réglementaire et améliorer la maintenabilité. L'approche incrémentale doit prioriser la décomposition des God Classes, l'élimination des duplications dans core.py, et la réduction du couplage dans handler.py, tout en renforçant la couverture de tests pour ces modules. La conformité réglementaire sera ainsi traitée par des corrections locales plutôt que par une révolution technologique.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit approfondi des modules réglementaires (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) pour identifier les exigences techniques critiques et les points de défaillance potentiels dans la codebase actuelle.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns majeurs : décomposition de service.py (God Class), extraction des duplications dans core.py, et réduction du couplage dans handler.py. Chaque modification doit être accompagnée d'une augmentation ciblée de la couverture de tests (objectif : +15% sur les modules modifiés).", "duration_days_range": "45-60"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de conformité automatisé (linting, tests de sécurité, vérifications RGPD/PCI-DSS) pour valider chaque évolution et prévenir les régressions. Intégration progressive des bonnes pratiques d'architecture (hexagonale, DDD léger) dans les nouveaux développements.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe aux principes de conception modulaire et aux patterns adaptés à un contexte réglementé. Documentation des décisions architecturales et des limites actuelles pour guider les futures évolutions.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque réside dans l'accumulation de dettes techniques pendant les phases de refactoring, qui pourrait impacter les délais de conformité réglementaire. Cependant, une approche incrémentale avec des vérifications automatisées réduit ce risque. La complexité cyclomatique élevée et la faible couverture de tests initiale augmentent le risque de régressions, mais celui-ci est maîtrisable via des tests ciblés sur les modules modifiés. Enfin, la résistance au changement dans une équipe de 27 développeurs (dont 35% de juniors) pourrait ralentir l'adoption des nouvelles pratiques, d'où l'importance de la phase 4 dédiée à la formation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0181", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 30.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature e-commerce platform built over 12 years using PHP, Laravel, and MySQL, serving a team of 27 developers. It operates under strict regulatory constraints (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) and requires continuous compliance updates, making maintainability and stability critical for ongoing business operations.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with coupling (5.2/10) and cohesion (5.4/10) scores near the midpoint, indicating room for improvement but not severe degradation. Test coverage at 30.3% is low and poses a risk to regression safety, especially under regulatory scrutiny. Cyclomatic complexity (5.3) is acceptable but could benefit from refactoring in hotspots. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.24) suggests a reactive maintenance pattern, likely due to tight coupling and lack of automated test coverage. Anti-patterns such as high coupling, god classes, and long methods are concentrated in a few critical files, increasing the risk of change-induced defects during compliance updates.", "recommendation": "A full technology stack migration is not justified at this time. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the dominant constraint (regulatory compliance) while reducing technical debt. The existing PHP/Laravel/MySQL stack is well-understood by the team and can be safely evolved with disciplined refactoring and testing practices.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement targeted refactoring to address anti-patterns in the hottest files (handler.py, core.py, service.py). Prioritize breaking down the God Class and Long Method in service.py and handler.py to reduce cyclomatic complexity and coupling. Extract duplicate code blocks in core.py into reusable components.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage from 30.3% to at least 60% by adding unit and integration tests for the refactored components. Focus on critical paths related to regulatory compliance (e.g., payment handling, user data processing). Introduce mutation testing to validate test effectiveness.", "duration_days_range": "30-40"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural patterns (e.g., CQRS, Domain-Driven Design) to improve cohesion and reduce coupling in the e-commerce core. Gradually decouple the compliance-sensitive modules from the rest of the system to isolate regulatory changes and reduce regression risk.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish continuous monitoring of code quality metrics (coupling, cohesion, complexity) and enforce them via CI/CD pipelines. Introduce automated compliance checks (e.g., data flow analysis for RGPD) to ensure regulatory requirements are met with every change.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium risk. The current state is manageable but fragile, especially under regulatory pressure. The lack of test coverage and presence of anti-patterns increase the risk of defects during compliance updates. However, a full rewrite would introduce higher risk (unknowns, team ramp-up, extended downtime) without clear benefits. The proposed phased approach mitigates risk by delivering incremental value and validating improvements through testing."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0182", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.2, "cohesion_score": 9.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 88.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a green-field e-commerce platform built over the past 0.8 years using .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server. The team of 26 developers—with a mix of junior and senior profiles—faces a talent shortage in their current technology stack, which is now becoming a bottleneck for scaling the product and onboarding new engineers.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits excellent structural health: very low coupling (1.2/10), outstanding cohesion (9.6/10), high test coverage (88.9%), and low complexity (avg. 1.6). No significant anti-patterns were detected, and the bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file (0.12) suggests stable maintainability. These metrics indicate a well-designed system that is currently easy to extend and debug. The primary constraint—talent scarcity—is external to the code quality and stems from market conditions rather than technical debt.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, address the talent shortage through targeted improvements that make the stack more attractive to engineers and easier to staff. The current architecture is healthy and does not justify a costly full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Adopt a polyglot-friendly architecture pattern (e.g., modular monolith with clear boundaries) to allow gradual language or framework shifts in high-impact areas without a full migration.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Introduce a lightweight internal developer platform (IDP) to simplify onboarding, environment provisioning, and CI/CD, reducing ramp-up time for new hires regardless of stack.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Expand documentation and run internal tech talks/workshops to upskill junior developers and attract candidates by showcasing a modern, well-structured codebase.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Low technical risk. The main risk lies in delayed hiring due to market conditions, which could be mitigated by improving developer experience and making the platform more appealing to potential candidates."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0183", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 34, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet medtech de 1.6 ans développe une plateforme de gestion de données patients en Node.js/Express avec MongoDB, utilisée par plusieurs cliniques partenaires. L'équipe de 34 développeurs, majoritairement junior, fait face à une pénurie de talents sur sa stack actuelle, ce qui ralentit les recrutements et limite la montée en compétences sur des technologies plus modernes.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines mais avec des points de friction majeurs : le couplage (4.8/10) et la cohésion (5.4/10) indiquent une architecture modulaire mais avec des zones de forte dépendance. La couverture de tests à 58.7% est insuffisante pour une application de santé critique, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.6) et les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Circular Dependency) révèlent des problèmes de maintenabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.39) suggère une stabilité relative mais masque probablement des dettes techniques accumulées.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer la stack actuelle. Privilégier une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns identifiés, avec une attention particulière à la couverture de tests et à la réduction de la complexité cyclomatique. La pénurie de talents sur Node.js peut être atténuée par une montée en compétences progressive de l'équipe sur des frameworks plus modernes (comme NestJS) plutôt qu'un changement radical de stack.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi avec focus sur les fichiers identifiés (sante/processor.py, sante/service.py, sante/handler.py) pour prioriser les corrections", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'un plan de tests automatisés (unitaires et d'intégration) avec couverture minimale de 80% sur les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns identifiés (God Class, Circular Dependency) en suivant une approche strangler fig pattern", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur des bonnes pratiques modernes (NestJS, architecture hexagonale) et mise à jour progressive de la stack", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré si la refonte incrémentale est mal planifiée. Le principal danger serait une tentative de refactoring trop ambitieuse qui perturberait la stabilité du système. La priorité doit être donnée à la stabilité opérationnelle (tests) avant toute modification structurelle. La pénurie de talents pourrait être partiellement résolue par la formation plutôt qu'un changement de stack."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0183", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 34, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 5.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 58.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.39}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 1.6-year-old medtech application built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB, serving as a critical component in the healthcare sector. With a team of 34 developers—67% junior and 33% senior—the project faces challenges in talent retention due to the niche nature of its current stack, which is becoming increasingly difficult to staff and maintain.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with a coupling score of 4.8/10 and cohesion score of 5.4/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe degradation. Test coverage at 58.7% is suboptimal, particularly given the safety-critical nature of the medtech sector, where reliability is paramount. Cyclomatic complexity of 6.6 is manageable but suggests potential maintainability issues in complex logic paths. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.39 on the hottest file signals a reactive maintenance pattern, which may indicate underlying design or testing gaps. Anti-patterns such as high coupling, god classes, long methods, and circular dependencies are concentrated in a few critical files (processor.py, service.py, handler.py), pointing to localized technical debt rather than systemic architectural flaws. The team’s junior-heavy composition may exacerbate these issues, as refactoring complex areas requires experienced oversight.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the identified anti-patterns and strengthen the codebase’s robustness. Prioritize refactoring the files with high anti-pattern severity (service.py, handler.py) to reduce coupling, eliminate god classes, and break down long methods. Introduce stricter testing practices to improve coverage, particularly in the safety-critical components, and enforce modular design principles to mitigate circular dependencies. Additionally, invest in upskilling the junior-heavy team on modern refactoring techniques and testing strategies to improve long-term maintainability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor critical files (service.py, handler.py) to address god classes, long methods, and circular dependencies. Implement modular design patterns to reduce coupling and improve cohesion.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage to at least 75% by adding unit and integration tests for the refactored components and high-risk areas. Introduce automated testing gates in the CI pipeline.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a team workshop on modern refactoring techniques and testing strategies tailored to the medtech domain. Document best practices and update internal guidelines.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement static analysis tools (e.g., SonarQube) to continuously monitor code quality metrics (coupling, cohesion, complexity) and enforce anti-pattern prevention.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is the potential for introducing regressions during refactoring, particularly in the safety-critical components. This can be mitigated by rigorous testing and incremental rollouts. A secondary risk is the team’s junior-heavy composition, which may slow down refactoring efforts or lead to suboptimal solutions without proper guidance. Addressing this requires close mentorship from senior developers and structured knowledge-sharing sessions. The lack of talent availability for the current stack remains a long-term risk, but migrating prematurely could introduce even greater instability. Incremental improvements provide a safer path to address both technical debt and team capability gaps."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0185", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 6.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 55.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.34}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Système de monitoring et contrôle pour des équipements IoT industriels critiques, développé en Ruby on Rails avec une base MySQL. L'application gère le traitement en temps réel de millions de données de télémétrie tout en garantissant une disponibilité maximale pour éviter des pertes de production coûteuses. La stack actuelle, vieillissante de 12 ans, subit une pression croissante due à l'augmentation des incidents en production et à la complexité accumulée dans les modules cœur de traitement.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs contrastés : un couplage élevé (3.1/10) et une cohésion moyenne (6.0/10) suggèrent une architecture trop monolithique avec des responsabilités mal définies. La couverture de tests à 55.8% est insuffisante pour une application critique, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5.0 indique une logique métier potentiellement trop dense. Les anti-patterns détectés (dépendances circulaires dans les modules cœur, duplication de code dans le processor) confirment une dégradation progressive de la maintenabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.34 sur le fichier le plus chaud révèle un hotspot de bugs, typique d'un code devenu trop complexe à faire évoluer. Cependant, la stack Ruby/Rails reste adaptée au domaine IoT industriel si on corrige ces problèmes structurels.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack. Privilégier une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur l'architecture et la qualité du code existant. Les métriques ne justifient pas un rewrite complet (coût prohibitif, risque élevé de régression) mais révèlent des opportunités d'amélioration majeures dans la conception et les tests. Une approche progressive permettra de réduire les incidents tout en capitalisant sur l'expertise de l'équipe.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des modules critiques à restructurer. Identification des dépendances circulaires et planification des corrections d'architecture (ex: extraction de services, inversion de dépendances).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correction des anti-patterns identifiés : résolution des dépendances circulaires dans service.py et processor.py, et élimination de la duplication dans processor.py. Mise en place de mécanismes de découplage (ex: interfaces, events).", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests : ajout de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules critiques (priorité aux hotspots). Introduction de tests de charge pour valider la fiabilité sous stress.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Migration progressive vers une architecture plus modulaire : extraction des fonctionnalités IoT les plus volatiles vers des services dédiés (ex: processing, alerting). Déploiement en feature flags pour limiter les risques.", "duration_days_range": "30-40"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de code strictes. Le principal risque réside dans l'introduction de nouvelles régressions lors des corrections d'architecture, atténué par les feature flags et une couverture de tests renforcée. La dépendance à la stack Ruby/Rails existante est maîtrisée grâce à une équipe senior expérimentée dans cette technologie."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0185", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 11, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.1, "cohesion_score": 6.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 55.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.34}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/iot/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 12.7-year-old industrial IoT platform built with Ruby on Rails and MySQL, serving as the backbone for critical infrastructure monitoring. The team of 11 developers (with a mix of junior and senior engineers) faces frequent production incidents, driving a strong focus on reliability and uptime. The codebase has accumulated technical debt over time, particularly in core processing modules where reliability issues are most acute.", "analysis": "The current codebase exhibits concerning reliability challenges, as evidenced by frequent production incidents and a high bugfix-commit ratio in critical files. While the coupling score (3.1/10) and cyclomatic complexity (5.0) are not extreme, they indicate structural fragility, particularly when combined with cohesion issues (6.0/10) and low test coverage (55.8%). The presence of high-severity anti-patterns—circular dependencies in two core modules and duplicate code in the processor—directly correlates with the uptime problems. The team's seniority suggests they can handle incremental refactoring, but the lack of tests increases the risk of regression during changes.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, prioritize targeted incremental improvements to address the root causes of reliability issues. The anti-patterns and low test coverage are the primary drivers of incidents, and these can be resolved without a full rewrite. Focus first on breaking circular dependencies and adding test coverage to the hottest files, then address the duplicate code and long parameter lists.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Break circular dependencies in src/iot/service.py and src/iot/processor.py by introducing interfaces or dependency inversion. Add targeted unit and integration tests to the hottest files to reach at least 70% coverage in the most critical modules.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor src/iot/processor.py to eliminate duplicate code and reduce the long parameter list by introducing value objects or configuration classes. Pair with the team to ensure knowledge transfer and maintain consistency.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement observability improvements (e.g., structured logging, metrics) in the refactored modules to reduce mean time to detect (MTTD) and mean time to resolve (MTTR) incidents. Conduct a post-mortem review to identify additional reliability gaps.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium risk. The team's seniority mitigates some risk, but the low test coverage and presence of high-severity anti-patterns increase the likelihood of regression during refactoring. A phased approach with rollback plans and incremental testing will help manage this risk. The biggest risk is not addressing the circular dependencies and duplicate code promptly, which could lead to further reliability degradation."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0186", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.36}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce en .NET Core, lancé il y a 8 mois, supporte une plateforme de vente en ligne avec une exigence critique de disponibilité. L'équipe de 19 développeurs, composée majoritairement de profils seniors, fait face à des incidents de production récurrents qui impactent l'expérience utilisateur et la fiabilité du système.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase jeune mais déjà fragilisée par des problèmes structurels majeurs. Le couplage élevé (4.6/10) et la cohésion moyenne (6.3/10) indiquent une architecture trop monolithique où les responsabilités sont mal délimitées. La couverture de tests insuffisante (34.1%) et la complexité cyclomatique élevée (4.9) aggravent la situation, tandis que le ratio de commits correctifs (0.36) confirme un cycle de maintenance coûteux. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, High Coupling, Long Method) sont concentrés sur quelques classes critiques, ce qui suggère une dette technique localisée plutôt qu'un problème systémique.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration coûteuse et risquée, il est préférable de traiter la dette technique de manière ciblée. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont gérables par des refactorings incrémentaux, une amélioration de la couverture de tests et une optimisation de l'architecture modulaire. Une approche progressive réduira les incidents tout en limitant l'exposition aux risques.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyse approfondie des classes problématiques (handler.py, processor.py, service.py) pour identifier les dépendances critiques et les responsabilités à extraire. Définition d'un plan de refactoring par étapes.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'une stratégie de tests automatisés pour les modules critiques, en commençant par les endpoints exposés aux incidents fréquents. Priorisation des tests unitaires et d'intégration.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des classes identifiées : extraction de responsabilités, réduction de la complexité cyclomatique et découplage des dépendances. Validation par des revues de code strictes et des tests de non-régression.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation de l'architecture modulaire : identification des opportunités de découplage (ex: séparation des handlers, introduction d'interfaces pour les services critiques). Documentation des nouvelles conventions.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Mise en place d'outils de monitoring et d'alertes pour suivre l'impact des refactorings sur la fiabilité (uptime, temps de réponse, taux d'incidents). Ajustement continu des priorités.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal réside dans l'amplification des incidents pendant les phases de refactoring, surtout si les tests automatisés sont incomplets. Pour l'atténuer, il est crucial de : (1) limiter les changements en période de forte charge, (2) déployer les modifications par petits lots avec rollback immédiat, et (3) impliquer l'équipe dans des revues de code approfondies. La dette technique actuelle ne justifie pas un risque de migration radicale."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0186", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 19, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.36}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "An e-commerce platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, developed by a team of 19 engineers (mix of junior and senior) over the past 0.7 years. The system is mission-critical, with uptime and reliability as the dominant constraints due to frequent production incidents.", "analysis": "The codebase shows mixed structural health: coupling (4.6/10) and cohesion (6.3/10) scores are suboptimal, and test coverage is low at 34.1%. Cyclomatic complexity is moderate (4.9), but the bugfix-commit ratio of 0.36 on the hottest file signals instability in a critical path. Anti-patterns are concentrated in a few files—handler.py, processor.py, and service.py—indicating localized technical debt rather than systemic decay. The system is still relatively young, which means foundational refactoring is feasible without a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Avoid a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the dominant reliability constraint. The anti-patterns are concentrated in a few files, making them ideal candidates for focused refactoring. Improving test coverage and reducing coupling in these areas will have the highest impact on stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a root-cause analysis of production incidents to identify the most critical failure paths. Prioritize files with high bugfix-commit ratios and anti-patterns for refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally refactor the identified hotspots (handler.py, processor.py, service.py) to reduce coupling and eliminate god classes. Introduce unit and integration tests in parallel to improve coverage.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement observability improvements (e.g., structured logging, metrics) to reduce mean time to detect and resolve incidents. Pair with junior developers to upskill them on refactoring techniques.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system is young, and the anti-patterns are localized, reducing the risk of a full rewrite. However, refactoring critical paths without adequate test coverage introduces short-term risk of regressions. Mitigate this by prioritizing files with the highest bugfix-commit ratios and introducing tests before refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0188", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.4, "cohesion_score": 8.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 69.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.19}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a core e-commerce platform built over 7 years with a Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL stack, serving a team of 43 developers (68% junior, 24% senior). The primary business constraint is slow feature delivery velocity, prompting an evaluation of the codebase's maintainability and delivery efficiency.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy structural metrics: low coupling (2.4/10) and high cohesion (8.5/10) indicate modularity and separation of concerns are well-maintained. Test coverage at 69.6% is acceptable but leaves room for improvement, while a low average cyclomatic complexity (1.5) suggests straightforward, readable code. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.19 on the hottest file is within an acceptable range, and no significant anti-patterns were detected. These metrics collectively point to a maintainable codebase where delivery bottlenecks are likely process- or workflow-related rather than structural.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the system. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the velocity constraint without incurring the high cost and risk of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 80% by adding missing unit and integration tests, prioritizing critical paths and high-traffic endpoints. Pair senior developers with junior team members to accelerate knowledge transfer and improve test quality.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement a CI/CD pipeline with automated testing, deployment gates, and rollback mechanisms to reduce manual errors and accelerate feature delivery. Introduce feature flags to decouple deployments from releases.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize development workflows by introducing lightweight architectural decision records (ADRs) for major changes, enforcing modular design reviews, and adopting a more granular task breakdown to improve estimation accuracy.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a team workshop to identify and document performance bottlenecks in the delivery pipeline, then iteratively address them with measurable outcomes tracked over the next quarter.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The codebase is structurally sound, so the primary risks lie in process changes and team adoption. A full rewrite would introduce high risk without clear justification. The proposed phases focus on incremental improvements with measurable outcomes, reducing exposure to disruption."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0189", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 31, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.0, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.1}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise, développé en Python/Flask avec PostgreSQL, est en production depuis 1,8 an. Il supporte une équipe de 31 développeurs et doit garantir un uptime élevé pour ses clients entreprises, une exigence critique pour son modèle économique. La base de code, bien que jeune, montre des signes de fragilité opérationnelle avec des incidents fréquents en production.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une base de code globalement saine avec un couplage maîtrisé (score de 1.0/10) et une cohésion acceptable (7.7/10). La couverture de tests à 72,6% est correcte mais perfectible, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 3,4 reste dans une fourchette raisonnable. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0,1 sur le fichier le plus chaud suggère que les bugs critiques sont rares et localisés. L'anti-pattern de *High Coupling* détecté dans `src/saas/core.py` est isolé et ne semble pas impacter significativement la maintenabilité globale du projet.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. Une refonte complète serait coûteuse et risquée sans preuve d'un gain tangible. À la place, une approche incrémentale ciblée sur l'amélioration de la fiabilité et de la maintenabilité est recommandée, en priorisant les zones à risque identifiées.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Analyse approfondie des incidents récents pour identifier les causes racines (ex: problèmes de concurrence, gestion des ressources, etc.) et établir un plan d'action correctif.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests dans les modules critiques (ex: `src/saas/core.py`) et ajout de tests de charge pour valider la stabilité sous trafic réel. Prioriser les tests end-to-end pour les scénarios utilisateurs fréquents.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactorisation ciblée de `src/saas/core.py` pour réduire la complexité et améliorer l'isolation des composants. Introduire des interfaces claires et des dépendances explicites pour limiter les risques de régression.", "duration_days_range": "12-20 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'outils de monitoring et d'alerting avancés (ex: métriques de latence, taux d'erreur par endpoint) pour détecter proactivement les anomalies et réduire le MTTR (Mean Time To Repair).", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques de développement (ex: revues de code, tests automatisés) et documentation des décisions architecturales pour faciliter l'onboarding des nouveaux développeurs.", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal réside dans l'absence de visibilité sur les causes exactes des incidents en production. Une approche itérative avec validation des correctifs en staging avant déploiement réduira ce risque. La refactorisation de `core.py` doit être menée avec prudence pour éviter les régressions, en s'appuyant sur une suite de tests robuste. Aucun risque majeur de migration n'est identifié, car aucune migration n'est proposée."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0191", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 9, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 8.7, "cohesion_score": 1.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 13.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 10.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.52}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/fintech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/fintech/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/fintech/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet fintech, en production depuis 7 ans, gère l'infrastructure de paiements pour plusieurs partenaires bancaires. Il repose sur une stack Ruby/Rails avec MySQL, et doit garantir une disponibilité élevée tout en intégrant régulièrement de nouvelles fonctionnalités réglementaires. L'équipe, majoritairement junior, fait face à une dette technique croissante qui ralentit les évolutions récentes.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques contrastées : un couplage élevé (8.7/10) suggère une architecture globalement bien structurée, mais une cohésion très faible (1.9/10) indique des responsabilités mal réparties entre les modules. La couverture de tests à 13.1% et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 10.1 révèlent un manque de tests automatisés et des méthodes trop complexes. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Duplicate Code, Circular Dependency) sont concentrés dans quelques fichiers critiques, ce qui explique le ratio de commits correctifs élevé (0.52) sur ces composants. Ces problèmes sont typiques d'une croissance organique sans refactoring systématique.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. La dette technique est concentrée dans des zones limitées de la codebase et peut être traitée par des améliorations incrémentales ciblées. Une approche de refactoring progressif, combinée à l'ajout de tests automatisés, permettra d'améliorer la maintenabilité sans prendre les risques d'un rewrite complet.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi pour identifier les dépendances critiques et prioriser les zones à refactorer. Mise en place d'un plan de tests automatisés pour les composants identifiés comme prioritaires.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Duplicate Code, Long Method) dans les fichiers src/fintech/service.py, src/fintech/processor.py et src/fintech/core.py. Introduction de tests unitaires pour valider les modifications.", "duration_days_range": "40-60"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la cohésion en réorganisant les responsabilités des modules. Ajout de tests d'intégration pour valider les interactions entre les composants refactorés.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques de conception (SOLID, Clean Code) et mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour prévenir la réintroduction des anti-patterns.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal réside dans l'absence de tests automatisés avant les modifications, ce qui pourrait introduire des régressions. Cependant, en ciblant des zones limitées et en validant systématiquement avec des tests, ce risque est maîtrisable. La complexité cyclomatique élevée nécessite une attention particulière lors du refactoring pour éviter d'aggraver la situation. L'équipe junior devra être accompagnée pour garantir la qualité des modifications."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0192", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet IoT industriel gère le monitoring en temps réel de milliers de capteurs déployés sur des sites clients critiques. L'application Django, alimentée par PostgreSQL, doit absorber des pics de trafic soudains lors d'événements industriels majeurs, tout en garantissant une latence inférieure à 200ms pour les requêtes de télémétrie. L'équipe de 33 développeurs maintient une codebase vieillissante de 11 ans, où la scalabilité est devenue le principal goulot d'étranglement malgré des fonctionnalités stables en production depuis des années.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour une application mature de 11 ans : un couplage modéré (3.7/10) indique une architecture suffisamment modulaire pour éviter une refonte totale, tandis qu'une cohésion moyenne (5.5/10) suggère des opportunités d'amélioration ciblée sans risque de désintégration. La couverture de tests à 50.6% est typique pour un projet long terme où les tests ont été ajoutés progressivement, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.0) reste dans une plage acceptable pour du Python. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class et Circular Dependency) sont localisés et de gravité moyenne, ce qui les rend gérables sans impact majeur sur la stabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.49) reflète une dette technique gérable, mais pas critique. La contrainte de scalabilité n'est pas liée à un problème de design fondamental, mais plutôt à des goulots d'étranglement infra ou algorithmiques.", "recommendation": "Éviter un rewrite complet ou une migration technologique radicale. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour résoudre les anti-patterns identifiés et renforcer la résilience face aux pics de trafic. Une approche par petites itérations permettra de valider l'impact de chaque changement sans risquer une dégradation globale de la stabilité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Décomposer le God Class dans src/iot/handler.py en classes spécialisées (ex: HandlerFactory, MessageValidator, AlertProcessor) avec extraction des responsabilités selon le principe de responsabilité unique. Ajouter des tests unitaires pour chaque nouvelle classe (objectif : +15% de couverture sur ce module).", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Résoudre la Circular Dependency dans src/iot/core.py en appliquant l'injection de dépendances ou en restructurant les imports. Documenter les interfaces entre les modules concernés pour éviter les régressions.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimiser les requêtes PostgreSQL les plus lentes (identifiées via les logs) en ajoutant des index ciblés et en révisant les schémas de données pour les tables fréquemment accédées. Mettre en place un cache Redis pour les données statiques (ex: configurations de capteurs).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Améliorer la couverture de tests globale en ciblant les modules critiques (ex: src/iot/api/) avec des tests d'intégration et de charge. Automatiser la détection des régressions via des pipelines CI/CD renforcés.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global MODÉRÉ. Les anti-patterns identifiés sont gérables et leur correction ne devrait pas impacter la stabilité du système. Le principal risque réside dans une mauvaise estimation des goulots d'étranglement infra (ex: goulot réseau ou base de données mal dimensionnée), qui pourrait masquer les gains des optimisations logicielles. Il est recommandé de valider chaque phase par des tests de charge avant de passer à la suivante. La dette technique accumulée sur 11 ans ne justifie pas une migration coûteuse, mais une approche itérative et mesurable est essentielle pour éviter les surprises."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0192", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 5.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.49}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 11.7-year-old industrial IoT platform built in Python/Django with PostgreSQL, serving a team of 33 developers (29% junior, 52% senior). It faces unpredictable traffic spikes and must scale efficiently while maintaining reliability in a critical infrastructure context.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.7/10 and cohesion at 5.5/10, indicating room for improvement but not critical failure. Test coverage at 50.6% is suboptimal but not catastrophic, and cyclomatic complexity averaging 5.0 suggests manageable maintainability. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.49 on the hottest file signals moderate fragility in a critical component. Anti-patterns like a God Class and circular dependency are present but localized, not systemic.", "recommendation": "A full technology stack migration is not justified by the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the dominant scalability constraint while reducing technical debt. The team’s senior-heavy composition supports iterative refactoring over a risky rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/iot/handler.py into smaller, single-responsibility components and introduce dependency injection to break circular dependencies in src/iot/core.py. Pair this with adding targeted test coverage (aim for +15%) around these components.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement horizontal scaling mechanisms for the Django application layer, such as caching (Redis) and asynchronous task queues (Celery), to handle unpredictable traffic spikes. Validate scalability improvements with load testing.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Gradually improve test coverage to 70% by adding unit and integration tests for high-risk modules, prioritizing areas with high cyclomatic complexity or frequent bugfixes. Introduce static analysis gates in CI to prevent regression.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The anti-patterns are localized and addressable without a full rewrite. The team’s experience level mitigates refactoring risks, but incremental changes must be validated with thorough testing to avoid introducing regressions during scalability improvements."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0194", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.3, "cohesion_score": 9.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 66.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built on a Node.js/Express/MongoDB stack, with a codebase that has evolved over 12.6 years. The team of 45 developers maintains a system where cost efficiency in cloud infrastructure is a critical concern, while ensuring reliable media processing and delivery remains the core operational focus.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits strong structural health with a coupling score of 1.3/10 and cohesion score of 9.6/10, indicating a well-organized architecture with minimal interdependencies. Cyclomatic complexity is low at 2.5, and the bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file is minimal at 0.02, suggesting stable and maintainable components. Test coverage at 66.1% is suboptimal but not critically low, and the only detected anti-pattern—a low-severity circular dependency—does not significantly impact system stability. The primary pain point is cloud cost overruns, which is more likely a runtime optimization issue than a code-level problem.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the entire stack. Instead, focus on targeted improvements to address the cloud cost constraint and enhance test coverage incrementally. The current architecture is healthy enough to support these changes without a high-risk rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a cloud cost audit to identify inefficiencies in resource allocation, storage, and compute usage. Implement cost-monitoring tools and tagging strategies to gain visibility into spending drivers.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage by adding unit and integration tests to critical paths, prioritizing areas with the highest business impact. Aim to raise coverage from 66.1% to at least 80% over time.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the identified circular dependency in src/media/processor.py to eliminate the low-severity anti-pattern, improving maintainability without disrupting the broader system.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimize media processing pipelines for cost efficiency by evaluating alternative storage solutions (e.g., tiered storage) and compute strategies (e.g., serverless functions for burst workloads).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system’s structural health minimizes the risk of introducing regressions during incremental changes. The primary risks lie in cloud cost overruns, which are operational rather than architectural, and can be mitigated with monitoring and targeted optimizations. No full rewrite is justified given the current metrics."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0196", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.3, "cohesion_score": 1.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 28.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.54}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet pilote une plateforme de suivi en temps réel des flux logistiques pour un acteur majeur de la supply chain, avec une exigence de latence inférieure à 100ms pour les opérations critiques. Développée en Python/Django avec MongoDB, l'application gère actuellement 120 routes API et 8 flux de données temps réel simultanés, avec une base de code en croissance constante depuis son lancement il y a 13 mois.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase jeune mais déjà fragilisée par des anti-patterns structurels majeurs : des dépendances circulaires critiques dans les handlers, une cohésion très faible (1.9/10) et une complexité cyclomatique élevée (11.8) qui impactent directement la maintenabilité et la performance temps réel. La couverture de tests à 28.6% est insuffisante pour garantir la stabilité des évolutions futures. Le couplage modéré (6.3/10) suggère que le cœur métier pourrait être isolé, mais les dépendances circulaires dans les modules critiques (processor.py, handler.py) rendent toute refactoring profond risqué sans une approche incrémentale.", "recommendation": "Ne pas envisager de migration technologique ou de rewrite complet. La priorité absolue est de stabiliser la plateforme en traitant les anti-patterns identifiés et en améliorant la testabilité, tout en réduisant progressivement la latence via des optimisations ciblées. Une migration prématurée vers une stack alternative (ex: Go/Rust) serait contre-productive compte tenu de l'expertise de l'équipe et de la criticité du temps réel.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des anti-patterns à corriger, avec focus sur la rupture des dépendances circulaires dans handler.py et processor.py", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des méthodes longues dans service.py et extraction des duplications dans processor.py, avec ajout de tests unitaires pour les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des flux temps réel via l'implémentation de caches distribués (Redis) et révision des requêtes MongoDB pour réduire la latence", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline CI/CD avec analyse statique renforcée et couverture de tests minimale à 60% pour les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque élevé de régression en cas de refactoring des modules handler.py et processor.py sans tests suffisants. La complexité cyclomatique actuelle et les dépendances circulaires rendent toute modification structurelle délicate. Cependant, une approche incrémentale avec validation systématique des changements (via feature flags) limite ce risque. Le principal danger reste l'absence de tests automatisés pour valider les optimisations de latence."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0196", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 6, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 6.3, "cohesion_score": 1.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 28.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.54}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a real-time logistics tracking system built with Python, Django, and MongoDB, designed to handle supply chain operations with strict latency constraints. The codebase, developed over the past 1.1 years by a team of six developers with a mix of junior and senior expertise, currently faces challenges with maintainability due to high coupling, low cohesion, and significant anti-patterns in critical modules.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase under stress from real-time performance demands, with concerning structural issues. Coupling is moderately high (6.3/10), suggesting tight interdependencies that could hinder scalability or future changes. Cohesion is critically low (1.9/10), meaning components are poorly aligned with their responsibilities, likely contributing to the observed anti-patterns. Test coverage is dangerously low (28.6%), and cyclomatic complexity is elevated (11.8), increasing the risk of defects. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.54) on the hottest file signals frequent reactive fixes, a red flag for technical debt. Anti-patterns like circular dependencies, duplicate code, and long methods are concentrated in core modules (processor.py, service.py, handler.py), directly threatening the system's ability to meet real-time latency requirements reliably.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is premature and unjustified given the current state. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the most critical anti-patterns and structural issues. Prioritize breaking circular dependencies, extracting long methods, and reducing duplicate code in the core modules to improve cohesion and coupling. Concurrently, incrementally improve test coverage to at least 60% to stabilize the codebase and reduce regression risks. These steps will directly address the latency constraints by reducing overhead in critical paths while avoiding the high cost and risk of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address circular dependencies and extract long methods in src/logistique/service.py and src/logistique/handler.py to reduce coupling and improve cohesion. Implement targeted unit tests for the refactored modules.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor src/logistique/processor.py to eliminate duplicate code and reduce method complexity. Introduce a domain-driven design approach to improve cohesion in the processor logic.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Incrementally increase test coverage to 60% by adding integration and unit tests for the most critical paths, particularly those affecting real-time latency.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a performance audit to identify latency bottlenecks in the refactored modules. Optimize database queries and caching strategies to meet real-time constraints.", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression if refactoring is not accompanied by comprehensive testing. The team's junior-heavy composition may slow progress, but senior oversight can mitigate risks. Without immediate action, the accumulation of technical debt could force a costly migration in the future. The circular dependencies and low cohesion pose the highest risk to system stability and real-time performance."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0200", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 62.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme de streaming média en temps réel utilisée par 2,5M d'utilisateurs actifs mensuels, développée en PHP/Laravel avec une base de données MySQL. Le système doit garantir une latence inférieure à 200ms pour les requêtes critiques, tout en supportant des pics de trafic liés à des événements en direct. L'équipe de 24 développeurs maintient une codebase de 8,8 ans avec une exigence forte de stabilité et de performance.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines : un couplage très faible (1,1/10) indique une architecture modulaire bien structurée, tandis qu'une cohésion élevée (8,2/10) confirme que les composants sont bien alignés sur leurs responsabilités. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2,5 et l'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs suggèrent un code maintenable malgré son âge. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0,15 sur le fichier le plus chaud est modéré, ce qui limite les risques de dette technique critique. La couverture de tests à 62,6% est perfectible mais acceptable pour une application mature où les tests manuels et les validations en production jouent un rôle complémentaire.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. La stack PHP/Laravel/MySQL, bien que perçue comme 'vieillissante', répond aux exigences de performance et de maintenabilité grâce à une architecture saine. Une refonte complète introduirait des risques majeurs (perte de stabilité, courbe d'apprentissage, coûts cachés) sans garantie de gains proportionnels. L'accent doit être mis sur des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour renforcer la résilience et la scalabilité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests à 80% via des tests automatisés (unitaires et d'intégration) pour les endpoints critiques et les services temps réel. Prioriser les modules avec une complexité cyclomatique > 3.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Optimiser les requêtes SQL les plus fréquentes (identifiées via les logs) en ajoutant des index ciblés et en révisant les schémas de données pour les tables à fort trafic (ex: logs d'événements en temps réel).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mettre en place un système de monitoring avancé (APM) pour tracer les latences par endpoint et identifier les goulots d'étranglement. Intégrer des alertes proactives basées sur des seuils de performance.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Moderniser progressivement les dépendances critiques (ex: Laravel, PHP) via des mises à jour incrémentales (mineures) pour bénéficier des optimisations de performance sans risque de rupture.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible à modéré. Les risques principaux sont liés à l'introduction de bugs lors des optimisations (tests insuffisants) ou à une surcharge de l'équipe pendant les phases 1 et 2. Une approche itérative avec revues de code strictes et tests de charge avant déploiement réduira ces risques. Aucun risque de migration technologique n'est présent, ce qui élimine les dangers associés (ex: perte de données, incompatibilités)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0200", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 62.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a real-time streaming platform built on PHP/Laravel/MySQL, serving a media sector with 24 developers. The system operates under strict latency constraints, requiring continuous optimization to maintain performance for end-users.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy structural metrics: low coupling (1.1/10) and high cohesion (8.2/10) indicate a well-modularized system, while low cyclomatic complexity (2.5) suggests maintainable logic. Test coverage (62.6%) is suboptimal but not critical, and the bugfix-commit ratio (0.15) on the hottest file is within acceptable bounds. No significant anti-patterns were detected, and the team's seniority balance (65% senior) supports incremental improvements over a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the primary constraint (real-time latency) and enhance test coverage. The current architecture is sound and does not justify a high-risk, high-cost rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement targeted performance optimizations for real-time latency bottlenecks, prioritizing database queries and caching strategies.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally increase test coverage to at least 80% by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths, leveraging the existing modular structure.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce lightweight observability tools to monitor latency and system health, enabling data-driven optimizations.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The current architecture is stable, and incremental improvements mitigate risks associated with large-scale changes. The team's experience further reduces execution risk."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0201", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.3}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet SaaS B2B mature, en production depuis près de 10 ans, gère des données sensibles pour des entreprises clientes dans un environnement hautement régulé (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). Il repose sur une stack .NET/ASP.NET Core avec SQL Server, et évolue avec une équipe de 44 développeurs dont la moitié a moins de 3 ans d'expérience dans le codebase. La conformité réglementaire est le principal driver d'évolution, avec des exigences de traçabilité et de sécurité strictes qui impactent fortement la roadmap technique.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase vieillissante mais globalement saine pour son âge, avec des métriques dans la moyenne basse pour un projet de cette taille et complexité. Le score de couplage (5.2/10) et de cohésion (4.7/10) indique une architecture modulaire mais avec des zones de friction, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.3) reste acceptable malgré une couverture de tests faible (32.1%). Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.3) suggère une stabilité relative du code malgré les anti-patterns détectés. Les deux anti-patterns identifiés (God Class et Long Parameter List) sont localisés et gérables sans refonte majeure.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. Une approche incrémentale de modernisation ciblée est préférable pour : 1) améliorer la maintenabilité sans disruption, 2) renforcer la conformité réglementaire par des refactorings localisés, et 3) monter en compétences sur des patterns modernes sans courbe d'apprentissage brutale. Les gains de productivité viendront d'améliorations incrémentales plutôt que d'un big bang.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactorings ciblés sur les anti-patterns identifiés (God Class et Long Parameter List) avec ajout de tests unitaires pour sécuriser les modifications. Priorité aux modules impactant directement les exigences de conformité.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests via une stratégie de tests par couches (unitaires, intégration, E2E) avec focus sur les endpoints critiques pour la conformité. Intégration dans le pipeline CI/CD existant.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Modernisation incrémentale de l'architecture par modules : extraction des responsabilités transverses (logging, sécurité, validation) dans des composants dédiés, avec une approche 'strangler pattern' pour éviter les régressions.", "duration_days_range": "25-35 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les patterns modernes (Clean Architecture, CQRS léger) appliqués aux modules refactorés, avec ateliers pratiques sur des cas concrets du codebase.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global modéré si les refactorings sont menés avec une couverture de tests suffisante et une validation manuelle des fonctionnalités critiques. Le principal risque réside dans l'impact potentiel sur les exigences de conformité lors des modifications de code sensible. Une approche itérative avec revues de code renforcées et tests de non-régression automatisés réduira significativement ce risque. La conformité réglementaire doit être vérifiée après chaque phase de refactoring."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0201", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.2, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 32.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.3}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 9.4-year-old SaaS B2B platform for business management, built on .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, serving enterprise clients with strict regulatory compliance requirements (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). The team of 44 developers (mix of junior and senior) maintains a codebase under heavy regulatory scrutiny, where reliability and maintainability are critical to avoid compliance risks and operational disruptions.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (5.2/10) and cohesion (4.7/10), indicating structural issues that could hinder maintainability and scalability. Test coverage is critically low at 32.1%, leaving large portions of the system unprotected against regressions. Cyclomatic complexity is elevated (6.3), suggesting potential fragility in critical paths. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.3) on the hottest file signals a hotspot prone to frequent fixes, likely due to poor design. Anti-patterns like God Class and Long Parameter List further degrade readability and increase the risk of defects. While the regulatory constraints justify caution, the current state suggests technical debt is accumulating faster than it can be addressed incrementally.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full technology migration at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. The regulatory constraints make a high-risk rewrite unjustifiable unless the system’s stability is demonstrably at risk. Prioritize stability and incremental improvements to reduce defect rates and improve maintainability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address critical anti-patterns: split the God Class in src/saas/processor.py and refactor the Long Parameter List in src/saas/handler.py. Introduce unit tests for the refactored components to ensure behavioral consistency.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage in high-risk modules (e.g., payment processing, user data handling) to at least 50%. Focus on critical paths identified by the bugfix-commit ratio.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural patterns (e.g., CQRS, Domain-Driven Design) in isolated modules to improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Pair with senior developers to mentor junior team members on best practices.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk for incremental improvements. The primary risk lies in the low test coverage, which could lead to regressions during refactoring. Mitigate by introducing comprehensive test suites before and after refactoring. The regulatory constraints add pressure, but a full rewrite would introduce higher risk without clear benefits. Focus on stability and incremental progress to avoid compliance gaps."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0202", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 13, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 9.2, "cohesion_score": 2.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 16.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 11.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.59}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 12-year-old logistics and supply-chain platform built with Node.js/Express and MongoDB, currently facing unpredictable traffic spikes that strain its scalability. The team of 13 developers (mix of junior and senior) maintains a monolithic codebase where core logistics logic, services, and handlers are tightly coupled, leading to frequent regressions and slow bug fixes during peak loads.", "analysis": "The system exhibits severe structural decay: coupling is critically high (9.2/10), cohesion critically low (2.9/10), and test coverage is dangerously low at 16%. Cyclomatic complexity is elevated (11.6), and the hottest file shows a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.59, indicating instability. Anti-patterns are concentrated in core modules (core.py, service.py, handler.py, processor.py), including god classes, circular dependencies, duplicate code, and high coupling. These issues directly undermine scalability and maintainability, especially under unpredictable load. The junior-heavy team composition increases the risk of missteps during any structural change.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full rewrite. Instead, embark on an incremental refactoring and stabilization program focused on reducing coupling, improving cohesion, and increasing test coverage. The current technical debt is severe enough to justify targeted interventions, but not a complete technology shift. The team should first stabilize the system, then gradually decouple critical paths.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Stabilize and isolate the most problematic module (src/logistique/core.py) by extracting cohesive components, breaking circular dependencies, and introducing targeted unit tests. Address the God Class and Long Method anti-patterns first.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage in core modules (core.py, service.py, handler.py) by adding integration and unit tests for critical paths. Aim to raise coverage from 16% to at least 40% in these areas to enable safer refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor src/logistique/service.py and handler.py to eliminate duplicate code and reduce God Class issues. Introduce service layer abstractions and handler decomposition to improve cohesion and reduce coupling.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Address circular dependencies across core modules and introduce dependency injection patterns to further decouple components. Begin migrating critical paths toward a modular, layered architecture.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Implement observability and basic performance testing to monitor scalability under load. Use findings to guide further decoupling and caching strategies.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression during refactoring due to low test coverage and high coupling. Risk is mitigated by incremental, module-by-module approach and mandatory test coverage improvements before structural changes. Team skill mix (54% junior) increases risk of introducing new bugs; pairing and code reviews are essential. Without intervention, scalability issues will worsen during peak traffic, increasing downtime risk."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0205", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme SaaS éducative en croissance continue, utilisée par des milliers d'établissements scolaires et des millions d'utilisateurs. L'application PHP/Laravel gère des pics de trafic imprévisibles liés aux périodes d'examens ou aux lancements de nouveaux contenus pédagogiques. L'équipe technique de 27 développeurs (majoritairement seniors) maintient un produit stable mais rencontre des défis de scalabilité horizontale sous charge variable.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour une application de 14 ans : couplage modéré (3.7/10) et cohésion acceptable (5.0/10) indiquent une architecture maintenable sans être optimale. La couverture de tests à 41.8% est insuffisante mais pas critique, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.4) reste dans une fourchette acceptable pour du PHP/Laravel. Les anti-patterns détectés (high coupling dans service.py et handler.py) sont concentrés dans des modules critiques mais gérables. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.42) suggère une dette technique modérée mais pas explosive. La contrainte de scalabilité est réelle mais ne justifie pas un rewrite complet : une approche incrémentale ciblée sur les goulots d'étranglement serait plus efficace.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack. Privilégier une refonte incrémentale des modules les plus couplés (service.py et handler.py) pour améliorer la scalabilité et la maintenabilité, tout en augmentant progressivement la couverture de tests. Une migration partielle vers des services asynchrones (queues Laravel) pour absorber les pics de trafic serait plus judicieuse qu'un changement radical de technologie.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des modules service.py et handler.py pour identifier les dépendances circulaires et les goulots d'étranglement scalabilité. Proposition d'une architecture modulaire ciblée.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'une stratégie de découplage progressif des modules identifiés, avec extraction des responsabilités critiques vers des services dédiés (ex: service de gestion des utilisateurs, service de traitement des contenus).", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Migration partielle vers des queues Laravel pour les opérations gourmandes en ressources (ex: génération de rapports, envoi de notifications), avec monitoring des gains de performance.", "duration_days_range": "15-25 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests via des tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés sur les modules refactorisés, avec intégration continue dans le pipeline CI/CD.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré si la refonte est mal planifiée : dépendances non détectées entre modules, ou sous-estimation des impacts sur les performances. Cependant, l'approche incrémentale limite fortement ce risque. Le principal danger serait de vouloir aller trop vite sur la phase 2 sans avoir consolidé les bases (phase 1). Une revue technique hebdomadaire avec l'équipe est recommandée pour valider chaque étape."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0205", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.7, "cohesion_score": 5.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.42}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a long-running edtech platform built with PHP/Laravel and MySQL, serving a growing user base with unpredictable traffic spikes. The codebase has evolved over 14 years, and the team of 27 developers—mostly senior—faces scalability challenges due to inconsistent traffic patterns and tight coupling in core service and handler components.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.7/10 and cohesion at 5.0/10, indicating room for improvement but not an immediate crisis. Test coverage at 41.8% is low and concerning, especially given the traffic unpredictability and the presence of high-coupling anti-patterns in critical files like src/edtech/service.py and src/edtech/handler.py. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 4.4, but the bugfix-commit ratio of 0.42 in the hottest file suggests fragility in frequently modified areas. While a full rewrite could address these issues, the existing architecture is not yet at a breaking point that would justify such a high-risk, high-cost move.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to reduce coupling, increase test coverage, and improve maintainability in the most problematic areas. A full rewrite would introduce significant disruption without clear evidence that it would solve the scalability challenges better than incremental refactoring.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Improve test coverage and introduce targeted refactoring in high-coupling files (src/edtech/service.py, src/edtech/handler.py) to reduce coupling and improve cohesion. Prioritize adding unit and integration tests to the most frequently modified and bug-prone areas.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement caching and queue-based processing strategies to handle unpredictable traffic spikes. Evaluate and optimize database queries, indexing, and connection pooling to improve scalability without changing the core architecture.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce modular design patterns (e.g., domain-driven design or service-oriented architecture) incrementally to further decouple components. Focus on extracting high-coupling logic into well-defined, independently testable modules.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The recommended approach avoids the high-risk strategy of a full rewrite and instead focuses on incremental improvements that can be validated and rolled back if necessary. The primary risks lie in the low test coverage and the presence of high-coupling anti-patterns, which could lead to unintended side effects during refactoring. Mitigation involves thorough testing, feature flags, and gradual rollouts."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0206", "language": "fr", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 9.6, "cohesion_score": 3.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 21.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.56}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet SaaS B2B mature, en production depuis 6.7 ans, propose une solution de gestion d'entreprise pour des clients soumis à des exigences réglementaires strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). Développé initialement en Node.js/NestJS avec PostgreSQL, il compte 22 développeurs dont une majorité de juniors, et doit constamment adapter son codebase pour répondre aux évolutions des normes de conformité tout en maintenant une stabilité opérationnelle critique pour ses clients entreprises.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une architecture globalement saine malgré une dette technique non négligeable. Le score de couplage élevé (9.6/10) indique une structure modulaire bien découpée, ce qui est un atout majeur pour une migration future si nécessaire. En revanche, la cohésion faible (3.3/10) et la couverture de tests insuffisante (21.4%) sont des signaux d'alerte critiques, surtout dans un contexte réglementaire où la fiabilité du code est primordiale. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne élevée (9.8) et les anti-patterns détectés (notamment les listes de paramètres longues et méthodes trop longues) confirment une dégradation progressive de la maintenabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.56) suggère que les développeurs passent plus de temps à corriger des bugs qu'à développer de nouvelles fonctionnalités, ce qui impacte directement la vélocité de l'équipe.", "recommendation": "Ne pas envisager de migration technologique complète à ce stade. La stack actuelle (Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL) est adaptée au contexte SaaS B2B et les métriques de couplage montrent une architecture modulaire viable. L'effort doit se concentrer sur l'amélioration incrémentale de la maintenabilité et de la fiabilité du code existant, avec une priorité absolue sur la conformité réglementaire. Une refonte partielle ciblée des modules les plus critiques (comme ceux identifiés avec des anti-patterns) serait plus judicieuse qu'un rewrite complet.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi pour identifier les modules les plus critiques pour la conformité réglementaire et prioriser les zones à risque. Mise en place d'un plan de refactoring incrémental avec des revues de code systématiques.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests (objectif initial : 40-50%) en ciblant d'abord les modules critiques pour la conformité. Introduction de tests d'intégration pour les flux réglementaires (RGPD, PCI-DSS).", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring des anti-patterns détectés (Long Parameter List, Long Method) dans les fichiers src/saas/service.py et src/saas/processor.py. Décomposition des méthodes complexes et application du principe de responsabilité unique (SRP).", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'une stratégie de tests automatisés pour les évolutions futures, incluant des tests de mutation pour renforcer la robustesse. Formation de l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques de développement (clean code, SOLID) et les enjeux de conformité.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la dégradation continue de la maintenabilité du code, qui pourrait à terme impacter la capacité à répondre aux exigences réglementaires ou à livrer de nouvelles fonctionnalités. Cependant, une migration complète présenterait des risques encore plus élevés : perte de connaissances sur la stack actuelle, courbe d'apprentissage pour une nouvelle technologie, et surtout un risque de non-conformité pendant la transition. L'approche incrémentale proposée limite ces risques tout en améliorant progressivement la qualité du code. La conformité réglementaire doit rester le fil conducteur de toutes les décisions techniques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0206", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 22, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 9.6, "cohesion_score": 3.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 21.4, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 9.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.56}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 6.7-year-old SaaS B2B platform for business management built with Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, serving enterprise clients with strict regulatory compliance requirements (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). The codebase has evolved under a team of 22 developers, 77% of whom are junior, and now faces maintainability challenges that threaten its ability to meet evolving compliance standards efficiently.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits severe structural issues: extreme coupling (9.6/10) and poor cohesion (3.3/10) indicate a monolithic architecture where components are tightly interdependent, making changes risky and testing difficult. Test coverage at 21.4% is critically low, and the high bugfix-commit ratio (0.56) on the hottest file suggests a maintenance hotspot. Cyclomatic complexity (9.8) and recurring anti-patterns (long methods, long parameter lists, duplicate code) compound the technical debt, creating a fragile system where regulatory compliance fixes are likely to introduce regressions. The junior-heavy team further exacerbates these risks, as complex refactoring requires experienced oversight.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, prioritize targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical structural issues while building team capacity. Focus first on reducing coupling and improving cohesion through modularization, then incrementally increase test coverage and address the worst anti-patterns. This approach will stabilize the codebase for compliance work without the high risk and cost of a rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a modularization audit to identify and extract the most tightly coupled domains (e.g., payment processing, user management) into separate services or modules. Introduce clear interfaces and dependency injection to reduce coupling. Parallelly, assign senior developers to mentor juniors on refactoring techniques.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the highest-impact anti-patterns: refactor the long methods and parameter lists in src/saas/service.py and src/saas/processor.py using the Extract Method and Introduce Parameter Object patterns. Decompose the duplicate code in src/saas/core.py into reusable utilities or shared modules.", "duration_days_range": "15-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage by writing characterization tests for the hottest files (e.g., the bugfix hotspot) to capture existing behavior before refactoring. Gradually expand coverage to critical paths, prioritizing compliance-related modules.", "duration_days_range": "10-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement a continuous compliance pipeline to validate regulatory requirements (e.g., RGPD data deletion, PCI-DSS encryption) as part of the CI/CD process. Use the improved modularity to isolate compliance-sensitive logic for easier validation.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression during refactoring due to extreme coupling and low test coverage. Mitigate by enforcing strict code review for all changes, prioritizing small, reversible steps, and leveraging senior developers to guide juniors. The regulatory constraint adds urgency, but a rewrite would carry prohibitive risk; incremental improvements are the safer path."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0207", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Marketplace en croissance avec une base de code vieillissante de près de 4 ans, développée en Node.js/NestJS et PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 42 développeurs, composée majoritairement de profils seniors, fait face à des défis opérationnels majeurs : des incidents de production récurrents qui impactent la fiabilité du système, malgré une stack technique mature et une équipe expérimentée. La complexité croissante du code et les anti-patterns détectés commencent à peser sur la vélocité et la stabilité des livraisons.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent un système à la fois complexe et fragile : un couplage et une cohésion médiocres (5.1/10) indiquent une architecture peu modulaire, tandis qu'une complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5.4 et des méthodes trop longues (notamment dans core.py et service.py) confirment une dette technique accumulée. La couverture de tests à 50.6% est insuffisante pour garantir la stabilité, surtout dans un contexte où la fiabilité est critique. Les anti-patterns identifiés (God Class, High Coupling, Circular Dependency) sont des symptômes classiques d'un codebase qui a évolué sans refactoring systématique. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.35 suggère que près d'un tiers des modifications sont des corrections d'urgence, ce qui est un signe clair de dégradation de la maintenabilité. Cependant, la stack technique actuelle (Node.js/NestJS) est adaptée au domaine du marketplace et ne présente pas de risque de obsolescence majeure à court terme.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration technologique coûteuse et risquée, une stratégie de stabilisation et de modernisation incrémentale est fortement recommandée. L'objectif prioritaire est de réduire la fréquence des incidents en production en améliorant la fiabilité du code existant. Cela passe par une combinaison de refactoring ciblé pour éliminer les anti-patterns majeurs, une augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests (en priorité sur les modules les plus critiques et instables), et l'introduction de bonnes pratiques d'architecture (modularité, séparation des responsabilités) via des revues de code et des ateliers techniques. Une migration ne serait justifiée que si ces actions s'avéraient insuffisantes après 12-18 mois de travail discipliné.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des modules critiques pour la stabilité. Identification des 5-10 fichiers les plus problématiques (incluant handler.py, processor.py, service.py, core.py) et création d'un plan de refactoring incrémental avec des critères de succès mesurables (réduction du couplage, élimination des anti-patterns).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'une stratégie de tests : augmentation de la couverture sur les modules identifiés comme instables (cible initiale : +15% de couverture sur les fichiers critiques). Introduction de tests d'intégration pour valider les interactions entre modules fortement couplés. Automatisation des tests de non-régression pour les endpoints critiques du marketplace.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring des anti-patterns majeurs : décomposition des God Classes (handler.py, core.py), réduction du couplage dans processor.py, et élimination des dépendances circulaires. Chaque refactoring doit s'accompagner de tests automatisés pour valider le comportement avant/après. Documentation des nouvelles interfaces et contrats pour faciliter la maintenance future.", "duration_days_range": "30-40"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Amélioration continue de l'architecture : introduction de principes de modularité (ex: séparation claire entre handlers, services, et processors), mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour détecter les nouveaux anti-patterns, et formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques (ex: SOLID, Clean Architecture). Mise à jour de la documentation technique pour refléter les changements.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la sous-estimation de la dette technique : si les incidents de production persistent malgré les refactorings, la pression pour une migration complète pourrait devenir ingérable. Un autre risque est la résistance au changement dans une équipe de 42 développeurs, où les juniors (39%) pourraient être moins enclins à adopter des pratiques strictes de qualité. Pour mitiger ces risques, il est crucial de : (1) impliquer l'équipe dans la priorisation des modules à refactorer, (2) mesurer l'impact des changements sur la stabilité (ex: réduction du nombre d'incidents) après chaque phase, et (3) communiquer clairement les bénéfices attendus (ex: temps de résolution des incidents réduit, vélocité améliorée)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0207", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 42, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 50.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 3.9-year-old Node.js/NestJS marketplace platform operated by a team of 42 developers, with a critical reliability constraint due to frequent production incidents. The codebase has grown organically, leading to structural issues such as high coupling and low cohesion, which contribute to maintenance challenges and incident frequency.", "analysis": "The computed metrics reveal a codebase with moderate structural integrity (coupling and cohesion scores of 5.1/10) and concerning maintainability indicators. The test coverage of 50.6% and a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.35 on the hottest file suggest fragility in critical paths. Anti-patterns such as circular dependencies, high coupling, long methods, and a god class are concentrated in core marketplace modules (handler, processor, service, core), which directly correlates with the uptime issues. The cyclomatic complexity of 5.4 is acceptable but masks localized hotspots where complexity is likely much higher. The team composition (mix of junior and senior developers) is adequate for incremental improvements but not for a large-scale rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the anti-patterns and structural issues in the most critical modules. Improve test coverage incrementally, particularly around the files with high bugfix ratios. Implement modularization and dependency inversion to reduce coupling and improve cohesion. These steps will directly address the reliability constraint without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the god class in src/marketplace/handler.py and break it into smaller, single-responsibility classes. Introduce dependency injection to eliminate circular dependencies. Add targeted unit tests for the refactored components.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address high coupling in src/marketplace/processor.py by introducing interfaces and facade patterns. Extract long methods into smaller, focused functions. Add integration tests to validate processor behavior.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Improve test coverage in critical modules (handler, processor, service) by adding missing unit and integration tests, prioritizing files with high bugfix-commit ratios. Implement CI checks to enforce coverage thresholds.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Refactor src/marketplace/core.py to reduce cyclomatic complexity by breaking down long methods and extracting domain logic into separate modules. Introduce architectural boundaries to improve cohesion.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Implement observability improvements (logging, metrics) in refactored modules to reduce incident detection and resolution time. Conduct a reliability review to validate improvements.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The phased approach minimizes disruption by targeting the most problematic modules first. The risk of regression is mitigated by incremental changes and increased test coverage. However, without strict governance, there is a risk of scope creep or incomplete refactoring. The team's mixed experience level may slow progress, but senior developers can lead the effort to ensure quality."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0208", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 31, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.9, "cohesion_score": 7.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.15}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est une plateforme IoT industrielle dédiée à la gestion de données sensibles issues de capteurs industriels. Elle doit répondre à des exigences strictes de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) tout en assurant une scalabilité adaptée à un écosystème en croissance. L'équipe de 31 développeurs, majoritairement junior, maintient une codebase mature en Ruby/Rails et MySQL depuis 5 ans, avec une forte pression sur la stabilité et la sécurité des données.", "analysis": {"coupling_score": "Le score de couplage à 1.9/10 indique une architecture très modulaire avec des dépendances maîtrisées, ce qui est idéal pour une maintenance à long terme et une évolutivité progressive. Ce niveau de découplage réduit significativement les risques de propagation d'erreurs et facilite les tests unitaires.", "cohesion_score": "Un score de cohésion à 7.7/10 est excellent pour une codebase de cette taille et de cet âge. Cela suggère que les modules sont bien conçus autour de responsabilités claires, limitant la duplication de code et améliorant la lisibilité.", "test_coverage": "Avec 72.1% de couverture de tests, le projet se situe dans une fourchette acceptable pour une application métier critique. Cependant, une couverture plus élevée (80%+) serait préférable pour les zones sensibles (traitement des données personnelles, paiements, etc.) afin de renforcer la conformité réglementaire.", "cyclomatic_complexity": "Une complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 1.1 est remarquablement basse, signe d'un code simple et facile à maintenir. Cela réduit les risques de bugs et simplifie les revues de code.", "corrective_commits_ratio": "Un ratio de 0.15 de commits correctifs sur le fichier le plus chaud est modéré et suggère que les hotspots sont gérés de manière proactive. Cela indique une bonne stabilité globale malgré la présence de développeurs juniors.", "anti_patterns": "La détection d'une *Circular Dependency* (même de faible criticité) dans `src/iot/handler.py` est un signal à surveiller. Bien que peu impactante aujourd'hui, elle pourrait devenir problématique avec l'ajout de nouvelles fonctionnalités ou une refonte partielle."}, "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. La stack Ruby/Rails/MySQL est parfaitement adaptée au contexte IoT industriel et aux contraintes de conformité, à condition d'appliquer des améliorations ciblées. Une migration vers une autre stack (ex: Java/Spring, Go) n'apporterait pas de gain significatif en termes de maintenabilité ou de performance, tout en introduisant des risques élevés (courbe d'apprentissage pour l'équipe, coûts cachés de réécriture partielle, etc.).", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Renforcer la couverture de tests sur les zones critiques (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) en ciblant d'abord les modules les plus exposés aux risques réglementaires. Prioriser les tests d'intégration et de sécurité.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Résoudre l'anti-pattern de *Circular Dependency* dans `src/iot/handler.py` en appliquant des principes de conception SOLID (ex: inversion de dépendances). Documenter la solution pour éviter les récidives.", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mettre en place un programme de mentorat pour les développeurs juniors (72% de l'équipe) afin d'améliorer la qualité du code et réduire les risques de régression. Inclure des revues de code systématiques sur les modules sensibles.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimiser les performances de la base de données MySQL en analysant les requêtes lentes et en ajoutant des index stratégiques. Prioriser les tables les plus sollicitées par les endpoints critiques.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": {"technical": "Faible à modéré. La codebase est saine et bien structurée, mais la présence de développeurs juniors (72%) introduit un risque humain non négligeable. Une mauvaise gestion des hotspots ou une accumulation de dette technique pourrait dégrader la qualité à moyen terme.", "regulatory": "Modéré. La conformité est un enjeu majeur, mais les métriques actuelles (couplage, cohésion, tests) suggèrent que le code est suffisamment robuste pour répondre aux exigences réglementaires, à condition de renforcer les tests dans les zones sensibles.", "operational": "Faible. La stack Ruby/Rails/MySQL est mature et bien supportée, avec une communauté active pour les correctifs de sécurité. Les risques opérationnels sont donc limités, sous réserve d'une maintenance proactive."}}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0209", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 31, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.6, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.21}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est une plateforme de streaming média en Node.js/NestJS avec PostgreSQL, en production depuis 13 ans. Elle doit gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles tout en supportant une équipe majoritairement junior, ce qui impose une architecture à la fois robuste et maintenable malgré une dette technique accumulée sur le long terme.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour une application mature : un couplage modéré (5.6/10) et une complexité cyclomatique moyenne (7.0) restent dans des limites acceptables. La couverture de tests à 46% est faible mais pas critique pour une application existante, surtout avec une équipe junior majoritaire. Les anti-patterns détectés (duplicate code, long parameter list, long method) sont concentrés dans 3 fichiers critiques liés au traitement média, ce qui limite leur impact global. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.21) suggère une stabilité relative malgré la dette technique.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. La priorité doit être une refonte incrémentale ciblée des composants identifiés comme problématiques (processor.py, handler.py, core.py) pour améliorer la cohésion et réduire la dette technique. Une approche progressive permettra de maintenir la plateforme opérationnelle tout en améliorant sa maintenabilité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des 3 fichiers problématiques pour identifier les dépendances critiques et les points d'entrée/sortie", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation incrémentale des méthodes longues et des listes de paramètres dans processor.py et handler.py avec extraction de services dédiés", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Déduplication du code dans core.py via l'extraction de composants réutilisables et mise en place de tests unitaires pour valider les changements", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests sur les modules refactorisés (objectif : +20% minimum) avec intégration continue", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Documentation des nouvelles interfaces et bonnes pratiques pour l'équipe junior, avec sessions de pair programming pour la transmission des connaissances", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré lié à la refactorisation de fichiers critiques pendant les pics de trafic. Stratégie de mitigation : déploiement par étapes avec feature flags, sauvegardes automatiques de la base de données, et monitoring renforcé des endpoints media. Le risque majeur serait une dégradation des performances si les extractions de services ne sont pas optimisées pour le scale horizontal."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0209", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 31, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.6, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 46.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.21}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a media streaming platform built on Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, serving a user base that experiences unpredictable traffic spikes. Over its 13.2-year lifespan, the codebase has grown organically, now maintained by a team of 31 developers with a majority of junior members. The primary technical challenge is ensuring scalability to handle sudden load increases without compromising performance or stability.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (5.6/10) and cohesion (4.7/10), indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage at 46.1% is below the threshold for confident refactoring, and the average cyclomatic complexity of 7.0 suggests some methods may be difficult to maintain. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.21 on the hottest file is concerning but not alarming. Anti-patterns such as duplicate code and long parameter lists are localized and addressable without a full rewrite. The team's junior-heavy composition may struggle with large-scale architectural changes, making incremental improvements more viable.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the critical scalability constraint while improving code quality incrementally. The team should prioritize reducing anti-patterns, increasing test coverage, and simplifying complex methods to enhance maintainability and stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-impact anti-patterns: refactor Long Method and Long Parameter List in src/media/processor.py and src/media/handler.py, and deduplicate code in src/media/core.py. Introduce unit tests for the refactored modules to raise coverage incrementally.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage by adding integration tests for critical media processing flows and API endpoints. Parallelly, introduce basic performance monitoring to identify bottlenecks during traffic spikes.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor the media processing pipeline to reduce coupling and improve cohesion, focusing on modularizing the core media handling logic. Implement caching strategies to mitigate scalability issues during unpredictable traffic.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a scalability stress test to validate improvements and identify remaining gaps. Document architectural decisions and onboard junior developers with targeted training on the refactored modules.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the junior-heavy team composition and low test coverage, which could lead to regressions during refactoring. However, the localized nature of anti-patterns and the absence of systemic architectural flaws reduce the overall risk. Incremental improvements mitigate the likelihood of major disruptions."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0211", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 34, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet MedTech en Python/Django gère des flux de données critiques pour des dispositifs médicaux connectés, avec une base de code vieillissant de 9 ans. L'équipe de 34 développeurs, majoritairement juniors, maintient un système central pour le traitement des données patients et la génération de rapports réglementaires, sous contraintes de conformité strictes mais sans pression de performance immédiate.", "analysis": "La base de code présente des indicateurs globalement sains pour son âge : couplage et cohésion dans une fourchette acceptable (4.5/10 et 4.7/10), une complexité cyclomatique moyenne modérée (5.4) et un ratio de commits correctifs raisonnable (0.33). La couverture de tests à 49.8% est perfectible mais pas alarmante pour un système de cette maturité. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method et God Class en medium) sont localisés et gérables sans refonte majeure.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. Une approche incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns identifiés et l'amélioration de la couverture de tests serait plus efficace et moins risquée qu'un rewrite complet. L'équipe devrait prioriser la stabilisation du code existant avant d'envisager des changements majeurs.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Décomposition des anti-patterns identifiés (Long Method dans handler.py et God Class dans service.py) via des refactorings incrémentaux avec tests de régression automatisés", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests à 65-70% via des tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés sur les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "15-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un plan de maintenance préventive incluant revues de code systématiques et documentation des décisions architecturales", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le risque principal réside dans l'inertie de l'équipe junior face à des refactorings complexes. Une approche progressive avec revues de code renforcées et mentorat des seniors est essentielle pour éviter les régressions. Aucun risque majeur de blocage fonctionnel n'est identifié à court terme."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0211", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 34, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.5, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.33}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 9.3-year-old medtech application built with Python/Django and PostgreSQL, serving as a critical backend system for healthcare workflows. The team of 34 developers (79% junior, 5% senior) maintains a codebase under no immediate critical constraints but faces challenges with code maintainability and test coverage. The system processes sensitive patient data, requiring high reliability and incremental improvements over a full rewrite.", "analysis": "The computed metrics indicate a moderately healthy codebase with no critical constraints, but several areas require attention. Coupling (4.5/10) and cohesion (4.7/10) scores suggest the system is neither overly tangled nor excessively modular, leaning toward manageable complexity. The test coverage (49.8%) is suboptimal but not alarmingly low, while the average cyclomatic complexity (5.4) is within acceptable limits for a mature system. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.33) on the hottest file implies some instability in critical paths, likely exacerbated by the detected anti-patterns: a Long Method and a God Class in core service files. These anti-patterns are medium-severity and can be incrementally refactored without disrupting the system's stability.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the identified anti-patterns and enhance test coverage. A full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk given the absence of critical constraints and the manageable complexity of the existing codebase.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in src/sante/service.py into smaller, cohesive components using the Extract Class and Move Method refactorings. Introduce clear separation of concerns and reduce method complexity.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the Long Method in src/sante/handler.py by breaking it into smaller, single-responsibility functions. Pair with senior developers to ensure the refactoring aligns with the system's domain logic.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage by writing missing unit and integration tests for the refactored components. Prioritize critical paths identified during the refactoring phase.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Introduce static analysis tools (e.g., SonarQube, Pylint) to enforce coding standards and detect anti-patterns early. Configure CI/CD pipelines to block merges for new violations.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The absence of critical constraints and the manageable complexity of the codebase reduce the risk of a full rewrite. However, refactoring core service files without comprehensive test coverage introduces some risk of introducing regressions. Mitigate this by prioritizing test coverage improvements alongside refactoring and leveraging pair programming with senior developers. The team's junior-heavy composition may slow progress but can be offset by structured mentorship and incremental delivery."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0212", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "fintech / paiements", "team_size": 5, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 65.3, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 3.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet fintech gère des transactions de paiement en temps réel avec une stack historique Node.js/Express et MongoDB. L'application doit absorber des pics de trafic imprévisibles tout en garantissant une haute disponibilité, avec une équipe de 5 développeurs dont une majorité de profils juniors. La base de code, âgée de 13,8 ans, est considérée comme stable mais nécessite une optimisation continue pour répondre aux exigences de scalabilité actuelles.", "analysis": "Les métriques indiquent une architecture saine et mature : un couplage très faible (1.1/10) suggère une bonne modularité, tandis qu'une cohésion élevée (8.3/10) confirme une séparation claire des responsabilités. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (3.0) reste dans une plage acceptable, et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.12) montre une stabilité relative du code. L'absence d'anti-patterns significatifs est un indicateur fort de la qualité de la conception. La couverture de tests (65,3%) est perfectible mais suffisante pour des améliorations incrémentales ciblées.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données actuelles. La stack Node.js/Express/MongoDB, bien que mature, reste adaptée au contexte fintech sous réserve d'optimisations ciblées. Une refonte complète serait risquée et coûteuse sans preuve tangible d'un gain de scalabilité supérieur à l'existant. L'accent doit être mis sur des améliorations incrémentales pour renforcer la résilience et la maintenabilité.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit de performance et profiling des endpoints critiques sous charge pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement spécifiques aux pics de trafic.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests via des tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés sur les modules les plus sollicités (priorité aux endpoints de paiement).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes MongoDB et mise en place d'un cache distribué (ex: Redis) pour les données fréquemment accédées, avec validation des gains de performance.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques de scalabilité (ex: load balancing, horizontal scaling) et documentation des procédures de déploiement pour les pics de trafic.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des validations intermédiaires. Les risques principaux résident dans les optimisations de performance (régressions possibles) et la formation de l'équipe (nécessité d'un accompagnement adapté aux juniors). Aucun risque majeur de migration technologique n'est présent, contrairement à une refonte complète."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0214", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.7, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 38.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est un marketplace mature développé en Node.js/NestJS avec une base de code de plus de 12 ans, hébergeant une équipe de 43 développeurs majoritairement juniors. L'application gère des transactions complexes entre acheteurs et vendeurs avec une stack technique PostgreSQL, et nécessite une stabilité opérationnelle élevée pour garantir la fluidité des échanges.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase avec des métriques globalement acceptables pour un projet de cette maturité, mais des anti-patterns structurels significatifs (God Class, Circular Dependencies, Duplicate Code) qui impactent la maintenabilité. Le couplage modéré (5.7/10) et la cohésion faible (4.7/10) suggèrent une architecture qui a évolué organiquement sans refactoring systématique. La couverture de tests à 38.7% est insuffisante pour un projet critique, mais le ratio de commits correctifs (0.24) indique une stabilité relative malgré les défauts structurels. L'équipe junior majoritaire rend prioritaire la simplification du code avant toute migration.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack. Privilégier un refactoring ciblé pour éliminer les anti-patterns critiques (God Class, Circular Dependencies) et améliorer la cohésion. La couverture de tests doit être augmentée progressivement pour atteindre au moins 60% avant toute modification majeure. Une migration serait prématurée sans base technique plus solide.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi avec identification des dépendances circulaires et des duplications de code prioritaires à corriger", "duration_days_range": "5-7 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental du God Class dans handler.py et des Circular Dependencies critiques dans service.py et core.py", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Ajout de tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules refactorisés (objectif : couverture > 50%)", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Migration progressive des duplications de code dans processor.py et service.py vers des modules réutilisables", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Revue d'architecture pour proposer des améliorations structurelles (ex: séparation des responsabilités, introduction de DDD léger)", "duration_days_range": "7-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de code systématiques. Le principal risque est la résistance au changement dans une équipe majoritairement junior, mais l'approche incrémentale limite l'exposition. Aucun risque critique identifié pour la stabilité opérationnelle si les refactorings sont testés rigoureusement."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0214", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "marketplace", "team_size": 43, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.7, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 38.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/marketplace/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/marketplace/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "This is a 12-year-old marketplace platform built with Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, maintained by a team of 43 developers with a majority of junior members. The system has evolved organically over time, serving as the core transactional backbone for a growing digital marketplace with no critical constraints currently identified by the team.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with a coupling score of 5.7/10 and cohesion score of 4.7/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe architectural decay. Test coverage at 38.7% is below industry standards, which may impact maintainability and reliability. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 4.6, suggesting the code is not excessively convoluted. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.24 on the hottest file is concerning but not alarming, as it may reflect active maintenance rather than inherent fragility. Anti-patterns such as circular dependencies and god classes are present but localized, with high-severity issues in specific modules (processor.py, handler.py, service.py). These findings suggest the system is functional but would benefit from targeted refactoring rather than a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve test coverage. The current metrics do not justify a full rewrite, which would introduce significant risk given the team's size and experience distribution.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-severity anti-patterns: break circular dependencies in src/marketplace/service.py, split the God Class in src/marketplace/handler.py, and reduce duplicate code in src/marketplace/processor.py. Introduce automated tests for these modules to reach at least 60% coverage in the refactored areas.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage across the codebase by adding missing unit and integration tests, prioritizing critical paths and modules with high bugfix ratios. Introduce static analysis tools to detect and prevent anti-patterns in CI/CD pipelines.", "duration_days_range": "30-45"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor remaining medium-severity anti-patterns (e.g., duplicate code in service.py, circular dependencies in core.py) and conduct a code review to enforce better separation of concerns and modularity. Document architectural decisions and update onboarding materials for junior developers.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The absence of critical constraints reduces immediate risk, but the high proportion of junior developers may slow down refactoring efforts. The localized nature of anti-patterns limits the blast radius of changes. However, inadequate test coverage could lead to regressions during refactoring, necessitating careful planning and incremental rollouts. The team's lack of experience with large-scale migrations further increases the risk of a full rewrite being ill-advised."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0215", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.0, "cohesion_score": 5.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet MedTrack est une plateforme de gestion des dossiers patients pour un réseau de cliniques spécialisées en imagerie médicale. Développée en Python avec Flask et PostgreSQL, cette application critique doit garantir un uptime de 99,9% pour éviter tout risque sur la continuité des soins. L'équipe de 38 développeurs, majoritairement junior, maintient une base de code de 2,2 ans qui subit des incidents de production récurrents, principalement liés à des problèmes de fiabilité dans les services métiers critiques.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase avec des métriques globalement médiocres mais pas catastrophiques : un couplage élevé (4.0/10) et une cohésion faible (5.2/10) indiquent une architecture qui peine à isoler les responsabilités. La couverture de tests à 47,1% est insuffisante pour une application de santé, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 6.9 suggère des fonctions difficiles à maintenir. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Parameter List dans les handlers, couplage élevé dans les services) confirment des problèmes de conception qui expliquent en partie les incidents récurrents. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.45 sur le fichier le plus chaud est préoccupant mais pas alarmant.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack technologique n'est pas justifiée par les données actuelles. Les métriques ne montrent pas de blocage technique absolu (comme une dette technique insurmontable ou une stack obsolète sans support), mais plutôt des problèmes de conception et de qualité de code qui peuvent être résolus par des améliorations incrémentales. Une refonte partielle ciblée sur les composants les plus critiques (comme les services fortement couplés) serait plus pertinente et moins risquée qu'un rewrite complet.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit approfondi des composants critiques (src/sante/core.py et src/sante/service.py) pour identifier les dépendances circulaires et les responsabilités mal définies. Mise en place d'un plan de découplage progressif avec des interfaces claires.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests sur les modules les plus instables (cibler d'abord les services avec un ratio de commits correctifs élevé). Introduction de tests d'intégration pour valider les interactions critiques.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring des handlers identifiés avec des Long Parameter List (src/sante/handler.py) pour appliquer le pattern Command ou introduire des objets DTO. Validation par des revues de code strictes et des tests de charge simulés.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place de mécanismes de monitoring avancés (APM, logs structurés) et de rollback automatisés pour réduire l'impact des incidents. Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques de conception logicielle adaptées au contexte santé.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la persistance des incidents de production pendant la phase de refactoring, surtout si les tests ne couvrent pas suffisamment les cas critiques. Un autre risque est la résistance au changement de l'équipe junior, qui pourrait privilégier des solutions rapides plutôt que des améliorations structurelles. Pour mitiger ces risques, il est crucial de prioriser les composants les plus instables et de valider chaque changement par des tests automatisés avant déploiement. La contrainte de fiabilité impose une approche prudente et incrémentale."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0215", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 38, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.0, "cohesion_score": 5.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 47.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.45}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 2.2-year-old medtech application built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, serving a healthcare sector where system reliability and uptime are critical. The team of 38 developers (with a majority of junior members) maintains a codebase that has recently faced frequent production incidents, prompting a need for stability improvements and architectural refinement.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (4.0/10) and cohesion (5.2/10), indicating structural issues that likely contribute to the reliability problems. With a test coverage of 47.1% and an average cyclomatic complexity of 6.9, the system lacks sufficient safeguards against regressions. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.45 on the hottest file suggests this component is a hotspot for defects. Anti-patterns like Long Parameter List and High Coupling are concentrated in critical modules (handler.py, core.py, service.py), which explains the frequent production incidents. The team's junior-heavy composition may exacerbate these issues, as complex or tightly coupled code is harder to maintain without strong testing and design practices.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this stage. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the root causes of instability: high coupling, low test coverage, and anti-patterns. Prioritize refactoring the most problematic files (handler.py, core.py, service.py) to reduce coupling and improve cohesion, while incrementally increasing test coverage. Pair this with mentorship for junior developers to improve code quality and reduce defect rates.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a detailed architectural review to identify the most critical coupling points and anti-patterns, then define a refactoring strategy for the top 3-5 most problematic files.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted refactoring for the identified files, starting with handler.py to address the Long Parameter List anti-pattern. Pair refactoring with unit test development to ensure no regression.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Expand test coverage incrementally, focusing on the refactored modules and critical paths. Introduce static analysis tools to enforce coding standards and detect anti-patterns early.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Run a reliability improvement sprint: address the remaining high-coupling issues in core.py and service.py, and conduct a blameless post-mortem on recent production incidents to extract actionable insights.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Establish ongoing mentorship and code review practices to sustain improvements, with a focus on knowledge sharing between senior and junior developers.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium risk. The proposed incremental approach mitigates the high risk of a full rewrite by focusing on small, reversible changes. However, refactoring core modules without sufficient test coverage could introduce regressions. To mitigate this, prioritize test development alongside refactoring and ensure all changes are backed by feature flags or canary deployments. The team's junior-heavy composition may slow progress, but targeted mentorship can offset this risk."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0217", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 6.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Système de monitoring IoT industriel en Python/Flask pour une usine connectée, gérant des milliers de capteurs avec des contraintes de latence modérées. L'application centralise les données de production et déclenche des alertes en temps réel, avec une base de données PostgreSQL optimisée pour des requêtes analytiques. L'équipe actuelle, majoritairement junior, maintient ce système depuis 3 ans avec une dette technique progressive mais non bloquante.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour un projet de 3.3 ans avec une équipe majoritairement junior. Le couplage (5.8/10) et la cohésion (6.2/10) restent dans une fourchette acceptable, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (6.3) est modérée pour un système IoT. La couverture de tests à 45.7% est faible mais pas critique, surtout pour un projet où la logique métier est relativement simple. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.24) indique une stabilité acceptable malgré la présence de juniors. Les anti-patterns détectés (duplicate code et circular dependency) sont localisés et gérables sans refonte majeure.", "recommendation": "Éviter un rewrite complet ou une migration technologique radicale. Privilégier une stratégie d'amélioration incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns critiques et l'augmentation de la couverture de tests, tout en renforçant les compétences de l'équipe via du pair programming et des revues de code systématiques.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Résolution des anti-patterns critiques : découplage de la circular dependency dans src/iot/core.py via l'extraction d'interfaces, et refactorisation du duplicate code dans src/iot/service.py avec des utilitaires dédiés.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests : ajout de tests unitaires pour les modules critiques (ex: gestion des alertes) et intégration de tests d'intégration pour les endpoints Flask, avec formation des juniors aux bonnes pratiques de test.", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la documentation technique et mise en place d'un pipeline de qualité (linting, analyse statique automatisée) pour prévenir la régression des anti-patterns résolus.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré : les améliorations incrémentales limitent l'exposition aux bugs, mais la faible couverture de tests initiale et l'expérience junior de l'équipe pourraient ralentir l'adoption des nouvelles pratiques. Un accompagnement par un senior dédié pendant les phases 1 et 2 est recommandé pour mitiger ces risques."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0217", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 33, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.8, "cohesion_score": 6.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 45.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.24}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/iot/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 3.3-year-old industrial IoT platform built with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL, serving as the backbone for a growing fleet of connected devices. The team of 33 developers, predominantly junior, maintains a codebase under moderate coupling and cohesion constraints while facing challenges with test coverage and code maintainability in critical modules like service orchestration and core system logic.", "analysis": "The current metrics indicate a moderately healthy codebase with no critical constraints identified by the team. Coupling (5.8/10) and cohesion (6.2/10) scores suggest the system is neither overly tangled nor excessively modular, which is typical for a mid-aged IoT platform. The test coverage (45.7%) is suboptimal but not alarming, especially given the junior-heavy team, where prioritizing testability may not yet be a cultural norm. Cyclomatic complexity (6.3) is within acceptable limits for Python, though improvements in specific files could reduce maintenance friction. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.24) on the hottest file is concerning but not catastrophic, implying reactive fixes are common but not overwhelming. The detected anti-patterns—duplicate code in `src/iot/service.py` and a circular dependency in `src/iot/core.py`—are localized and high-impact, warranting immediate attention but not a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate or rewrite the system. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the anti-patterns and boost test coverage. The current architecture is functional, and the team’s junior-heavy composition makes a full migration risky without stronger foundational practices. Prioritize refactoring the circular dependency and deduplicating the service layer to reduce technical debt incrementally.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor circular dependency in `src/iot/core.py` by introducing dependency injection or breaking the cycle into smaller, cohesive modules. Pair with a senior developer to mentor juniors on the refactoring process.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Deduplicate `src/iot/service.py` by extracting shared logic into reusable utilities or services. Add unit tests for the refactored components to prevent regression.", "duration_days_range": "7-10 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage by adding missing tests for critical paths, starting with the refactored modules. Introduce lightweight code review guidelines to enforce testability standards.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a workshop for the team on identifying and avoiding anti-patterns (e.g., circular dependencies, duplication) and best practices for modular design in Python.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the junior-heavy team’s unfamiliarity with refactoring complex dependencies and the potential for introducing new bugs during targeted improvements. Mitigation involves pairing seniors with juniors during refactoring and enforcing incremental testing. No existential risks to the system are identified."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0218", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 5, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.1, "cohesion_score": 8.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 79.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.9, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.12}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un service de streaming média en Python/Django avec MongoDB, lancé il y a 7 ans, qui a connu une croissance organique sans refonte majeure. L'équipe de 5 développeurs gère une codebase mature avec une complexité cyclomatique maîtrisée et une bonne couverture de tests, mais subit une pression sur les coûts cloud due à une architecture peu optimisée pour l'efficacité des ressources.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs sains : couplage faible (1.1/10), cohésion élevée (8.6/10), et complexité cyclomatique contenue (1.9). La couverture de tests à 79.8% est acceptable pour un projet mature, et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.12) suggère une stabilité fonctionnelle. L'unique anti-pattern détecté (circular dependency mineure dans un service média) est isolé et n'impacte pas la maintenabilité globale. Le problème de coût cloud semble davantage lié à des choix d'infrastructure qu'à la qualité du code. L'équipe expérimentée (78% seniors) est capable de maintenir et d'optimiser l'existant sans risque majeur.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer ou refactorer massivement. Privilégier une optimisation ciblée de l'architecture cloud et des améliorations incrémentales de la codebase pour réduire les coûts et éliminer les anti-patterns résiduels.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit détaillé des coûts cloud par service et identification des gaspillages (instances surdimensionnées, requêtes MongoDB inefficaces, etc.)", "duration_days_range": "5-8"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correction de la circular dependency dans src/media/service.py et mise en place de tests automatisés pour valider la correction", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes MongoDB (indexation, agrégations) et mise en cache des données fréquemment accédées", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Migration progressive vers des instances cloud plus adaptées (ex: passage à des instances spot pour les tâches batch) avec monitoring renforcé", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Documentation des bonnes pratiques cloud et formation de l'équipe sur l'optimisation des coûts", "duration_days_range": "3-5"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global faible à modéré. Les risques principaux sont liés à l'optimisation cloud (impact potentiel sur les performances si mal configuré) et à la correction de la circular dependency (risque de régression si mal testé). Cependant, ces risques sont maîtrisables avec une approche incrémentale et des tests automatisés. Aucun risque de blocage majeur ou de dette technique insurmontable n'a été identifié."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0220", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.5, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 56.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.22}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Système de monitoring IoT industriel pour une flotte de capteurs déployés dans des environnements critiques (usines, réseaux énergétiques). L'application Python/Django centralise les données des capteurs via une API REST, gère les alertes en temps réel et génère des rapports d'analyse pour les opérateurs. La stack actuelle, en place depuis près de 9 ans, doit évoluer pour répondre à des exigences de scalabilité tout en surmontant une pénurie croissante de développeurs maîtrisant Python/Django et MongoDB.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs globalement sains pour son âge : un couplage modéré (3.5/10) et une cohésion acceptable (4.9/10) suggèrent une architecture modulaire malgré son ancienneté. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.6) reste dans une fourchette gérable, et le ratio de commits correctifs (0.22) indique une stabilité relative. Cependant, la couverture de tests (56.8%) est un point de vigilance majeur, surtout pour un système critique où la fiabilité est primordiale. Les anti-patterns détectés dans `src/iot/core.py` (couplage élevé) confirment des zones de friction technique qui pourraient freiner les évolutions futures.", "recommendation": "Une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. En revanche, une refonte ciblée des composants identifiés comme problématiques (notamment `core.py`) est nécessaire pour améliorer la maintenabilité et préparer l'équipe à des évolutions futures. L'accent doit être mis sur l'amélioration de la couverture de tests et la réduction du couplage dans les modules critiques, tout en capitalisant sur les compétences existantes de l'équipe.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des modules critiques (notamment `src/iot/core.py`) pour identifier les dépendances cachées et les responsabilités mal définies. Définition d'un plan de découplage progressif avec des interfaces claires.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration incrémentale de la couverture de tests (objectif : +20% en 3 mois) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés sur les modules les plus instables. Intégration d'outils de mutation testing pour valider l'efficacité des tests.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring des anti-patterns détectés (couplage élevé dans `core.py`) en appliquant le principe de responsabilité unique (SRP) et en introduisant des interfaces pour isoler les dépendances externes (ex: MongoDB). Mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour prévenir les régressions.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques de découplage et de testabilité, avec un focus sur les outils modernes (ex: pytest, factory_boy) compatibles avec la stack actuelle. Documentation des décisions architecturales pour faciliter l'onboarding.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré lié à la pénurie de talents : une migration complète vers une nouvelle stack pourrait aggraver cette situation en réduisant l'expertise disponible sur le code existant. Le principal risque réside dans l'absence de tests suffisants pour valider les changements incrémentaux, ce qui pourrait introduire des régressions dans un système critique. Une approche progressive avec des jalons clairs minimise ce risque, mais nécessite une discipline stricte dans la gestion des tests et des revues de code."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0220", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "IoT industriel", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.5, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 56.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.22}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/iot/core.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 8.8-year-old IoT industrial platform built with Python, Django, and MongoDB, serving as the backbone for critical device management and data processing. With a team of 20 developers (41% senior, 28% junior), the system faces growing challenges in maintaining and scaling due to a scarcity of available talent proficient in the current stack, threatening long-term sustainability and innovation velocity.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.5/10 and cohesion at 4.9/10, indicating room for improvement but not critical failure. Test coverage at 56.8% is suboptimal and contributes to a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.22 on the hottest file, suggesting areas of fragility. Cyclomatic complexity averages 5.6, which is manageable but not ideal for maintainability. The detected anti-patterns (high coupling in src/iot/core.py) are localized and do not appear systemic. The primary constraint—talent scarcity—is real but does not yet justify a full stack migration, which would introduce significant risk and cost without clear evidence of architectural failure.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the talent scarcity constraint and improve maintainability. The current architecture can be sustained with focused refactoring and process improvements, avoiding the high risk and disruption of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address the most critical anti-pattern: refactor src/iot/core.py to reduce high coupling by decomposing into smaller, focused modules with clear responsibilities. Introduce dependency injection to isolate components and improve testability.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage incrementally by adding targeted unit and integration tests for the most critical paths, prioritizing areas with high bugfix ratios. Aim to raise coverage to at least 70% over time.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce modern Python tooling (e.g., type hints, linters, static analysis) and enforce coding standards to reduce complexity and improve readability. Pair this with knowledge-sharing sessions to upskill junior developers and reduce dependency on niche stack expertise.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Pilot a gradual migration of non-critical modules to a more widely adopted stack (e.g., Python/FastAPI/PostgreSQL) to reduce talent scarcity risks. Start with a small, low-risk service to validate the approach before broader adoption.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the talent scarcity constraint and localized architectural issues. A full migration would introduce high risk of disruption, extended downtime, and potential data loss, while incremental improvements carry lower risk and allow for controlled validation. The team’s seniority (41%) provides a strong foundation for executing targeted refactoring safely."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0222", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 28, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Plateforme SaaS éducative en Python/Flask utilisée par 120 000 utilisateurs mensuels, centralisant la gestion des cours, des évaluations et des interactions en temps réel. L'application subit des pannes récurrentes en période de forte charge (examens, rentrées scolaires), impactant la satisfaction des utilisateurs et la réputation de l'entreprise. L'équipe technique, majoritairement junior, peine à stabiliser le système en raison d'une architecture monolithique vieillissante et d'une dette technique accumulée sur 9 ans.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase mature mais fragilisée par des anti-patterns structurels majeurs : couplage élevé (4.6/10), méthodes trop longues et classes monolithiques (complexité cyclomatique moyenne à 5.0), et une couverture de tests insuffisante (41.5%) qui limite la capacité à détecter les régressions. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.44) sur les fichiers critiques confirme un cycle de maintenance réactif plutôt que préventif. Ces problèmes expliquent directement les incidents de fiabilité en production, sans pour autant justifier une migration technologique radicale. La stack actuelle (Python/Flask/PostgreSQL) reste adaptée au domaine edtech, où la stabilité et la maintenabilité priment sur l'innovation technologique.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une réécriture complète, privilégier une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns identifiés pour réduire la dette technique et améliorer la fiabilité. L'objectif est de briser le monolithe en modules plus petits et testables, tout en augmentant progressivement la couverture de tests. Cette approche permet de traiter la cause racine des incidents (couplage, méthodes longues, classes god) sans perturber l'activité ni nécessiter une montée en compétences massive sur une nouvelle stack. Une migration technologique ne serait justifiée que si les améliorations incrémentales échouaient à stabiliser le système après 12-18 mois.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des fichiers critiques (src/edtech/processor.py, src/edtech/handler.py, src/edtech/core.py) via une analyse des dépendances et des chemins de code les plus chauds.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Décomposition des classes God et extraction des méthodes longues en services dédiés (ex: un service de traitement des évaluations séparé de la logique métier principale). Mise en place de tests unitaires pour les nouveaux composants.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Réduction du couplage dans src/edtech/handler.py via l'introduction d'une couche d'abstraction (ex: interface pour les handlers) et suppression des duplications dans src/edtech/core.py. Intégration continue des tests existants.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests (objectif : +15% en 3 mois) via des tests d'intégration ciblés sur les modules refactorisés. Déploiement en staging avec monitoring renforcé.", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Validation en production par vagues (canary releases) des modules refactorisés, avec rollback automatique en cas de dégradation des métriques de fiabilité (uptime, temps de réponse).", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré lié à la complexité de la refonte incrémentale : les juniors pourraient sous-estimer les dépendances entre modules, entraînant des régressions temporaires. Cependant, ce risque est maîtrisable avec une revue de code stricte et des tests automatisés. Le vrai danger serait une migration technologique prématurée (ex: vers FastAPI ou un micro-service), qui ajouterait une couche de complexité inutile sans résoudre les problèmes de couplage ou de tests. La priorité absolue reste la stabilité opérationnelle, pas l'innovation technologique."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0222", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 28, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.6, "cohesion_score": 6.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.44}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a core learning management system in the edtech sector, built over 9.5 years with a Python/Flask/PostgreSQL stack. It serves 28 developers, including a majority of junior engineers, and operates under strict reliability constraints due to frequent production incidents. The system is critical for delivering educational content and must maintain high uptime to support continuous learning environments.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 4.6/10 and cohesion at 6.9/10, indicating room for improvement but not outright failure. Test coverage at 41.5% is low and likely contributes to the frequent production incidents. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 5.0 on average, but the presence of high-severity anti-patterns—such as a God Class in processor.py, long methods in core.py and handler.py, and high coupling in handler.py—suggests that maintenance is becoming increasingly difficult. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.44 on the hottest file implies that changes are frequently reactive, further indicating fragility. The team’s junior-heavy composition may exacerbate these issues, as complex refactoring requires experienced oversight.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this time. Instead, focus on targeted, incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve test coverage. This approach will reduce production incidents more rapidly and build team confidence without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite. The existing stack is capable of supporting these changes, and the team’s size and skill mix make incremental refactoring feasible with proper guidance.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a focused refactoring of the hottest files (handler.py, core.py, processor.py) to address the God Class, long methods, and high coupling. Implement modularization by extracting responsibilities into smaller, well-named functions and classes. Introduce dependency injection to reduce coupling in handler.py. Parallel to this, incrementally increase test coverage for these files to at least 70%, prioritizing critical paths and failure scenarios.", "duration_days_range": "45-60 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement a lightweight monitoring and observability layer to improve incident detection and response. Add structured logging, error tracking, and basic alerting for key endpoints. Pair this with a post-incident review process to identify recurring issues and feed findings back into the refactoring backlog.", "duration_days_range": "20-30 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce automated testing at the integration level, focusing on API endpoints and database interactions. Gradually expand coverage to include edge cases and user workflows. Use this phase to onboard junior developers to testing best practices through pair programming and code reviews.", "duration_days_range": "30-45 days"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Establish a technical debt backlog and a lightweight governance process to prevent regression. Introduce static analysis tools (e.g., SonarQube, pylint) into the CI pipeline to enforce coding standards and flag new anti-patterns early. Schedule regular refactoring sprints (e.g., one per quarter) to address remaining issues in lower-priority modules.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risk is the potential for production incidents during refactoring, particularly if changes are not thoroughly tested or if rollbacks are not straightforward. To mitigate this, changes should be made behind feature flags where possible, and a rollback plan should be prepared for each refactoring task. Another risk is the team’s junior-heavy composition, which could slow progress or lead to new anti-patterns if not properly mentored. This can be addressed by pairing senior developers with juniors and providing targeted training on refactoring techniques and testing practices. Overall, the risks are manageable with disciplined execution and incremental delivery."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0223", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce, en production depuis 7 ans, gère un catalogue de plusieurs milliers de produits avec un trafic saisonnier marqué. L'application repose sur une stack Node.js/NestJS avec PostgreSQL, déployée sur un cloud public où les coûts d'infrastructure ont augmenté de 35% sur les 12 derniers mois sans amélioration proportionnelle des performances.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs contrastés : un couplage modéré (5.0/10) et une cohésion perfectible (4.3/10) suggèrent une architecture globalement maintenable mais avec des zones de friction. La couverture de tests à 54.5% et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 6.7 indiquent un besoin d'amélioration de la robustesse, particulièrement dans les modules critiques. Les anti-patterns identifiés (Long Method et Duplicate Code) sont concentrés dans deux fichiers centraux, ce qui limite leur impact systémique. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.47) reste dans une fourchette acceptable pour une codebase de cet âge, bien qu'il pointe vers des zones à risque. La contrainte cloud n'est pas liée à la stack technique mais à l'architecture d'infrastructure et aux pratiques de scaling.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration technologique coûteuse et risquée, privilégier une refonte ciblée des deux fichiers identifiés comme problématiques, couplée à une amélioration progressive de la couverture de tests et à une optimisation de l'architecture cloud. Cette approche permet de réduire les coûts opérationnels immédiats tout en préparant le terrain pour des évolutions futures si nécessaire.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Découpage des Long Methods et élimination des Duplicate Codes dans src/e-commerce/service.py et src/e-commerce/handler.py, avec ajout de tests unitaires pour les nouvelles fonctions (objectif : porter la couverture de ces modules à 80%).", "duration_days_range": "20-25 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Audit des pratiques de scaling cloud et mise en place de politiques de right-sizing pour les instances critiques, avec monitoring des coûts par service.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la cohésion globale en identifiant et isolant les responsabilités transverses (ex: logging, caching) dans des modules dédiés, avec revue d'architecture pour valider les changements.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de tests automatisés amélioré (intégration continue) et formation des développeurs juniors aux bonnes pratiques de test et de découplage.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global modéré : les anti-patterns sont concentrés et gérables, mais leur correction nécessite une attention particulière pour éviter les régressions. Le risque principal réside dans la résistance au changement de l'équipe, particulièrement pour les juniors (58% de l'effectif). Une communication claire des bénéfices (stabilité, maintenabilité, réduction des coûts cloud) et un accompagnement technique sont essentiels pour minimiser ce risque."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0223", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 41, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.0, "cohesion_score": 4.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 54.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.47}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mid-sized e-commerce platform built on Node.js/NestJS with a PostgreSQL backend, running for 7.7 years with a team of 41 developers (58% junior, 25% senior). The primary operational concern is escalating cloud costs, which the team aims to address while maintaining stability and scalability during peak traffic periods.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate structural health with a coupling score of 5.0/10 and cohesion score of 4.3/10, indicating room for improvement but not severe architectural decay. Test coverage at 54.5% is suboptimal and contributes to a bugfix-commit ratio of 0.47 on the hottest file, suggesting that defects are being addressed reactively rather than proactively. Cyclomatic complexity of 6.7 is within acceptable bounds but signals potential maintainability challenges as the codebase evolves. The detected anti-patterns—Long Method in service.py and Duplicate Code in handler.py—are localized issues that, if resolved, could improve maintainability and reduce technical debt without requiring a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the dominant constraint (cloud cost) and structural weaknesses. Prioritize refactoring the identified anti-patterns, improving test coverage, and optimizing database queries to reduce cloud expenses. These changes will yield measurable benefits with lower risk and shorter feedback cycles than a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the Long Method in src/e-commerce/service.py to improve readability and maintainability, splitting it into smaller, single-responsibility functions. Introduce unit tests for the refactored components to ensure behavioral consistency.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the Duplicate Code in src/e-commerce/handler.py by extracting shared logic into reusable utility functions or classes. Update existing tests and add new ones to cover the refactored code.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Increase test coverage from 54.5% to at least 70% by writing missing unit and integration tests for critical paths. Focus on areas with high cyclomatic complexity to reduce defect rates.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimize database queries and indexes to reduce cloud costs. Profile slow queries, implement caching where appropriate, and review schema design for potential improvements.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The proposed changes are incremental and localized, minimizing the risk of introducing systemic failures. However, refactoring without sufficient test coverage could introduce regressions, which is mitigated by the planned increase in test coverage in Phase 3. The team's junior-heavy composition may slow progress, so pairing senior developers with juniors during refactoring is recommended to ensure quality."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0225", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 9.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 64.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.0}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 2.7-year-old SaaS B2B application for business management, built on .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server. The team of 27 developers (with a majority of junior members) faces challenges in feature delivery speed, prompting an evaluation of the codebase's maintainability and architectural health.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a healthy codebase with strong cohesion (9.0/10) and low cyclomatic complexity (1.2), suggesting the current architecture is well-structured and maintainable. The coupling score (3.0/10) is moderate but not alarming, and the absence of bugfix commits in the hottest file implies stability. The test coverage (64%) is suboptimal but not critical, especially given the low complexity and high cohesion. The only detected anti-pattern is a low-severity circular dependency, which is unlikely to significantly impact delivery speed. The junior-heavy team may benefit from targeted improvements rather than a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the primary constraint: feature delivery speed. The current architecture is sound, and a full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk and delay without clear justification.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Increase test coverage to at least 80% by adding missing unit and integration tests, prioritizing high-impact modules. Pair junior developers with seniors to improve testing practices and knowledge sharing.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Address the circular dependency by refactoring the affected module (src/saas/processor.py) into smaller, more focused components. Use dependency inversion to reduce coupling and improve testability.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement lightweight architectural reviews for new features to ensure they align with the existing high-cohesion design. Introduce automated code quality gates in CI/CD to prevent regressions.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risk is the potential for scope creep during incremental improvements, but this is mitigated by the healthy baseline metrics. The circular dependency is minor and can be resolved without major disruption. The junior-heavy team may slow progress initially, but pairing and mentoring will mitigate this."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0226", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.4, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 35.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.37}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un backend de streaming pour un acteur majeur du secteur media, exploitant une stack .NET/ASP.NET Core avec SQL Server. Il doit garantir une latence temps réel critique pour des millions d'utilisateurs, tout en étant maintenu par une équipe majoritairement junior. La base de code, vieillissante de 8,5 ans, présente des défis de scalabilité et de performance qui impactent l'expérience utilisateur.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase modérément complexe avec des scores de couplage et cohésion médiocres (4,4/10 et 5,1/10), indiquant une architecture fragile et des dépendances mal maîtrisées. La couverture de tests à 35,6% est insuffisante pour des évolutions sûres, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5,8 et les anti-patterns détectés (dépendances circulaires, God Class, duplication) confirment un code difficile à maintenir. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0,37) suggère une dette technique croissante, mais reste gérable sans réécriture complète. La contrainte de latence temps réel n'est pas directement liée à ces problèmes structurels, mais pourrait être aggravée par un refactoring mal maîtrisé.", "recommendation": "Éviter une migration complète ou un rewrite, qui serait risqué avec une équipe majoritairement junior et une couverture de tests insuffisante. Privilégier une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns critiques et l'amélioration de la testabilité, en parallèle d'une optimisation des goulots d'étranglement de latence. Une approche progressive réduira les risques tout en apportant des gains mesurables.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des dettes techniques à corriger en priorité (anti-patterns high/medium, classes critiques pour la latence). Mise en place d'un plan de refactoring incrémental avec des revues de code strictes.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests via des tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés sur les modules critiques (ex: processor.py, handler.py). Introduction de tests de performance pour valider les gains de latence.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring des classes God et des dépendances circulaires identifiées, avec validation des performances en conditions réelles. Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques (SOLID, Clean Architecture) pour limiter la récidive.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des goulots d'étranglement de latence via des techniques comme le caching, l'asynchronicité ou l'optimisation des requêtes SQL. Monitoring renforcé pour mesurer l'impact des changements.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque élevé de régression si le refactoring est mal planifié ou trop ambitieux. Cependant, une approche incrémentale avec des tests solides et des revues de code réduit significativement ce risque. La latence temps réel pourrait être temporairement impactée pendant les optimisations, mais des benchmarks préalables permettront de cibler les zones critiques. L'équipe junior nécessite un accompagnement fort pour éviter l'introduction de nouveaux anti-patterns."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0226", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "media / streaming", "team_size": 32, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.4, "cohesion_score": 5.1, "test_coverage_estimate": 35.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.37}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/media/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/media/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "A real-time media streaming platform built on .NET/ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, serving a growing user base with strict latency requirements. The codebase has evolved over 8.5 years with a team of 32 developers, predominantly junior, and faces challenges in maintainability due to historical architectural decisions and anti-patterns in critical components.", "analysis": "The metrics reveal a system with moderate structural health: coupling and cohesion scores are neither alarmingly high nor ideal, while test coverage at 35.6% leaves significant room for improvement. Cyclomatic complexity is within acceptable bounds, but the presence of high-impact anti-patterns (circular dependencies, god classes) in critical files like `handler.py` and `processor.py` indicates fragility in the core logic. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.37 suggests these files are hotspots for defects, likely due to their monolithic design and tight coupling. The team's junior-heavy composition exacerbates these risks, as refactoring complex areas without adequate test coverage could introduce regressions.", "recommendation": "Do not pursue a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve test coverage. The real-time latency constraint can be preserved by avoiding sweeping changes to the core architecture. The team should prioritize breaking down the god class in `processor.py` and resolving circular dependencies in `handler.py`, paired with immediate test coverage expansion around these components.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a focused refactoring of the god class in `processor.py` by applying the Single Responsibility Principle, splitting it into smaller, cohesive components. Simultaneously, address circular dependencies in `handler.py` through interface extraction and dependency inversion. Introduce comprehensive unit and integration tests for the refactored components, aiming to increase coverage in these areas from ~35% to at least 60%.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Expand test coverage across the remaining critical paths in the media processing pipeline, targeting files with high bugfix-commit ratios. Implement observability improvements (e.g., structured logging, metrics) to monitor latency and stability post-refactoring.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural patterns (e.g., CQRS, event sourcing) in a non-breaking manner to further reduce coupling and improve scalability, but only in areas where the current anti-patterns are resolved. Pair this with mentorship sessions for junior developers to ensure sustainable practices.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression if refactoring is attempted without sufficient test coverage. The junior-heavy team may struggle with complex architectural changes, increasing the likelihood of introducing new defects. However, the risks are mitigated by focusing on incremental, test-driven improvements rather than large-scale rewrites. The real-time latency constraint is preserved by avoiding changes to the core data flow."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0229", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 6.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet medtech, en production depuis plus de 11 ans, gère des fonctionnalités critiques pour le suivi de patients et l'intégration avec des équipements médicaux. La stack historique PHP/Laravel/MySQL supporte une base de code monolithique qui a évolué avec les besoins métiers, mais dont la vélocité de développement s'est progressivement dégradée en raison d'une accumulation de dette technique et d'une complexité croissante des services métiers.", "analysis": "L'analyse révèle une codebase avec des métriques globalement saines mais des points de friction localisés. Le couplage modéré (4.8/10) et la cohésion acceptable (6.7/10) indiquent une architecture potentiellement refactorisable. La couverture de tests à 52% est insuffisante mais pas rédhibitoire, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 6.0 reste dans une plage gérable. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, Long Method) sont concentrés dans des zones spécifiques, ce qui suggère une dette technique ciblée plutôt qu'un problème systémique. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.31 est préoccupant mais pourrait être amélioré par des tests plus robustes. L'équipe de 20 développeurs, avec une proportion importante de juniors, bénéficierait d'un accompagnement méthodologique pour les refactoring.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique complète n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées : refactoring des anti-patterns identifiés, augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests, et mise en place de bonnes pratiques de développement pour réduire la dette technique. Ces actions permettront d'améliorer la vélocité de développement sans prendre les risques d'une réécriture complète.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des zones à risque", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring des anti-patterns identifiés (God Class, Long Method) avec couverture de tests augmentée", "duration_days_range": "20-30 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de tests automatisés et de revues de code systématiques", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe aux bonnes pratiques de développement et de refactoring", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Évaluation post-refactoring et planification d'éventuels refactorings supplémentaires", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la résistance au changement de l'équipe, particulièrement les développeurs juniors qui pourraient percevoir les refactorings comme une perte de temps. Un accompagnement méthodologique est crucial pour garantir l'adoption des bonnes pratiques. Le risque de régression fonctionnelle existe mais est atténué par l'approche incrémentale et la couverture de tests progressive. La contrainte de vélocité pourrait temporairement être impactée pendant les phases de refactoring, mais devrait s'améliorer significativement à moyen terme."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0229", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 20, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 4.8, "cohesion_score": 6.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 52.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 6.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.31}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/sante/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a healthcare software suite built on PHP/Laravel/MySQL, serving a team of 20 developers (42% junior, 5% senior) with a dominant constraint of slow feature delivery. The 11.3-year-old codebase supports critical medtech operations, where recent static analysis reveals moderate coupling (4.8/10) and cohesion (6.7/10), alongside uneven test coverage (52.2%) and structural anti-patterns that hinder velocity.", "analysis": "The metrics indicate a codebase with moderate structural health but clear bottlenecks in delivery speed. While coupling (4.8/10) and cohesion (6.7/10) are not alarming, the presence of high-severity anti-patterns (Long Parameter List, Long Method, God Class) in critical files directly correlates with the team's velocity constraint. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.31) and cyclomatic complexity (6.0) suggest fragility in core components, but the overall architecture remains salvageable. A full rewrite would be premature given the lack of systemic decay (e.g., coupling >7/10 or cohesion <4/10) and the team's junior-heavy composition, which would amplify migration risks.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, execute targeted refactoring to address the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. The current stack (PHP/Laravel/MySQL) is adequate for the domain, and the team's size/composition favors iterative improvements over a risky rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-severity anti-patterns in src/sante/service.py and src/sante/core.py by splitting God Classes, extracting Long Methods, and reducing Long Parameter Lists. Pair with junior developers to ensure knowledge transfer.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage from 52.2% to ≥70% by writing characterization tests for modified components first, then expanding to critical paths. Use mutation testing to validate test effectiveness.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural boundaries (e.g., domain layers, CQRS) to reduce coupling in hotspots. Implement lightweight monitoring (e.g., SonarQube) to track coupling/cohesion trends post-refactor.", "duration_days_range": "10-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from junior-heavy team involvement in refactoring and potential regression during anti-pattern fixes. Mitigate by pairing seniors with juniors, enforcing strict code reviews, and limiting refactor scope to one module at a time. The absence of systemic decay (e.g., high coupling/low cohesion) reduces rewrite risks."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0231", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.6, "cohesion_score": 4.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 57.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet medtech, développé en .NET/ASP.NET Core avec SQL Server, gère des données sensibles de santé sous contraintes réglementaires strictes (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). Il s'agit d'une application critique pour les workflows médicaux d'un groupe de cliniques, avec une équipe de 27 développeurs majoritairement juniors, nécessitant une stabilité maximale pour éviter tout risque de non-conformité.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une base de code modérément complexe (couplage à 5.6/10, cohésion faible à 4.0/10) avec des anti-patterns critiques comme un God Class et des duplications dans un module central. La couverture de tests à 57.8% est insuffisante pour une application réglementée, mais la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.3) reste dans une fourchette gérable. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.4) suggère une stabilité relative malgré les problèmes structurels. L'équipe, majoritairement junior, bénéficierait davantage d'une amélioration incrémentale que d'une refonte radicale.", "recommendation": "Ne pas migrer vers une nouvelle stack. Privilégier une refactorisation ciblée des anti-patterns identifiés (God Class et duplication) combinée à une augmentation progressive de la couverture de tests, en priorisant les modules critiques pour la conformité réglementaire. Une migration complète serait risquée avec cette équipe et ces contraintes.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit réglementaire et priorisation des modules critiques pour la conformité (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS)", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation incrémentale du God Class et des duplications dans src/sante/handler.py, avec extraction de responsabilités en services dédiés", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests (objectif : +15% sur les modules critiques) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration, avec revue des tests existants", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place de revues de code systématiques et de guidelines pour éviter les anti-patterns futurs, avec formation de l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque MODÉRÉ si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de code rigoureuses. Le principal risque est une dégradation temporaire de la stabilité pendant la refactorisation du God Class, mais ce risque est atténué par une approche incrémentale et une priorisation des modules réglementaires. Une migration complète aurait un risque ÉLEVÉ de non-conformité et de perte de productivité avec cette équipe."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0231", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 27, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.6, "cohesion_score": 4.0, "test_coverage_estimate": 57.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.3, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.4}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "God Class", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 2.6-year-old .NET/ASP.NET Core application in the medtech sector, developed by a team of 27 developers (70% junior). It operates under strict regulatory constraints (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS) and serves as a critical system for healthcare data processing, requiring high reliability and compliance adherence.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits moderate coupling (5.6/10) and low cohesion (4.0/10), indicating structural fragility that could hinder maintainability and scalability. Test coverage at 57.8% is suboptimal but not critically low, while cyclomatic complexity (5.3) remains within acceptable bounds for a .NET application. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.4) suggests recurring issues in the hottest file, compounded by the presence of a God Class and duplicate code in a critical handler module. These anti-patterns directly threaten regulatory compliance and increase the risk of defects. The team's junior-heavy composition may exacerbate maintenance challenges, but their familiarity with the codebase is a mitigating factor.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified given the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the God Class and duplicate code in the handler module, alongside incremental improvements to test coverage and structural quality. These steps will reduce technical debt while maintaining regulatory compliance and leveraging the team's existing expertise.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class and duplicate code in src/sante/handler.py to improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Introduce modular design patterns (e.g., CQRS or mediator pattern) to separate concerns and enforce single responsibility.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally increase test coverage to at least 70% by adding unit and integration tests for the refactored modules. Prioritize critical paths and regulatory-sensitive components.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Conduct a structural analysis to identify and resolve additional coupling/cohesion hotspots. Implement static analysis tools (e.g., SonarQube) to enforce quality gates and monitor progress.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Organize knowledge-sharing sessions and pair programming with senior developers to upskill junior team members on refactoring techniques and architectural best practices.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Medium risk. The presence of regulatory constraints and a junior-heavy team increases the risk of introducing defects during refactoring. However, the phased approach with incremental improvements mitigates this risk by allowing controlled changes and continuous validation. The primary risk lies in underestimating the effort required to address the God Class and duplicate code, which could lead to schedule overruns."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0232", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 40, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.5, "cohesion_score": 9.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 77.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.07}, "anti_patterns": [], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a healthcare and medtech application built on PHP/Laravel/MySQL, serving a team of 40 developers (60% junior, 34% senior) over 11.7 years. The primary operational constraint is escalating cloud costs, which the team aims to address while maintaining system reliability and performance.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits strong structural health with a low coupling score (2.5/10) and high cohesion (9.2/10), indicating a well-modularized architecture. Test coverage stands at 77.7%, which is acceptable for a mature system, and cyclomatic complexity is low (1.6), suggesting maintainable code. The bugfix-commit ratio on the hottest file (0.07) is healthy, and no significant anti-patterns were detected. The team’s junior-heavy composition may benefit from targeted mentorship rather than a full rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the cloud cost constraint while preserving system stability.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Optimize cloud resource usage through profiling, right-sizing, and caching strategies (e.g., Redis for session storage, query optimization). Pair with senior developers to mentor juniors on cost-aware coding practices.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage in critical modules to reach ≥85%, reducing regression risks during future optimizations.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce automated cost-monitoring dashboards and alerts to prevent future cost overruns.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The system’s structural health reduces migration risks, but cloud cost issues require immediate attention to avoid operational disruptions. Incremental changes minimize disruption to the team’s workflow."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0233", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.3, "cohesion_score": 5.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 36.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.26}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet pilote une plateforme de gestion logistique en temps réel pour un réseau de 50 entrepôts, avec une stack Python/Django et MongoDB. L'application doit absorber des pics de trafic soudains lors de promotions commerciales ou de ruptures d'approvisionnement, tout en garantissant une traçabilité des flux en temps réel pour les opérateurs terrain et les clients B2B.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines pour une application en production depuis près de 2 ans. Le score de couplage (3.3/10) indique une architecture modulaire, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.8) reste dans une plage acceptable pour du Python. La couverture de tests (36.6%) est faible mais pas critique pour une application où la logique métier est majoritairement dans Django (ORM, vues, formulaires). Les anti-patterns détectés (duplication de code dans core.py et service.py) sont localisés et de criticité moyenne, sans impact sur la scalabilité. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.26) suggère une stabilité relative du code malgré des pics de trafic imprévisibles.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données. La priorité doit être donnée à des améliorations incrémentales ciblées sur la maintenabilité et la résilience, sans toucher à la stack principale. Une refonte complète serait un risque majeur pour la stabilité opérationnelle, surtout avec des pics de trafic à gérer.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests sur les modules critiques (logistique/core.py et logistique/service.py) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration ciblés, en priorisant les endpoints exposés aux pics de trafic.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactorisation des duplications de code identifiées en extrayant des fonctions utilitaires réutilisables, avec validation par des revues de code strictes pour éviter l'introduction de nouveaux bugs.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimisation des requêtes MongoDB les plus sollicitées lors des pics de trafic, en collaboration avec l'équipe DevOps pour ajuster les index et les stratégies de cache (Redis).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mise en place d'un monitoring avancé (APM) pour tracer les goulots d'étranglement en temps réel, avec des alertes automatisées sur les métriques de performance (latence, erreurs 5xx).", "duration_days_range": "7-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible à modéré si les phases sont exécutées séquentiellement avec des revues de code rigoureuses. Le principal risque serait une tentative de refonte trop ambitieuse qui perturberait la stabilité opérationnelle. L'équipe doit éviter toute modification majeure de l'architecture (ex: passage à une stack synchrone comme Go ou une base SQL) sans preuve tangible de goulot d'étranglement dans les métriques actuelles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0233", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.3, "cohesion_score": 5.3, "test_coverage_estimate": 36.6, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.26}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a logistics and supply-chain platform built in Python/Django with MongoDB, designed to handle unpredictable traffic spikes. The 1.9-year-old codebase supports a team of 7 developers (mix of junior and senior) and must scale efficiently under variable load while maintaining reliability in a critical operational domain.", "analysis": "The current architecture shows moderate coupling (3.3/10) and cohesion (5.3/10), indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage at 36.6% is low and likely hinders safe refactoring. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable (4.8), but the bugfix ratio of 0.26 on the hottest file suggests a potential hotspot that may become a maintenance burden. Two medium-level duplicate code issues are present in core service files, which could be consolidated to reduce redundancy and improve maintainability.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified by the current metrics. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address scalability constraints and technical debt. Prioritize increasing test coverage, reducing duplication, and improving cohesion through refactoring of the identified hotspots. These steps will enhance maintainability and prepare the system for future scaling needs without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Implement targeted test coverage improvements around the hottest file and duplicate code locations to reach at least 60% overall coverage. Pair with senior developers to identify critical paths and write integration tests for core logistics workflows.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor duplicate code blocks in src/logistique/core.py and src/logistique/service.py into shared utility modules. Introduce abstraction layers to improve cohesion and reduce coupling in the logistics domain logic.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Optimize MongoDB schema and indexing strategy to better support unpredictable traffic patterns. Introduce caching layers for frequent queries and implement rate-limiting at the API gateway level.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a scalability review to evaluate current bottlenecks under load. Introduce horizontal scaling mechanisms (e.g., Celery for async tasks, Redis for session/cache) and implement monitoring for traffic spikes.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate risk. The absence of high coupling or extreme complexity limits the risk of major refactoring. However, low test coverage increases the risk of regression during changes. The presence of duplicate code and a moderate bugfix ratio suggests some technical debt that must be managed carefully. Incremental improvements with strong testing discipline will mitigate most risks. A full rewrite is not recommended due to the relatively young age of the codebase and lack of severe architectural flaws."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0234", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.6, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.34}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce en Python/Flask avec PostgreSQL, maintenu par une équipe de 44 développeurs, supporte une plateforme en croissance avec des exigences élevées en termes de vélocité de livraison. Malgré une stack technique mature, la base de code accumule des anti-patterns qui ralentissent significativement l'ajout de nouvelles fonctionnalités et augmentent la dette technique.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une situation contrastée : une couverture de tests à peine à 50% combinée à une complexité cyclomatique moyenne élevée (4.2) et un couplage modéré (3.6/10) indique un risque élevé de régressions lors des modifications. Les anti-patterns détectés (God Class, High Coupling, Long Method) sont concentrés dans trois fichiers centraux, ce qui explique la lenteur des livraisons. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.34) suggère que près d'un tiers des modifications sont des corrections de bugs, ce qui impacte directement la productivité. L'équipe senior majoritaire est un atout pour mener des refactorings ciblés sans risque majeur.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration technologique coûteuse et risquée, une stratégie de refactoring incrémental ciblé sur les trois fichiers identifiés comme problématiques est recommandée. Cette approche permettra d'améliorer significativement la vélocité de développement en réduisant la dette technique sans perturber l'activité opérationnelle. L'amélioration de la couverture de tests doit être prioritaire pour sécuriser les modifications futures.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et plan de refactoring détaillé pour les trois fichiers problématiques (handler.py, core.py, processor.py), incluant des tests de non-régression automatisés", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring incrémental du fichier processor.py (God Class) avec extraction de responsabilités en nouveaux modules, parallèlement à l'augmentation de la couverture de tests pour ce module", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring des méthodes à haute complexité cyclomatique dans core.py (Long Method) avec découpage en fonctions plus petites et mieux nommées, incluant des revues de code strictes", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Réduction du couplage dans handler.py (High Coupling) par extraction d'interfaces et injection de dépendances, avec validation par des tests d'intégration", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 5, "action": "Amélioration globale de la couverture de tests (objectif 70%) via des tests unitaires et d'intégration, avec formation de l'équipe junior sur les bonnes pratiques de test", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré : les refactorings ciblés sur des fichiers spécifiques limitent l'exposition aux régressions. Le principal risque réside dans l'augmentation temporaire de la complexité pendant les modifications, atténué par la présence majoritaire de seniors. La couverture de tests actuelle (50%) nécessite une amélioration progressive pour sécuriser les changements. Aucun risque de migration technologique n'est présent dans cette approche incrémentale."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0234", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 44, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.6, "cohesion_score": 4.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 49.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.2, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.34}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "An e-commerce platform built in Python with Flask and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 44 developers (33% junior, 62% senior). The codebase is 2.1 years old, but feature delivery velocity has become a bottleneck due to architectural friction and code quality issues.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling (3.6/10) and cohesion (4.9/10), with a test coverage of 49.8% and cyclomatic complexity averaging 4.2. While these metrics are not alarming, the presence of high-severity anti-patterns—such as a God Class in `processor.py`, a Long Method in `core.py`, and High Coupling in `handler.py`—significantly impacts development velocity. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.34 on the hottest file suggests maintenance overhead is already non-trivial. The team’s constraint of slow feature delivery is likely exacerbated by these structural issues rather than a need for a full technology shift.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the anti-patterns and improve test coverage incrementally. A full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk and delay without addressing the root cause of the velocity issue.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the God Class in `processor.py` into smaller, single-responsibility components, and break down the Long Method in `core.py`. Introduce unit tests for the refactored modules to reach at least 60% coverage.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Decouple `handler.py` by extracting domain logic into separate services and introduce dependency injection to reduce coupling. Add integration tests for the handler layer.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address the Long Parameter List in `core.py` by introducing DTOs or parameter objects. Expand test coverage to 70% and perform a performance regression check.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Implement observability (logging, metrics) for the refactored components and conduct a post-refactor review to assess velocity improvements.", "duration_days_range": "5-10"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The refactoring is incremental and test-driven, reducing the risk of introducing regressions. However, without strict adherence to the refactoring plan and continuous testing, there is a risk of scope creep or partial fixes that don’t fully address the anti-patterns. The team’s senior-heavy composition mitigates this risk."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0235", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "santé / medtech", "team_size": 15, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 1.2, "cohesion_score": 8.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 72.9, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.8, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.02}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/sante/handler.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet est un système de gestion de données médicales pour une plateforme de santé en ligne, développé en Python avec FastAPI et PostgreSQL. Il sert de backend pour une application utilisée par des professionnels de santé pour suivre des dossiers patients et générer des rapports analytiques.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs techniques solides : un couplage très faible (1.2/10) et une cohésion élevée (8.6/10) indiquent une architecture modulaire et bien structurée. La couverture de tests à 72.9% est acceptable pour un projet de cette maturité, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 2.8 reste dans une plage raisonnable. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.02) suggère une stabilité relative du code. L'anti-pattern détecté (dépendance circulaire mineure) est isolé et ne semble pas impacter la maintenabilité globale.", "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les métriques actuelles. L'équipe devrait plutôt se concentrer sur des améliorations incrémentales ciblées pour renforcer la robustesse du système, notamment en traitant l'anti-pattern de dépendance circulaire et en augmentant progressivement la couverture de tests.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Corriger la dépendance circulaire dans src/sante/handler.py et valider l'impact sur les tests existants", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Identifier les modules critiques sous-traités et renforcer leur couverture de tests (objectif : +5%)", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Documenter les décisions d'architecture et former les juniors sur les bonnes pratiques de modularité", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Faible risque à court terme. Les métriques stables suggèrent une base solide, mais l'équipe junior pourrait bénéficier d'un accompagnement pour éviter l'introduction de nouveaux anti-patterns. Le traitement de la dépendance circulaire doit être prioritaire pour éviter une dégradation future."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0237", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 44.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.48}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet EdTech, lancé il y a 6 mois, vise à moderniser une plateforme d'apprentissage en ligne pour les écoles primaires. Développé en .NET/ASP.NET Core avec SQL Server, il est porté par une équipe de 7 développeurs majoritairement juniors, avec une expertise limitée sur les patterns d'architecture avancés. La stack actuelle répond aux besoins fonctionnels initiaux, mais l'équipe anticipe une croissance rapide des fonctionnalités pédagogiques dans les 12-18 prochains mois.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase jeune mais déjà fragilisée par des anti-patterns structurels (God Class, couplage élevé) et un manque de tests (44.5% de couverture). Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.48) suggère des difficultés de maintenance récurrentes, tandis que la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (5.7) indique des fonctions difficiles à tester et à faire évoluer. Cependant, ces problèmes sont localisés dans quelques modules (handler.py, core.py) et ne remettent pas en cause la viabilité globale du projet. L'absence de contrainte critique actuelle permet une approche progressive.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration technologique coûteuse et risquée, privilégier une refonte incrémentale ciblée sur les anti-patterns détectés. L'objectif est d'améliorer la maintenabilité sans bouleverser la stack existante, en capitalisant sur l'expérience de l'équipe avec .NET. Une approche par étapes permettra de réduire les risques tout en préparant le terrain pour d'éventuelles évolutions futures.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi et priorisation des modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "5-8 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Correction des anti-patterns identifiés (God Class, Long Parameter List) via des refactorings ciblés", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Amélioration de la couverture de tests (objectif : +20%) avec ajout de tests unitaires pour les modules critiques", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Documentation des décisions architecturales et mise en place de revues de code systématiques", "duration_days_range": "5-10 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global MODÉRÉ. Les principaux risques sont liés à la faible expérience de l'équipe sur les patterns d'architecture (risque de régression fonctionnelle) et à la complexité cyclomatique élevée (difficulté à tester les modifications). Ces risques sont atténués par l'approche incrémentale et la possibilité de revenir en arrière sur chaque étape. Aucun risque critique (ex: blocage fonctionnel) n'est identifié à ce stade."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0237", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "edtech", "team_size": 7, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.9, "cohesion_score": 6.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 44.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.7, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.48}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/edtech/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/edtech/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": ".NET", "database_name": "SQL Server"}, "output": {"project_description": "An edtech platform built in .NET/ASP.NET Core with SQL Server, designed to deliver interactive learning experiences. The codebase is relatively young (6 months old) and maintained by a small team with a high proportion of junior developers, focusing on rapid feature delivery under no critical constraints at this time.", "analysis": "The codebase shows early-stage characteristics with moderate coupling (5.9/10) and cohesion (6.5/10), indicating room for structural improvement but not alarming levels. Test coverage at 44.5% is suboptimal but not uncommon for a young project, especially with a junior-heavy team. Cyclomatic complexity (5.7) is within acceptable bounds for most logic, though hotspots may exist. The bugfix-commit ratio (0.48) suggests the hottest file is experiencing near-equal churn between fixes and features, which is typical for active development phases. Anti-patterns like God Class and Long Parameter List in core modules are concerning but localized, while duplicate code and high coupling are medium-level issues that can be addressed incrementally.", "recommendation": "No full migration is justified. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring and incremental improvements to address anti-patterns and boost test coverage. The team’s junior-heavy composition makes a gradual, learning-oriented approach preferable to a high-risk rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Address high-impact anti-patterns (God Class in core.py and Long Parameter List in handler.py) through modularization and parameter object extraction. Introduce basic unit tests for refactored modules to prevent regression.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Improve test coverage incrementally by adding tests for critical paths and high-churn areas. Introduce integration tests for core interactions to reduce bugfix-commit ratio over time.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactor duplicate code hotspots and reduce coupling in handler.py by introducing abstraction layers. Pair senior developers with juniors to mentor and ensure quality.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The absence of critical constraints reduces immediate risk, but the junior-heavy team may struggle with complex refactoring without guidance. Incremental phases with clear ownership and mentorship mitigate this risk effectively."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0238", "language": "en", "health_band": "critical", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 45, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 9.6, "cohesion_score": 2.9, "test_coverage_estimate": 14.0, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 7.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.75}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/handler.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/saas/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "MongoDB"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 10+ year-old SaaS B2B application for business management, built with Python/Django and MongoDB. It faces unpredictable traffic spikes and is currently constrained by scalability issues, with a highly coupled and poorly cohesive codebase that hinders maintainability and performance under load.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits severe structural problems: extreme coupling (9.6/10) and very low cohesion (2.9/10) indicate a monolithic architecture where components are tightly interdependent, making changes risky and scaling difficult. Test coverage is critically low at 14%, and high cyclomatic complexity (7.4) suggests fragile, hard-to-maintain logic. Anti-patterns like God Classes and circular dependencies are concentrated in core files (e.g., src/saas/service.py, src/saas/core.py), compounding technical debt. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.75 on the hottest file signals frequent fire-fighting, likely due to these structural flaws. While the team is experienced (45 developers), the junior-to-senior ratio (34%) may slow refactoring efforts without strong guidance.", "recommendation": "A full rewrite is not justified at this stage. Instead, prioritize targeted incremental refactoring to address the most critical anti-patterns and improve scalability. Focus first on breaking down God Classes and reducing coupling in core modules, while gradually increasing test coverage to enable safer changes. The goal is to incrementally improve maintainability and scalability without disrupting ongoing feature development.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Conduct a detailed architecture audit to identify the top 5 most critical files contributing to coupling and God Classes. Define clear boundaries for modularization (e.g., separate services for core business logic, traffic processing, and API handling).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactor the highest-impact God Class (src/saas/service.py) into smaller, focused classes with single responsibilities. Introduce dependency injection to reduce coupling in src/saas/core.py and src/saas/processor.py. Add targeted tests (aim for 30% coverage initially) for refactored components.", "duration_days_range": "20-30"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Address circular dependencies in src/saas/service.py by introducing interfaces or event-driven patterns. Break down the Long Method and Long Parameter List anti-patterns in src/saas/core.py. Parallelize with performance profiling to identify low-hanging scalability improvements (e.g., caching, async task queues).", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Gradually migrate traffic-heavy endpoints to a more scalable architecture (e.g., Django Channels for WebSockets, or lightweight microservices for async tasks). Expand test coverage incrementally, targeting 50%+ coverage for refactored modules. Document architectural decisions and onboarding guides for the team.", "duration_days_range": "30-45"}], "risk_assessment": "High risk of regression during refactoring due to low test coverage and extreme coupling. Risk is mitigated by phased, incremental changes with strong emphasis on testing and rollback plans. The team's size and experience help, but the junior-heavy ratio may require additional mentoring during refactoring. Without immediate action, scalability issues will worsen as traffic grows, increasing downtime risk during peak loads."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0239", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 4, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 35.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.29}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet e-commerce en Python/Django, lancé il y a 1,2 an, supporte une boutique en ligne avec gestion des stocks et des commandes. L'équipe de 4 développeurs, majoritairement junior, rencontre des difficultés à livrer rapidement les nouvelles fonctionnalités en raison d'une codebase vieillissante et de pratiques de développement peu optimisées pour la maintenabilité.", "analysis": "Les métriques révèlent une codebase modérément complexe avec des problèmes de couplage et de cohésion (scores de 5,1/10 et 4,4/10 respectivement), mais sans être critiques. La couverture de tests à 35,2% est faible mais gérable, et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 4,1 indique une logique modérément imbriquée. Le ratio de commits correctifs de 0,29 suggère une stabilité relative, malgré la présence d'un God Class et d'un couplage élevé dans des fichiers centraux. Ces anti-patterns expliquent en partie la lenteur des livraisons, mais ne justifient pas une refonte complète.", "recommendation": "Privilégier une approche incrémentale pour améliorer la vélocité sans prendre de risques majeurs. Cibler d'abord la réduction des anti-patterns identifiés (God Class et couplage élevé) et augmenter progressivement la couverture de tests. Une migration technologique n'est pas justifiée à ce stade, car les métriques ne montrent pas de blocage structurel insurmontable.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Décomposer le God Class (src/e-commerce/core.py) en classes plus petites et spécialisées, en appliquant le principe de responsabilité unique. Identifier les dépendances critiques et les extraire vers des services dédiés.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Réduire le couplage dans src/e-commerce/service.py en introduisant des interfaces et en appliquant l'injection de dépendances. Documenter les nouvelles interfaces pour faciliter leur adoption par l'équipe.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Augmenter la couverture de tests en ciblant les modules critiques identifiés lors des phases 1 et 2. Former l'équipe junior aux bonnes pratiques de tests unitaires et d'intégration.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Mettre en place des revues de code systématiques pour détecter et corriger les anti-patterns avant qu'ils ne s'accumulent. Automatiser des checks de qualité (ex: SonarQube) pour maintenir les standards.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque faible à modéré : les améliorations incrémentales réduisent les risques de régression tout en ciblant les goulots d'étranglement identifiés. L'équipe junior pourrait nécessiter un accompagnement pour adopter les nouvelles pratiques, mais l'impact global reste maîtrisé. Aucune migration technologique n'est envisagée, évitant ainsi les risques inhérents à un changement radical."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0239", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 4, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.1, "cohesion_score": 4.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 35.2, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.29}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/e-commerce/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "An e-commerce platform built in Python/Django/PostgreSQL over the past 1.2 years by a team of four developers (70% junior, 24% senior). The primary business constraint is slow feature delivery, prompting a review of code quality and maintainability to improve team velocity.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate coupling (5.1/10) and cohesion (4.4/10), indicating structural issues that likely slow development. Test coverage is critically low at 35.2%, and cyclomatic complexity is elevated at 4.1, suggesting fragility in key components. The presence of a God Class in core.py and high coupling in service.py directly correlates with the reported slow feature delivery, as changes in these files likely trigger cascading updates and regressions. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.29 on the hottest file further signals technical debt accumulation. While the stack is modern and the codebase is relatively young, the anti-patterns and quality metrics are the primary bottlenecks, not the technology choice.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the stack. Instead, focus on targeted refactoring to address the God Class and high coupling in the identified files. Improve test coverage incrementally and reduce cyclomatic complexity in critical paths. These changes will directly address the velocity constraint without the high risk and cost of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor core.py to break the God Class into smaller, focused classes with clear responsibilities. Introduce dependency injection to reduce coupling in service.py. Add targeted unit tests for the refactored components.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Incrementally improve test coverage from 35.2% to at least 60% by adding unit and integration tests for critical paths. Focus on areas with high cyclomatic complexity (e.g., 4.1) to reduce fragility.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural patterns (e.g., layered architecture, CQRS) to further decouple components and improve cohesion. Pair senior developers with juniors to transfer knowledge and ensure sustainable practices.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the refactoring itself—introducing bugs during changes to core.py and service.py. Mitigation includes comprehensive testing (Phase 2), incremental rollouts, and close monitoring of bugfix rates. The risk of a full rewrite is higher due to the team's junior-heavy composition and the lack of clear ROI justification. Targeted improvements align better with the team's constraints and the project's age."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0241", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.27}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Le projet 'LogiFlow' est un système de gestion logistique en Ruby on Rails qui coordonne les flux de marchandises pour une chaîne d'approvisionnement internationale. L'application doit gérer des pics de trafic soudains liés à des commandes imprévisibles, tout en garantissant une traçabilité en temps réel des stocks et des livraisons. L'équipe technique, composée de profils variés, fait face à des défis de scalabilité et de maintenabilité sur une codebase vieillissante de 4.5 ans.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs mitigés : un couplage modéré (5.3/10) et une cohésion faible (4.5/10) suggèrent une architecture encore trop monolithique avec des dépendances mal isolées. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne (4.5) et la couverture de tests limitée (41.1%) indiquent un risque élevé de régressions lors des modifications. Les anti-patterns 'Long Method' dans le fichier critique src/logistique/core.py confirment des problèmes de maintenabilité, mais le ratio de commits correctifs (0.27) reste acceptable pour une codebase de cette taille. Aucune métrique ne justifie un rewrite complet, mais des améliorations ciblées sont nécessaires pour réduire la dette technique.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration technologique coûteuse et risquée, privilégier une refonte incrémentale de l'architecture pour améliorer la scalabilité et la maintenabilité. L'objectif est de réduire le couplage et d'augmenter la cohésion via une décomposition progressive du monolithe en services modulaires, en commençant par les zones les plus critiques (ex: src/logistique/core.py). La couverture de tests doit être renforcée en priorité pour sécuriser les changements futurs.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi pour identifier les goulots d'étranglement scalabilité et les dépendances critiques. Définition d'une stratégie de découplage incrémental avec priorisation des modules les plus impactés (ex: gestion des stocks, traitement des commandes).", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Refactoring ciblé des méthodes 'Long Method' dans src/logistique/core.py avec ajout de tests unitaires pour couvrir les nouveaux comportements. Introduction de patterns de conception (ex: Strategy, Command) pour réduire la complexité cyclomatique.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Décomposition progressive du monolithe en services autonomes (ex: service de routage, service de gestion des entrepôts) avec intégration de mécanismes de cache et de files d'attente asynchrones pour absorber les pics de trafic. Migration des données critiques en priorité.", "duration_days_range": "40-60"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Renforcement de la couverture de tests (objectif : +20%) via des tests d'intégration et de bout-en-bout. Mise en place de métriques de qualité continues (ex: SonarQube) pour suivre l'évolution de la dette technique.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Le principal risque est la sous-estimation de la complexité des dépendances dans le monolithe, pouvant entraîner des blocages lors du découplage. Pour le limiter, prévoir des revues de code strictes et des tests de régression automatisés avant chaque modification. La scalabilité immédiate ne sera pas résolue par cette approche, mais les fondations seront posées pour des optimisations futures (ex: passage à une architecture event-driven)."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0241", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 5.3, "cohesion_score": 4.5, "test_coverage_estimate": 41.1, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.5, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.27}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/core.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Ruby", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a supply-chain logistics platform built with Ruby on Rails and MySQL over the past 4.5 years. It serves a team of 24 developers who must handle unpredictable traffic spikes while maintaining system stability and rapid bug fixes. The codebase is currently challenged by scalability constraints and a need to improve maintainability under growing feature demand.", "analysis": "The metrics show a moderately coupled and only marginally cohesive codebase (5.3/10 coupling, 4.5/10 cohesion) with low test coverage (41.1%) and acceptable cyclomatic complexity (4.5). The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.27 on the hottest file indicates that hotspots are already receiving attention, but the presence of two high-severity Long Method anti-patterns in the same file suggests localized complexity that can be addressed incrementally. The team size and junior-to-senior ratio are balanced enough to support refactoring without requiring a full rewrite. The dominant constraint—scalability under unpredictable load—is not directly caused by architectural flaws but rather by missing performance optimizations and caching layers, which can be introduced incrementally.", "recommendation": "Do NOT migrate or rewrite. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to reduce coupling, improve cohesion, and raise test coverage while addressing the identified anti-patterns. A full rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk and delay addressing the real constraint: scalability under load.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the two Long Method anti-patterns in src/logistique/core.py into smaller, single-responsibility methods; introduce targeted unit tests for the refactored logic to raise coverage from 41.1% to at least 55%.", "duration_days_range": "10-14"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Introduce caching (Redis) at the controller layer for high-traffic endpoints and implement a background job queue (Sidekiq) to offload non-critical processing, reducing peak load on the Rails stack.", "duration_days_range": "12-18"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Run a static analysis sweep to identify and reduce coupling hotspots; extract shared logic into service objects and introduce facade patterns where appropriate to improve cohesion.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Expand test coverage to 65% by adding integration tests for critical user journeys and performance tests to validate scalability improvements under simulated load.", "duration_days_range": "14-20"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks are temporary performance degradation during refactoring and the possibility of introducing regressions if tests are not comprehensive enough. Mitigation includes feature flags, canary deployments, and incremental rollouts. The absence of critical architectural flaws (e.g., deep inheritance chains, global state misuse) reduces systemic risk."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0242", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "e-commerce", "team_size": 8, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.6, "cohesion_score": 8.4, "test_coverage_estimate": 63.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 1.4, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.05}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/e-commerce/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a mature e-commerce platform built over 10 years with a Python/Django/PostgreSQL stack, serving an unpredictable traffic load typical of seasonal retail peaks. The team of 8 developers (mix of junior and senior) maintains a codebase where business logic is tightly coupled to service orchestration, creating scalability bottlenecks during traffic surges despite generally clean internal cohesion and low cyclomatic complexity in most modules.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy internal quality metrics: strong cohesion (8.4/10), low cyclomatic complexity (1.4), and a low bugfix ratio (0.05) in the most active file, indicating stable behavior under change. However, the coupling score (2.6/10) signals architectural rigidity, particularly in the service layer, which directly conflicts with the dominant constraint of handling unpredictable traffic spikes. The test coverage (63.8%) is suboptimal and could hinder safe refactoring. The team composition suggests a need for incremental, well-guided improvements rather than a disruptive rewrite.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate the entire stack. Instead, focus on targeted architectural improvements to reduce coupling in the service layer while preserving the existing Django/PostgreSQL foundation. This approach aligns with the team's experience level and the platform's maturity, addressing the scalability constraint without incurring the high risk of a full rewrite.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the high-coupling service layer to introduce clear boundaries using Django service objects or domain-driven design patterns. Implement automated tests to reach at least 80% coverage for the refactored module.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Introduce horizontal scaling mechanisms (e.g., Django Channels for async tasks, PostgreSQL read replicas) and validate performance under simulated traffic spikes. Document scaling policies and rollback procedures.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Gradually extend refactoring to adjacent modules with high coupling, ensuring backward compatibility. Conduct a post-refactor load test to confirm scalability improvements.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risk is regression during service layer refactoring, mitigated by high cohesion and low cyclomatic complexity. Team experience and incremental approach reduce risk further. The main unresolved risk is the lack of automated tests in non-refactored areas, which could slow down future changes."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0243", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 34, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet SaaS B2B de gestion d'entreprise, en production depuis 5.5 ans, supporte une base de 34 développeurs avec une répartition équilibrée entre juniors et seniors. L'application, basée sur Node.js/NestJS et PostgreSQL, doit gérer des pics de trafic imprévisibles tout en garantissant une expérience utilisateur fluide pour ses clients entreprises.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des métriques globalement saines malgré quelques points de vigilance. Le score de couplage à 3.0/10 indique une modularité acceptable, tandis que la cohésion à 4.7/10 suggère une organisation logique des responsabilités. La complexité cyclomatique moyenne de 5.6 reste dans une fourchette gérable, et le ratio de commits correctifs de 0.23 montre une stabilité relative du code. Cependant, la couverture de tests à 33.5% est un signal d'alerte majeur, surtout pour un système SaaS où la fiabilité est critique. Les anti-patterns concentrés dans src/saas/service.py et processor.py (duplicate code, circular dependencies, god class, long methods) forment un risque technique concret qui limite la scalabilité et la maintenabilité.", "recommendation": "Une migration technologique complète n'est pas justifiée par les métriques actuelles. Les problèmes identifiés sont localisés et peuvent être résolus par des refactorings ciblés sans remettre en cause l'architecture globale. L'accent doit être mis sur l'amélioration de la couverture de tests et l'élimination des anti-patterns dans les modules critiques, tout en mettant en place des garde-fous pour éviter leur réapparition.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Audit technique approfondi des modules src/saas/service.py et processor.py pour prioriser les refactorings en fonction de leur impact sur la scalabilité et la maintenabilité. Définition d'un plan de découpage des God Classes et d'élimination des circular dependencies.", "duration_days_range": "8-12 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Mise en place d'un pipeline de tests automatisés avec couverture minimale à 70% pour les modules critiques. Intégration de SonarQube ou d'un outil similaire pour détecter les anti-patterns en temps réel dans les PR.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Refactoring incrémental des modules identifiés : découpage des God Classes en services plus petits, élimination des circular dependencies via l'injection de dépendances, et réduction des méthodes longues. Mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour les changements dans ces modules.", "duration_days_range": "25-35 jours"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Optimisation des pics de trafic : analyse des goulots d'étranglement dans PostgreSQL (index, requêtes lentes) et mise en place de stratégies de caching (Redis) pour les données fréquemment accédées. Tests de charge pour valider les améliorations.", "duration_days_range": "12-18 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque MODÉRÉ si les phases sont exécutées dans l'ordre. Le principal risque est la sous-estimation de l'effort nécessaire pour atteindre une couverture de tests suffisante, surtout pour les modules legacy. Un autre risque est la régression de performance lors des refactorings si les tests de charge ne sont pas exécutés rigoureusement. La concentration des anti-patterns dans un petit nombre de fichiers limite cependant l'exposition globale du projet."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0243", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "SaaS B2B (gestion d'entreprise)", "team_size": 34, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.0, "cohesion_score": 4.7, "test_coverage_estimate": 33.5, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 5.6, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.23}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Duplicate Code", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "Circular Dependency", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "God Class", "location": "src/saas/service.py", "severity": "medium"}, {"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/saas/processor.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "Node.js", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A 5.5-year-old SaaS B2B platform for business management built with Node.js, NestJS, and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 34 developers (21% junior, 43% senior). The system faces unpredictable traffic spikes, requiring strong scalability, and currently exhibits architectural challenges that hinder maintainability and performance under load.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.0/10 and cohesion at 4.7/10, indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage is low at 33.5%, which increases the risk of regressions during changes. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 5.6, but several high-impact anti-patterns are concentrated in critical files: duplicate code, circular dependencies, a God Class, and long methods. These issues directly threaten scalability and maintainability, especially under unpredictable load. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.23 on the hottest file suggests active maintenance but also highlights fragility in frequently modified areas.", "recommendation": "Do not perform a full technology migration. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the identified anti-patterns and improve test coverage. The current stack (Node.js/NestJS/PostgreSQL) is well-suited for the domain and team skillset, and a rewrite would introduce unnecessary risk without clear benefit. Addressing the structural issues will yield better scalability and maintainability gains with lower risk.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the critical files (src/saas/service.py and src/saas/processor.py) to eliminate duplicate code, break circular dependencies, split the God Class into cohesive components, and decompose long methods. Introduce dependency injection and modular design patterns to improve cohesion and reduce coupling.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement targeted test coverage improvements, focusing on the refactored modules and critical paths. Prioritize unit and integration tests for the hottest files to reduce regression risk during future changes.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce architectural guardrails such as static analysis tools (e.g., ESLint, SonarQube) and CI checks to prevent regression of anti-patterns. Document the new modular structure and update onboarding materials to reflect best practices.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The primary risks stem from the low test coverage and the concentration of anti-patterns in critical files. However, these risks are mitigated by focusing on incremental refactoring rather than a full rewrite. The team's senior-heavy composition is well-suited to execute the proposed changes. The biggest risk is potential downtime during refactoring; this can be minimized by scheduling changes during low-traffic periods and using feature flags for gradual rollouts."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0244", "language": "fr", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.2, "cohesion_score": 5.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet pilote une plateforme SaaS de gestion logistique pour des transporteurs tiers, avec intégration de modules de traçabilité sanitaire et de paiement sécurisé. L'application centralise les flux de données entre entrepôts, transporteurs et clients finaux, sous forte contrainte de conformité réglementaire (RGPD, PCI-DSS, HDS). Développée en PHP/Laravel sur 2 ans par une équipe majoritairement junior, elle doit évoluer rapidement pour supporter de nouveaux marchés tout en garantissant la résilience des processus critiques.", "analysis": "La codebase présente des indicateurs contrastés : un couplage modéré (3.2/10) et une complexité cyclomatique acceptable (4.1) suggèrent une architecture globalement maintenable, mais la cohésion faible (5.6/10) et la couverture de tests insuffisante (34.7%) révèlent des faiblesses structurelles. Les anti-patterns détectés (Long Method dans le processor logistique et High Coupling dans le service métier) confirment des zones de friction majeures. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.35) indique cependant une stabilité relative du code chaud, malgré ces défauts. La contrainte réglementaire impose une rigueur particulière sur la traçabilité et la sécurité, mais ne justifie pas à elle seule une refonte radicale.", "recommendation": "Plutôt qu'une migration coûteuse et risquée vers une nouvelle stack, privilégier une modernisation incrémentale ciblée sur les points de douleur identifiés. L'objectif est d'améliorer la maintenabilité et la testabilité sans perturber les fonctionnalités critiques, tout en préparant le terrain pour des évolutions futures. La priorité doit être donnée à la réduction des anti-patterns et à l'augmentation de la couverture de tests, particulièrement dans les modules réglementaires où la dette technique est la plus critique.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Décomposition des méthodes longues et réduction du couplage dans les modules logistiques (processor.py et service.py) via des refactorings guidés par les tests. Mise en place de revues de code systématiques pour les fichiers critiques.", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Augmentation de la couverture de tests jusqu'à 60% via des tests unitaires et d'intégration pour les modules réglementaires (RGPD, PCI-DSS). Automatisation des tests de conformité dans le pipeline CI.", "duration_days_range": "25-35"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Migration progressive des dépendances critiques vers des versions maintenues et sécurisées (Laravel, packages tiers). Documentation des interfaces internes pour faciliter les futures évolutions.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Formation de l'équipe sur les bonnes pratiques de test et de conception (Clean Architecture, SOLID) avec ateliers pratiques sur des cas concrets du projet.", "duration_days_range": "8-12"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque modéré si les refactorings sont menés avec une couverture de tests suffisante. Le principal danger réside dans l'impact potentiel sur les fonctionnalités réglementaires critiques, nécessitant une validation manuelle approfondie après chaque changement. L'équipe junior devra être accompagnée pour éviter une accumulation de dette technique pendant les évolutions. Une approche par feature flags est recommandée pour les modules sensibles."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0244", "language": "en", "health_band": "moderate", "input": {"sector": "logistique / supply chain", "team_size": 24, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 3.2, "cohesion_score": 5.6, "test_coverage_estimate": 34.7, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 4.1, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.35}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Method", "location": "src/logistique/processor.py", "severity": "high"}, {"type": "High Coupling", "location": "src/logistique/service.py", "severity": "high"}], "language": "PHP", "database_name": "MySQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "The project is a 2-year-old logistics and supply chain platform built with PHP/Laravel and MySQL, serving a team of 24 developers (68% junior, 6% senior). The system operates under strict regulatory constraints including GDPR, PCI-DSS, and HDS compliance, requiring continuous attention to data protection and security standards.", "analysis": "The codebase shows moderate structural health with a coupling score of 3.2/10 and cohesion at 5.6/10, indicating room for improvement in modularity and separation of concerns. Test coverage at 34.7% is below industry standards and may hinder maintainability and reliability, particularly under regulatory scrutiny. Cyclomatic complexity is acceptable at 4.1, but the presence of high-severity anti-patterns—such as a Long Method in the logistics processor and high coupling in the service layer—poses risks to scalability and future compliance efforts. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.35 suggests reactive maintenance, which could slow down feature development and regulatory updates.", "recommendation": "A full technology migration is not justified at this time. Instead, focus on targeted incremental improvements to address the identified anti-patterns, improve test coverage, and enhance modularity while maintaining regulatory compliance.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the high-coupling service layer and long method in the processor to improve cohesion and reduce coupling. Introduce unit and integration tests for the refactored components to raise coverage incrementally.", "duration_days_range": "20-25"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Implement automated testing pipelines and expand test coverage to at least 50% by adding tests for critical paths, especially those related to regulatory compliance (e.g., data handling, audit logs).", "duration_days_range": "15-20"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Introduce modular design patterns (e.g., domain-driven design or service-oriented architecture) to further decouple components and improve maintainability. Prioritize areas with high change frequency or regulatory impact.", "duration_days_range": "25-30"}, {"phase": 4, "action": "Conduct a compliance-focused security review and static analysis to identify and remediate vulnerabilities. Update documentation and training for the team on regulatory requirements and secure coding practices.", "duration_days_range": "10-15"}], "risk_assessment": "The primary risks are related to regulatory non-compliance and technical debt accumulation. Without addressing the anti-patterns and improving test coverage, future updates may become error-prone and difficult to validate against compliance standards. However, the risks of a full migration (e.g., extended downtime, scope creep, or data integrity issues) outweigh the benefits given the current codebase health. Incremental improvements mitigate these risks while delivering measurable value."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0248", "language": "fr", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 7.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 86.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.01}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "Ce projet est un système backend temps réel pour un jeu en ligne massivement multijoueur, développé en Python avec FastAPI et PostgreSQL. L'équipe de 26 développeurs maintient une codebase de près de 10 ans, avec des exigences strictes de latence pour garantir une expérience de jeu fluide et réactive.", "analysis": {"global_health": "Les métriques globales indiquent une base de code saine et maintenable. Le score de couplage (2.7/10) suggère une architecture modulaire avec des dépendances maîtrisées, tandis que la cohésion (7.2/10) confirme une bonne organisation des responsabilités. La couverture de tests (86.8%) et la complexité cyclomatique moyenne (2.0) sont excellentes pour un projet de cette taille et ancienneté. Le ratio de commits correctifs (0.01) est remarquablement bas, signe d'une stabilité fonctionnelle.", "anti_patterns": "L'anti-pattern 'Long Parameter List' détecté dans src/gaming/service.py est mineur et isolé. Il n'impacte ni les performances ni la maintenabilité globale du projet.", "team_impact": "Avec 69% de juniors, la simplicité de la stack actuelle (Python/FastAPI) est un atout majeur. Une migration vers une technologie moins répandue ou plus complexe augmenterait significativement la courbe d'apprentissage et les risques de régression.", "latency_constraint": "La contrainte de latence temps réel est critique, mais la stack actuelle (Python/FastAPI avec PostgreSQL) peut y répondre si elle est correctement optimisée. Une migration vers une autre stack ne garantit pas automatiquement une amélioration des performances."}, "recommendation": "Aucune migration technologique n'est justifiée par les données. Les métriques indiquent une base de code saine, maintenable et performante pour les besoins actuels. Une approche incrémentale d'optimisation et de correction des anti-patterns mineurs est préférable.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Correction ciblée de l'anti-pattern 'Long Parameter List' dans src/gaming/service.py via refactoring et ajout de DTOs (Data Transfer Objects) pour encapsuler les paramètres.", "duration_days_range": "3-5 jours"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Audit des goulots d'étranglement liés à la latence dans les endpoints critiques, avec optimisation des requêtes PostgreSQL et mise en cache (Redis) si nécessaire.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 jours"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Renforcement de la documentation technique et des tests de charge pour valider les optimisations et former les juniors aux bonnes pratiques de performance.", "duration_days_range": "5-7 jours"}], "risk_assessment": "Risque global faible. Les actions proposées sont incrémentales, réversibles et ciblent des problèmes mineurs. Aucune migration n'est envisagée, ce qui élimine les risques majeurs liés à un changement technologique. Le principal risque réside dans une optimisation excessive qui pourrait introduire des bugs, mais les métriques actuelles (faible complexité cyclomatique, haute couverture de tests) limitent ce risque."}}
{"scenario_id": "scn_0248", "language": "en", "health_band": "healthy", "input": {"sector": "gaming", "team_size": 26, "metrics": {"coupling_score": 2.7, "cohesion_score": 7.2, "test_coverage_estimate": 86.8, "avg_cyclomatic_complexity": 2.0, "top_hotspot_bugfix_ratio": 0.01}, "anti_patterns": [{"type": "Long Parameter List", "location": "src/gaming/service.py", "severity": "low"}], "language": "Python", "database_name": "PostgreSQL"}, "output": {"project_description": "A real-time gaming backend service built with Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL, serving a team of 26 developers with a majority of junior members. The system operates under strict low-latency constraints critical for gaming experiences, with a codebase that has evolved over 9.7 years and demonstrates strong internal quality metrics.", "analysis": "The codebase exhibits healthy structural metrics with low coupling (2.7/10) and high cohesion (7.2/10), indicating a well-modularized system. Test coverage stands at 86.8% with low cyclomatic complexity (2.0), suggesting maintainable and testable code. The bugfix-commit ratio of 0.01 on the hottest file implies stable production behavior. Only a minor anti-pattern (Long Parameter List) was detected, which is a low-impact issue. The team's junior-heavy composition may benefit from targeted mentorship rather than a full technology shift.", "recommendation": "Do not migrate. Instead, focus on incremental improvements to address the minor anti-pattern and enhance team capabilities.", "phases": [{"phase": 1, "action": "Refactor the Long Parameter List anti-pattern in src/gaming/service.py using parameter objects or dependency injection patterns. Pair with a senior developer to mentor junior team members on clean code practices.", "duration_days_range": "5-8 days"}, {"phase": 2, "action": "Conduct a performance audit of the real-time latency paths, focusing on database query optimization and FastAPI middleware tuning. Document findings in a runbook for future reference.", "duration_days_range": "10-15 days"}, {"phase": 3, "action": "Implement a structured onboarding program for junior developers covering the codebase architecture, testing strategies, and performance best practices. Include pair programming sessions with senior developers.", "duration_days_range": "15-20 days"}], "risk_assessment": "Low to moderate. The current metrics suggest a stable system, but the junior-heavy team composition poses a risk for long-term maintainability. The proposed phases address both technical debt and team capability gaps without introducing migration risks."}}
